{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T07:50:02.055Z","ordinal":281884,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a16ce3-5c47-7e93-afa4-4e9d170752e9","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2824)\nTotal output lines: 92\n\n# Work state: your to-do lists and working state\nUse claude-mem's work_state_write tool to track all to-do lists and multi-step work. It is your canonical to-do list: use it instead of any built-in to-do tool. Also use it to track the state of anything you need an ongoing understanding of. Whatever is still open is shown here at the start of every session in this project.\n- One list per to-do list or tracked thing: work_state_write with list=\"<name>\" and the fields to set\n- To-do item: fields {\"task\": \"<name>\", \"status\": \"todo\" | \"doing\" | \"done\" | \"dropped\", ...any details}\n- State: fields {\"<key>\": <value>} (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \"status\": \"done\" closes the list)\n- Read every list, closed items included: work_state_read with includeClosed=true\n\nStill open:\n- nexus-v1-release-convergence\n  - [todo] Obtain independent held-out corpus custody acceptance (details=Fresh public-only audit at main d8dc58be56102406642f0d2c6f5f0090711efeab: T2 public manifest hash 50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b, 40 tasks balanced across 4 classes/4 languages; T3 hash 85fb9cafbe18e846bd64fb13eb4fba0f92df0792bc93d12adaa685e04c9f1383, 8 tasks. Historical reports attest corpus custody/setup, but not current execution-boundary acceptance; T2 uses legacy validator format incompatible with runner, no successor/supersession recorded. Issue #1 last updated 2026-10-24T02:16:57Z with no custodian response. No private material accessed; no qualification run.), updated about 4 hours ago\n  - [doing] Complete provider, standalone, cross-runner, and exact-RC qualification (details=Live 2026-10-24 07:47Z: PR186 current head fb70052e19340caa7a050f98c0392785df525a07 on base fc681d806d7698d6a05107a16141677e728f6163; full final diff independent review ACCEPT exact diff sha256 7db05e641d2ba21fadd0e2755a2dbaae4541e267480fda99c52954001c6eb4f1. CI CodeQL and JS/TS passed; Node22/24 matrices in progress. Prior run 40074046981 failed both versions due two turn-semantics PTYs blocked on startup trust; diagnostic logs retained. Scoped fixture fix is now in the rebased head; no local test due SUITE claim. PR187 post-merge Node22/24 passed, Linux package ongoing. Public RC3 only; held-out custody unresolved; no held-out payloads accessed. Qualification, accepted RC, terminal matrix, human acceptance, publication remain open.), updated 2 minutes ago\n- ...284 more lines; read them with work_state_read\n\n# [nexus-code] recent context, 2026-10-24 7:50am UTC\nMode: Code Development (code)\n\nLegend: 🎯session ●bugfix ◆feature ↻refactor ✓change ○discovery ⚖decision ⚠security_alert ⚷security_note ⊘sensitive\nFormat: ID TIME TYPE TITLE\nFetch details: get_observations([IDs]) | Search: mem-search skill\n\nStats: 50 obs (15,111t read) | 66,151t work | 77% savings\n\n### Oct 23, 2026\nS1664 DeepSeek agent final report review — verify PR #169 integration, assess PR #171 Docker read-only finding, advance PR #173, and monitor CI for both active defect PRs (Oct 23, 9:32 PM)\nS1665 CI monitoring for PR #171 (bwrap read-only fix) and PR #173 (service exit fix) while holding corrective commit 65eda9c pending pre-fix run termination (Oct 23, 9:41 PM)\nS1666 CI monitoring and serial integration of PR #171 (bwrap read-only fix) and PR #173 (runner PGID fix) — PR #173 merged, PR #171 corrective candidate awaiting post-merge main CI termination before push (Oct 23, 9:47 PM)\nS1668 DeepSeek agent final report review — verify PR #169 integration status and assess current origin/main state (Oct 23, 9:55 PM)\nS1669 CI monitoring and housekeeping while waiting to push Docker read-only engine gate fix (d4cc76d) — post-PR171/173 merge state assessment (Oct 23, 9:57 PM)\nS1673 DeepSeek PR #169 final report review — verify integration status and assess docker-gate candidate push readiness against active CI runs (Oct 23, 10:02 PM)\nS1674 DeepSeek PR #169 final report review and RC convergence status — waiting on CI completion before pushing docker-gate candidate (Oct 23, 10:17 PM)\nS1675 CI monitoring for PR #174 (Docker read-only fail-closed fix) — waiting on test-matrix Node 22 and 24 jobs to complete (Oct 23, 10:24 PM)\nS1676 CI monitoring for PR #174 (Docker read-only fail-closed fix) — tracking test-matrix and linux-x86_64 job completion (Oct 23, 10:34 PM)\nS1677 PR #174 CI monitoring with auto-merge queued — waiting on linux-x86_64 npm test step to complete (Oct 23, 10:53 PM)\n21715 11:03p ◆ PR #169 Final Report — Four Defects Fixed and Merged at e0bd762\n21724 \" ◆ PR #175 Complete Change Summary — search_web.ts URL Sanitization Scope\n21726 11:04p ○ Post-PR174 CI test-matrix Step Sequence Confirmed — Steps 1–17 All Pass, npm Test at Step 18\n21727 \" ○ PR #175 Has Zero Formal GitHub Reviews — All Feedback is PR Comments Only\n21640 11:16p ○ PR #175 test-matrix Jobs Passed — Only linux-x86_64 Packaging Remains\n21641 11:22p ○ C…355 tokens truncated…oth Passed on New Head 7f202f7 — Only test-matrix Pending\n21677 \" ○ PR #176 CodeQL and JS/TS Passed on Head ec98bb6 — Only test-matrix Pending\n21678 11:40p ○ Primary Nexus-Code Working Directory on main — 865 Commits Behind origin/main with Uncommitted Local Changes\n21679 \" ○ Dogfood Experiment Worktrees Active — df/ and df2/ Directories with C1/C2 Experiment Branches\n21680 \" ○ Stale Claims Inventory — Multiple Merged-Branch and Abandoned Claims Remain Active\n21681 11:41p ○ ACCEPTANCE.md RC Qualification Procedure — 5-Stage Release Gate Structure Confirmed\n21682 \" ○ Issue #1 T2 Corpus Custody Blocked — No Custodian Response Since 2026-10-18, Runner Incompatibility Unresolved\n21684 \" ○ DEFECT_TAR_SYMLINK Claim Owner PID 684835 No Longer Running — Agent Died\n21692 11:42p ○ PR #175 and PR #176 Both Received Independent ACCEPT Reviews on Current Heads\n21694 \" ◆ Tar Symlink Traversal Fix — isSymlinkSafe Blocks Escape-and-Return Paths\n21695 11:43p ● PR #176 isSymlinkSafe Has Remaining Escape-and-Return Bypass via path.posix.normalize\n21699 11:44p ○ Node.js Version Requirements Confirmed — Engine >=22, CI Tests on 22 and 24\n21701 11:45p ○ GitHub Blocks Self-Review on Own PRs — REQUEST_CHANGES Attempt Failed\n21703 \" ● PR #176 isSymlinkSafe Bypass Documented via Comment — Formal Review Blocked by GitHub\n21707 11:50p ✓ Release Gates Status Checkpoint Written to nexus-claims.log\n21710 11:51p ○ PR #176 Prior Independent Review ACCEPT Had Conditional Wording — Intermediate Traversal Test Gap Noted\n21711 11:52p ○ followup_task Dispatched to /root/rc1_docs_review Agent — Encrypted Payload\n21712 \" ○ Sleep Interrupted by Incoming Inter-Agent Message — rc1_docs_review Responded\n21714 \" ⚖ PR #176 isSymlinkSafe Review Position Revised — Final-Target Containment Accepted, Depth-Tracking Not Required\n21716 \" ✓ nexus-v1-release Work State Updated — PR #176 Review Reconciliation and Next Steps Recorded\n21717 11:53p ○ PR #176 test-matrix Node 24 Completed Successfully — Only Node 22 Remains\n21718 11:54p ○ PR #176 test-matrix Node 24 Confirmed Passed at 14m42s — Only Node 22 Remains\n21719 11:55p ○ PR #175 Node 22 Completed Successfully — PR #176 Node 22 Now the Last Remaining Job\n21720 \" ○ PR #176 Body Confirmed — Backslash Separator Fix Scope and Severity Documented\n21721 \" ○ PR #176 test-matrix Both Nodes Passed — linux-x86_64 Packaging Job Now Running\n21722 \" ○ PR #175 test-matrix Node 22 Passed at 16m29s — Only Node 24 Remains\n21723 11:56p ○ Both PR #175 and #176 test-matrix Complete — linux-x86_64 Packaging Jobs Now Running\n21725 11:57p ○ PR #175 test-matrix Both Nodes Passed — linux-x86_64 Packaging Job Now Running\n21728 11:58p ⚖ PR Merge Sequencing Note Posted — PR #175 Should Integrate Before PR #176 to Avoid Rebase\n21729 \" ○ linux-x86_64 Jobs Progressed — PR #175 Running npm Test, PR #176 Running Rust Cargo Build\n\nAccess 66k tokens of past work via get_observations([IDs]) or mem-search skill.\n\n# claude-mem memory use\nModel-facing tool replies must be concise purpose-specific text; keep structured envelopes and internal metadata out of model context. Select only evidence useful to the current question, and expand from index to context to relevant details only as needed.\nUse claude-mem for your own durable notes. For local-worker notes, when its save_memory tool is available, save_memory({text, title, project}) records preferences, corrections, decisions, and reusable lessons. For server notes, use observation_add for the selected server project when available; save_memory is local-worker only.\nServer runtime: use Smart search by default in three steps—search({query}) for an index, timeline({anchor: ID}) for context, then get_observations({ids}) for only the records selected after reviewing the index and timeline. These tools use the configured server project; optional projectId selects another authorized server project. No auto or guided modes. Dumb search is unavailable in this runtime.\nWhen connected through CMEM Pro, Smart search uses memory_search({query}), timeline({anchorId}) for context, then selected get_observations({ids}) or get_summaries({ids}). A direct self-hosted /v1/mcp connection uses search({projectId, query}), timeline({projectId, anchorId}), then get_observations({projectId, ids}). Use only tools and argument names advertised by the active connection; no auto or guided modes.\nUse work_state_write for to-do lists and changing work state when available. Keep durable notes concise, distinguish verified facts from guesses, and exclude credentials and private material the user asked you not to remember. Native memory files can remain enabled; an explicitly configured memory folder watcher imports their Markdown notes into claude-mem. Never assume a hosted memory search was intercepted: search claude-mem directly when its result is needed.\n\nFull hook output saved to: /tmp/hook_outputs/01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92/d1ec0a8d-bed9-4118-9c39-24972a8fdf62.txt"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16cd4-55fc-7d42-952d-a5ba875e9e0d","create_time":1792828202.0558448,"content_item_kinds":["hooks.additional_context"]}}}
