{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T07:50:05.569Z","ordinal":281889,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a16ce3-6a00-7ac1-8aa5-2d294e70ea1f","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT** — exact head `c92861fd7de4bb9f74739aeaaa93b59e4895c625` against base `fc681d806d7698d6a05107a16141677e728f6163`.\n\nThe cleanup path pins the `.nexus` state root, checkpoints root, partition, snapshots root, and snapshot parents with directory file descriptors opened using `O_NOFOLLOW`; it checks planned identities before unlinking the record or recursively removing the snapshot ([retention.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/retention-partition-symlink/cli/src/core/retention.ts:899), [retention.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/retention-partition-symlink/cli/src/core/retention.ts:1006)). Recursive deletion stays anchored to pinned parent descriptors and unlinks symlinks without following them ([retention.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/retention-partition-symlink/cli/src/core/retention.ts:979)).\n\nIf Linux `/proc/self/fd`, `O_DIRECTORY`, or `O_NOFOLLOW` is unavailable, the guard throws before checkpoint mutation; execution records an error and preserves that checkpoint. This also means checkpoint GC is unavailable on non-Linux platforms, an intentional fail-closed compatibility limit.\n\nThe new tests cover root, partition, and snapshots-root replacement after planning, both symlink and real-directory replacements, plus successful deletion of a normal in-store snapshot ([retention_checkpoint_confinement.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/retention-partition-symlink/cli/test/retention_checkpoint_confinement.test.ts:91)). I did not run tests."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16cd4-55fc-7d42-952d-a5ba875e9e0d","create_time":1792828205.5688806}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":14461}}
