{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T07:50:23.220Z","ordinal":281901,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16cd4-55fc-7d42-952d-a5ba875e9e0d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-40af7c06-e4a5-4c11-92f0-ed8c10a4ec4f","process_id":"15150","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git fetch origin main --prune; printf 'REMOTE_MAIN '; git rev-parse origin/main; printf 'CLAIMS_DIR '; git rev-parse --git-common-dir; cat docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md | sed -n '1,180p'; printf '\\nRETENTION STATUS\\n'; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/retention-partition-symlink status --short --branch; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/retention-partition-symlink log -5 --oneline --decorate; printf '\\nCLAIMS\\n'; for x in DEFECT_RETENTION_PARTITION_SYMLINK_20261024 SUITE_RETENTION_PARTITION_SYMLINK_20261024 FILE_cli_src_core_retention.ts FILE_cli_test_retention_checkpoint_confinement.test.ts; do f=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/$x/owner.json\"; test ! -f \"$f\" || { echo \"$x\"; cat \"$f\"; }; done; printf '\\nPR186 DETAILS\\n'; gh pr view 186 --json body,reviews,comments,mergeable,mergeStateStatus; printf '\\nACTIVE MAIN CI\\n'; gh run list --branch main --limit 5 --json databaseId,headSha,status,conclusion,workflowName,createdAt"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git fetch origin main --prune; printf 'REMOTE_MAIN '; git rev-parse origin/main; printf 'CLAIMS_DIR '; git rev-parse --git-common-dir; cat docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md | sed -n '1,180p'; printf '\\nRETENTION STATUS\\n'; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/retention-partition-symlink status --short --branch; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/retention-partition-symlink log -5 --oneline --decorate; printf '\\nCLAIMS\\n'; for x in DEFECT_RETENTION_PARTITION_SYMLINK_20261024 SUITE_RETENTION_PARTITION_SYMLINK_20261024 FILE_cli_src_core_retention.ts FILE_cli_test_retention_checkpoint_confinement.test.ts; do f=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/$x/owner.json\"; test ! -f \"$f\" || { echo \"$x\"; cat \"$f\"; }; done; printf '\\nPR186 DETAILS\\n'; gh pr view 186 --json body,reviews,comments,mergeable,mergeStateStatus; printf '\\nACTIVE MAIN CI\\n'; gh run list --branch main --limit 5 --json databaseId,headSha,status,conclusion,workflowName,createdAt"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"From https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code\n * branch            main       -> FETCH_HEAD\nREMOTE_MAIN fc681d806d7698d6a05107a16141677e728f6163\nCLAIMS_DIR .git\n# Running multiple agents on this plan without collisions\n\nThese rules apply to every agent (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Nexus itself, or a human) that implements any part of this package at the same time as another. The repository's root `AGENTS.md` points here. The rules come from incidents recorded in `tasks/lessons.md`:\n\n- a concurrent agent overwrote newer evidence;\n- full test suites were contaminated by edits made mid-run;\n- `pkill -f` killed the agent's own shell;\n- HEAD moved during a pause.\n\nThey also follow from audit finding PER-03: the test suite writes into the real `~/.nexus`.\n\n## 1. Unit of work: one claimed PR slice per agent\n\n- The unit of concurrent work is **one PR slice** from a plan, for example `PLAN-01/PR-1a`. Every slice lists its tasks and its safe change boundary in its plan.\n- An agent works on exactly one claimed slice at a time.\n- An agent must not edit files outside its slice's boundary. The exceptions are the ledger rows and the shared files covered by §4. If the work needs a file outside the boundary, the agent stops and records a **boundary request** (§6). It does not edit the file.\n\n## 2. Claiming a slice (atomic and machine-local)\n\nClaims live in the repository's shared git directory. They are visible to every worktree, and they are never committed.\n\n```sh\nCLAIMS=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"\nmkdir -p \"$CLAIMS\"\nSLICE=\"PLAN-01_PR-1a\"\nif mkdir \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\" 2>/dev/null; then          # mkdir is atomic: exactly one agent wins\n  printf '{\"agent\":\"%s\",\"branch\":\"%s\",\"since\":\"%s\",\"pid\":%s}\\n' \\\n    \"$AGENT_NAME\" \"v1/plan-01-pr-1a\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" \"$$\" > \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\"\nelse\n  echo \"claimed by: $(cat \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\")\"; exit 1\nfi\n```\n\n- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\n- **Hot-file claims** use the same mechanism with the name `FILE_<path with / replaced by _>`, for example `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`. See §4.\n- **Stale claims.** A claim older than 24 h whose PID is gone may be broken, but only by the owner, or by an agent that first records the broken claim in the log.\n- If the MCP Agent Mail server is available, its file reservations (`file_reservation_paths`) may be used as well. The git-common-dir claim stays authoritative, because every agent can see it without extra tooling.\n\n## 3. Isolation: worktree, branch, HOME, ports, processes\n\n| Resource | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| Source | One `git worktree` per claimed slice: `git worktree add ../nexus-wt/<slice> -b v1/<plan>-<slice> origin/main`. Never edit `~/nexus-code` itself. It is the owner's checkout, and `/usr/local/bin/nexus` runs from it. |\n| Branch | `v1/plan-NN-pr-Nx`. One branch per slice. Never commit to `main` directly. |\n| HOME and state | Until PLAN-08 PR-8a lands, every test, build and probe run sets `HOME=$(mktemp -d)` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$HOME/.config\"`. After PR-8a, the test setup enforces this, but scripts and probes outside `npm test` must still set it. **Never** run anything that writes to the real `~/.nexus` or `~/.config/nexus`. |\n| Test runs | Full suites run on a **snapshot copy** of the worktree (`git worktree add` at the commit under test, or `git archive`), never on the tree being edited. `tsx` reads `src/` live. |\n| Builds | Each worktree builds into its own `core/target`, and `cli/dist` is per worktree. To share the Rust build cache, set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` per worktree, never to one shared directory. |\n| Ports | Mock servers bind `127.0.0.1:0` (an ephemeral port) and publish the chosen port to a file. Fixed ports are forbidden. |\n| Processes | Kill only PIDs you started, taken from `$!` or `ps -eo pid,args \\| grep -v grep`. **Never `pkill -f` or `killall`.** Long background jobs are stopped through the agent's own task controls. |\n| Inference | There is one inference host (DEC-16). Any run that uses the gateway takes the claim `GATEWAY` first. That includes eval runs, live checks and stripped-proxy runs. One gateway run at a time, which keeps eval timings valid and prevents overload. Small cloud checks (E5) take `CLOUD` to avoid duplicate spend. |\n| Credentials | Agents never read or copy `~/.config/nexus/credentials.json`, `config.env` values, or gateway tokens. The stripped proxy reads the token file itself. |\n\n## 4. Hot files: serialise, do not merge blindly\n\nThese files are touched by several plans. An agent editing one must hold its `FILE_` claim for the **shortest** period: edit, test, push, merge, then release.\n\n| File | Plans that touch it | Rule |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cli/src/agent.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 04, 05, 11 | Claim required. Keep each change local to the line ranges the plan names. Rebase immediately before merge and re-run that slice's tests on the rebased snapshot. |\n| `cli/src/index.ts` | 01, 03, 04, 06, 08, 10, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-06 PR-6b (unified launcher) lands first.** Other plans add commands and flags afterwards. |\n| `cli/src/tools.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 06, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-02 PR-2b (signal plumbing) lands before PLAN-03 PR-3c (`safeFetch`)**. |\n| `cli/src/sidecar.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 05, 08 | Claim required |\n| `cli/src/doctor.ts` | 01, 03, 05, 06, 08 | Claim required. Each plan adds **new check functions** in separate blocks. Only PLAN-06 PR-6d changes existing checks. |\n| `cli/src/client.ts` | 03, 05, 08, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-03 PR-3a (env layering) lands before any PLAN-05 slice.** |\n| `cli/src/repl.ts` | 01, 05, 08 | Claim required |\n| `cli/src/config.ts`, `security.ts`, `sandbox.ts`, `mcp.ts`, `plugins.ts` | 01, 03 | Claim required. PLAN-01 PR-1e and PLAN-03 must not run at the same time on `sandbox.ts` or `security.ts`. |\n| `cli/src/core/capabilities.ts` | 01, 02 | **PLAN-01 PR-1a (effect classes) lands first.** PLAN-02 PR-2c adds schema fields afterwards. |\n| `cli/src/tester.ts` | 01, 11 | **PLAN-01 PR-1c lands before PLAN-11 PR-11b/11c.** |\n| `cli/src/core/state.ts` | 04, 08 | **PLAN-08 PR-8a (HOME isolation) lands before everything.** |\n| `core/src/runner.rs`, `core/src/main.rs` | 01, 02, 06 | Claim required. The protocol version number is owned by PLAN-02 PR-2a. PLAN-06 PR-6c only reads it. |\n| `core/src/bin/nexus_tui/{live_state,live_view}.rs` | 01, 02 | Claim required |\n| `package.json`, `cli/package.json`, `core/Cargo.toml`, lockfiles | 01, 06, 07, 08 | **Only one agent at a time.** Version fields are written only by `scripts/sync-version.mjs`. Dependency changes are separate commits that touch only the lockfile and manifest. |\n| `harness.sh`, `install.sh`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `.github/workflows/*` | 05, 06, 07, 09, C1 | Claim required. Workflow edits are separate commits. |\n| `cli/dist/**` | all, while tracked | Do not commit `cli/dist` from slices. PLAN-07 PR-7d untracks it (DEC-10). Until that merges, only the merging agent rebuilds and commits dist, in a final separate commit, after rebasing. |\n| `docs/USER_MANUAL.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md`, `quickstart.md` | 05, 09 and doc tasks in every plan | Edit only the sections your slice changes. Hold a short `FILE_` claim. |\n\n### Ledger updates (`docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md`)\n\nA slice changes only the rows for its own requirement IDs: the status, test-reference and evidence cells, in place. It never reorders, adds or removes rows, and never edits another slice's rows. New requirements discovered during work go to §6, not into the ledger. Because rows are independent lines, git merges these edits cleanly. If a conflict appears anyway, resolve it row by row, keeping both changes.\n\n## 5. Commit and merge discipline\n\n1. Before **every** commit, compare `git rev-parse HEAD` with the commit you last made. Then run `git log <yours>..HEAD` on the branch. If anything foreign appears, stop and reconcile. Never commit generated artifacts (evidence, dist, lockfiles) over a branch that moved (lessons 2026-10-13).\n2. Commits are scoped to the slice. Do not reformat or clean up files outside the boundary.\n3. Merge order follows the precedence rules in §4 and the ROADMAP milestone order. Within a milestone, the slice with fewer hot-file claims merges first.\n4. Rebase onto `origin/main` immediately before merging. Re-run the slice's targeted tests, plus `make test`, on a snapshot of the rebased commit. Merge only if both pass.\n5. Pushing, tagging, publishing and changing GitHub state (issues, milestones, releases) are **owner-approved actions** (DECISIONS X-list). Agents prepare them and do not perform them.\n6. Preserve unrelated user work: the untracked `nexus-continuity-validation/`, the stashes, and any dirty files you did not create. Never stash, reset, clean or check out over them.\n\n## 6. Coordination records\n\n| Record | Where | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\n| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\n| Boundary requests and discovered requirements | The PR description, under the heading `Needs from other slices`. Mirrored as one line in the claim log. | So the owning slice's agent can pick it up. Never fixed silently out of scope. |\n| Slice evidence | `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/<plan>-<slice>/` (new directory per slice) | No shared evidence files, so agents cannot overwrite each other's evidence |\n\n## 7. Safe parallel lanes\n\nThe following groupings can run at the same time with no hot-file contention beyond §4 claims. They are listed by milestone.\n\n| Phase | Parallel lanes |\n|---|---|\n| M0 | (a) PLAN-08 PR-8a, which must merge first. Then in parallel: (b) PLAN-06 PR-6a, (c) PLAN-09 PR-9a. |\n| M1 | (a) PLAN-01 PR-1a → PR-1b → PR-1c (sequential, owns `capabilities.ts`, `agent.ts` dispatch). (b) PLAN-02 PR-2a (Rust only). (c) PLAN-03 PR-3a → PR-3b (config/egress). (d) PLAN-11 PR-11a (`parser.ts`) and PR-11b (`tester.ts`, after PR-1c). Lanes (b), (c) and (d) do not touch `capabilities.ts`. |\n| M2 (alongside M1) | (a) PLAN-07 PR-7a/7b/7c (workflows, scripts). (b) PLAN-06 PR-6b after PLAN-01 PR-1b (shares `index.ts` flags). |\n| M3 | (a) PLAN-04 (`agent.ts` turn, operation runner). (b) PLAN-05 (`client.ts`, provider modules). (c) PLAN-10 harness (`eval/`, no product files). (d) Held-out task authoring by the agent author, **outside the repository**: no access to Nexus source or the development set (DEC-05). |\n| M4 (alongside M3) | PLAN-08 PR-8b..8e. Coordinate with PLAN-04 on `state.ts` through `FILE_` claims. |\n| M5 | **Serial on `GATEWAY`.** The eval runner, the stripped-proxy runs and the independent reviewer's live task each take the `GATEWAY` claim. The terminal matrix (E3) and the install matrix (E2) can run in parallel with gateway runs. |\n\n## 8. Independence constraints\n\n- The held-out task author must not see Nexus source, the development tasks or tuning history. It runs in a separate session with only the task schema and external repositories. Its output is sealed by a sha256 manifest committed before RC1.\n- The independent reviewer in ACCEPTANCE §8 must not be the agent or session that implemented the slices under review.\n- An implementing agent never edits `eval/heldout-manifest.json`, scorer thresholds or ACCEPTANCE §6.4 after the freeze.\n\nRETENTION STATUS\n## v1/defect-retention-partition-symlink...origin/main [ahead 3]\nc92861f (HEAD -> v1/defect-retention-partition-symlink) fix(retention): pin checkpoint cleanup directories\n741a017 fix(retention): require canonical snapshots root\n84d23ff fix(retention): reject symlinked checkpoint partitions\nfc681d8 (origin/main) Merge pull request #187 from mikeholownych/v1/defect-checkpoint-state-injection\n6e008a8 (origin/v1/defect-checkpoint-state-injection, v1/defect-checkpoint-state-injection) fix(checkpoint): strip controls from timestamps and exercise prune git path\n\nCLAIMS\nDEFECT_RETENTION_PARTITION_SYMLINK_20261024\n{\"agent\":\"codex-root\",\"host\":\"mike-dev\",\"branch\":\"v1/defect-retention-partition-symlink\",\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/retention-partition-symlink\",\"base\":\"a6b8e3fccb65cbca0bbef716f4b9a377b011844a\",\"since\":\"2026-10-24T06:33:00Z\",\"scope\":\"fix reviewer finding: prevent symlinked partition directory from redirecting checkpoint snapshot deletion outside state store; add targeted regression tests only\"}\nSUITE_RETENTION_PARTITION_SYMLINK_20261024\n{\"agent\":\"codex-root\",\"host\":\"mike-dev\",\"branch\":\"v1/defect-retention-partition-symlink\",\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/retention-partition-symlink\",\"base\":\"a6b8e3fccb65cbca0bbef716f4b9a377b011844a\",\"since\":\"2026-10-24T06:40:00Z\",\"scope\":\"focused retention checkpoint confinement regression only; no full suite\"}\nFILE_cli_src_core_retention.ts\n{\"agent\":\"codex-root\",\"host\":\"mike-dev\",\"branch\":\"v1/defect-retention-partition-symlink\",\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/retention-partition-symlink\",\"base\":\"a6b8e3fccb65cbca0bbef716f4b9a377b011844a\",\"since\":\"2026-10-24T06:33:00Z\",\"scope\":\"symlink partition path escape remediation and regression\"}\nFILE_cli_test_retention_checkpoint_confinement.test.ts\n{\"agent\":\"codex-root\",\"host\":\"mike-dev\",\"branch\":\"v1/defect-retention-partition-symlink\",\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/retention-partition-symlink\",\"base\":\"a6b8e3fccb65cbca0bbef716f4b9a377b011844a\",\"since\":\"2026-10-24T06:33:00Z\",\"scope\":\"symlink partition path escape remediation and regression\"}\n\nPR186 DETAILS\n{\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\n- Add an interactive startup trust chooser before the REPL or TUI starts in an untrusted workspace.\\n- Offer **Trust and continue**, **Continue without trusting**, and **Exit**. Trust persists through the existing trust store; continuing untrusted does not change the configured permission mode.\\n- Load project instruction files only after explicit workspace trust. Non-interactive launches never grant trust implicitly and continue under the existing untrusted-workspace behavior.\\n- Sanitize terminal control and Unicode format characters in displayed paths and fit text by grapheme display-cell width.\\n- Document the startup behavior and add prompt, trust persistence, failure, non-TTY, prompt ordering behavior, and path display regressions.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- Focused startup/workspace trust tests: 16/16 passed on the committed source.\\n- `npm run build`: passed.\\n- Independent read-only source review: ACCEPT on the exact reviewed diff.\\n- A full CLI `npm test` attempt ran in an isolated snapshot under the suite claim but did not complete. It reported failures across engine-backed, continuity, qualification, and packaged-entrypoint tests; this local attempt omitted the CI job's built Rust binaries and qualification host setup. It is not passing evidence. Exact-head CI is running on this PR.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nThis implements the startup folder-trust interaction shown by the operator. It does not change release acceptance status; RC and release qualification remain separate gates.\\n\",\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfFAcEA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"coderabbitai\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"NONE\",\"body\":\"<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\\n\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\\n\\n> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> - [ ] <!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"e9bb8d72-00e8-4f67-9cb2-caf3b22574fe\\\"} --> 🔍 Trigger review\\n> \\n> This repository does not receive automatic reviews because it has fewer than 10 stars.\\n> \\n> <details>\\n> <summary><strong><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog-dark.svg\\\"><img src=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog.svg\\\" width=\\\"16\\\" height=\\\"16\\\" align=\\\"absmiddle\\\" alt=\\\"\\\"></picture> Run configuration</strong></summary>\\n> <dl>\\n> <dd>\\n> \\n> - **Source mode**: Auto\\n> - **Repository**: Unavailable\\n> - **Branch**: Unavailable\\n> - **File**: No configuration file from this repository applied\\n> - **Commit**: Unavailable\\n> - **Layers**: defaults\\n> - **Review profile**: CHILL\\n> - **Plan**: Advanced\\n> - **Run ID**: `9ba197ee-1610-44eb-831c-c1866972b6c4`\\n> \\n> </dd>\\n> </dl>\\n> </details>\\n\\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\\n\\n<!-- autopilot:start -->\\n- [ ] <!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"2708ad07-9f24-4260-9c11-7dc76a49f2e3\\\"} --> <strong title=\\\"Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\\">Autofix</strong> · Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\n<!-- autopilot:end -->\\n<!-- tips_start -->\\n\\n\\n\\nThanks for using [CodeRabbit](https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=oss&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=mikeholownych/nexus-code&utm_content=186)! It's free for OSS, and your support helps us grow. If you like it, consider giving us a shout-out.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary><strong>❤️ Share</strong></summary>\\n<dl>\\n<dd>\\n\\n- [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A&url=https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [Mastodon](https://mastodon.social/share?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai)\\n- [Reddit](https://www.reddit.com/submit?title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&text=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai&mini=true&title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&summary=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code)\\n\\n</dd>\\n</dl>\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands.</sub>\\n\\n<!-- tips_end -->\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T05:53:18Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":true,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/186#issuecomment-6380592144\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":false},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfF9Dsg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Independent Review: CHANGES_REQUESTED\\n\\n**Target commit**: `f4d40cdc5c4cf1196b7beb88f51953d721a370a8`  \\n**Base commit**: `fc681d806d7698d6a05107a16141677e728f6163` (origin/main)  \\n**CI Run**: [40074046981](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40074046981) (`test-matrix (22)` and `test-matrix (24)` failed)\\n\\n#### Finding: Interactive PTY Tests Hang at Startup Trust Prompt\\nThe implementation of `promptWorkspaceTrust` displays an interactive prompt whenever `input.isTTY && output.isTTY` in an untrusted workspace. While `cli/test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts` was updated with `trustWorkspace(home, repo)`, `cli/test/turn_semantics.test.ts` was not updated.\\n\\nAs a result, the `interactive REPL (pty)` subtests run under `util-linux script` (which provides pseudo-terminal TTY streams), encounter the trust prompt, and hang waiting for user input, causing a 30s timeout failure:\\n\\n1. `cli/test/turn_semantics.test.ts:708`: `Ctrl-C during a delayed mutating trajectory: one interrupt, no new mutation, prompt returns, next turn works`\\n```\\nError: timeout waiting for /❯ /; output tail: \\nTrust this folder?\\n↑↓ navigate · Enter select · Esc exit\\n/tmp/nexus-turn-...\\nLoad project instructions\\n…\\n› Trust and continue\\n  Continue without trusting\\n  Exit\\n```\\n2. `cli/test/turn_semantics.test.ts:751`: `multiple prompts in one session keep working; Ctrl-C at idle still exits deliberately`\\n(Fails with identical timeout waiting for `/❯ /` at the trust prompt).\\n\\n#### Recommended Resolution\\nIn `cli/test/turn_semantics.test.ts`, import `trustWorkspace` from `./helpers/fixtures.js` and ensure the workspace is trusted before launching the REPL in the `session` helper:\\n```ts\\nimport { startGateway, makeRepo, makeHome, Reply, ptyTest, trustWorkspace } from \\\"./helpers/fixtures.js\\\";\\n// ...\\nasync function session(gw: Gateway, repo: string, home: string) {\\n  trustWorkspace(home, repo);\\n  const cmd = ...\\n```\\nOnce updated and rebased, exact-head CI should be re-run.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T07:42:55Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/186#issuecomment-6381585330\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfF_DoA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Independent Review: ACCEPT\\n\\n**Target commit**: `fb70052e19340caa7a050f98c0392785df525a07`  \\n**Base commit**: `fc681d806d7698d6a05107a16141677e728f6163` (origin/main)  \\n**Files changed**: 11 files (+606, -8)\\n\\n#### Verification & Assessment\\n1. **Resolution of CHANGES_REQUESTED Finding**:\\n   - `cli/test/turn_semantics.test.ts` has been updated with `NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE: \\\"1\\\"` in the PTY `session` helper environment, allowing the turn semantics test suite to run in the pseudo-terminal without being blocked at the interactive startup trust prompt.\\n   - Verified that `cli/src/workspace_trust.ts` supports `NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE === \\\"1\\\"` to return true for `isWorkspaceTrusted()`.\\n2. **Interactive Trust & Sanitization Implementation**:\\n   - Non-interactive launches fail closed to untrusted mode and emit a notice without blocking.\\n   - Interactive TTY prompt provides clean navigation and choices: \\\"Trust and continue\\\", \\\"Continue without trusting\\\", \\\"Exit\\\".\\n   - Project instructions (`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `CODEX.md`, `.nexusrules`) are gated on explicit workspace trust via `trustedProjectRules`.\\n   - Control characters and Unicode format characters in display paths are safely sanitized with grapheme cell-width fitting.\\n3. **Hygiene & Verification**:\\n   - `git diff --check` passes cleanly with 0 errors.\\n   - CodeQL run [40075233603](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40075233603): `✓ SUCCESS`.\\n   - Hosted CI run [40075233633](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40075233633): in progress.\\n\\nNo regressions or security concerns. Recommended for merge once CI completes.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T07:46:42Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/186#issuecomment-6381618080\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true}],\"mergeStateStatus\":\"BLOCKED\",\"mergeable\":\"MERGEABLE\",\"reviews\":[]}\n\nACTIVE MAIN CI\n[{\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T07:21:25Z\",\"databaseId\":40073807182,\"headSha\":\"fc681d806d7698d6a05107a16141677e728f6163\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"workflowName\":\"CodeQL\"},{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T07:21:25Z\",\"databaseId\":40073807127,\"headSha\":\"fc681d806d7698d6a05107a16141677e728f6163\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"workflowName\":\"CI\"},{\"conclusion\":\"failure\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T07:03:53Z\",\"databaseId\":40072663440,\"headSha\":\"a6b8e3fccb65cbca0bbef716f4b9a377b011844a\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"workflowName\":\"Dependabot Updates\"},{\"conclusion\":\"failure\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T07:03:52Z\",\"databaseId\":40072662458,\"headSha\":\"a6b8e3fccb65cbca0bbef716f4b9a377b011844a\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"workflowName\":\"Dependabot Updates\"},{\"conclusion\":\"failure\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T07:03:52Z\",\"databaseId\":40072662354,\"headSha\":\"a6b8e3fccb65cbca0bbef716f4b9a377b011844a\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"workflowName\":\"Dependabot Updates\"}]\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":700816735}},"started_at_ms":1792828221518,"completed_at_ms":1792828223220}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T07:50:24.714Z","ordinal":281902,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a16ce3-b4c9-79b1-ba32-db4fb551ab18","call_id":"call_f68f10f871d4465bbae96fdbcfb7fc8a","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 6052)\nTotal output lines: 144\n\nFrom https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code\n * branch            main       -> FETCH_HEAD\nREMOTE_MAIN fc681d806d7698d6a05107a16141677e728f6163\nCLAIMS_DIR .git\n# Running multiple agents on this plan without collisions\n\nThese rules apply to every agent (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Nexus itself, or a human) that implements any part of this package at the same time as another. The repository's root `AGENTS.md` points here. The rules come from incidents recorded in `tasks/lessons.md`:\n\n- a concurrent agent overwrote newer evidence;\n- full test suites were contaminated by edits made mid-run;\n- `pkill -f` killed the agent's own shell;\n- HEAD moved during a pause.\n\nThey also follow from audit finding PER-03: the test suite writes into the real `~/.nexus`.\n\n## 1. Unit of work: one claimed PR slice per agent\n\n- The unit of concurrent work is **one PR slice** from a plan, for example `PLAN-01/PR-1a`. Every slice lists its tasks and its safe change boundary in its plan.\n- An agent works on exactly one claimed slice at a time.\n- An agent must not edit files outside its slice's boundary. The exceptions are the ledger rows and the shared files covered by §4. If the work needs a file outside the boundary, the agent stops and records a **boundary request** (§6). It does not edit the file.\n\n## 2. Claiming a slice (atomic and machine-local)\n\nClaims live in the repository's shared git directory. They are visible to every worktree, and they are never committed.\n\n```sh\nCLAIMS=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"\nmkdir -p \"$CLAIMS\"\nSLICE=\"PLAN-01_PR-1a\"\nif mkdir \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\" 2>/dev/null; then          # mkdir is atomic: exactly one agent wins\n  printf '{\"agent\":\"%s\",\"branch\":\"%s\",\"since\":\"%s\",\"pid\":%s}\\n' \\\n    \"$AGENT_NAME\" \"v1/plan-01-pr-1a\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" \"$$\" > \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\"\nelse\n  echo \"claimed by: $(cat \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\")\"; exit 1\nfi\n```\n\n- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\n- **Hot-file claims** use the same mechanism with the name `FILE_<path with / replaced by _>`, for example `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`. See §4.\n- **Stale claims.** A claim older than 24 h whose PID is gone may be broken, but only by the owner, or by an agent that first records the broken claim in the log.\n- If the MCP Agent Mail server is available, its file reservations (`file_reservation_paths`) may be used as well. The git-common-dir claim stays authoritative, because every agent can see it without extra tooling.\n\n## 3. Isolation: worktree, branch, HOME, ports, processes\n\n| Resource | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| Source | One `git worktree` per claimed slice: `git worktree add ../nexus-wt/<slice> -b v1/<plan>-<slice> origin/main`. Never edit `~/nexus-code` itself. It is the owner's checkout, and `/usr/local/bin/nexus` runs from it. |\n| Branch | `v1/plan-NN-pr-Nx`. One branch per slice. Never commit to `main` directly. |\n| HOME and state | Until PLAN-08 PR-8a lands, every test, build and probe run sets `HOME=$(mktemp -d)` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$HOME/.config\"`. After PR-8a, the test setup enforces this, but scripts and probes outside `npm test` must still set it. **Never** run anything that writes to the real `~/.nexus` or `~/.config/nexus`. |\n| Test runs | Full suites run on a **snapshot copy** of the worktree (`git worktree add` at the commit under test, or `git archive`), never on the tree being edited. `tsx` reads `src/` live. |\n| Builds | Each worktree builds into its own `core/target`, and `cli/dist` is per worktree. To share the Rust build cache, set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` per worktree, never to one shared directory. |\n| Ports | Mock servers bind `127.0.0.1:0` (an ephemeral port) and publish the chosen port to a file. Fixed ports are forbidden. |\n| Processes | Kill only PIDs you started, taken from `$!` or `ps -eo pid,args \\| grep -v grep`. **Never `pkill -f` or `killall`.** Long background jobs are stopped through the agent's own task controls. |\n| Inference | There is one inference host (DEC-16). Any run that uses the gateway takes the claim `GATEWAY` first. That includes eval runs, live checks and stripped-proxy runs. One gateway run at a time, which keeps eval timings valid and prevents overload. Small cloud checks (E5) take `CLOUD` to avoid duplicate spend. |\n| Credentials | Agents never read or copy `~/.config/nexus/credentials.json`, `config.env` values, or gateway tokens. The stripped proxy reads the token file itself. |\n\n## 4. Hot files: serialise, do not merge blindly\n\nThese files are touched by several plans. An agent editing one must hold its `FILE_` claim for the **shortest** period: edit, test, push, merge, then release.\n\n| File | Plans that touch it | Rule |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cli/src/agent.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 04, 05, 11 | Claim required. Keep each change local to the line ranges the plan names. Rebase immediately before merge and re-run that slice's tests on the rebased snapshot. |\n| `cli/src/index.ts` | 01, 03, 04, 06, 08, 10, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-06 PR-6b (unified launcher) lands first.** Other plans add commands and flags afterwards. |\n| `cli/src/tools.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 06, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-02 PR-2b (signal plumbing) lands before PLAN-03 PR-3c (`safeFetch`)**. |\n| `cli/src/sidecar.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 05, 08 | Claim required |\n| `cli/src/doctor.ts` | 01, 03, 05, 06, 08 | Claim required. Each plan adds **new check functions** in separate blocks. Only PLAN-06 PR-6d changes existing checks. |\n| `cli/src/client.ts` | 03, 05, 08, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-03 PR-3a (env layering) lands before any PLAN-05 slice.** |\n| `cli/src/repl.ts` | 01, 05, 08 | Claim required |\n| `cli/src/config.ts`, `security.ts`, `sandbox.ts`, `mcp.ts`, `plugins.ts` | 01, 03 | Claim required. PLAN-01 PR-1e and PLAN-03 must not run at the same time on `sandbox.ts` or `security.ts`. |\n| `cli/src/core/capabilities.ts` | 01, 02 | **PLAN-01 PR-1a (effect classes) lands first.** PLAN-02 PR-2c adds schema fields afterwards. |\n| `cli/src/tester.ts` | 01, 11 | **PLAN-01 PR-1c lands before PLAN-11 PR-11b/11c.** |\n| `cli/src/core/state.ts` | 04, 08 | **PLAN-08 PR-8a (HOME isolation) lands before everything.** |\n| `core/src/runner.rs`, `core/src/main.rs` | 01, 02, 06 | Claim required. The protocol version number is owned by PLAN-02 PR-2a. PLAN-06 PR-6c only reads it. |\n| `core/src/bin/nexus_tui/{live_state,live_view}.rs` | 01, 02 | Claim required |\n| `package.json`, `cli/package.json`, `core/Cargo.toml`, lockfiles | 01, 06, 07, 08 | **Only one agent at a time.** Version fields are written only by `scripts/sync-version.mjs`. Dependency changes are separate commits that touch only the lockfile and manifest. |\n| `harness.sh`, `install.sh`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `.github/workflows/*` | 05, 06, 07, 09, C1 | Claim required. Workflow edits are separate commits. |\n| `cli/dist/**` | all, while tracked | Do not commit `cli/dist` from slices. PLAN-07 PR-7d untracks it (DEC-10). Until that merges, only the merging agent rebuilds and commits dist, in a final separate commit, after rebasing. |\n| `docs/USER_MANUAL.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md`, `quickstart.md` | 05, 09 and doc tasks in every plan | Edit only the sections your slice changes. Hold a short `FILE_` claim. |\n\n### Ledger updates (`docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md`)\n\nA slice changes only the rows for its own requirement IDs: the status, test-reference and evidence cells, in place. It never reorders, adds or removes rows, and never edits another slice's rows. New requirements discovered during work go to §6, not into the ledger. Because rows are independent lines, git merges these edits cleanly. If a conflict appears anyway, resolve it row by row, keeping both changes.\n\n## 5. Commit and merge discipline\n\n1. Before **every** commit, compare `git rev-parse HEAD` with the commit you last made. Then run `git log <yours>..HEAD` on the branch. If anything foreign appears, stop and reconcile. Never commit generated artifacts (evidence, dist, lockfiles) over a branch that moved (lessons 2026-10-13).\n2. Commits are scoped to the slice. Do not reformat or clean up files outside the boundary.\n3. Merge order follows the precedence rules in §4 and the ROADMAP milestone order. Within a milestone, the slice with fewer hot-file claims merges first.\n4. Rebase onto `origin/main` immediately before merging. Re-run the slice's targeted tests, plus `make test`, on a snapshot of the rebased commit. Merge only if both pass.\n5. Pushing, tagging, publishing and changing GitHub state (issues, milestones, releases) are **owner-approved actions** (DECISIONS X-list). Agents prepare them and do not perform them.\n6. Preserve unrelated user work: the untracked `nexus-continuity-validation/`, the stashes, and any dirty files you did not create. Never stash, reset, clean or check out over them.\n\n## 6. Coordination records\n\n| Record | Where | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\n| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\n| Boundary requests and discovered requirements | The PR description, under the heading `Needs from other slices`. Mirrored as one line in the claim log. | So the owning slice's agent can pick it up. Never fixed silently out of scope. |\n| Slice evidence | `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/<plan>-<slice>/` (new directory per slice) | No shared evidence files, so agents cannot overwrite each other's evidence |\n\n## 7. Safe parallel lanes\n\nThe following groupings can run at the same time with no hot-file contention beyond §4 claims. They are listed by milestone.\n\n| Phase | Parallel lanes |\n|---|---|\n| M0 | (a) PLAN-08 PR-8a, which must merge first. Then in parallel: (b) PLAN-06 PR-6a, (c) PLAN-09 PR-9a. |\n| M1 | (a) PLAN-01 PR-1a → PR-1b → PR-1c (sequential, owns `capabilities.ts`, `agent.ts` dispatch). (b) PLAN-02 PR-2a (Rust only). (c) PLAN-03 PR-3a → PR-3b (config/egress). (d) PLAN-11 PR-11a (`parser.ts`) and PR-11b (`tester.ts`, after PR-1c). Lanes (b), (c) and (d) do not touch `capabilities.ts`. |\n| M2 (alongside M1) | (a) PLAN-07 PR-7a/7b/7c (workflows, scripts). (b) PLAN-06 PR-6b after PLAN-01 PR-1b (shares `index.ts` flags). |\n| M3 | (a) PLAN-04 (`agent.ts` turn, operation runner). (b) PLAN-05 (`client.ts`, provider modules). (c) PLAN-10 harness (`eval/`, no product files). (d) Held-out task authoring by the agent author, **outside the repository**: no access to Nexus source or the development set (DEC-05). |\n| M4 (alongside M3) | PLAN-08 PR-8b..8e. Coordinate with PLAN-04 on `state.ts` through `FILE_` claims. |\n| M5 | **Serial on `GATEWAY`.** The eval runner, the stripped-proxy runs and the independent reviewer's live task each take the `GATEWAY` claim. The terminal matrix (E3) and the install matrix (E2) can run in parallel with gateway runs. |\n\n## 8. Independence constraints\n\n- The held-out task author must not see Nexus source, the development tasks or tuning history. It runs in a separate session with only the task schema and external repositories. Its output is sealed by a sha256 manifest committed before RC1.\n- The independent reviewer in ACCEPTANCE §8 must not be the agent or session that implemented the slices under review.\n- An implementing agent never edits `eval/heldout-manifest.json`, scorer thresholds or ACCEPTANCE §6.4 after the freeze.\n\nRETENTION STATUS\n## v1/defect-retention-partition-symlink...origin/main [ahead 3]\nc92861f (HEAD -> v1/defect-retention-partition-symlink) fix(retention): pin checkpoint cleanup directories\n741a017 fix(retention): require canonical snapshots root\n84d23ff fix(retention): reject symlinked checkpoint partitions\nfc681d8 (origin/main) Merge pull request #187 from mikeholownych/v1/defect-checkpoint-state-injection\n6e008a8 (origin/v1/defect-checkpoint-stat…52 tokens truncated…\"mike-dev\",\"branch\":\"v1/defect-retention-partition-symlink\",\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/retention-partition-symlink\",\"base\":\"a6b8e3fccb65cbca0bbef716f4b9a377b011844a\",\"since\":\"2026-10-24T06:33:00Z\",\"scope\":\"fix reviewer finding: prevent symlinked partition directory from redirecting checkpoint snapshot deletion outside state store; add targeted regression tests only\"}\nSUITE_RETENTION_PARTITION_SYMLINK_20261024\n{\"agent\":\"codex-root\",\"host\":\"mike-dev\",\"branch\":\"v1/defect-retention-partition-symlink\",\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/retention-partition-symlink\",\"base\":\"a6b8e3fccb65cbca0bbef716f4b9a377b011844a\",\"since\":\"2026-10-24T06:40:00Z\",\"scope\":\"focused retention checkpoint confinement regression only; no full suite\"}\nFILE_cli_src_core_retention.ts\n{\"agent\":\"codex-root\",\"host\":\"mike-dev\",\"branch\":\"v1/defect-retention-partition-symlink\",\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/retention-partition-symlink\",\"base\":\"a6b8e3fccb65cbca0bbef716f4b9a377b011844a\",\"since\":\"2026-10-24T06:33:00Z\",\"scope\":\"symlink partition path escape remediation and regression\"}\nFILE_cli_test_retention_checkpoint_confinement.test.ts\n{\"agent\":\"codex-root\",\"host\":\"mike-dev\",\"branch\":\"v1/defect-retention-partition-symlink\",\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/retention-partition-symlink\",\"base\":\"a6b8e3fccb65cbca0bbef716f4b9a377b011844a\",\"since\":\"2026-10-24T06:33:00Z\",\"scope\":\"symlink partition path escape remediation and regression\"}\n\nPR186 DETAILS\n{\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\n- Add an interactive startup trust chooser before the REPL or TUI starts in an untrusted workspace.\\n- Offer **Trust and continue**, **Continue without trusting**, and **Exit**. Trust persists through the existing trust store; continuing untrusted does not change the configured permission mode.\\n- Load project instruction files only after explicit workspace trust. Non-interactive launches never grant trust implicitly and continue under the existing untrusted-workspace behavior.\\n- Sanitize terminal control and Unicode format characters in displayed paths and fit text by grapheme display-cell width.\\n- Document the startup behavior and add prompt, trust persistence, failure, non-TTY, prompt ordering behavior, and path display regressions.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- Focused startup/workspace trust tests: 16/16 passed on the committed source.\\n- `npm run build`: passed.\\n- Independent read-only source review: ACCEPT on the exact reviewed diff.\\n- A full CLI `npm test` attempt ran in an isolated snapshot under the suite claim but did not complete. It reported failures across engine-backed, continuity, qualification, and packaged-entrypoint tests; this local attempt omitted the CI job's built Rust binaries and qualification host setup. It is not passing evidence. Exact-head CI is running on this PR.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nThis implements the startup folder-trust interaction shown by the operator. It does not change release acceptance status; RC and release qualification remain separate gates.\\n\",\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfFAcEA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"coderabbitai\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"NONE\",\"body\":\"<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\\n\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\\n\\n> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> - [ ] <!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"e9bb8d72-00e8-4f67-9cb2-caf3b22574fe\\\"} --> 🔍 Trigger review\\n> \\n> This repository does not receive automatic reviews because it has fewer than 10 stars.\\n> \\n> <details>\\n> <summary><strong><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog-dark.svg\\\"><img src=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog.svg\\\" width=\\\"16\\\" height=\\\"16\\\" align=\\\"absmiddle\\\" alt=\\\"\\\"></picture> Run configuration</strong></summary>\\n> <dl>\\n> <dd>\\n> \\n> - **Source mode**: Auto\\n> - **Repository**: Unavailable\\n> - **Branch**: Unavailable\\n> - **File**: No configuration file from this repository applied\\n> - **Commit**: Unavailable\\n> - **Layers**: defaults\\n> - **Review profile**: CHILL\\n> - **Plan**: Advanced\\n> - **Run ID**: `9ba197ee-1610-44eb-831c-c1866972b6c4`\\n> \\n> </dd>\\n> </dl>\\n> </details>\\n\\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\\n\\n<!-- autopilot:start -->\\n- [ ] <!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"2708ad07-9f24-4260-9c11-7dc76a49f2e3\\\"} --> <strong title=\\\"Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\\">Autofix</strong> · Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\n<!-- autopilot:end -->\\n<!-- tips_start -->\\n\\n\\n\\nThanks for using [CodeRabbit](https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=oss&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=mikeholownych/nexus-code&utm_content=186)! It's free for OSS, and your support helps us grow. If you like it, consider giving us a shout-out.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary><strong>❤️ Share</strong></summary>\\n<dl>\\n<dd>\\n\\n- [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A&url=https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [Mastodon](https://mastodon.social/share?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai)\\n- [Reddit](https://www.reddit.com/submit?title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&text=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai&mini=true&title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&summary=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code)\\n\\n</dd>\\n</dl>\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands.</sub>\\n\\n<!-- tips_end -->\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T05:53:18Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":true,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/186#issuecomment-6380592144\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":false},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfF9Dsg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Independent Review: CHANGES_REQUESTED\\n\\n**Target commit**: `f4d40cdc5c4cf1196b7beb88f51953d721a370a8`  \\n**Base commit**: `fc681d806d7698d6a05107a16141677e728f6163` (origin/main)  \\n**CI Run**: [40074046981](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40074046981) (`test-matrix (22)` and `test-matrix (24)` failed)\\n\\n#### Finding: Interactive PTY Tests Hang at Startup Trust Prompt\\nThe implementation of `promptWorkspaceTrust` displays an interactive prompt whenever `input.isTTY && output.isTTY` in an untrusted workspace. While `cli/test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts` was updated with `trustWorkspace(home, repo)`, `cli/test/turn_semantics.test.ts` was not updated.\\n\\nAs a result, the `interactive REPL (pty)` subtests run under `util-linux script` (which provides pseudo-terminal TTY streams), encounter the trust prompt, and hang waiting for user input, causing a 30s timeout failure:\\n\\n1. `cli/test/turn_semantics.test.ts:708`: `Ctrl-C during a delayed mutating trajectory: one interrupt, no new mutation, prompt returns, next turn works`\\n```\\nError: timeout waiting for /❯ /; output tail: \\nTrust this folder?\\n↑↓ navigate · Enter select · Esc exit\\n/tmp/nexus-turn-...\\nLoad project instructions\\n…\\n› Trust and continue\\n  Continue without trusting\\n  Exit\\n```\\n2. `cli/test/turn_semantics.test.ts:751`: `multiple prompts in one session keep working; Ctrl-C at idle still exits deliberately`\\n(Fails with identical timeout waiting for `/❯ /` at the trust prompt).\\n\\n#### Recommended Resolution\\nIn `cli/test/turn_semantics.test.ts`, import `trustWorkspace` from `./helpers/fixtures.js` and ensure the workspace is trusted before launching the REPL in the `session` helper:\\n```ts\\nimport { startGateway, makeRepo, makeHome, Reply, ptyTest, trustWorkspace } from \\\"./helpers/fixtures.js\\\";\\n// ...\\nasync function session(gw: Gateway, repo: string, home: string) {\\n  trustWorkspace(home, repo);\\n  const cmd = ...\\n```\\nOnce updated and rebased, exact-head CI should be re-run.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T07:42:55Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/186#issuecomment-6381585330\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfF_DoA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Independent Review: ACCEPT\\n\\n**Target commit**: `fb70052e19340caa7a050f98c0392785df525a07`  \\n**Base commit**: `fc681d806d7698d6a05107a16141677e728f6163` (origin/main)  \\n**Files changed**: 11 files (+606, -8)\\n\\n#### Verification & Assessment\\n1. **Resolution of CHANGES_REQUESTED Finding**:\\n   - `cli/test/turn_semantics.test.ts` has been updated with `NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE: \\\"1\\\"` in the PTY `session` helper environment, allowing the turn semantics test suite to run in the pseudo-terminal without being blocked at the interactive startup trust prompt.\\n   - Verified that `cli/src/workspace_trust.ts` supports `NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE === \\\"1\\\"` to return true for `isWorkspaceTrusted()`.\\n2. **Interactive Trust & Sanitization Implementation**:\\n   - Non-interactive launches fail closed to untrusted mode and emit a notice without blocking.\\n   - Interactive TTY prompt provides clean navigation and choices: \\\"Trust and continue\\\", \\\"Continue without trusting\\\", \\\"Exit\\\".\\n   - Project instructions (`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `CODEX.md`, `.nexusrules`) are gated on explicit workspace trust via `trustedProjectRules`.\\n   - Control characters and Unicode format characters in display paths are safely sanitized with grapheme cell-width fitting.\\n3. **Hygiene & Verification**:\\n   - `git diff --check` passes cleanly with 0 errors.\\n   - CodeQL run [40075233603](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40075233603): `✓ SUCCESS`.\\n   - Hosted CI run [40075233633](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40075233633): in progress.\\n\\nNo regressions or security concerns. Recommended for merge once CI completes.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T07:46:42Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/186#issuecomment-6381618080\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true}],\"mergeStateStatus\":\"BLOCKED\",\"mergeable\":\"MERGEABLE\",\"reviews\":[]}\n\nACTIVE MAIN CI\n[{\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T07:21:25Z\",\"databaseId\":40073807182,\"headSha\":\"fc681d806d7698d6a05107a16141677e728f6163\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"workflowName\":\"CodeQL\"},{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T07:21:25Z\",\"databaseId\":40073807127,\"headSha\":\"fc681d806d7698d6a05107a16141677e728f6163\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"workflowName\":\"CI\"},{\"conclusion\":\"failure\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T07:03:53Z\",\"databaseId\":40072663440,\"headSha\":\"a6b8e3fccb65cbca0bbef716f4b9a377b011844a\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"workflowName\":\"Dependabot Updates\"},{\"conclusion\":\"failure\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T07:03:52Z\",\"databaseId\":40072662458,\"headSha\":\"a6b8e3fccb65cbca0bbef716f4b9a377b011844a\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"workflowName\":\"Dependabot Updates\"},{\"conclusion\":\"failure\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T07:03:52Z\",\"databaseId\":40072662354,\"headSha\":\"a6b8e3fccb65cbca0bbef716f4b9a377b011844a\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"workflowName\":\"Dependabot Updates\"}]\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16cd4-55fc-7d42-952d-a5ba875e9e0d","create_time":1792828224.7139761}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
