{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T07:50:45.469Z","ordinal":281917,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016adc63531f7081a0836d6c76a579c99a","status":"completed","call_id":"call_4e99cf5c4c8d4826baacd2cd7a408612","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"gh pr create --base main --head v1/defect-retention-partition-symlink --title \\\"fix(retention): pin checkpoint cleanup directories\\\" --body-file - <<'EOF'\\n## Summary\\n\\n- Pin the Nexus state root, checkpoint partition, and snapshot directories with no-follow directory descriptors before deleting checkpoint data.\\n- Recheck planned directory identities and anchor record/snapshot deletion to those descriptors, preventing path replacement from redirecting cleanup outside the state store.\\n- Fail closed and preserve checkpoints where Linux `/proc/self/fd`, `O_DIRECTORY`, or `O_NOFOLLOW` is unavailable. This means checkpoint garbage collection is intentionally unavailable on those platforms.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- Exact candidate: `c92861fd7de4bb9f74739aeaaa93b59e4895c625`, rebased on `fc681d806d7698d6a05107a16141677e728f6163`.\\n- `retention_checkpoint_confinement.test.ts`: 15/15 passed.\\n- Targeted checkpoint pruning test: 1/1 passed.\\n- `npm run build`: passed.\\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\\n- Independent read-only review: ACCEPT on this exact head.\\n\\nHosted exact-head checks are required before integration. Full local suite was not claimed as passing.\\nEOF\",\"workdir\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/retention-partition-symlink\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":1000});\ntext(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16cd4-55fc-7d42-952d-a5ba875e9e0d","create_time":1792828243.1315024}}}
