{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T08:23:23.994Z","ordinal":282547,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16cd4-55fc-7d42-952d-a5ba875e9e0d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-f5a4466a-1524-4f1e-ba6c-b61eff3702cc","process_id":"74311","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n \"NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE|trusted_workspaces.json|workspace trust\" docs README.md cli/src cli/test scripts | head -100"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/startup-workspace-trust","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE|trusted_workspaces.json|workspace trust' docs README.md cli/src cli/test scripts","query":"NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE|trusted_workspaces.json|workspace trust","path":"docs"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"scripts/package-smoke-pty.py:34:    os.environ[\"NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE\"] = \"1\"\ncli/test/tui_surface_e2e.test.ts:103:  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(trustDir, \"trusted_workspaces.json\"), JSON.stringify({ trustedPaths: [fs.realpathSync(repo)] }, null, 2));\ncli/test/startup_trust_prompt.test.ts:108:test(\"trust choice persists workspace trust and returns trusted\", async () => {\ncli/test/startup_trust_prompt.test.ts:250:test(\"AutonomousAgent omits project rules until workspace trust is explicit\", () => {\ncli/test/startup_trust_prompt.test.ts:252:  const savedTrust = process.env.NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE;\ncli/test/startup_trust_prompt.test.ts:256:    delete process.env.NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE;\ncli/test/startup_trust_prompt.test.ts:269:    process.env.NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE = \"1\";\ncli/test/startup_trust_prompt.test.ts:283:    if (savedTrust === undefined) delete process.env.NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE;\ncli/test/startup_trust_prompt.test.ts:284:    else process.env.NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE = savedTrust;\ncli/test/helpers/fixtures.ts:185:    path.join(trustDir, \"trusted_workspaces.json\"),\ncli/test/security.test.ts:44:      assert.equal(sm.isPathProtected(\"trusted_workspaces.json\").protected, true);\ncli/test/turn_semantics.test.ts:688:        NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE: \"1\",\ncli/test/project_env_allowlist.test.ts:24:  NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE: \"1\",\ncli/test/workspace_trust.test.ts:23:  const saved = { HOME: process.env.HOME, TRUST: process.env.NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE, AUTO: process.env.NEXUS_KNOWLEDGE_AUTOEXTRACT };\ncli/test/workspace_trust.test.ts:25:  delete process.env.NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE;\ncli/test/workspace_trust.test.ts:31:    if (saved.TRUST === undefined) delete process.env.NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE;\ncli/test/workspace_trust.test.ts:32:    else process.env.NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE = saved.TRUST;\ncli/test/workspace_trust.test.ts:40:describe(\"workspace trust\", () => {\ncli/test/workspace_trust.test.ts:75:      const store = path.join(home, \".config\", \"nexus\", \"trusted_workspaces.json\");\ncli/src/core/capabilities.ts:12: * `egress`; `context_inject` is gated by workspace trust instead; `read_workspace`, `delegate` (the child's own calls are\ncli/test/tui_diff_e2e.test.ts:123:  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(trustDir, \"trusted_workspaces.json\"), JSON.stringify({ trustedPaths: [fs.realpathSync(repo)] }, null, 2));\ncli/test/harness_entry.test.ts:50:    NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE: \"1\",\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:296:| 1 | B1 execution authority + B2 workspace trust (+ R4 listing confinement, T13 dry-run) | 0 | capability × mode × context matrix complete and enforced; adversarial suite blocked; no regression in existing suites |\ncli/src/knowledge.ts:211:   * Gated by workspace trust: returns empty string if workspace is untrusted (REQ-SEC-113).\ncli/src/knowledge.ts:238:   * Gated by workspace trust and read-only mode.\ncli/src/security.ts:28:  \"trusted_workspaces.json\",\ncli/src/workspace_trust.ts:28:  return path.join(os.homedir(), \".config\", \"nexus\", \"trusted_workspaces.json\");\ncli/src/workspace_trust.ts:33: * In --read-only mode, workspace trust never authorizes executing project plugins/MCP.\ncli/src/workspace_trust.ts:37:  if (process.env.NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE === \"1\") return true;\ncli/src/skills.ts:64:    // Project workspace locations (gated by workspace trust)\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/trust_inference.md:68:- Remediation: load workspace-scoped plugins/MCP only after an explicit, persisted per-workspace trust decision (hash of the config/plugin\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:5:This release delivers the complete Nexus Code client architecture with comprehensive boundary hardening, process ownership, workspace trust enforcement, and egress protection.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:80:- **New behavior:** Default interactive posture is determined by workspace trust:\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:86:  - `--approve` / `--mode review`: Enforces review posture regardless of workspace trust.\ndocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:61:4. **Workspace trust.** Trust is managed via `nexus trust` and stored in `~/.config/nexus/trusted_workspaces.json`; interactive startup asks for trust before loading project instructions (`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `CODEX.md`, `.nexusrules`). In untrusted workspaces, project instructions, workspace MCP configs, plugins, skills, and `.nexus/knowledge.json` are not loaded (REQ-SEC-113, REQ-SEC-114). The operator may continue without trust under the existing permission mode or exit. *Limit:* configuration in the operator's home directory (`~/.config/nexus/`, `~/.nexus/`) is always trusted.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-11_PR-11d_REVIEW_AGT-118/post-integration-verification-d2c4.md:14:- REQ-AGT-010 coverage: the focused suite exercised ACC-TRUST-04 and adjacent workspace trust behavior. This does not establish provenance for every injected-context source.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:37:| **C (chosen)** | Posture follows workspace trust. **Untrusted workspace → review** for `write_workspace`, `exec`, `egress` and `context_inject`. **Trusted workspace → auto** for `write_workspace` and `exec`; `egress` asks once per origin per session. `--yes` or `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` force auto. `--sandbox` stays available. | Safe for cloned or unknown repos. Low friction on the operator's own repos after one `nexus trust .`. Reuses the existing trust store, so there is no new concept. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:39:  - workspace trust;\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:24:Nexus Code resolves execution posture per workspace trust (DEC-01 option C):\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:30:- **Review mode (human-in-the-loop):** Run `nexus --approve` (or `nexus --mode review`) to require explicit approval for all actions regardless of workspace trust.\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:371:  Trust is managed via `nexus trust [path]` (undo with `nexus trust --remove`, list with `nexus trust --list`; stored in `~/.config/nexus/trusted_workspaces.json`, which the agent's file tools cannot write). In an untrusted workspace:\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:52:| VER-01 | S2 | Any session on a cloned/untrusted repo, including `--approve` review mode | agent.ts:1602-1617 (baseline), 3432-3436 (oracle), 1630 (independence copy run); tester.ts:113-136 | SOURCE. Before the first file edit (agent.ts:4034, after the edit's own approval) and at every `task_completed`, Nexus runs `make test` / `npm test` / `cargo test` / `pytest` through `bridge.executeTool` directly. These run arbitrary repo-defined code with no approval prompt and no workspace-trust check (unlike MCP/plugins, workspace_trust.ts), and unsandboxed unless `--sandbox`. Review mode shows an approval for `edit_file` but never for the hidden repo script that follows. Builds on SEC-01; it is a separate path because it bypasses even review mode. | Cloning a hostile repo and asking for any edit runs its test script on the host without a prompt. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: gate discovered verifiers on workspace trust or a one-time approval of the exact command (shown with its script body), and run them sandboxed when one is available. Document this. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:35:  - Workspace MCP configs and plugin JS are gated by `~/.config/nexus/trusted_workspaces.json` (workspace_trust.ts:35).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:53:| SEC-05 | S2 | untrusted repo opened | skills.ts:31-33; agent.ts:3301,3789 | SOURCE. Workspace skills (SKILL.md) are loaded and advertised in the system prompt with no workspace-trust check, unlike MCP and plugins (workspace_trust.ts:5-24). `activate_skill` is non-mutating, so it is never approved. | Persistent prompt injection from a cloned repo. Combined with SEC-01 this gives command execution. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: gate workspace skill directories on workspace trust, or show them as untrusted and require approval to activate. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:136:| R-SEC-5 | Workspace skills are subject to workspace trust. | safety | RELEASE-REQUIRED | An untrusted fixture repo with `skills/x/SKILL.md` does not appear in the system prompt or `/skills` without trust. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:112:| AGT-R8 | No implicit standing rules from prompts; no workspace writes in read-only mode; workspace-supplied knowledge gated by workspace trust. | safety (AGT-10) | RELEASE-REQUIRED | Read-only run leaves no `.nexus/`; prompt \"never run tests\" does not appear in next session's system prompt. |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":829009406}},"started_at_ms":1792830203164,"completed_at_ms":1792830203994}}
