{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T08:24:29.806Z","ordinal":282588,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a16d02-e96e-7913-ab2d-2255326e0e95","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2815)\nTotal output lines: 105\n\n# Work state: your to-do lists and working state\nUse claude-mem's work_state_write tool to track all to-do lists and multi-step work. It is your canonical to-do list: use it instead of any built-in to-do tool. Also use it to track the state of anything you need an ongoing understanding of. Whatever is still open is shown here at the start of every session in this project.\n- One list per to-do list or tracked thing: work_state_write with list=\"<name>\" and the fields to set\n- To-do item: fields {\"task\": \"<name>\", \"status\": \"todo\" | \"doing\" | \"done\" | \"dropped\", ...any details}\n- State: fields {\"<key>\": <value>} (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \"status\": \"done\" closes the list)\n- Read every list, closed items included: work_state_read with includeClosed=true\n\nStill open:\n- nexus-v1-release-convergence\n  - [todo] Obtain independent held-out corpus custody acceptance (details=Fresh public-only audit at main d8dc58be56102406642f0d2c6f5f0090711efeab: T2 public manifest hash 50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b, 40 tasks balanced across 4 classes/4 languages; T3 hash 85fb9cafbe18e846bd64fb13eb4fba0f92df0792bc93d12adaa685e04c9f1383, 8 tasks. Historical reports attest corpus custody/setup, but not current execution-boundary acceptance; T2 uses legacy validator format incompatible with runner, no successor/supersession recorded. Issue #1 last updated 2026-10-24T02:16:57Z with no custodian response. No private material accessed; no qualification run.), updated about 5 hours ago\n  - [doing] Complete provider, standalone, cross-runner, and exact-RC qualification (details=Live 2026-10-24 08:24Z: PR186 latest head c34d2ba559dd9b1efddb6efd80fcb26e637c741a rebased onto newly merged PR181 main 1a5365b11e99c49e835740438fd70937c310cd0e. Original full review ACCEPT; follow-up package-smoke fixture ACCEPT exact diff; final review refresh requested. Latest exact-head CI40077862009 and CodeQL40077862158 in progress. Prior fb70052 Node22/24 passed but Linux smoke-package failed because PTY trust prompt blocked expected TUI header; log retained /var/tmp/nexus-pr186-linux-40075233633.log. Added scoped trust env to PTY child; package tests need rerun on latest head. PR187 post-merge CI fully passed. Public RC3 only; custody unresolved and no held-out payload access. No local tests under SUITE claim. RC qualification, terminal/human acceptance and stable publication remain outstanding.), updated 1 minute ago\n- ...286 more lines; read them with work_state_read\n\n# [nexus-code] recent context, 2026-10-24 8:24am UTC\nMode: Code Development (code)\n\nLegend: 🎯session ●bugfix ◆feature ↻refactor ✓change ○discovery ⚖decision ⚠security_alert ⚷security_note ⊘sensitive\nFormat: ID TIME TYPE TITLE\nFetch details: get_observations([IDs]) | Search: mem-search skill\n\nStats: 50 obs (13,383t read) | 43,924t work | 70% savings\n\n### Oct 23, 2026\nS1675 CI monitoring for PR #174 (Docker read-only fail-closed fix) — waiting on test-matrix Node 22 and 24 jobs to complete (Oct 23, 10:24 PM)\nS1676 CI monitoring for PR #174 (Docker read-only fail-closed fix) — tracking test-matrix and linux-x86_64 job completion (Oct 23, 10:34 PM)\nS1677 PR #174 CI monitoring with auto-merge queued — waiting on linux-x86_64 npm test step to complete (Oct 23, 10:47 PM)\nS1678 Nexus RC.4 release gate review — assess PR #169 DeepSeek final report, PR #174 merge, PR #175 terminal control injection fix status, and CR sanitization gap (Oct 23, 10:53 PM)\nS1682 User shared an image (likely a screenshot of Nexus startup behavior) indicating missing functionality — session is reviewing current state to address the gap (Oct 23, 11:07 PM)\n21699 11:44p ○ Node.js Version Requirements Confirmed — Engine >=22, CI Tests on 22 and 24\n21701 11:45p ○ GitHub Blocks Self-Review on Own PRs — REQUEST_CHANGES Attempt Failed\n21703 \" ● PR #176 isSymlinkSafe Bypass Documented via Comment — Formal Review Blocked by GitHub\n21707 11:50p ✓ Release Gates Status Checkpoint Written to nexus-claims.log\n21710 11:51p ○ PR #176 Prior Independent Review ACCEPT Had Conditional Wording — Intermediate Traversal Test Gap Noted\n21711 11:52p ○ followup_task Dispatched to /root/rc1_docs_review Agent — Encrypted Payload\n21712 \" ○ Sleep Interrupted by Incoming Inter-Agent Message — rc1_docs_review Responded\n21714 \" ⚖ PR #176 isSymlinkSafe Review Position Revised — Final-Target Containment Accepted, Depth-Tracking Not Required\n21716 \" ✓ nexus-v1-release Work State Updated — PR #176 Review Reconciliation and Next Steps Recorded\n21717 11:53p ○ PR #176 test-matrix Node 24 Completed Successfully — Only Node 22 Remains\n21718 11:54p ○ PR #176 test-matrix Node 24 Confirmed Passed at 14m42s — Only Node 22 Remains\n21719 11:55p ○ PR #175 Node 22 Completed Successfully — PR #176 Node 22 Now the Last Remaining Job\n21720 \" ○ PR #176 Body Confirmed — Backslas…346 tokens truncated…1752 \" ✓ PR #175 Merged — HTML Control Injection Fix Now on Main\n21754 12:13a ✓ PR #176 Integration Sequencing Comment Updated — Rebase Required on New Main\n21755 \" ✓ nexus-v1-release Work State Updated — Post-PR175-Merge RC.4 Blocking Items\n21757 \" ○ PR #176 CI Run 40040813520 — test-matrix Complete, linux-x86_64 Packaging Active\n21759 12:14a ○ PR #176 All Checks Passed Except linux-x86_64 Packaging Still Pending\n21761 12:15a ○ Post-PR175-Merge Main CodeQL Completed Successfully\n21763 12:17a ○ PR #176 All CI Checks Passed — mergeStateStatus CLEAN on Stale Base\n21767 12:20a ○ DEFECT_TAR_SYMLINK Claim Owner PID 684835 Confirmed Dead — Claim Orphaned\n21769 \" ○ Stale Claim Protocol — Orphaned Claims Can Be Broken by Non-Owner with Log Entry\n21771 12:21a ○ PR #176 Rebased — New Head 7ea63567 on Current Main d92f38b\n21772 \" ○ Tar-Symlink Worktree HEAD Matches PR #176 New Head — Rebase Done In-Worktree\n21773 \" ○ PR #176 New CI Triggered on Rebased Head 7ea63567 — mergeStateStatus BLOCKED\n21774 \" ● PR #176 isSymlinkSafe Fix — Backslash Traversal and Escape-and-Return Both Blocked\n21775 \" ✓ PR #176 Independent Review Dispatched to rc1_docs_review Agent\n21778 12:22a ✓ PR #176 Independent Review Comment Updated — Evidence Accuracy Issues Documented\n21780 12:23a ○ PR #176 Rebased Head — CodeQL and JS/TS Passed, test-matrix Still Pending\n21782 \" ○ Issue #1 T2 Corpus Custody Updated — New Activity at 2026-10-24T00:19:17Z\n21785 \" ✓ Issue #1 T2 Corpus Custody Checkpoint Posted — RC.4 Qualification Remains Blocked\n21790 12:27a ✓ PR #176 Independent Review Updated to ACCEPT — Final-Target Containment Sufficient\n21792 12:30a ○ Post-PR175 Main CI test-matrix Both Nodes Passed — linux-x86_64 Packaging Now Running\n21793 12:34a ○ PR #176 CI Run — test-matrix Node 24 Passed, Node 22 Running npm cli test\n21794 12:36a ○ PR #176 test-matrix Both Nodes Passed — linux-x86_64 Packaging Now Running\n21796 12:37a ○ Post-PR175 Main CI Run 40043840844 Completed Successfully\n\nAccess 44k tokens of past work via get_observations([IDs]) or mem-search skill.\n\n⚠️ Heads up: claude-mem is paused while a provider quota cooldown is active.\n\nMemory capture is paused on claude (five_hour) to preserve your Claude allowance, until 2026-10-24T08:33:32.995Z (9 minutes from now).\n\nReason: Memory capture paused: five-hour Claude usage is 95.0%, at or above the 95% pause threshold. This reserves allowance for interactive work.\n\nThis is not a failure. Incoming observations stay queued in memory and are written\nwhen the cooldown clears — the worker is intentionally not starting the generator\nso interactive work keeps the remaining allowance.\n\nRestarting will NOT help here: it does not replenish the allowance or clear the\npersisted cooldown — so please leave the worker alone.\n\n(Assistant: tell the user that memory capture is paused for a quota cooldown\nat the very start of your first reply. Do NOT restart the worker and do NOT\nsuggest restarting it.)\n\n# claude-mem memory use\nModel-facing tool replies must be concise purpose-specific text; keep structured envelopes and internal metadata out of model context. Select only evidence useful to the current question, and expand from index to context to relevant details only as needed.\nUse claude-mem for your own durable notes. For local-worker notes, when its save_memory tool is available, save_memory({text, title, project}) records preferences, corrections, decisions, and reusable lessons. For server notes, use observation_add for the selected server project when available; save_memory is local-worker only.\nServer runtime: use Smart search by default in three steps—search({query}) for an index, timeline({anchor: ID}) for context, then get_observations({ids}) for only the records selected after reviewing the index and timeline. These tools use the configured server project; optional projectId selects another authorized server project. No auto or guided modes. Dumb search is unavailable in this runtime.\nWhen connected through CMEM Pro, Smart search uses memory_search({query}), timeline({anchorId}) for context, then selected get_observations({ids}) or get_summaries({ids}). A direct self-hosted /v1/mcp connection uses search({projectId, query}), timeline({projectId, anchorId}), then get_observations({projectId, ids}). Use only tools and argument names advertised by the active connection; no auto or guided modes.\nUse work_state_write for to-do lists and changing work state when available. Keep durable notes concise, distinguish verified facts from guesses, and exclude credentials and private material the user asked you not to remember. Native memory files can remain enabled; an explicitly configured memory folder watcher imports their Markdown notes into claude-mem. Never assume a hosted memory search was intercepted: search claude-mem directly when its result is needed.\n\nFull hook output saved to: /tmp/hook_outputs/01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92/ffff831d-ccee-4628-bee0-c42e708d580f.txt"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16cd4-55fc-7d42-952d-a5ba875e9e0d","create_time":1792830269.806301,"content_item_kinds":["hooks.additional_context"]}}}
