{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T08:32:53.602Z","ordinal":282949,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16cd4-55fc-7d42-952d-a5ba875e9e0d","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adc6d34a39481a0af8fc1adfea87f21","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The local command accidentally launched the entire CLI suite instead of just retention tests: the package script forwards extra arguments to its final shell command, not the test runner. That bare worktree also lacks the CI build prerequisites, and early unrelated tests report core-daemon disconnects. I’m stopping that invalid local run, then I’ll run the focused retention files through the test runner directly; the required full suites are already running on the exact PR head in hosted CI."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1792830772677,"completed_at_ms":1792830773601}}
