{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T08:44:42.239Z","ordinal":283443,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016adc6ff9b8e881a0a1279570aa109fe5","status":"completed","call_id":"call_d6cd899fbd85434f97ed7829163ee477","name":"exec","input":"const r=await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '20,70p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; sed -n '100,130p' .github/workflows/release.yml\",workdir:\"/tmp/nexus-release-gate-1a5365\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:2000});\ntext(r);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16cd4-55fc-7d42-952d-a5ba875e9e0d","create_time":1792831481.724816}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T08:44:42.346Z","ordinal":283444,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16cd4-55fc-7d42-952d-a5ba875e9e0d","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a16cd4-55fc-7d42-952d-a5ba875e9e0d","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016adc6ff81c8081a0a43e518ddf2c6146","usage":{"input_tokens":200086,"cached_input_tokens":199296,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":197,"reasoning_output_tokens":104,"total_tokens":200283},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":44290137,"cached_input_tokens":43845760,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":145016,"reasoning_output_tokens":89569,"total_tokens":44435153},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":5109196414,"cached_input_tokens":5054141824,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":14328370,"reasoning_output_tokens":8150265,"total_tokens":5123524784}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T08:44:44.360Z","ordinal":283445,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16cd4-55fc-7d42-952d-a5ba875e9e0d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-ddde9c33-b1ae-495e-a0f6-9ce6329b7860","process_id":"95089","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '20,70p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; sed -n '100,130p' .github/workflows/release.yml"],"cwd":"file:///tmp/nexus-release-gate-1a5365","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '20,70p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md","name":"ACCEPTANCE.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '100,130p' .github/workflows/release.yml","name":"release.yml","path":".github/workflows/release.yml"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"## 1.1 Release-candidate lifecycle and evidence identity\n\nThe release sequence has five distinct stages. Passing an earlier stage is a prerequisite for the next stage, not a substitute for it. Every G0–G4 acceptance ID remains mandatory; the stage determines which exact input and evidence it evaluates, not whether the check applies.\n\n1. **Pre-RC source gates.** Before creating an RC tag, run required source CI and every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method evaluates source, a source-built test binary, or an environment without requiring a published RC. Record the full commit ID and check results. Source checks do not establish behavior of the installed package.\n2. **RC artifact construction.** After the required owner authorization, create the version-matched RC tag on that exact source commit and use the repository release workflow to build and publish the RC artifacts. Record the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance. The workflow-produced artifacts are the candidates for qualification; a local build or a different commit is not interchangeable. RC artifact publication is not product qualification or final release acceptance.\n3. **RC artifact gates.** Before installed-RC product qualification, run every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method requires the RC archive, RC attestation/release, or workflow-produced artifact. This includes ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08. ACC-PKG checks that explicitly require an installed package run against this RC as specified by their test method. Record the RC tag commit, workflow run, artifact digests, and each check result. A source-level analogue does not replace an artifact-bound check.\n4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\n5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\n\nThe final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\n\nExact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\n\nThe post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\n\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:START -->\n### Qualification-only requirements for exact-RC enforcement\n\n| Requirement | Acceptance criteria required in the exact-RC record | Remaining stage |\n|---|---|---|\n| REQ-REL-003 | ACC-PLAT | Installed-RC platform and Node-version matrix |\n| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\n| REQ-AGT-010 | ACC-TRUST-04 | Independent acceptance of the DEC-04 v1 subset |\n| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\n| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\n| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\n| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\n| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\n| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\n### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\n\n| Requirement | Approved decision | Scope |\n|---|---|---|\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:END -->\n\n## 1. Rules\n\n1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\n2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n3. Thresholds (DEC-05) are frozen before the first M5 run. A failing gate is fixed in code and the run is repeated as `rc.N+1`. A threshold is never relaxed after results are known.\n4. Evidence goes to `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. The directory contains:\n   - `manifest.json`: commit, package sha256, environment, model fingerprint, dates;\n   - raw outputs;\n   - a `SHA256SUMS` file.\n      - run: cmp \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/SHA256SUMS\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check/SHA256SUMS\"\n      - run: cmp \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt\"\n      - run: cyclonedx validate --input-file \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/sbom.cdx.json\" --fail-on-errors\n      - run: cmp \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/sbom.cdx.json\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check/sbom.cdx.json\"\n      - run: cmp \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/install.sh\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check/install.sh\"\n      - run: bash scripts/smoke-package.sh \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/nexus-linux-x86_64-$GITHUB_REF_NAME.tar.gz\"\n      - run: bash scripts/installer-smoke.sh \"$GITHUB_WORKSPACE/install.sh\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/nexus-linux-x86_64-$GITHUB_REF_NAME.tar.gz\"\n      - name: Attest build provenance\n        uses: actions/attest-build-provenance@92c65d2898f1f53cfdc910b962cecff86e7f8fcc # v1\n        with:\n          subject-path: |\n            ${{ runner.temp }}/dist/nexus-linux-x86_64-${{ github.ref_name }}.tar.gz\n            ${{ runner.temp }}/dist/SHA256SUMS\n      # RC tags (vX.Y.Z-rc.N) publish a prerelease: the workflow-produced RC is the qualification candidate\n      # (ACCEPTANCE §1.1 stage 2). Stable tags only build an unpublished draft (stage 5); it is published by hand with\n      # `gh release edit <tag> --draft=false` after the stable artifact checks and the signed acceptance disposition.\n      - uses: softprops/action-gh-release@3bb12739c298aeb8a4eeaf626c5b8d85266b0e65 # v2\n        with:\n          files: ${{ runner.temp }}/dist/*\n          body_path: docs/releases/${{ github.ref_name }}.md\n          prerelease: ${{ contains(github.ref_name, '-') }}\n          draft: ${{ !contains(github.ref_name, '-') }}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":905171497}},"started_at_ms":1792831483455,"completed_at_ms":1792831484360}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T08:44:45.449Z","ordinal":283446,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a16d15-7609-7a52-9560-fb53d44ce1e7","call_id":"call_d6cd899fbd85434f97ed7829163ee477","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"fc2c57\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.905243113,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2378,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2378)\\nTotal output lines: 73\\n\\n## 1.1 Release-candidate lifecycle and evidence identity\\n\\nThe release sequence has five distinct stages. Passing an earlier stage is a prerequisite for the next stage, not a substitute for it. Every G0–G4 acceptance ID remains mandatory; the stage determines which exact input and evidence it evaluates, not whether the check applies.\\n\\n1. **Pre-RC source gates.** Before creating an RC tag, run required source CI and every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method evaluates source, a source-built test binary, or an environment without requiring a published RC. Record the full commit ID and check results. Source checks do not establish behavior of the installed package.\\n2. **RC artifact construction.** After the required owner authorization, create the version-matched RC tag on that exact source commit and use the repository release workflow to build and publish the RC artifacts. Record the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance. The workflow-produced artifacts are the candidates for qualification; a local build or a different commit is not interchangeable. RC artifact publication is not product qualification or final release acceptance.\\n3. **RC artifact gates.** Before installed-RC product qualification, run every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method requires the RC archive, RC attestation/release, or workflow-produced artifact. This includes ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08. ACC-PKG checks that explicitly require an installed package run against this RC as specified by their test method. Record the RC tag commit, workflow run, artifact digests, and each check result. A source-level analogue does not replace an artifact-bound check.\\n4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\\n5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\\n\\nThe final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signe…378 tokens truncated…red row omitted from this table still fails.\\n\\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:START -->\\n### Qualification-only requirements for exact-RC enforcement\\n\\n| Requirement | Acceptance criteria required in the exact-RC record | Remaining stage |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| REQ-REL-003 | ACC-PLAT | Installed-RC platform and Node-version matrix |\\n| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\\n| REQ-AGT-010 | ACC-TRUST-04 | Independent acceptance of the DEC-04 v1 subset |\\n| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\\n| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\\n| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\\n| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\\n| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\\n| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\\n| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\\n| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\\n| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\\n\\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\\n### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\\n\\n| Requirement | Approved decision | Scope |\\n|---|---|---|\\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:END -->\\n\\n## 1. Rules\\n\\n1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\\n2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\\n3. Thresholds (DEC-05) are frozen before the first M5 run. A failing gate is fixed in code and the run is repeated as `rc.N+1`. A threshold is never relaxed after results are known.\\n4. Evidence goes to `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. The directory contains:\\n   - `manifest.json`: commit, package sha256, environment, model fingerprint, dates;\\n   - raw outputs;\\n   - a `SHA256SUMS` file.\\n      - run: cmp \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/SHA256SUMS\\\" \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check/SHA256SUMS\\\"\\n      - run: cmp \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt\\\" \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt\\\"\\n      - run: cyclonedx validate --input-file \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/sbom.cdx.json\\\" --fail-on-errors\\n      - run: cmp \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/sbom.cdx.json\\\" \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check/sbom.cdx.json\\\"\\n      - run: cmp \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/install.sh\\\" \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check/install.sh\\\"\\n      - run: bash scripts/smoke-package.sh \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/nexus-linux-x86_64-$GITHUB_REF_NAME.tar.gz\\\"\\n      - run: bash scripts/installer-smoke.sh \\\"$GITHUB_WORKSPACE/install.sh\\\" \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/nexus-linux-x86_64-$GITHUB_REF_NAME.tar.gz\\\"\\n      - name: Attest build provenance\\n        uses: actions/attest-build-provenance@92c65d2898f1f53cfdc910b962cecff86e7f8fcc # v1\\n        with:\\n          subject-path: |\\n            ${{ runner.temp }}/dist/nexus-linux-x86_64-${{ github.ref_name }}.tar.gz\\n            ${{ runner.temp }}/dist/SHA256SUMS\\n      # RC tags (vX.Y.Z-rc.N) publish a prerelease: the workflow-produced RC is the qualification candidate\\n      # (ACCEPTANCE §1.1 stage 2). Stable tags only build an unpublished draft (stage 5); it is published by hand with\\n      # `gh release edit <tag> --draft=false` after the stable artifact checks and the signed acceptance disposition.\\n      - uses: softprops/action-gh-release@3bb12739c298aeb8a4eeaf626c5b8d85266b0e65 # v2\\n        with:\\n          files: ${{ runner.temp }}/dist/*\\n          body_path: docs/releases/${{ github.ref_name }}.md\\n          prerelease: ${{ contains(github.ref_name, '-') }}\\n          draft: ${{ !contains(github.ref_name, '-') }}\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16cd4-55fc-7d42-952d-a5ba875e9e0d","create_time":1792831485.449085}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
