on base `faf95803714a3c543f5c59bc0610ca6291a6184d`; exact PR CI run `39141379739`, CodeQL run `39141379747`, and the `javascript-typescript` check passed. Independent read-only review accepted the only post-review delta. Post-merge CodeQL run `39144374432` passed on `4bce876`. Post-merge CI run `39144374445` is still running Node 20/22/24; its Cloudflare contract job passed. Exact integration CI on the parent `faf9580` passed as run `39139084949`, but it does not replace checks on `4bce876`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-162-- **PR state:** PRs #9, #13, #15, #16, and #44 are integrated. PR #9's stale readiness changes were merged earlier and are retained in history. PR #33 remains open at `0ca77e5ee64f80db02e2b16178c5be551ce5de0c`, based on now-stale `faf9580`; its exact CI run `39141771002` passed all five jobs, including 1,243 CLI tests with zero failures, resource enforcement fixtures, staged Git-history/external-store canaries, security gates, deterministic package/SBOM comparison, and installer/package smoke. Independent review found a release-critical gap: preflight does not compare protected corpus paths with the evaluator's unconditional system mounts such as `/usr/local/lib`. The reviewer requested refusal of protected paths beneath every mounted host path and regression coverage. The evaluator claim remains active; no transfer or remediation checkpoint has been reported. Do not run held-out qualification. PR #33 must incorporate `4bce876`, fix this finding, pass exact-head checks, and receive independent re-review.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:163:- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` ran from a detached worktree at exact revision `4bce8760893b222789b76011a477dd61988ecba6` with isolated `HOME`; it failed as required. Ledger result: 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 11 below threshold: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, `REQ-QUAL-109`. `REQ-AGT-118` remains tested. `REQ-AGT-010` remains partial; its existing ACC-TRUST-04 source evidence is pinned to `2c70d39`, and the current row still needs exact-revision evidence and a DEC-04-aligned disposition before promotion. The ledger owner was given this exact checker output; no ledger status was changed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-164-- **Evaluator boundary and T2 custody:** PR #33's exact source CI passes resource-bound and Git-history canary fixtures, but the independent unconditional-system-mount finding remains open. Separately, the custodian report accepts the sealed manifest identity `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`, its custody, author-session provenance, private digest validation, and reference validation; private payloads were not inspected for this checkpoint. The sealed tasks use legacy `hidden: { dir, into, command }` checks, while evaluator qualification requires `blackbox-v1`. Custody acceptance does not resolve this format mismatch or evaluator-boundary acceptance. No T2 qualification has started.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-165-- **Qualification host and terminal:** Qualification-host tooling is integrated through PR #31 (`8c0ab7b`), but this checkpoint has no evidence that the qualification host was provisioned and validated at `4bce876`. Terminal acceptance procedure is integrated; the required human matrix remains unexecuted. It requires five environments × three sizes on the exact installed RC, with per-cell PASS/FAIL and screenshots of the approval panel and post-exit state.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-166-- **Version, RC, and publication:** Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`. PR #44's deterministic package checks are source CI evidence for that alpha package; they do not establish cross-runner RC reproducibility or installed-RC acceptance. No RC artifact, installed-RC provider/standalone, held-out, T3/T4, cross-runner, human-terminal, or independent acceptance evidence exists. The staged lifecycle in `ACCEPTANCE.md` remains authoritative. Publication authorization remains granted and gated; no RC tag, stable tag, npm publication, or GitHub release exists.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-167-\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-191-  - Kernel-enforced resource contract (`91406bd`, PR #19, `eval/resources.mjs`, `eval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs`, `scripts/ensure-ci-user-cgroups.sh`) executes each task phase (setup, candidate sandbox, hidden/regression, oracle) inside a transient delegated `systemd --user` scope with verified cgroup v2 `CPUQuota`, `MemoryMax`, `MemorySwapMax=0`, `TasksMax`, `memory.oom.group=1`, dedicated size-capped tmpfs `workspaceRoot` storage enforcement, and `cgroup.kill` process-tree cleanup verified to `populated == 0`. These controls are source-implemented, independently reviewed, and CI-tested (`1,152/1,152` on `0cee0b7`, run `39104943950`), not live qualification results. Qualification-host provisioning (`nexus-eval` account, narrow sudoers rule, dedicated tmpfs mount, and frozen `config.resources` profile) remains a prerequisite before running held-out T2/T3/T4 workloads.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-192-- **Governance, tokenizer, and acceptance lifecycle reconciliations (PRs [#11](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/11)–[#15](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/15), [#17](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/17)):**\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-193-  - `DEC-05` amendment (`f771a3c`, PR #11) and `ACCEPTANCE.md` §6.2 (`77102c5`, PR #13) resolve the historical eight-vs-nine T4 denominator conflict by retaining all **9 fault classes × 5 runs** (including SIGTERM + `run --resume`).\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-194-  - `DEC-17` (`f771a3c`, PR #11), `REQ-AGT-118` reconciliation (`d2c4bfc`, PR #12), and published independent review records (`19dedc6`, PR #14; `f8e19e4`, PR #15; `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-11_PR-11d_REVIEW_AGT-118/`) resolve the CJK/Hangul admission-safety floor vs `≤ 1.5×` accuracy band conflict: the `≥ 1` token/character safety floor takes precedence, `≤ 1.5×` applies to corpora not dominated by the floor, and recorded Chinese (`2.00×`) and Hangul (`1.67×`) exceptions remain preserved. `REQ-AGT-118` is `tested` at the source level (`tokens.test.ts` 3/3 pass); this does not claim installed-RC product qualification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:195:  - `REQ-AGT-010` and historical `CTX-001` rows (`f68b5bc`, PR #17) are reconciled with `DEC-04`: the v1 subset (`ACC-TRUST-04` trust gating and source/trust annotations in `workspace_trust.test.ts`, 5/5 pass) is source-tested and independently accepted, while the full provenance graph and `CTX-002` remain post-v1.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-196-  - `ACCEPTANCE.md` §1.1 (`77102c5`, PR #13) defines the five-stage RC lifecycle binding source gates, workflow-built RC artifact construction, RC artifact gates (`ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08`), installed-RC qualification, and version-only stable promotion.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-197-- **Supply-chain reproducibility and draft-then-publish release workflow (PRs [#20](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/20), [#21](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/21)):**\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-198-  - `.github/workflows/repro.yml` and `scripts/repro-identity.mjs` (`86bdbe6`, PR #20) enforce fail-closed tag/commit/clean-tree/version identity across independent Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 builders.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-199-  - `.github/workflows/release.yml` and `scripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs` (`a7126aa`, PR #21) build RC tags (`vX.Y.Z-rc.N`) as prereleases and build stable tags (`vX.Y.Z`) as **unpublished drafts** (`draft: true`), requiring via the RC's own checker that a stable tag is a single commit directly on its `vX.Y.Z-rc.N` parent changing only synchronized version metadata.\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md-253-| ID | Current state | Remaining behavior or evidence | Dependency | Owner role | Exact next action |\ndoc