{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T08:59:32.768Z","ordinal":283835,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16cd4-55fc-7d42-952d-a5ba875e9e0d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-e5722437-b8ba-4df2-853b-158ceadee46e","process_id":"42486","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 186 --comments | tail -n 90; gh pr view 188 --comments | tail -n 60; gh run view 40077862009 --json status,conclusion,updatedAt; gh run view 40078369394 --json status,conclusion,updatedAt"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 186 --comments | tail -n 90; gh pr view 188 --comments | tail -n 60; gh run view 40077862009 --json status,conclusion,updatedAt; gh run view 40078369394 --json status,conclusion,updatedAt"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"association:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n### Independent Review: CHANGES_REQUESTED\n\n**Target commit**: `f4d40cdc5c4cf1196b7beb88f51953d721a370a8`  \n**Base commit**: `fc681d806d7698d6a05107a16141677e728f6163` (origin/main)  \n**CI Run**: [40074046981](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40074046981) (`test-matrix (22)` and `test-matrix (24)` failed)\n\n#### Finding: Interactive PTY Tests Hang at Startup Trust Prompt\nThe implementation of `promptWorkspaceTrust` displays an interactive prompt whenever `input.isTTY && output.isTTY` in an untrusted workspace. While `cli/test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts` was updated with `trustWorkspace(home, repo)`, `cli/test/turn_semantics.test.ts` was not updated.\n\nAs a result, the `interactive REPL (pty)` subtests run under `util-linux script` (which provides pseudo-terminal TTY streams), encounter the trust prompt, and hang waiting for user input, causing a 30s timeout failure:\n\n1. `cli/test/turn_semantics.test.ts:708`: `Ctrl-C during a delayed mutating trajectory: one interrupt, no new mutation, prompt returns, next turn works`\n```\nError: timeout waiting for /❯ /; output tail: \nTrust this folder?\n↑↓ navigate · Enter select · Esc exit\n/tmp/nexus-turn-...\nLoad project instructions\n…\n› Trust and continue\n  Continue without trusting\n  Exit\n```\n2. `cli/test/turn_semantics.test.ts:751`: `multiple prompts in one session keep working; Ctrl-C at idle still exits deliberately`\n(Fails with identical timeout waiting for `/❯ /` at the trust prompt).\n\n#### Recommended Resolution\nIn `cli/test/turn_semantics.test.ts`, import `trustWorkspace` from `./helpers/fixtures.js` and ensure the workspace is trusted before launching the REPL in the `session` helper:\n```ts\nimport { startGateway, makeRepo, makeHome, Reply, ptyTest, trustWorkspace } from \"./helpers/fixtures.js\";\n// ...\nasync function session(gw: Gateway, repo: string, home: string) {\n  trustWorkspace(home, repo);\n  const cmd = ...\n```\nOnce updated and rebased, exact-head CI should be re-run.\n--\nauthor:\tmikeholownych\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n### Independent Review: ACCEPT\n\n**Target commit**: `fb70052e19340caa7a050f98c0392785df525a07`  \n**Base commit**: `fc681d806d7698d6a05107a16141677e728f6163` (origin/main)  \n**Files changed**: 11 files (+606, -8)\n\n#### Verification & Assessment\n1. **Resolution of CHANGES_REQUESTED Finding**:\n   - `cli/test/turn_semantics.test.ts` has been updated with `NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE: \"1\"` in the PTY `session` helper environment, allowing the turn semantics test suite to run in the pseudo-terminal without being blocked at the interactive startup trust prompt.\n   - Verified that `cli/src/workspace_trust.ts` supports `NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE === \"1\"` to return true for `isWorkspaceTrusted()`.\n2. **Interactive Trust & Sanitization Implementation**:\n   - Non-interactive launches fail closed to untrusted mode and emit a notice without blocking.\n   - Interactive TTY prompt provides clean navigation and choices: \"Trust and continue\", \"Continue without trusting\", \"Exit\".\n   - Project instructions (`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `CODEX.md`, `.nexusrules`) are gated on explicit workspace trust via `trustedProjectRules`.\n   - Control characters and Unicode format characters in display paths are safely sanitized with grapheme cell-width fitting.\n3. **Hygiene & Verification**:\n   - `git diff --check` passes cleanly with 0 errors.\n   - CodeQL run [40075233603](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40075233603): `✓ SUCCESS`.\n   - Hosted CI run [40075233633](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40075233633): in progress.\n\nNo regressions or security concerns. Recommended for merge once CI completes.\n--\nauthor:\tmikeholownych\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n### Independent Review: ACCEPT\n\n**Target commit**: `c34d2ba559dd9b1efddb6efd80fcb26e637c741a`  \n**Base commit**: `1a5365b11e99c49e835740438fd70937c310cd0e` (origin/main)  \n**Files changed**: 12 files (+608, -8)\n\n#### Verification & Assessment\n1. **Package Smoke PTY Resolution**:\n   - In `scripts/package-smoke-pty.py`, sets `os.environ[\"NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE\"] = \"1\"` in the slave PTY environment before launching the packaged TUI, correctly bypassing the startup interactive trust chooser during package smoke validation.\n2. **Rebase & Invariants**:\n   - Cleanly rebased onto `main@1a5365b`.\n   - `git diff --check` passes with 0 errors.\n   - CodeQL run [40077862158](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40077862158): `✓ SUCCESS`.\n   - Hosted CI run [40077862009](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40077862009): in progress.\n\nNo regressions or security concerns found. Recommended for merge once CI completes.\n--\n**Planning:**\n- It records dev/ino identities for the state root, the checkpoints root, the partition, the `snapshots/` directory, and the snapshot object itself.\n- It rejects symlinked or non-canonical directories (`lstat` plus `realpath === path`) and accepts only `snapshots/<cpId>` with a validated `cpId`.\n\n**Execution:**\n- `openDirectoryNoFollow` walks from `/` component by component through `/proc/self/fd/<fd>/<name>` with `O_DIRECTORY|O_NOFOLLOW`, and re-verifies each planned identity with `fstat`.\n- `openChildDirectory` rejects `.`, `..` and separators.\n- Any identity change, or a platform without `/proc/self/fd`, `O_DIRECTORY` or `O_NOFOLLOW`, preserves the checkpoint and throws. That's fail-closed, as the PR states, at the documented cost of no checkpoint GC on those platforms.\n\n**Readability:** in the snapshot block, `const rootStat = fs.lstatSync(snapshotsPath)` (around :612) shadows the outer checkpoints-root `rootStat`. `snapshotsRootIdentity = directoryIdentity(rootStat)` is therefore correctly the `snapshots/` directory's identity, and `openChildDirectory(partitionFd, \"snapshots\", …)` at :1038 checks against it. But the shadowing reads like a bug. Renaming it to `snapshotsStat` would prevent a future regression.\n\nMerge after exact-head `linux-x86_64` is green. If this lands before the rc.4 tag, it needs a line in the rc.4 notes (#181).\n--\nauthor:\tmikeholownych\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n### Independent Review: ACCEPT\n\n**Target commit**: `c92861fd7de4bb9f74739aeaaa93b59e4895c625`  \n**Base commit**: `fc681d806d7698d6a05107a16141677e728f6163` (origin/main)  \n**Files changed**: 2 files (+471, -41)\n\n#### Verification & Assessment\n1. **Descriptor-Pinned Confinement & Anti-Race Architecture**:\n   - `openDirectoryNoFollow` walks directory components from the filesystem root using `O_DIRECTORY | O_NOFOLLOW` via `/proc/self/fd/<fd>/<component>`, eliminating symlink substitution and directory swap races at every hop.\n   - Preserves planned identities: explicitly compares filesystem device, inode, and mode (`dev:ino` and `dev:ino:mode`) against the planned identity before proceeding.\n   - Deletion confinement: `removeConfinedTreeAt` operates strictly relative to opened parent descriptors, unlinking leaf entries directly and refusing to follow symlinks.\n   - Fail-closed semantics: explicitly checks for Linux platform support, `O_DIRECTORY`, `O_NOFOLLOW`, and `/proc/self/fd`. Preserves checkpoints and reports clean error if unsupported.\n2. **Hygiene & Tests**:\n   - Comprehensive test suite in `cli/test/retention_checkpoint_confinement.test.ts` exercises symlinked partitions, replaced directories, changed roots, and non-conforming paths (15/15 passed).\n   - `git diff --check` passes cleanly with 0 errors.\n   - CodeQL run [40075741419](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40075741419): `✓ SUCCESS`.\n   - Hosted CI run [40075741401](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40075741401): in progress.\n\nNo regressions or security concerns found. Recommended for merge once CI completes.\n--\nauthor:\tmikeholownych\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n### Independent Review: ACCEPT\n\n**Target commit**: `faebcc0ffabd1bd1be2829c79499226fe6c9a217`  \n**Base commit**: `1a5365b11e99c49e835740438fd70937c310cd0e` (origin/main)  \n**Files changed**: 2 files (+471, -41)\n\n#### Verification & Assessment\n1. **Rebase & Exact Diff Validation**:\n   - Cleanly rebased onto `main@1a5365b`.\n   - The descriptor-pinned directory walk, `/proc/self/fd/` unlinking, and `dev:ino` identity checks remain intact and unchanged.\n   - `git diff --check` passes cleanly with 0 errors.\n2. **CI Status**:\n   - CodeQL run [40078369339](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40078369339): `✓ SUCCESS`.\n   - Hosted CI run [40078369394](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40078369394): in progress.\n\nNo regressions or security concerns. Ready for merge once CI finishes.\n--\n{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-24T08:57:12Z\"}\n{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-24T08:47:52Z\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":3,"nanos":62385190}},"started_at_ms":1792832369702,"completed_at_ms":1792832372765}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T08:59:33.795Z","ordinal":283836,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a16d23-0423-7ce2-be9c-8d2642a2955c","call_id":"call_c9687ee002f94ad69c1dffd374df729d","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 5.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"association:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n### Independent Review: CHANGES_REQUESTED\n\n**Target commit**: `f4d40cdc5c4cf1196b7beb88f51953d721a370a8`  \n**Base commit**: `fc681d806d7698d6a05107a16141677e728f6163` (origin/main)  \n**CI Run**: [40074046981](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40074046981) (`test-matrix (22)` and `test-matrix (24)` failed)\n\n#### Finding: Interactive PTY Tests Hang at Startup Trust Prompt\nThe implementation of `promptWorkspaceTrust` displays an interactive prompt whenever `input.isTTY && output.isTTY` in an untrusted workspace. While `cli/test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts` was updated with `trustWorkspace(home, repo)`, `cli/test/turn_semantics.test.ts` was not updated.\n\nAs a result, the `interactive REPL (pty)` subtests run under `util-linux script` (which provides pseudo-terminal TTY streams), encounter the trust prompt, and hang waiting for user input, causing a 30s timeout failure:\n\n1. `cli/test/turn_semantics.test.ts:708`: `Ctrl-C during a delayed mutating trajectory: one interrupt, no new mutation, prompt returns, next turn works`\n```\nError: timeout waiting for /❯ /; output tail: \nTrust this folder?\n↑↓ navigate · Enter select · Esc exit\n/tmp/nexus-turn-...\nLoad project instructions\n…\n› Trust and continue\n  Continue without trusting\n  Exit\n```\n2. `cli/test/turn_semantics.test.ts:751`: `multiple prompts in one session keep working; Ctrl-C at idle still exits deliberately`\n(Fails with identical timeout waiting for `/❯ /` at the trust prompt).\n\n#### Recommended Resolution\nIn `cli/test/turn_semantics.test.ts`, import `trustWorkspace` from `./helpers/fixtures.js` and ensure the workspace is trusted before launching the REPL in the `session` helper:\n```ts\nimport { startGateway, makeRepo, makeHome, Reply, ptyTest, trustWorkspace } from \"./helpers/fixtures.js\";\n// ...\nasync function session(gw: Gateway, repo: string, home: string) {\n  trustWorkspace(home, repo);\n  const cmd = ...\n```\nOnce updated and rebased, exact-head CI should be re-run.\n--\nauthor:\tmikeholownych\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n### Independent Review: ACCEPT\n\n**Target commit**: `fb70052e19340caa7a050f98c0392785df525a07`  \n**Base commit**: `fc681d806d7698d6a05107a16141677e728f6163` (origin/main)  \n**Files changed**: 11 files (+606, -8)\n\n#### Verification & Assessment\n1. **Resolution of CHANGES_REQUESTED Finding**:\n   - `cli/test/turn_semantics.test.ts` has been updated with `NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE: \"1\"` in the PTY `session` helper environment, allowing the turn semantics test suite to run in the pseudo-terminal without being blocked at the interactive startup trust prompt.\n   - Verified that `cli/src/workspace_trust.ts` supports `NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE === \"1\"` to return true for `isWorkspaceTrusted()`.\n2. **Interactive Trust & Sanitization Implementation**:\n   - Non-interactive launches fail closed to untrusted mode and emit a notice without blocking.\n   - Interactive TTY prompt provides clean navigation and choices: \"Trust and continue\", \"Continue without trusting\", \"Exit\".\n   - Project instructions (`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `CODEX.md`, `.nexusrules`) are gated on explicit workspace trust via `trustedProjectRules`.\n   - Control characters and Unicode format characters in display paths are safely sanitized with grapheme cell-width fitting.\n3. **Hygiene & Verification**:\n   - `git diff --check` passes cleanly with 0 errors.\n   - CodeQL run [40075233603](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40075233603): `✓ SUCCESS`.\n   - Hosted CI run [40075233633](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40075233633): in progress.\n\nNo regressions or security concerns. Recommended for merge once CI completes.\n--\nauthor:\tmikeholownych\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n### Independent Review: ACCEPT\n\n**Target commit**: `c34d2ba559dd9b1efddb6efd80fcb26e637c741a`  \n**Base commit**: `1a5365b11e99c49e835740438fd70937c310cd0e` (origin/main)  \n**Files changed**: 12 files (+608, -8)\n\n#### Verification & Assessment\n1. **Package Smoke PTY Resolution**:\n   - In `scripts/package-smoke-pty.py`, sets `os.environ[\"NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE\"] = \"1\"` in the slave PTY environment before launching the packaged TUI, correctly bypassing the startup interactive trust chooser during package smoke validation.\n2. **Rebase & Invariants**:\n   - Cleanly rebased onto `main@1a5365b`.\n   - `git diff --check` passes with 0 errors.\n   - CodeQL run [40077862158](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40077862158): `✓ SUCCESS`.\n   - Hosted CI run [40077862009](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40077862009): in progress.\n\nNo regressions or security concerns found. Recommended for merge once CI completes.\n--\n**Planning:**\n- It records dev/ino identities for the state root, the checkpoints root, the partition, the `snapshots/` directory, and the snapshot object itself.\n- It rejects symlinked or non-canonical directories (`lstat` plus `realpath === path`) and accepts only `snapshots/<cpId>` with a validated `cpId`.\n\n**Execution:**\n- `openDirectoryNoFollow` walks from `/` component by component through `/proc/self/fd/<fd>/<name>` with `O_DIRECTORY|O_NOFOLLOW`, and re-verifies each planned identity with `fstat`.\n- `openChildDirectory` rejects `.`, `..` and separators.\n- Any identity change, or a platform without `/proc/self/fd`, `O_DIRECTORY` or `O_NOFOLLOW`, preserves the checkpoint and throws. That's fail-closed, as the PR states, at the documented cost of no checkpoint GC on those platforms.\n\n**Readability:** in the snapshot block, `const rootStat = fs.lstatSync(snapshotsPath)` (around :612) shadows the outer checkpoints-root `rootStat`. `snapshotsRootIdentity = directoryIdentity(rootStat)` is therefore correctly the `snapshots/` directory's identity, and `openChildDirectory(partitionFd, \"snapshots\", …)` at :1038 checks against it. But the shadowing reads like a bug. Renaming it to `snapshotsStat` would prevent a future regression.\n\nMerge after exact-head `linux-x86_64` is green. If this lands before the rc.4 tag, it needs a line in the rc.4 notes (#181).\n--\nauthor:\tmikeholownych\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n### Independent Review: ACCEPT\n\n**Target commit**: `c92861fd7de4bb9f74739aeaaa93b59e4895c625`  \n**Base commit**: `fc681d806d7698d6a05107a16141677e728f6163` (origin/main)  \n**Files changed**: 2 files (+471, -41)\n\n#### Verification & Assessment\n1. **Descriptor-Pinned Confinement & Anti-Race Architecture**:\n   - `openDirectoryNoFollow` walks directory components from the filesystem root using `O_DIRECTORY | O_NOFOLLOW` via `/proc/self/fd/<fd>/<component>`, eliminating symlink substitution and directory swap races at every hop.\n   - Preserves planned identities: explicitly compares filesystem device, inode, and mode (`dev:ino` and `dev:ino:mode`) against the planned identity before proceeding.\n   - Deletion confinement: `removeConfinedTreeAt` operates strictly relative to opened parent descriptors, unlinking leaf entries directly and refusing to follow symlinks.\n   - Fail-closed semantics: explicitly checks for Linux platform support, `O_DIRECTORY`, `O_NOFOLLOW`, and `/proc/self/fd`. Preserves checkpoints and reports clean error if unsupported.\n2. **Hygiene & Tests**:\n   - Comprehensive test suite in `cli/test/retention_checkpoint_confinement.test.ts` exercises symlinked partitions, replaced directories, changed roots, and non-conforming paths (15/15 passed).\n   - `git diff --check` passes cleanly with 0 errors.\n   - CodeQL run [40075741419](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40075741419): `✓ SUCCESS`.\n   - Hosted CI run [40075741401](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40075741401): in progress.\n\nNo regressions or security concerns found. Recommended for merge once CI completes.\n--\nauthor:\tmikeholownych\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n### Independent Review: ACCEPT\n\n**Target commit**: `faebcc0ffabd1bd1be2829c79499226fe6c9a217`  \n**Base commit**: `1a5365b11e99c49e835740438fd70937c310cd0e` (origin/main)  \n**Files changed**: 2 files (+471, -41)\n\n#### Verification & Assessment\n1. **Rebase & Exact Diff Validation**:\n   - Cleanly rebased onto `main@1a5365b`.\n   - The descriptor-pinned directory walk, `/proc/self/fd/` unlinking, and `dev:ino` identity checks remain intact and unchanged.\n   - `git diff --check` passes cleanly with 0 errors.\n2. **CI Status**:\n   - CodeQL run [40078369339](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40078369339): `✓ SUCCESS`.\n   - Hosted CI run [40078369394](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40078369394): in progress.\n\nNo regressions or security concerns. Ready for merge once CI finishes.\n--\n{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-24T08:57:12Z\"}\n{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-24T08:47:52Z\"}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16cd4-55fc-7d42-952d-a5ba875e9e0d","create_time":1792832373.795023}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
