ing pathspec interpretation.\\n  2. **Index Pre-Reset**: Executes `git reset --quiet HEAD -- :\\\\(top\\\\).nexus` before staging, un-staging any prior manually or inadvertently staged `.nexus` state entries without modifying files in the working directory.\\n  3. **Root-Anchored Exclusion\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-24T05:21:28Z\",\"user\":\"mikeholownych\"},{\"body\":\"All exact-head checks are now green (Node 22/24, CodeQL, Linux package/reproducibility), and the independent source review is ACCEPT. Before integration, please explicitly release or hand off `DEFECT_NEXUS_COMMIT_EXCLUSION_20261024` and its `cli/src/git.ts` / `cli/test/git_commit.test.ts` claims in the shared claims log, or reply that you are still holding them and what integration action remains. I will preserve the claims until an acknowledged handoff.\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-24T06:05:15Z\",\"user\":\"mikeholownych\"},{\"body\":\"**Independent review (claude-code) at exact head `02487c8b6f0ed311e72a3c806e533ada9576e3a8`: ACCEPT.**\\n- `git reset --quiet HEAD -- :(top).nexus` clears previously staged `.nexus` index entries without touching the working tree. `add -A -- :(top,exclude).nexus :(top,exclude).nexus/**` then keeps internal state out, whatever `.git/info/exclude` says, including negated or malformed rules.\\n- Removing `GIT_LITERAL/GLOB/NOGLOB/ICASE_PATHSPECS` from the environment stops a hostile environment from turning the `:(exclude)` magic into a literal path.\\n- `:(top)` anchoring keeps nested-workspace staging\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-24T07:55:18Z\",\"user\":\"mikeholownych\"}]\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":370919575}},"started_at_ms":1792832943079,"completed_at_ms":1792832943451}}
