{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T09:19:22.910Z","ordinal":284450,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16cd4-55fc-7d42-952d-a5ba875e9e0d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-6646addd-0ca4-44af-bba8-cb836415a947","process_id":"31421","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","find docs -iname '*rc.4*' -o -iname '*rc4*' | head -20; rg -n -i 'retention|checkpoint|workspace trust|trust prompt' docs/releases docs/v1.0.0 2>/dev/null | head -80"],"cwd":"file:///tmp/nexus-release-gate-82c5","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"find docs -iname '*rc.4*' -o -iname '*rc4*' | head -20; rg -n -i 'retention|checkpoint|workspace trust|trust prompt' docs/releases docs/v1.0.0 2>/dev/null | head -80"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.3.md:12:- Adds an interactive checkpoint decision when sensitive content cannot be persisted, allowing the user to choose read-only, continue without a rollback checkpoint, create a checkpoint after acknowledging the sensitivity warning, cancel, or revise the instruction. This behavior must be verified from the installed candidate; RC1 and RC2 do not contain it.\ndocs/releases/v0.1.0-alpha.2.md:15:- **No default step or time ceiling.** The 300-step / 120-minute defaults are gone. A turn continues across durable segment checkpoints while it makes progress, and stops on completion, cancellation, demonstrated lack of progress, a failure, or a step/time limit you set explicitly (`--max-total-steps`, `--max-turn-minutes`). Delegated helpers (`spawn_subagent`) no longer take a step allowance; its `max_steps` argument was removed.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:18:- Confines checkpoint handling: checkpoint records are validated and bound to their filenames, their fields are never interpolated into shell commands, and checkpoint restore, prune and retention only delete or copy snapshot directories inside the checkpoint store.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:19:| [DEC-11](#dec-11-retention-defaults) | Retention defaults | 90 days / 2 GB; audit log 10 MB × 5; first GC needs acknowledgement | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:37:| **C (chosen)** | Posture follows workspace trust. **Untrusted workspace → review** for `write_workspace`, `exec`, `egress` and `context_inject`. **Trusted workspace → auto** for `write_workspace` and `exec`; `egress` asks once per origin per session. `--yes` or `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` force auto. `--sandbox` stays available. | Safe for cloned or unknown repos. Low friction on the operator's own repos after one `nexus trust .`. Reuses the existing trust store, so there is no new concept. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:148:## DEC-11: Retention defaults\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:151:- Keep tasks, sessions, checkpoints and flights for 90 days or up to 2 GB in total, whichever limit is hit first. Never remove the current session or pinned sessions.\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:39:  - workspace trust;\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:41:  - checkpoints and undo;\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:119:- **Other stores.** Checkpoints at `~/.nexus/checkpoints` plus `refs/nexus/checkpoints/*`. The audit log at `~/.nexus/audit.log`. Flights at `<ws>/.nexus/flights`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:140:| Tools, security, persistence: `tools, safe_fs, sandbox, security, session, session_export, checkpoint, flight, evidence, git, worktree, mcp, plugins, skills, browser, lsp, file_diff, syntax, diagnostics, workspace_trust`, `core/{authority, resources, durable_file, persistence_protection, capabilities, workspace_path, independent_check, tool_groups}` | 28 | Full read for security-critical files. Grep or skim for session_export, file_diff, syntax, diagnostics, resources, browser, lsp, mcp transports. | C_tools_security_persistence; this file (workspace_trust, workspace_path, tool_groups, independent_check, approval_review, read by lead) | MCP remote transports, browser.ts and lsp.ts got only a skim review: **qualification gap** |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:290:| PER-01 | S2 | RR | State privacy | `checkpoint.ts`, `flight.ts`, … | MEAS | Other users can read code copies and prompts | REQ-PER-101 (SPEC-08) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:291:| PER-02 | S2 | RR | Retention | `state.ts` | MEAS (916 MB, 52,687 files) | Unbounded growth | REQ-PER-102 |\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:5:This release delivers the complete Nexus Code client architecture with comprehensive boundary hardening, process ownership, workspace trust enforcement, and egress protection.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:55:### Workspace Trust: Skills & Knowledge (REQ-SEC-113, REQ-SEC-114)\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:56:- Workspace trust now gates workspace skill directories (`skills/`, `.nexus/skills/`, `.claude/skills/`) and workspace knowledge (`.nexus/knowledge.json`).\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:80:- **New behavior:** Default interactive posture is determined by workspace trust:\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:86:  - `--approve` / `--mode review`: Enforces review posture regardless of workspace trust.\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:212:| REQ-PER-101 | PERS-002 (carried) | `~/.nexus` is 0700 and files are 0600. Doctor repairs both. | privacy on multi-user hosts | `checkpoint.ts`, `flight.ts`, `session.ts`, etc. | MEAS (PER-01) | tested | ACC-PER-01 | RR | PER-01 | SPEC-08 / PLAN-08 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:213:| REQ-PER-102 | Audit; DEC-11 | Retention and GC; audit log rotation; indexed session listing. | resource / failure | new `retention.ts` | MEAS (PER-02: 916 MB) | tested | ACC-PER-02, ACC-PER-06 | RR | PER-02 | SPEC-08 / PLAN-08 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:52:| VER-01 | S2 | Any session on a cloned/untrusted repo, including `--approve` review mode | agent.ts:1602-1617 (baseline), 3432-3436 (oracle), 1630 (independence copy run); tester.ts:113-136 | SOURCE. Before the first file edit (agent.ts:4034, after the edit's own approval) and at every `task_completed`, Nexus runs `make test` / `npm test` / `cargo test` / `pytest` through `bridge.executeTool` directly. These run arbitrary repo-defined code with no approval prompt and no workspace-trust check (unlike MCP/plugins, workspace_trust.ts), and unsandboxed unless `--sandbox`. Review mode shows an approval for `edit_file` but never for the hidden repo script that follows. Builds on SEC-01; it is a separate path because it bypasses even review mode. | Cloning a hostile repo and asking for any edit runs its test script on the host without a prompt. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: gate discovered verifiers on workspace trust or a one-time approval of the exact command (shown with its script body), and run them sandboxed when one is available. Document this. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-08-persistence-hygiene.md:12:- `cli/src/session.ts`, `cli/src/checkpoint.ts`, `cli/src/flight.ts`\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-08-persistence-hygiene.md:16:- new `cli/src/core/retention.ts`\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-08-persistence-hygiene.md:26:| 2 | Add `ensurePrivateDir` and `writePrivateFile`/`appendPrivateFile`, then route every writer under `~/.nexus` and `~/.nexus_history` through them. Add a grep test that forbids raw fs writes in these modules. | `durable_file.ts`; `checkpoint.ts:31,47,61,183`; `flight.ts:57,101`; `persistence_protection.ts:131-147`; `session.ts:41`; `state.ts:290`; `repl.ts` (history); `knowledge.ts`; the receipts writer | 1 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-08-persistence-hygiene.md:28:| 4 | Retention (`retention.ts`): age and size policy, applied across tasks, sessions, checkpoints (including `refs/nexus/checkpoints/*`) and flights. `nexus gc [--dry-run]`. Background daily GC, bounded to 2 s, with first-run acknowledgement (DEC-11). | new module; `index.ts`; `checkpoint.ts` (ref pruning via `git update-ref -d`) | 2 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-08-persistence-hygiene.md:51:| ACC-PER-02 | `retention.test.ts`, with seeded records and a session-listing time budget |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:34:| REQ-AGT-29 | CTX-001 | Every injected context item carries provenance+classification metadata | P2 §12 | **PARTIALLY_DEMONSTRATED_BLOCKING** (Issue #12 closure blocker) | Y (final closure review) | Still open per CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST_CRITICAL_PATH_ASSESSMENT.md:42 and cloudflare/OVERNIGHT_CHECKPOINT.md:54; no later closure found |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:42:| REQ-SEC-39 | PERS-001 | Distinguish volatile/durable/outbound/export/retention/deletion/recovery | P2 §18 | DEMONSTRATED | P | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:43:| REQ-SEC-40 | PERS-002 | No unredacted durable copies (sessions, flights, audit, checkpoints, caches, crash) | P2 §18 | Blocker at a4f3e16 → **operator-accepted with bounded envelope** (typed WorkspacePath rule; legacy identity-sensitive files remain plaintext) a2d3051/5774a1a | Y (PERS002_INDEPENDENT_QUALIFICATION) | 10-12 T-08/T10: plaintext in sessions, diffs, audit, task state, flight log — regression vs accepted claim; MCP config not covered (qual Q17) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:83:| REQ-DX-03 | Manual feature promises | 24 native tools (incl. LSP, trigram, CST); `--sandbox` bwrap/Docker; `--dry-run`, `--read-only`; plugin worker-thread sandbox with memory caps; SSRF guard; audit log; checkpoints/`/undo`; hot reload; failover `--fallback` | USER_MANUAL.md §3–4 | All 24 tool names present in core/capabilities.ts (SOURCE). **Worker-thread plugin sandbox claim false at HEAD** (see HIST-03) | N |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:95:| docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST_CRITICAL_PATH_ASSESSMENT.md, docs/cloudflare/OVERNIGHT_CHECKPOINT.md | targeted (blocker status lines) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:237:- **Supported workflows:** interactive Ratatui TUI (`nexus`), REPL (`nexus repl`, `--approve`), headless `nexus run` with JSON/exit codes (0 verified, 2 REGRESSION_FREE), resume (`-r`, `/resume`), `nexus doctor`, `nexus trust`, providers/connect, `/team` and `nexus operation` durable multi-unit work, checkpoints/undo, MCP client + `serve-mcp`, skills/plugins, eval.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:15:| cli/src/checkpoint.ts | targeted 20-70, 125-200 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:43:  - Checkpoints: `~/.nexus/checkpoints/<hash>/`, writeFileSync with default mode, plus git refs `refs/nexus/checkpoints/*`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:53:| SEC-05 | S2 | untrusted repo opened | skills.ts:31-33; agent.ts:3301,3789 | SOURCE. Workspace skills (SKILL.md) are loaded and advertised in the system prompt with no workspace-trust check, unlike MCP and plugins (workspace_trust.ts:5-24). `activate_skill` is non-mutating, so it is never approved. | Persistent prompt injection from a cloned repo. Combined with SEC-01 this gives command execution. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: gate workspace skill directories on workspace trust, or show them as untrusted and require approval to activate. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:59:| SEC-11 | S4 | git tools | git_ops.rs (git2) | SOURCE. git_status/diff/log use libgit2, with no shell and no external diff/fsmonitor drivers. Good. `checkpoint.ts:142-145` interpolates an internally generated id into a shell string (safe today). | none | Note |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:60:| PER-01 | S2 | persistence permissions | checkpoint.ts:31,47,61,183; flight.ts:57,101; persistence_protection.ts:131-147; session.ts:41; state.ts:290 | RUNTIME (operator's real `~/.nexus`). Checkpoint and flight dirs/files, `audit.log`, `~/.nexus_history` and knowledge are created with default umask modes. Measured: `~/.nexus` 775, `checkpoints/` 775 with 1604 files o+r (fallback snapshots copy workspace file contents), `audit.log` 664, `~/.nexus_history` 664, 1233 of 1277 session JSONs 664 (inside a 700 dir). Only `writeFileDurably` uses 0600. | On multi-user hosts, other local users can read prompts, history, audit and checkpoint copies of code. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: create ~/.nexus with 0700 and every file with 0600. Have `doctor --fix` tighten existing files. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:61:| PER-02 | S2 | retention | state.ts (no pruning); ~/.nexus | MEASUREMENT. No retention or rotation anywhere: `tasks/` 52,687 files / 916 MB, `sessions/` 1332 files / 66 MB, `checkpoints/` 8104 dirs, `audit.log` 27 MB (doc: \"permanently recorded\"), git refs `refs/nexus/checkpoints/*` never pruned. | Unbounded disk growth. listSessions reads and parses every file on each call (session.ts:211-239), so it slows down. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: retention policy plus `nexus gc`, audit rotation, and an index for listing. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:63:| PER-04 | S3 | crash durability | durable_file.ts:49-62; file_ops.rs:101-188 | SOURCE. Routine saves outside `withDurableSync` skip fsync (documented trade-off). The Rust atomic write fsyncs the file but never fsyncs the parent dir after rename. Checkpoint metadata, flight logs and `writeProtectedTextFile` have no fsync. | After power loss, a recent edit or checkpoint can be lost. A torn file is not possible (rename). | POST-V1, except add a dir fsync in Rust (cheap). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:108:~/.nexus 775; audit.log 664 27M; checkpoints 775, 1604 files o+r, 8104 dirs; tasks 52,687 files 916M (52,660 task-*, workspacePath /tmp/nexus-app-test-*/repo); sessions 1233x664 + 44x600; ~/.nexus_history 664; ~/.config/nexus 775 (config.env 600, mcp.json 664)\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:136:| R-SEC-5 | Workspace skills are subject to workspace trust. | safety | RELEASE-REQUIRED | An untrusted fixture repo with `skills/x/SKILL.md` does not appear in the system prompt or `/skills` without trust. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:140:| R-PER-1 | `~/.nexus` 0700. All persisted files (sessions, tasks, checkpoints, audit, history, flights, knowledge) 0600. `doctor --fix` repairs existing ones. | safety | RELEASE-REQUIRED | Under umask 002, a run then `find ~/.nexus ~/.nexus_history -perm /077` is empty. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:141:| R-PER-2 | Retention and GC for tasks, sessions, checkpoints (incl. git refs) and audit rotation, with a configurable cap. | failure | RELEASE-REQUIRED | Seed 10k records. `nexus gc` (or automatic) brings them under the cap. Listing 1k sessions takes under 500 ms. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md:32:| 8 | Wrap `runTurn` and build an `UNHANDLED_ERROR` result in-agent; final checkpoint; cancel the steering and compaction queues with notices. | `agent.ts:4254-4995`; `turn.ts:444-460`; `app.ts:229` | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md:75:| `ARCHITECTURE.md` | Remove homelab hardware and port 18010. Name the Rust TUI and the sidecar. Rewrite §3 as \"controls and their limits\". Remove \"permanently recorded\" or match it to retention. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md:1:# SPEC-08: Persistence hygiene, including permissions, retention and corruption reporting\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md:5:| Status | Ready. Retention defaults per [DEC-11](../DECISIONS.md#dec-11-retention-defaults). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md:19:| Checkpoints | 1,604 world-readable checkpoint files: copies of workspace code (`checkpoint.ts:31,47,61,183`) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md:30:| Checkpoint directories | 8,104 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md:32:| `refs/nexus/checkpoints/*` | never pruned |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md:46:1. **REQ-PER-101.** `~/.nexus` and every subdirectory Nexus creates are 0700. Every file Nexus writes is 0600 (sessions, tasks, checkpoints, audit, history, flights, knowledge, receipts), regardless of umask. `nexus doctor --fix` tightens existing files with a confirmed, backed-up, idempotent repair.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md:47:2. **REQ-PER-102.** Retention:\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md:48:   - A configurable cap governs tasks, sessions, checkpoints (including the git refs) and flights. The default is proposed in DEC-11: 90 days or 2 GB, whichever is first, and never the current or pinned sessions.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md:67:- Add a single `ensurePrivateDir(path)` and `writePrivateFile(path, data, { durable })` in `cli/src/core/durable_file.ts`. Replace every direct `fs.writeFileSync`, `appendFileSync` and `mkdirSync` under `~/.nexus` with these: `checkpoint.ts`, `flight.ts`, `persistence_protection.ts:131-147`, `session.ts:41`, `state.ts:290`, the REPL history, `knowledge.ts`, and the receipts writer. Enforce this with a lint rule or a grep test that forbids `fs.writeFileSync(` in those modules.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md:68:- Retention lives in `cli/src/core/retention.ts`. Index sessions with a small `sessions/index.json` (id, updatedAt, workspace, title), rebuilt when it is missing or stale, so that listing does not parse every file.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md:82:| ACC-PER-01 | Under `umask 002`, run one scripted turn, a checkpoint and `/undo`. Then `find $HOME/.nexus $HOME/.nexus_history -perm /077` is empty. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md:92:- DEC-11 (retention defaults).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:29:| **M4 Persistence hygiene** (parallel with M2/M3) | PLAN-08 tasks 2–10 | Private state permissions, retention/GC, corruption reporting, schema policy | **G4**: ACC-PER-01..07 | 5–8 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:32:- Default turn has **no cumulative step ceiling**: `maxSteps`=30 is a segment (durable checkpoint) only (agent.ts:4379-4381, 4435). Confirmed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:45:| AGT-02 | S2 | `/team`, `nexus operation run/resume` (work units) | agent.ts:3081 (`durableUnit = this.depth === 0`), 3127, 1136-1139, 4389, 1489-1501; operation_runner.ts:559 | SOURCE + DOC-CLAIM. Work units run as `new AutonomousAgent(config, 1)` and ARE durable (resumed via `recoverFromTaskState`), but every depth-gated rule treats depth 1 as a non-durable in-turn subagent: (a) compaction is applied in memory only — no archive append, no checkpoint, never `PERSISTENCE_FAILED`; the next `persistProgress` then writes the compacted conversation and a `committedCompactions` id that has no archive lines, so originals are lost and `read_archive` cannot return them after resume (contradicts COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:145-160 \"Every compaction ... is committed in a fixed order\"); (b) no objective ledger: no requirement gating, no steering, `update_requirements`/`read_objective` not offered; (c) `ExecutionTracker.fresh()` per turn, so loop/stagnation history and cumulative steps reset at every resume/retry; (d) no change baseline / independence judgement (`captureChangeBaseline` depth 0 only, 4034) so discovered-verifier passes are at best REGRESSION_FREE. `runningAsSubagent` already distinguishes the two cases (5003). | Long team/operation units lose compaction originals and convergence history across resume; doc claims overstate durability. | Gate on `runningAsSubagent` (non-durable) instead of `depth`; add a work-unit compaction+resume test asserting archive lines exist. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:51:| AGT-08 | S3 | Unhandled errors in a turn | agent.ts:4570, 4655-4657, 4992; turn.ts:444-460; app.ts:229 | SOURCE. Non-`ContextBudgetError`/`InferenceError` exceptions in admission, and any `ContextBudgetError` surfacing from inference, are rethrown out of `runTurn`: no final checkpoint/ledger outcome, queued steering never reported cancelled (observer left hanging), queued /compact never reported. `failedTurnFromError` hard-codes `unverifiedChangesPending: false` and `steps.used: 0`. | A crash-type turn can report \"no pending changes\" while the workspace holds unverified edits. | Wrap loop body: build a FAILED/UNHANDLED_ERROR result in-agent with real obligation, cancel steering/compaction queues. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:57:| AGT-14 | S4 | Swallowed durable-write errors | agent.ts:4022-4032, 4051-4058, 3836-3840, 3853-3867, 4240-4243, 1182-1185 | SOURCE. `recordOperationStart/End`, plan/requirements checkpoints, provider-recovery checkpoints `catch {}` silently (unlike `persistProgress`, which reports once). Failure of `recordOperationStart` removes crash detection of an in-flight tool without telling anyone. | Recovery may miss an interrupted tool. | Route through the same reported-failure path. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:79:- No default cumulative step ceiling: `DEFAULT_CONTINUATION.maxTotalSteps/maxTurnMinutes = +Infinity` (types.ts:127-133); `maxSteps` is a segment/checkpoint (agent.ts:4379-4381, 4435-4445). Step-position notices only appear under an operator-set limit (`stepPosition`, 766; `stepNotedContent` 2932-2933). Subagents have no step allowance; model-supplied `max_steps` ignored (3584-3585). Recovery/iteration bounds that remain (provider `maxIterations` 1000, operation runner 10 000, compaction attempts 5) are resource-safety valves with explicit reasons, not completion substitutes.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:110:| AGT-R6 | Any exception escaping the loop yields an agent-built FAILED/UNHANDLED_ERROR TurnResult with the true `unverifiedChangesPending`, final checkpoint, and cancelled steering/compaction notifications. | safety/failure (AGT-08) | RELEASE-REQUIRED | Inject a throwing `admitContext` after a write; assert pending=true and onSteering cancelled. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:112:| AGT-R8 | No implicit standing rules from prompts; no workspace writes in read-only mode; workspace-supplied knowledge gated by workspace trust. | safety (AGT-10) | RELEASE-REQUIRED | Read-only run leaves no `.nexus/`; prompt \"never run tests\" does not appear in next session's system prompt. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md:58:| AGT-14 | Durable-write failures for op start/end, plan and recovery checkpoints are swallowed. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md:72:6. **REQ-AGT-106.** Any exception escaping the loop produces an agent-built `FAILED / UNHANDLED_ERROR` result. That result carries the true pending-change obligation and step count, a final checkpoint, and cancellation notices for queued steering and `/compact`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md:107:2. Attempt a final checkpoint. Failure here is reported, not thrown.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:1:# v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:9:**RC3, checkpoint choice, and Doctor:** RC3 remains the latest published prerelease, tagged at `1b9791f07d301c885fe48f04a796203583ab5a5c`; its archive digest and provenance are recorded in the snapshot below. The operator's `Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to checkpoint` failure occurred on immutable RC1, which predates the interactive choice flow. RC3 source contains the five choices: read-only, continue in the configured mode without a rollback checkpoint, create a checkpoint with the sensitivity risk acknowledged, cancel, or re-enter the instruction. Current RC3 source also scans saved-state metadata asynchronously in bounded batches, accepts schema-2 task `messageLog` records, and treats a configured model absent from `/models` as unverified rather than unavailable; a `--deep` inference probe can verify it. The interrupted-write temporary file reported by Doctor is a separate real warning and is not automatically repaired. These source checks and existing tests do not substitute for exercising the exact installed candidate on the operator's own state.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:23:**Installed-candidate and checkpoint-choice observation:** The published installer completed with `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1` and installed RC3 under `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.3`; installer provenance records the exact archive digest and source revision. `/home/mike/.local/bin/nexus --version` reports `1.0.0-rc.3 (1b9791f07d30)`. The previous RC1 directory remains installed at `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.1` for rollback. The coordinator reported an automated PTY probe of the installed default TUI using a synthetic Git workspace, fake credential-shaped canary, and unreachable loopback endpoint. The reported probe displayed the five choices and selected cancel before inference. Its transcript/capture was not retained in the release evidence tree, so this observation is unarchived and was not independently verified in the readiness review. It is diagnostic context only: it does not establish the checkpoint-choice gate, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, or provider/task qualification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:35:**Checkpoint failure:** `/home/mike/.local/bin/nexus` resolves to the installed `v1.0.0-rc.1` package and reports `1.0.0-rc.1 (cb364c386c42)`. That immutable package lacks checkpoint choices, so the reported failure before turn start is reproducible by version identity and will persist on RC1. The fix is integrated in PR #147 (TUI/sidecar) and PR #153 (legacy REPL): before starting a turn, Nexus asks the operator whether to use read-only mode, continue in the configured mode without a rollback checkpoint, create the checkpoint with the sensitive-content risk acknowledged, cancel, or enter a different instruction. Both PRs passed exact-head checks, and the subsequent exact-main CI on `dac465d` passed. No replacement package has been installed. The public release page still has RC1 only; RC2 has a tag but no published release, and RC3 has neither tag nor release.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:43:**Authoritative release source:** `origin/main` is `1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145`, the PR #155 merge commit. PRs #153, #154, and #155 are merged. PR #153 integrated the checkpoint-choice flow; PR #154 refreshed readiness and the terminal worksheet; PR #155 fixed the remaining doctor integrity-scan timeout by batching metadata checks. PR #155 exact-head CI `39893335185`, CodeQL `39893335167`, and independent review passed on head `76b34f1d18d766b06011176a85679e7c3434ba30`. Current-main CI run [39896372677](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39896372677) completed successfully on exact `1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145`: Node 24 at 03:56:55Z, Node 22 at 03:57:48Z, and Linux x86-64 packaging/reproducibility/package-smoke/installer-smoke at 04:11:34Z. Its Linux job validated identical package archives, checksums, notices, SBOM and installer across two builds. Current-main CodeQL run [39896372726](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39896372726) completed successfully at 03:43:55Z on that same SHA. CI’s Linux package used existing `1.0.0-rc.2` version metadata; it is source CI evidence, not an immutable RC3 artifact or qualification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:49:**Checkpoint failure and remediation:** The operator reports every launch attempt on installed RC1 fails before the turn starts with `Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to checkpoint`. This is confirmed as an RC1 limitation: immutable RC1 source predates the checkpoint-choice flow. PR #153 integrates that flow in current main, offering read-only, continue without a rollback checkpoint, create the checkpoint despite sensitive content, cancel, or re-enter the instruction. This is source-integrated behavior only; the installed candidate must exercise the prompt and selected actions before acceptance. RC1 and RC2 remain unchanged and do not contain this behavior.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:53:**RC identity and publication:** Remote immutable tags remain `v1.0.0-rc.1` at `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779` and `v1.0.0-rc.2` at `19d6f0a80e21f9b640a46ee12200c4f5f6d967a4`; both predate the accepted Node 22 floor and checkpoint-choice fix. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passes at exact main and reports all components at `1.0.0-rc.2`. No accepted RC or stable v1.0.0 tag/release is established. A new candidate must use the next RC identity after source CI and release prerequisites pass, then undergo installed-artifact qualification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:55:**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open; the latest custodian metadata request has no response in the available checkpoint, so T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T2/T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:57:## Historical integration checkpoint (observed 2026-10-23 02:13 UTC at `fa16045`; superseded by the current status above)\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:59:**Authoritative release source:** `origin/main` was `fa16045a6351ce61763bc3fcc93b562c50849285`, the merge of PR #152. PR #152 carried the readiness checkpoint refresh and terminal worksheet wording separating the §5.3 disposition gate from `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`; its exact head `deaf56fdb074df3f5cd3b62d50f811a2f14ca101` passed Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 package/repro/install-smoke CI in run `39881805268`; CodeQL `39881805274` passed. The independent reviewer accepted that exact head. Post-merge CI run `39885102002` passed Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 packaging/reproducibility/smoke/install; post-merge CodeQL `39885101945` passed. These checks are bound to exact main `fa16045`. Retained post-merge check summary: [CI and CodeQL result](../reviews/evidence/v1/plan10-readiness-post152/post-merge-ci-main-fa16045.txt).\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:65:**Checkpoint failure and remediation:** The operator reports that every attempt to start Nexus RC1 fails with `Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to checkpoint`. This is consistent with RC1's exact source predating PR #147's checkpoint-choice flow. PR #147 is integrated in current main and its exact-head CI and CodeQL passed; the interactive TUI now offers read-only, continue without a rollback checkpoint, create the checkpoint anyway with a sensitivity warning, cancel, or re-enter the instruction. RC1 and RC2 are immutable and do not contain this behavior. The next candidate must include the fix, and the installed candidate must be exercised to verify the choices before any acceptance claim.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:85:## Historical release checkpoint (2026-10-22 09:32 UTC; superseded by the integration update above)\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":792223069}},"started_at_ms":1792833562117,"completed_at_ms":1792833562910}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T09:19:23.919Z","ordinal":284451,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a16d35-2d0f-7031-9274-3e94302fc83d","call_id":"call_25f496d92c3d44259265b86be27cf3b4","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 7497)\nTotal output lines: 81\n\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.3.md:12:- Adds an interactive checkpoint decision when sensitive content cannot be persisted, allowing the user to choose read-only, continue without a rollback checkpoint, create a checkpoint after acknowledging the sensitivity warning, cancel, or revise the instruction. This behavior must be verified from the installed candidate; RC1 and RC2 do not contain it.\ndocs/releases/v0.1.0-alpha.2.md:15:- **No default step or time ceiling.** The 300-step / 120-minute defaults are gone. A turn continues across durable segment checkpoints while it makes progress, and stops on completion, cancellation, demonstrated lack of progress, a failure, or a step/time limit you set explicitly (`--max-total-steps`, `--max-turn-minutes`). Delegated helpers (`spawn_subagent`) no longer take a step allowance; its `max_steps` argument was removed.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:18:- Confines checkpoint handling: checkpoint records are validated and bound to their filenames, their fields are never interpolated into shell commands, and checkpoint restore, prune and retention only delete or copy snapshot directories inside the checkpoint store.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:19:| [DEC-11](#dec-11-retention-defaults) | Retention defaults | 90 days / 2 GB; audit log 10 MB × 5; first GC needs acknowledgement | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:37:| **C (chosen)** | Posture follows workspace trust. **Untrusted workspace → review** for `write_workspace`, `exec`, `egress` and `context_inject`. **Trusted workspace → auto** for `write_workspace` and `exec`; `egress` asks once per origin per session. `--yes` or `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` force auto. `--sandbox` stays available. | Safe for cloned or unknown repos. Low friction on the operator's own repos after one `nexus trust .`. Reuses the existing trust store, so there is no new concept. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:148:## DEC-11: Retention defaults\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:151:- Keep tasks, sessions, checkpoints and flights for 90 days or up to 2 GB in total, whichever limit is hit first. Never remove the current session or pinned sessions.\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:39:  - workspace trust;\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:41:  - checkpoints and undo;\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:119:- **Other stores.** Checkpoints at `~/.nexus/checkpoints` plus `refs/nexus/checkpoints/*`. The audit log at `~/.nexus/audit.log`. Flights at `<ws>/.nexus/flights`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:140:| Tools, security, persistence: `tools, safe_fs, sandbox, security, session, session_export, checkpoint, flight, evidence, git, worktree, mcp, plugins, skills, browser, lsp, file_diff, syntax, diagnostics, workspace_trust`, `core/{authority, resources, durable_file, persistence_protection, capabilities, workspace_path, independent_check, tool_groups}` | 28 | Full read for security-critical files. Grep or skim for session_export, file_diff, syntax, diagnostics, resources, browser, lsp, mcp transports. | C_tools_security_persistence; this file (workspace_trust, workspace_path, tool_groups, independent_check, approval_review, read by lead) | MCP remote transports, browser.ts and lsp.ts got only a skim review: **qualification gap** |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:290:| PER-01 | S2 | RR | State privacy | `checkpoint.ts`, `flight.ts`, … | MEAS | Other users can read code copies and prompts | REQ-PER-101 (SPEC-08) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:291:| PER-02 | S2 | RR | Retention | `state.ts` | MEAS (916 MB, 52,687 files) | Unbounded growth | REQ-PER-102 |\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:5:This release delivers the complete Nexus Code client architecture with comprehensive boundary hardening, process ownership, workspace trust enforcement, and egress protection.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:55:### Workspace Trust: Skills & Knowledge (REQ-SEC-113, REQ-SEC-114)\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:56:- Workspace trust now gates workspace skill directories (`skills/`, `.nexus/skills/`, `.claude/skills/`) and workspace knowledge (`.nexus/knowledge.json`).\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:80:- **New behavior:** Default interactive posture is determined by workspace trust:\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:86:  - `--approve` / `--mode review`: Enforces review posture regardless of workspace trust.\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:212:| REQ-PER-101 | PERS-002 (carried) | `~/.nexus` is 0700 and files are 0600. Doctor repairs both. | privacy on multi-user hosts | `checkpoint.ts`, `flight.ts`, `session.ts`, etc. | MEAS (PER-01) | tested | ACC-PER-01 | RR | PER-01 | SPEC-08 / PLAN-08 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:213:| REQ-PER-102 | Audit; DEC-11 | Retention and GC; audit log rotation; indexed session listing. | resource / failure | new `retention.ts` | MEAS (PER-02: 916 MB) | tested | ACC-PER-02, ACC-PER-06 | RR | PER-02 | SPEC-08 / PLAN-08 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:52:| VER-01 | S2 | Any session on a cloned/untrusted repo, including `--approve` review mode | agent.ts:1602-1617 (baseline), 3432-3436 (oracle), 1630 (independence copy run); tester.ts:113-136 | SOURCE. Before the first file edit (agent.ts:4034, after the edit's own approval) and at every `task_completed`, Nexus runs `make test` / `npm test` / `cargo test` / `pytest` through `bridge.executeTool` directly. These run arbitrary repo-defined code with no approval prompt and no workspace-trust check (unlike MCP/plugins, workspace_trust.ts), and unsandboxed unless `--sandbox`. Review mode shows an approval for `edit_file` but never for the hidden repo script that follows. Builds on SEC-01; it is a separate path because it bypasses even review mode. | Cloning a hostile repo and asking for any edit runs its test script on the host without a prompt. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: gate discovered verifiers on workspace trust or a one-time approval of the exact command (shown with its script body), and run them sandboxed when one is available. Document this. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-08-persistence-hygiene.md:12:- `cli/src/session.ts`, `cli/src/checkpoint.ts`, `cli/src/flight.ts`\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-08-persiste…4497 tokens truncated…v1.0.0/READINESS.md:35:**Checkpoint failure:** `/home/mike/.local/bin/nexus` resolves to the installed `v1.0.0-rc.1` package and reports `1.0.0-rc.1 (cb364c386c42)`. That immutable package lacks checkpoint choices, so the reported failure before turn start is reproducible by version identity and will persist on RC1. The fix is integrated in PR #147 (TUI/sidecar) and PR #153 (legacy REPL): before starting a turn, Nexus asks the operator whether to use read-only mode, continue in the configured mode without a rollback checkpoint, create the checkpoint with the sensitive-content risk acknowledged, cancel, or enter a different instruction. Both PRs passed exact-head checks, and the subsequent exact-main CI on `dac465d` passed. No replacement package has been installed. The public release page still has RC1 only; RC2 has a tag but no published release, and RC3 has neither tag nor release.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:43:**Authoritative release source:** `origin/main` is `1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145`, the PR #155 merge commit. PRs #153, #154, and #155 are merged. PR #153 integrated the checkpoint-choice flow; PR #154 refreshed readiness and the terminal worksheet; PR #155 fixed the remaining doctor integrity-scan timeout by batching metadata checks. PR #155 exact-head CI `39893335185`, CodeQL `39893335167`, and independent review passed on head `76b34f1d18d766b06011176a85679e7c3434ba30`. Current-main CI run [39896372677](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39896372677) completed succes