torical snapshots and do not claim acceptance.\",\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_READINESS.md/owner.json:12:  \"status\": \"local_commit_reviewed_ACCEPT_pending_owner_PR_integration\",\n{\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\n- Add an interactive startup trust chooser before the REPL or TUI starts in an untrusted workspace.\\n- Offer **Trust and continue**, **Continue without trusting**, and **Exit**. Trust persists through the existing trust store; continuing untrusted does not change the configured permission mode.\\n- Load project instruction files only after explicit workspace trust. Non-interactive launches never grant trust implicitly and continue under the existing untrusted-workspace behavior.\\n- Sanitize terminal control and Unicode format characters in displayed paths and fit text by grapheme display-cell width.\\n- Document the startup behavior and add prompt, trust persistence, failure, non-TTY, prompt ordering behavior, and path display regressions.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- Focused startup/workspace trust tests: 16/16 passed on the committed source.\\n- `npm run build`: passed.\\n- Independent read-only source review: ACCEPT on the exact reviewed diff.\\n- A full CLI `npm test` attempt ran in an isolated snapshot under the suite claim but did not complete. It reported failures across engine-backed, continuity, qualification, and packaged-entrypoint tests; this local attempt omitted the CI job's built Rust binaries and qualification host setup. It is not passing evidence. Exact-head CI is running on this PR.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nThis implements the startup folder-trust interaction shown by the operator. It does not change release acceptance status; RC and release qualification remain separate gates.\\n\",\"files\":[\"cli/src/agent.ts\",\"cli/src/index.ts\",\"cli/src/startup_trust.ts\",\"cli/test/harness_entry.test.ts\",\"cli/test/helpers/fixtures.ts\",\"cli/test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts\",\"cli/test/startup_trust_prompt.test.ts\",\"cli/te