{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T09:57:46.506Z","ordinal":285395,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16cd4-55fc-7d42-952d-a5ba875e9e0d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-5436ce80-d8a5-4a25-a751-9fa41c97376e","process_id":"90720","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 186 --json state,headRefOid,baseRefOid,mergeStateStatus,reviewDecision,url,comments --jq '{state,headRefOid,baseRefOid,mergeStateStatus,reviewDecision,url,comments:[.comments[]|{author:.author.login,createdAt,body}]}' && gh pr checks 186"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 186 --json state,headRefOid,baseRefOid,mergeStateStatus,reviewDecision,url,comments --jq '{state,headRefOid,baseRefOid,mergeStateStatus,reviewDecision,url,comments:[.comments[]|{author:.author.login,createdAt,body}]}' && gh pr checks 186"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"baseRefOid\":\"82c5c3c823f861fa3ac40a9ba42c9918f301d947\",\"comments\":[{\"author\":\"coderabbitai\",\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- This is an auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003e [!IMPORTANT]\\n\\u003e - [ ] \\u003c!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"e9bb8d72-00e8-4f67-9cb2-caf3b22574fe\\\"} --\\u003e 🔍 Trigger review\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e This repository does not receive automatic reviews because it has fewer than 10 stars.\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003csummary\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog-dark.svg\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog.svg\\\" width=\\\"16\\\" height=\\\"16\\\" align=\\\"absmiddle\\\" alt=\\\"\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e Run configuration\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003cdl\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003cdd\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e - **Source mode**: Auto\\n\\u003e - **Repository**: Unavailable\\n\\u003e - **Branch**: Unavailable\\n\\u003e - **File**: No configuration file from this repository applied\\n\\u003e - **Commit**: Unavailable\\n\\u003e - **Layers**: defaults\\n\\u003e - **Review profile**: CHILL\\n\\u003e - **Plan**: Advanced\\n\\u003e - **Run ID**: `6062b65f-f396-45da-abf5-28f9c33476e3`\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003c/dd\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003c/dl\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- end of auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- autopilot:start --\\u003e\\n- [ ] \\u003c!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"2708ad07-9f24-4260-9c11-7dc76a49f2e3\\\"} --\\u003e \\u003cstrong title=\\\"Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\\"\\u003eAutofix\\u003c/strong\\u003e · Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\n\\u003c!-- autopilot:end --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- tips_start --\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\nThanks for using [CodeRabbit](https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=oss\\u0026utm_medium=github\\u0026utm_campaign=mikeholownych/nexus-code\\u0026utm_content=186)! It's free for OSS, and your support helps us grow. If you like it, consider giving us a shout-out.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003e❤️ Share\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\u003cdl\\u003e\\n\\u003cdd\\u003e\\n\\n- [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A\\u0026url=https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [Mastodon](https://mastodon.social/share?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai)\\n- [Reddit](https://www.reddit.com/submit?title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit\\u0026text=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai\\u0026mini=true\\u0026title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit\\u0026summary=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code)\\n\\n\\u003c/dd\\u003e\\n\\u003c/dl\\u003e\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\u003csub\\u003eComment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands.\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- tips_end --\\u003e\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T05:53:18Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"### Independent Review: CHANGES_REQUESTED\\n\\n**Target commit**: `f4d40cdc5c4cf1196b7beb88f51953d721a370a8`  \\n**Base commit**: `fc681d806d7698d6a05107a16141677e728f6163` (origin/main)  \\n**CI Run**: [40074046981](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40074046981) (`test-matrix (22)` and `test-matrix (24)` failed)\\n\\n#### Finding: Interactive PTY Tests Hang at Startup Trust Prompt\\nThe implementation of `promptWorkspaceTrust` displays an interactive prompt whenever `input.isTTY \\u0026\\u0026 output.isTTY` in an untrusted workspace. While `cli/test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts` was updated with `trustWorkspace(home, repo)`, `cli/test/turn_semantics.test.ts` was not updated.\\n\\nAs a result, the `interactive REPL (pty)` subtests run under `util-linux script` (which provides pseudo-terminal TTY streams), encounter the trust prompt, and hang waiting for user input, causing a 30s timeout failure:\\n\\n1. `cli/test/turn_semantics.test.ts:708`: `Ctrl-C during a delayed mutating trajectory: one interrupt, no new mutation, prompt returns, next turn works`\\n```\\nError: timeout waiting for /❯ /; output tail: \\nTrust this folder?\\n↑↓ navigate · Enter select · Esc exit\\n/tmp/nexus-turn-...\\nLoad project instructions\\n…\\n› Trust and continue\\n  Continue without trusting\\n  Exit\\n```\\n2. `cli/test/turn_semantics.test.ts:751`: `multiple prompts in one session keep working; Ctrl-C at idle still exits deliberately`\\n(Fails with identical timeout waiting for `/❯ /` at the trust prompt).\\n\\n#### Recommended Resolution\\nIn `cli/test/turn_semantics.test.ts`, import `trustWorkspace` from `./helpers/fixtures.js` and ensure the workspace is trusted before launching the REPL in the `session` helper:\\n```ts\\nimport { startGateway, makeRepo, makeHome, Reply, ptyTest, trustWorkspace } from \\\"./helpers/fixtures.js\\\";\\n// ...\\nasync function session(gw: Gateway, repo: string, home: string) {\\n  trustWorkspace(home, repo);\\n  const cmd = ...\\n```\\nOnce updated and rebased, exact-head CI should be re-run.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T07:42:55Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"### Independent Review: ACCEPT\\n\\n**Target commit**: `fb70052e19340caa7a050f98c0392785df525a07`  \\n**Base commit**: `fc681d806d7698d6a05107a16141677e728f6163` (origin/main)  \\n**Files changed**: 11 files (+606, -8)\\n\\n#### Verification \\u0026 Assessment\\n1. **Resolution of CHANGES_REQUESTED Finding**:\\n   - `cli/test/turn_semantics.test.ts` has been updated with `NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE: \\\"1\\\"` in the PTY `session` helper environment, allowing the turn semantics test suite to run in the pseudo-terminal without being blocked at the interactive startup trust prompt.\\n   - Verified that `cli/src/workspace_trust.ts` supports `NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE === \\\"1\\\"` to return true for `isWorkspaceTrusted()`.\\n2. **Interactive Trust \\u0026 Sanitization Implementation**:\\n   - Non-interactive launches fail closed to untrusted mode and emit a notice without blocking.\\n   - Interactive TTY prompt provides clean navigation and choices: \\\"Trust and continue\\\", \\\"Continue without trusting\\\", \\\"Exit\\\".\\n   - Project instructions (`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `CODEX.md`, `.nexusrules`) are gated on explicit workspace trust via `trustedProjectRules`.\\n   - Control characters and Unicode format characters in display paths are safely sanitized with grapheme cell-width fitting.\\n3. **Hygiene \\u0026 Verification**:\\n   - `git diff --check` passes cleanly with 0 errors.\\n   - CodeQL run [40075233603](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40075233603): `✓ SUCCESS`.\\n   - Hosted CI run [40075233633](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40075233633): in progress.\\n\\nNo regressions or security concerns. Recommended for merge once CI completes.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T07:46:42Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"### Independent Review: ACCEPT\\n\\n**Target commit**: `c34d2ba559dd9b1efddb6efd80fcb26e637c741a`  \\n**Base commit**: `1a5365b11e99c49e835740438fd70937c310cd0e` (origin/main)  \\n**Files changed**: 12 files (+608, -8)\\n\\n#### Verification \\u0026 Assessment\\n1. **Package Smoke PTY Resolution**:\\n   - In `scripts/package-smoke-pty.py`, sets `os.environ[\\\"NEXUS_TRUST_WORKSPACE\\\"] = \\\"1\\\"` in the slave PTY environment before launching the packaged TUI, correctly bypassing the startup interactive trust chooser during package smoke validation.\\n2. **Rebase \\u0026 Invariants**:\\n   - Cleanly rebased onto `main@1a5365b`.\\n   - `git diff --check` passes with 0 errors.\\n   - CodeQL run [40077862158](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40077862158): `✓ SUCCESS`.\\n   - Hosted