{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T11:13:27.803Z","ordinal":287187,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a16d9d-9afb-7432-a3fb-46868d36ea3b","call_id":"call_5706215722e944ceba608b4bf93b35f3","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.8 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 3038)\nTotal output lines: 33\n\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:51:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:159:## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:192:Terminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:1:# Manual real-terminal acceptance worksheet\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:3:For `REQ-QUAL-108` / `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`, following [`ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3](ACCEPTANCE.md#53-manual-real-terminal-matrix-e3). This is an unfilled recording template; it contains no test results and does not qualify an RC.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:49:| 1 | xterm | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:52:| 4 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:55:| 7 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:58:| 10 | VS Code integrated terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:61:| 13 | GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:13:**Human terminal matrix:** The required environments remain xterm, kitty with keyboard protocol, tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal, and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14, and 200×60, with the two required screenshots for each cell. This coordination session is on `mike-dev`, an Ubuntu 24.04 remote TTY with no active display; it has tmux 3.4 and Xvfb but not the other terminal applications. Xvfb and PTY evidence do not satisfy the manual gate. The operator selected an Ubuntu/GNOME desktop as the target, but a direct SSH probe failed because `ubuntu-desktop` does not resolve from this runner and no desktop host is connected. The worksheet remains unfilled; no terminal cell is claimed passed. Matrix execution still requires the exact candidate artifact selected for qualification, installed and identified on that desktop.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:43:**Authoritative release source:** `origin/main` is `1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145`, the PR #155 merge commit. PRs #153, #154, and #155 are merged. PR #153 integrated the checkpoint-choice flow; PR #154 refreshed readiness and the terminal worksheet; PR #155 fixed the remaining doctor integrity-scan timeout by batching metadata checks. PR #155 exact-head CI `39893335185`, CodeQL `39893335167`, and independent review passed on head `76b34f1d18d766b06011176a85679e7c3434ba30`. Current-main CI run [39896372677](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39896372677) completed successfully on exact `1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145`: Node 24 at 03:56:55Z, Node 22 at 03:57:48Z, and Linux x86-64 packaging/reproducibility/package-smoke/installer-smoke at 04:11:34Z. Its Linux job validated identical package archives, checksums, notices, SBOM and installer across two builds. Current-main CodeQL run [39896372726](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39896372726) completed successfully at 03:43:55Z on that same SHA. CI’s Linux package used existing `1.0.0-rc.2` version metadata; it is source CI evidence, not an immutable RC3 artifact or qualification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:55:**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open; the latest custodian metadata request has no response in the available checkpoint, so T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T2/T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:59:**Authoritative release source:** `origin/main` was `fa16045a6351ce61763bc3fcc93b562c50849285`, the merge of PR #152. PR #152 carried the readiness checkpoint refresh and terminal worksheet wording separating the §5.3 disposition gate from `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`; its exact head `deaf56fdb074df3f5cd3b62d50f811a2f14ca101` passed Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 package/repro/install-smoke CI in run `39881805268`; CodeQL `39881805274` passed. The independent reviewer accepted that exact head. Post-merge CI run `39885102002` passed Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 packaging/reproducibility/smoke/install; post-merge CodeQL `39885101945` passed. These checks are bound to exact main `fa16045`. Retained post-merge check summary: [CI and CodeQL result](../reviews/evidence/v1/plan10-readiness-post152/post-merge-ci-main-fa16045.txt).\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:69:**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open, with no custodian response to the latest metadata-only compatibility request posted at 22:08 UTC; T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:117:- **Requirements gate:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` was independently rerun with isolated HOME/XDG on exact `7d6673f` and passed: 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open). Eleven requirements remain explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification: `REQ-AGT-…38 tokens truncated…EQ-QUAL-109`. This source-stage gate pass does not satisfy those qualification requirements.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:137:- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed on exact source tree `8f4504e` (tree `2a0799c8a32e88e34322b712cf937d73cbe4d637`), with isolated `HOME`/XDG: 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open). Eleven rows remain below the ordinary tested threshold pending their approved exact-RC evidence: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. The pre-RC checker pass does not imply those RC gates have passed or authorize an acceptance claim.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:153:- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` ran in a detached worktree at exact `6a16cb60635c9182f13be1635d5f44eddebdcde0` with isolated `HOME` and failed as required. It reports 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open) and 11 below threshold: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. The exact result is recorded in the claims log and was sent to the ledger owner in PR #17 comment `6252582027`; no ledger status changed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:163:- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` ran from a detached worktree at exact revision `4bce8760893b222789b76011a477dd61988ecba6` with isolated `HOME`; it failed as required. Ledger result: 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 11 below threshold: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, `REQ-QUAL-109`. `REQ-AGT-118` remains tested. `REQ-AGT-010` remains partial; its existing ACC-TRUST-04 source evidence is pinned to `2c70d39`, and the current row still needs exact-revision evidence and a DEC-04-aligned disposition before promotion. The ledger owner was given this exact checker output; no ledger status was changed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:173:- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` was run from a clean archive of exact `519398495b7c3a2e5915ed76eee0bb731feb0bcf`; it exited 1 as required. The ledger has 121 rows (107 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open) and 11 below-threshold rows: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. `REQ-AGT-118` is now `tested` with the DEC-17 accuracy exceptions preserved. `REQ-AGT-010` remains partial; its `CTX-001` blocking marker/mapping is under owner reconciliation against DEC-04. No requirement was promoted by this checkpoint.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:274:| `REQ-QUAL-108` | partial | Automated PTY suite passes on `a7126aa`; the human matrix is absent for xterm, kitty (keyboard protocol enabled), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60. | Human terminal access and RC install | Human acceptance operator | Execute the `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 manual matrix on the installed RC across all required terminal×size cells and archive screenshots and verdicts. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:7:| Requirements | REQ-QUAL-101, REQ-QUAL-102, REQ-QUAL-103, REQ-Q