:\"javascript-typescript\",\"state\":null},{\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (24)\",\"state\":null},{\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"name\":\"linux-x86_64\",\"state\":null},{\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"name\":\"CodeQL\",\"state\":null},{\"conclusion\":null,\"name\":null,\"state\":\"SUCCESS\"}],\"headRefName\":\"v1/defect-nexus-commit-exclusion\",\"headRefOid\":\"02487c8b6f0ed311e72a3c806e533ada9576e3a8\",\"isDraft\":false,\"lastComment\":{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"**Independent review (claude-code) at exact head `02487c8b6f0ed311e72a3c806e533ada9576e3a8`: ACCEPT.**\\n- `git reset --quiet HEAD -- :(top).nexus` clears previously staged `.nexus` index entries without touching the working tree. `add -A -- :(top,exclude).nexus :(top,exclude).nexus/**` then keeps internal state out, whatever `.git/info/exclude` says, including negated or malformed rules.\\n- Removing `GIT_LITERAL/GLOB/NOGLOB/ICASE_PATHSPECS` from the environment stops a hostile environment from tur\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T07:55:18Z\"},\"mergeStateStatus\":\"CLEAN\",\"number\":183,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"reviews\":[],\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"fix(git): exclude internal state from workspace commits\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-24T07:55:18Z\"}\n{\"agent\":\"RubyBridge\",\"host\":\"mike-dev\",\"branch\":\"v1/defect-nexus-commit-exclusion\",\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/nexus-commit-exclusion\",\"base\":\"0a80759de65d2d6909d1d259d1cbd11c5b9321f5\",\"since\":\"2026-10-24T05:12:20Z\",\"pid\":null,\"scope\":\"commitChanges must never stage .nexus state even when git exclude rules are malformed or negated; add focused integration tests. Disjoint defense-in-depth lane; original git_exclude claims remain owned by opencode-defect-scan.\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":644941278}},"started_at_ms":1792841188437,"completed_at_ms":1792841189082}}
