{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T11:32:43.331Z","ordinal":287639,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16cd4-55fc-7d42-952d-a5ba875e9e0d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-ed40b34e-f952-42a4-b85f-b2d2bfba0384","process_id":"41886","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n 'v1\\.0\\.0-rc|tag.*release|signed tag|annotated tag|release workflow|softprops|workflow_dispatch' docs/v1.0.0 .github/workflows"],"cwd":"file:///tmp/nexus-release-gate-82c5","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n \"v1\\\\.0\\\\.0-rc|tag.*release|signed tag|annotated tag|release workflow|softprops|workflow_dispatch\" docs/v1.0.0 .github/workflows","query":"v1\\.0\\.0-rc|tag.*release|signed tag|annotated tag|release workflow|softprops|workflow_dispatch","path":"v1.0.0"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":".github/workflows/codeql.yml:10:  workflow_dispatch:\n.github/workflows/ci.yml:7:  workflow_dispatch:\n.github/workflows/repro.yml:4:  workflow_dispatch:\n.github/workflows/repro.yml:7:        description: Published v1.0.0 RC tag with lock-pinned release tools (for example v1.0.0-rc.4)\n.github/workflows/repro.yml:44:            echo \"Expected a v1.0.0-rc.N tag; received an invalid tag.\" >&2\n.github/workflows/repro.yml:68:          gh release view \"$TARGET_TAG\" --json isPrerelease,isDraft \\\n.github/workflows/release.yml:113:      # RC tags (vX.Y.Z-rc.N) publish a prerelease: the workflow-produced RC is the qualification candidate\n.github/workflows/release.yml:116:      - uses: softprops/action-gh-release@3bb12739c298aeb8a4eeaf626c5b8d85266b0e65 # v2\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:88:5. Pushing, tagging, publishing and changing GitHub state (issues, milestones, releases) are **owner-approved actions** (DECISIONS X-list). Agents prepare them and do not perform them.\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:50:5. Cut `v1.0.0-rc.1` only when G0–G4 pass. Then run ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 against the **installed** RC.\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:21:| Versions | `package.json` and `cli/package.json`: `0.1.0-alpha.2`. **`core/Cargo.toml`: `1.2.1`** (mismatch, REL-04). Tags on origin: `v0.1.0-alpha.1` and `v0.1.0-alpha.2`, both GitHub prereleases. Local-only tags `v1.1.0`, `v1.2.0`, `v1.2.1` (never on the remote, per the owner and `git ls-remote`). | RT |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:25:2. **RC artifact construction.** After the required owner authorization, create the version-matched RC tag on that exact source commit and use the repository release workflow to build and publish the RC artifacts. Record the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance. The workflow-produced artifacts are the candidates for qualification; a local build or a different commit is not interchangeable. RC artifact publication is not product qualification or final release acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:28:5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:30:The final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:64:1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:87:Every ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:329:G6 passes only when every item below holds. It authorizes a version-only stable commit from the accepted RC source, followed by its source checks, stable tag, and unpublished draft candidate; it does not authorize making stable assets publicly available. RC tags are candidate construction inputs governed by §1.1; an RC tag or its successful build does not satisfy this release decision.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:341:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:346:After G6, complete source checks on the exact stable-version commit before tagging, then complete the stable artifact checks in §1.1 stage 5 before publishing the draft. A failure keeps publication blocked and requires remediation plus the applicable requalification; do not mark the campaign released until published artifacts are independently verified.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:133:- Release line: `v1.0.0-rc.N` prereleases, then `v1.0.0`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:159:This supersedes the earlier Node ≥ 20 decision. The immutable `v1.0.0-rc.2` tag targets `19d6f0a80e21f9b640a46ee12200c4f5f6d967a4`, whose package engine and workflows still use Node 20; that tag is not a qualifying RC under this decision.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:174:**Status amendment (2026-10-21):** The contest has concluded. The release coordinator confirmed that no contest freeze applies. The historical freeze above is no longer a restriction; PLAN-C1 and other contest-related maintenance may proceed through normal claims, review, and validation. Preserve submitted tags, run records, and manifests as historical evidence, and do not represent changed current sources as the original submission. The retired `cloudflare-contest-contract` check remains retired and must not be reintroduced as a release gate.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:249:| X7 | **Authorized by the owner in the implementation/release handoff, reaffirmed by the 2026-10-18 takeover instruction.** Necessary commits, pushes, PRs, merges, RC tags and final v1.0.0 publication are authorized, conditional on the existing checks and acceptance gates. Release publisher: `codex-api-root`, succeeding rate-limited `claude-code`; no duplicate publisher. See [authorization and handoff](../reviews/evidence/v1/RELEASE-TAKEOVER/authorization-and-handoff.md). | Release | Authorization resolved; execution remains gated |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:188:| REQ-REL-103 | Audit | A single version across tag, package.json files, Cargo and the core handshake. | compatibility / supportability | `core/Cargo.toml:3`; `release.yml` | TEST (ACC-PKG-03; test:cli/test/engine_handshake.test.ts, core/tests/rpc_shutdown.rs) | tested | ACC-PKG-03 | **B** | REL-04 | SPEC-06 / PLAN-06 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:198:| REQ-REL-109 | TOP_TIER D4 | Provenance attestation; tag-pinned installer asset. | supply chain | `release.yml` | TEST (ACC-SUP-03; test:release.yml, install.sh) | tested | ACC-SUP-03 | RR | REL-09 | SPEC-07 / PLAN-07 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:41:| 3 | Release resolver: fetch latest stable release or pinned release tag from GitHub Releases API; parse asset metadata; exclude drafts/prereleases from default selection; handle rate limits, network errors, and missing tags. | `cli/src/upgrade.ts` | 1 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md:46:3. **REQ-REL-103.** One version: tag == package.json == cli/package.json == core/Cargo.toml == harness-core `--version` == the sidecar protocol's reported core version. Release CI asserts this. A fresh install's doctor shows no version warning.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md:107:| ACC-PKG-03 | The release workflow fails on a version mismatch (negative test with a doctored Cargo.toml in CI). A fresh install's `doctor --json` has no `engine.binary` warning. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md:109:| ACC-PKG-05 | Installer: bad tag `v1.2.3/../x` is rejected before network. No-version with only prereleases prints the latest-prerelease hint. Deleting a dist file then reinstalling repairs it. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md:33:| 3 | `scripts/sync-version.mjs` writes `package.json` → `cli/package.json` + `core/Cargo.toml` (and `Cargo.lock` via `cargo update -p harness-core --offline`). Run it now to set Cargo to `0.1.0-alpha.2`. The release workflow asserts equality with the tag. | new script; `core/Cargo.toml:3`; `release.yml:27-31` | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md:37:| 7 | Installer: strict tag regex; `-fsSL --show-error`; no-stable-release hint naming the latest prerelease; rate-limit message; `MANIFEST.sha256` repair on reinstall; `NEXUS_FORCE=1`. | `install.sh:21-49`; `package-linux.sh` (write manifest) | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md:56:| `installer-smoke.sh` additions: bad tag, no-stable hint (mock API via `NEXUS_RELEASES_API` override used only in smoke), manifest repair | ACC-PKG-05 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:132:| HIST-07 | S2 | Release/supply chain | scripts/generate_sbom.sh:32-94; .github/workflows/release.yml | SOURCE: SBOM from direct deps only; not part of release workflow; no signing/attestation; no SECURITY.md. REL-002/003/004 marked DEMONSTRATED; REL-004 patch obligation now live (public prereleases) | No vulnerability intake path; SBOM incomplete | Lockfile-derived SBOM in release, SECURITY.md, provenance |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:198:| REQ-REL-V1-02 | SECURITY.md + CHANGELOG + lockfile-derived validated SBOM + checksum signing/provenance in release workflow | REL-002..004 obligations now live | RELEASE-REQUIRED | release.yml produces SBOM validated by cyclonedx-cli; attestation present |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:76:- Precedence: SemVer 2.0.0. Major, minor, patch compare numerically. Prerelease tags have lower precedence than normal releases; dot-separated prerelease identifiers compare numerically if both numeric, else ASCII-lexicographically.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:78:- Exact version resolution: Queries `/releases/tags/<tag>` with normalized `v` prefix. Prereleases are allowed only if explicitly targeted.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:118:| ACC-UPG-04 | Downgrade and pinned version safety | Reject downgrade unless explicitly confirmed or `--allow-downgrade` is provided. Rejects invalid tags and non-existent releases fail-closed. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:33:| 9 | Write `SECURITY.md` (private reporting via GitHub Security Advisories, supported versions, 7-day acknowledgement target) and `CHANGELOG.md` (back-filled from docs/releases). Set the release body from `docs/releases/<tag>.md` (`body_path`), and fail if that file is missing. | root; `release.yml` | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:34:| 10 | Cross-runner reproducibility: a workflow_dispatch job builds on ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04 with the pinned toolchain and compares the outputs. Run it once for the RC. | new `.github/workflows/repro.yml` | 1 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:32:- **Release pipeline.** A tag `v*.*.*` triggers `release.yml`. The workflow checks that the tag commit is an ancestor of origin/main and that the tag matches `package.json` version. It then runs `npm ci`, the cli build, `cargo test --locked`, the release build, `npm test`, and security_gates. Next it runs `package-linux.sh` twice and `cmp`s the outputs (a reproducibility check), then `smoke-package.sh` and `installer-smoke.sh`. Finally `softprops/action-gh-release` uploads `nexus-linux-x86_64-<tag>.tar.gz` + `SHA256SUMS`, setting prerelease when the tag contains `-`. Release notes come from `generate_release_notes`; `docs/releases/*.md` is not used.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:62:| REL-04 | S2 | versioning | core/Cargo.toml:3 (`1.2.1`) vs package.json:3 / cli/package.json:3 (`0.1.0-alpha.2`); doctor.ts:491-492; local tags v1.1.0/v1.2.0/v1.2.1 | RUNTIME. A fresh clean install gives `WARN engine.binary: The engine reports version 1.2.1, the CLI 0.1.0-alpha.2 → Rebuild with make build`. Every release user sees a warning, and its remedy is impossible in a packaged install (there is no Makefile). Local v1.x tags (not on origin, not ancestors of main, no release.yml at those commits, so not publishable by accident) conflict with the future v1.0.0 ordering. | A permanent false warning on a healthy install trains users to ignore doctor. Version identity is inconsistent across components. | Single-source the version: release workflow asserts Cargo.toml == package.json == cli/package.json == tag. Delete stale local v1.x tags. Make doctor remedies context-aware (packaged → \"reinstall\"). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:76:| MNT-05 | S4 | changelog | docs/releases/*.md; release.yml:47 | SOURCE + RUNTIME. The GitHub release bodies are only \"Full Changelog: compare…\". The curated notes in docs/releases are not attached, and there is no CHANGELOG.md. | Users on GitHub do not see known limits or breaking changes (e.g. `spawn_subagent max_steps` removed). | Use `body_path: docs/releases/${tag}.md`, and fail the release if the file is missing. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:125:  - The tag must be on main and match package.json (release.yml:27-31).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:150:| E-R3 | One version everywhere: tag == package.json == cli/package.json == Cargo.toml. A fresh install's doctor shows no version warning. | compat | BLOCKER | A release.yml assertion, plus smoke-package asserting no `warn` on `engine.binary`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:160:| E-R13 | GitHub release body comes from docs/releases/<tag>.md. | docs | POST-V1 | Release view shows the curated notes. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:7:**Distribution scope:** The release owner confirmed the supported distribution target is the GitHub installer/archive only; npm publication is inapplicable. The current release workflow is the authority for published assets.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:19:**Exact source gates:** `origin/main` and the signed `v1.0.0-rc.3` tag resolve to source commit `1b9791f07d301c885fe48f04a796203583ab5a5c`. Exact-main CI [39923089278](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089278) and CodeQL [39923089363](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089363) completed successfully on that commit. CI passed Node 22, Node 24, Linux CLI tests, security gates, requirements checks, two-build package reproducibility, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag v1.0.0-rc.3` and `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed at the same source; the latter reports 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 explicit exact-RC qualification deferrals. This is source-gate evidence, not product acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:21:**RC3 artifact publication and provenance:** The annotated tag object is `dd68c222c57d0be0a4245a5b88092ff9df69201f`; its PGP signature verified good and it points to the source commit above. Release workflow [39927176480](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39927176480) completed successfully and published the [v1.0.0-rc.3 prerelease](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.3). The workflow-produced Linux x86-64 archive is `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.3.tar.gz`, SHA-256 `efb446d2760f2e1aa7890e9d786b8a2ba8e4ebb784fbcac1e66afe827428864d`; `SHA256SUMS` is `9288edb4655a19caa40e1598c0a642ab7f7e93aafbb187c2bfc8cfa9e19f116f`; the CycloneDX SBOM is `3a3176b4b3890c1bc07fb7b3acd80f7372f043819e6a8b296346d014b07f9d3a`. Downloaded checksums and SBOM sidecars passed. GitHub attestations for the archive and `SHA256SUMS` verified against the Release workflow, run `39927176480`, tag `v1.0.0-rc.3`, and source `1b9791f`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:23:**Installed-candidate and checkpoint-choice observation:** The published installer completed with `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1` and installed RC3 under `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.3`; installer provenance records the exact archive digest and source revision. `/home/mike/.local/bin/nexus --version` reports `1.0.0-rc.3 (1b9791f07d30)`. The previous RC1 directory remains installed at `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.1` for rollback. The coordinator reported an automated PTY probe of the installed default TUI using a synthetic Git workspace, fake credential-shaped canary, and unreachable loopback endpoint. The reported probe displayed the five choices and selected cancel before inference. Its transcript/capture was not retained in the release evidence tree, so this observation is unarchived and was not independently verified in the readiness review. It is diagnostic context only: it does not establish the checkpoint-choice gate, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, or provider/task qualification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:35:**Checkpoint failure:** `/home/mike/.local/bin/nexus` resolves to the installed `v1.0.0-rc.1` package and reports `1.0.0-rc.1 (cb364c386c42)`. That immutable package lacks checkpoint choices, so the reported failure before turn start is reproducible by version identity and will persist on RC1. The fix is integrated in PR #147 (TUI/sidecar) and PR #153 (legacy REPL): before starting a turn, Nexus asks the operator whether to use read-only mode, continue in the configured mode without a rollback checkpoint, create the checkpoint with the sensitive-content risk acknowledged, cancel, or enter a different instruction. Both PRs passed exact-head checks, and the subsequent exact-main CI on `dac465d` passed. No replacement package has been installed. The public release page still has RC1 only; RC2 has a tag but no published release, and RC3 has neither tag nor release.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:53:**RC identity and publication:** Remote immutable tags remain `v1.0.0-rc.1` at `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779` and `v1.0.0-rc.2` at `19d6f0a80e21f9b640a46ee12200c4f5f6d967a4`; both predate the accepted Node 22 floor and checkpoint-choice fix. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passes at exact main and reports all components at `1.0.0-rc.2`. No accepted RC or stable v1.0.0 tag/release is established. A new candidate must use the next RC identity after source CI and release prerequisites pass, then undergo installed-artifact qualification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:67:**RC identity and publication:** Remote immutable tags are `v1.0.0-rc.1` at `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779` and `v1.0.0-rc.2` at `19d6f0a80e21f9b640a46ee12200c4f5f6d967a4`; both predate the accepted Node 22 floor. GitHub currently publishes RC1 as a prerelease; RC2 has a tag but no published release. No accepted RC or stable v1.0.0 tag/release is established. The next candidate needs a fresh RC3 identity after its source/version checks; it must be installed and qualified before acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:79:The public `v1.0.0-rc.1` release remains the only published v1 candidate. `v1.0.0-rc.2` points to older source and is nonqualifying under the Node 22 decision. There is no accepted RC or stable release. Held-out custody, provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, installed-RC packaging and qualification, five-terminal by three-size human evidence, and independent acceptance remain incomplete. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:93:**RC and publication:** The published `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag resolves to `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779`, an ancestor of current `main`, and is not an artifact built from current source. Its published asset digest is `8d7dd32f3d00adb98d4f0ea2c6a484ea8e04fc547b4d78b21b060000eda22b9d`. The next candidate needs a new immutable identity, currently expected to be `v1.0.0-rc.2`, with synchronized version metadata and release notes. Exact-RC artifact/install checks, held-out T2, provider and standalone qualification, T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, independent RC acceptance, and stable-promotion disposition remain outstanding. Publication authorization is granted but gated on those results. No stable `v1.0.0` tag or release exists.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:141:- **Version, RC, and publication:** Root and CLI package versions remain `0.1.0-alpha.2`. GitHub currently lists only alpha pre-releases `v0.1.0-alpha.1` and `v0.1.0-alpha.2`; no `v1.0.0-rc.N` artifact/tag or stable v1.0.0 tag, npm package, or GitHub release exists. Follow the staged lifecycle in `ACCEPTANCE.md`: pre-RC source gates, RC construction, artifact-bound RC gates, installed-RC qualification and independent G6 acceptance, then stable promotion/publication and post-publication verification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:147:The 17:16 checkpoint's phrase “nothing has been tagged or published” was too broad. GitHub lists the existing pre-releases `v0.1.0-alpha.1` and `v0.1.0-alpha.2`, with corresponding tags `7e46bb0da88d06552a66ef703f53a05d1de1f37d` and `c3dcafac93b5f52d913b4dfb6eb292bbcede4566`. Post-merge CI run `39146982849` and CodeQL passed on exact integration `6a16cb60635c9182f13be1635d5f44eddebdcde0`. No v1.0.0 release candidate or stable v1.0.0 publication exists. The superseded 17:16 text below is retained verbatim as historical evidence; this correction is authoritative for current release status.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:155:- **Other qualification and release gates:** Provider/standalone, T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, qualification-host validation, and human five-environment × three-size terminal acceptance remain incomplete. Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`; no RC artifact/tag, stable tag, npm publication, or GitHub release exists. Publication authorization remains granted but gated on accepted exact-RC evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:162:- **PR state:** PRs #9, #13, #15, #16, and #44 are integrated. PR #9's stale readiness changes were merged earlier and are retained in history. PR #33 remains open at `0ca77e5ee64f80db02e2b16178c5be551ce5de0c`, based on now-stale `faf9580`; its exact CI run `39141771002` passed all five jobs, including 1,243 CLI tests with zero failures, resource enforcement fixtures, staged Git-history/external-store canaries, security gates, deterministic package/SBOM comparison, and installer/package smoke. Independent review found a release-critical gap: preflight does not compare protected corpus paths with the evaluator's unconditional system mounts such as `/usr/local/lib`. The reviewer requested refusal of protected paths beneath every mounted host path and regression coverage. The evaluator claim remains active; no transfer or remediation checkpoint has been reported. Do not run held-out qualification. PR #33 must incorporate `4bce876`, fix this finding, pass exact-head checks, and receive independent re-review.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:166:- **Version, RC, and publication:** Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`. PR #44's deterministic package checks are source CI evidence for that alpha package; they do not establish cross-runner RC reproducibility or installed-RC acceptance. No RC artifact, installed-RC provider/standalone, held-out, T3/T4, cross-runner, human-terminal, or independent acceptance evidence exists. The staged lifecycle in `ACCEPTANCE.md` remains authoritative. Publication authorization remains granted and gated; no RC tag, stable tag, npm publication, or GitHub release exists.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:197:- **Supply-chain reproducibility and draft-then-publish release workflow (PRs [#20](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/20), [#21](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/21)):**\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:199:  - `.github/workflows/release.yml` and `scripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs` (`a7126aa`, PR #21) build RC tags (`vX.Y.Z-rc.N`) as prereleases and build stable tags (`vX.Y.Z`) as **unpublished drafts** (`draft: true`), requiring via the RC's own checker that a stable tag is a single commit directly on its `vX.Y.Z-rc.N` parent changing only synchronized version metadata.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:260:| `REQ-REL-005` | partial (RR) | Candidate source security gates passed on `a7126aa` (run `39108774170`); exact-RC artifact/security evidence is pending RC tag construction. `security_gates.sh` requires `cargo-deny` or `cargo-audit` and fails closed when neither is installed (`ACC-SUP-04`). | Exact RC and `ACC-SUP-05` release CI matrix | Release engineering | On the frozen RC tag, run and archive the release workflow security evidence. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:266:| `REQ-REL-114` | open (workflow enforced at `86bdbe6`; RC run pending) | `.github/workflows/repro.yml` and `scripts/repro-identity.mjs` (PR #20 `86bdbe6`) enforce fail-closed tag/commit/clean-tree/toolchain/artifact identity across Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 builders, covered by `repro_identity.test.ts`. Live execution on an actual RC tag remains pending RC construction. | Final RC tag and `.github/workflows/repro.yml` run | Release engineering | Dispatch `repro.yml` against the exact `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag/commit and archive both runner manifests and comparison evidence. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:292:2. **Stage 1 — Pre-RC source gates & integration to `main`:** Merge `v1/integration` to `main` (PR #8) once all pre-RC source checks pass, synchronize version metadata to `1.0.0-rc.1` (`scripts/sync-version.mjs`), add `docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.1.md`, and verify green source CI on `main`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:293:3. **Stage 2 — RC artifact construction:** Tag `v1.0.0-rc.1` on the verified `main` commit and build/publish the prerelease RC candidate via `.github/workflows/release.yml`, recording the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance attestation.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:294:4. **Stage 3 — RC artifact gates:** Run `ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08` and dispatch `.github/workflows/repro.yml` (`REQ-REL-114`) against the exact `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag and commit.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:295:5. **Stage 4 — Installed-RC qualification:** Install the workflow-produced `v1.0.0-rc.1` package via the documented installer and execute `ACCEPTANCE.md` §§4–8 (standalone/provider matrix, CI/scripted/manual terminal matrix, T2 40×5 held-out comparison, T4 9×5 fault matrix, T3 8×5 long-task matrix, install matrix, SPEC-09 §3.2 docs checklist, and §8 independent acceptance). Archive all evidence under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.1/`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:296:6. **Stage 5 — G6 decision, version-only stable promotion, draft verification, and publication:** After G6 passes on the accepted RC, create the version-only `v1.0.0` commit directly on the accepted RC commit (enforced by `scripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs` in `release.yml`), run source CI, tag `v1.0.0` to build the unpublished draft release, complete Stage 5 stable artifact/install/attestation checks, record the signed G6 and Stage 5 disposition, and publish the draft release (`gh release edit v1.0.0 --draft=false`).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:54:| VER-03 | S2 | Reasoning models (Qwen3/DeepSeek R1 via llama.cpp/vLLM templates that strip the opening `<think>`) | parser.ts:320-332 | RUNTIME (probe P2, P3). Reasoning is removed only when both tags are present. Text ending in `</think>` (opening tag stripped by the server), or an unclosed `<think>`, stays in the reply and its JSON is parsed. \"Maybe I should run {\"name\":\"run_command\",\"arguments\":{\"command\":\"echo PWNED\"}} ... no.</think>\" → executed. This contradicts the agent.ts:4719 comment that reasoning is never parsed for tools. | Actions the model considered and rejected get executed. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: treat text before a lone `</think>`, and after an unclosed `<think>`, as reasoning. Add tests. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:59:| VER-08 | S2 | `--tdd` / `/tdd` | synthesizer.ts:239-326; agent.ts:5236-5255 | SOURCE + INFERENCE. `runAutonomousTdd` never calls `verifyRedPhase` or `verifyGreenPhase`, ignores every `agent.run` result, and contains dead code (266-272). Success is only a full-suite exit 0, with no check that tests executed. Each `agent.run` calls `resetConversation()` (AGT-01), so GREEN starts with no memory of the RED test. The RED prompt asks the model to call `task_completed` with a deliberately failing test, but the completion oracle runs the discovered verifier, which fails → completion refused (INFERENCE). The success summary claims \"RED -> GREEN -> REFACTOR verified\". | The TDD mode advertises a protocol it does not enforce. RED turns likely end in NOT_ESTABLISHED or stagnation. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: enforce the phases (run the repro target and require fail, then pass), carry the conversation between phases, exempt the RED phase from the completion oracle; or mark the mode experimental. Add an e2e test with a mock model. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:135:| R-VER-2 | Text-embedded tool calls are parsed only on connections without native tool calling, and only from `<tool_call>` tags or a reply that is exactly one fenced call. Prose `{…}` is never executed. | safety | RELEASE-REQUIRED | parser tests P1/P9 yield 0 tool calls; existing local-model tests still pass. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:45:6. **REQ-REL-112.** SECURITY.md defines the reporting channel, the supported versions and the response targets. CHANGELOG.md is maintained, and the release body is taken from `docs/releases/<tag>.md` (the release fails if that file is missing).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:30:| **RC1** | After PLAN-09 task 7's pre-RC source-ledger reconciliation and enforce gate, tag `v1.0.0-rc.1` (owner approves publishing a prerelease; X7) | RC build installed through the documented command | G0–G4 green on the exact RC source; pre-RC requirements enforcement passed | <1 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:107:| AGT-R3 | Work units keep execution tracking (loops, stagnation, cumulative steps) across resume. | failure/convergence (AGT-02c) | RELEASE-REQUIRED | Resume a unit after 2 identical loops; third repetition triggers recovery note, not a fresh count. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:168:| CON-R5 | The video's source commits and run record are published (tag) | evidence | RELEASE-REQUIRED (contest) | `git branch -r --contains 98a8a813` is non-empty |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":705014901}},"started_at_ms":1792841562625,"completed_at_ms":1792841563331}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T11:32:44.354Z","ordinal":287640,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a16daf-40c2-7093-9f50-ad0879cc286b","call_id":"call_15802490379f4e689eee632e9823071d","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.8 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 8402)\nTotal output lines: 75\n\n.github/workflows/codeql.yml:10:  workflow_dispatch:\n.github/workflows/ci.yml:7:  workflow_dispatch:\n.github/workflows/repro.yml:4:  workflow_dispatch:\n.github/workflows/repro.yml:7:        description: Published v1.0.0 RC tag with lock-pinned release tools (for example v1.0.0-rc.4)\n.github/workflows/repro.yml:44:            echo \"Expected a v1.0.0-rc.N tag; received an invalid tag.\" >&2\n.github/workflows/repro.yml:68:          gh release view \"$TARGET_TAG\" --json isPrerelease,isDraft \\\n.github/workflows/release.yml:113:      # RC tags (vX.Y.Z-rc.N) publish a prerelease: the workflow-produced RC is the qualification candidate\n.github/workflows/release.yml:116:      - uses: softprops/action-gh-release@3bb12739c298aeb8a4eeaf626c5b8d85266b0e65 # v2\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:88:5. Pushing, tagging, publishing and changing GitHub state (issues, milestones, releases) are **owner-approved actions** (DECISIONS X-list). Agents prepare them and do not perform them.\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:50:5. Cut `v1.0.0-rc.1` only when G0–G4 pass. Then run ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 against the **installed** RC.\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:21:| Versions | `package.json` and `cli/package.json`: `0.1.0-alpha.2`. **`core/Cargo.toml`: `1.2.1`** (mismatch, REL-04). Tags on origin: `v0.1.0-alpha.1` and `v0.1.0-alpha.2`, both GitHub prereleases. Local-only tags `v1.1.0`, `v1.2.0`, `v1.2.1` (never on the remote, per the owner and `git ls-remote`). | RT |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:25:2. **RC artifact construction.** After the required owner authorization, create the version-matched RC tag on that exact source commit and use the repository release workflow to build and publish the RC artifacts. Record the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance. The workflow-produced artifacts are the candidates for qualification; a local build or a different commit is not interchangeable. RC artifact publication is not product qualification or final release acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:28:5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:30:The final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:64:1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:87:Every ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:329:G6 passes only when every item below holds. It authorizes a version-only stable commit from the accepted RC source, followed by its source checks, stable tag, and unpublished draft candidate; it does not authorize making stable assets publicly available. RC tags are candidate construction inputs governed by §1.1; an RC tag or its successful build does not satisfy this release decision.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:341:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:346:After G6, complete source checks on the exact stable-version commit before tagging, then complete the stable artifact checks in §1.1 stage 5 before publishing the draft. A failure keeps publication blocked and requires remediation plus the applicable requalification; do not mark the campaign released until published artifacts are independently verified.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:133:- Release line: `v1.0.0-rc.N` prereleases, then `v1.0.0`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:159:This supersedes the earlier Node ≥ 20 decision. The immutable `v1.0.0-rc.2` tag targets `19d6f0a80e21f9b640a46ee12200c4f5f6d967a4`, whose package engine and workflows still use Node 20; that tag is not a qualifying RC under this decision.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:174:**Status amendment (2026-10-21):** The contest has concluded. The release coordinator confirmed that no contest freeze applies. The historical freeze above is no longer a restriction; PLAN-C1 and other contest-related maintenance may proceed through normal claims, review, and validation. Preserve submitted tags, run records, and manifests as historical evidence, and do not represent changed current sources as the original submission. The retired `cloudflare-contest-contract` check remains retired and must not be reintroduced as a release gate.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:249:| X7 | **Authorized by the owner in the implementation/release handoff, reaffirmed by the 2026-10-18 takeover instruction.** Necessary commits, pushes, PRs, merges, RC tags and final v1.0.0 publication are authorized, conditional on the existing checks and acceptance gates. Release publisher: `codex-api-root`, succeeding rate-limited `claude-code`; no duplicate publisher. See [authorization and handoff](../reviews/evidence/v1/RELEASE-TAKEOVER/authorization-and-handoff.md). | Release | Authorization resolved; execution remains gated |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:188:| REQ-REL-103 | Audit | A single version across tag, package.json files, Cargo and the core handshake. | compatibility / supportability | `core/Cargo.toml:3`; `release.yml` | TEST (ACC-PKG-03; test:cli/test/engine_handshake.test.ts, core/tests/rpc_shutdown.rs) | tested | ACC-PKG-03 | **B** | REL-04 | SPEC-06 / PLAN-06 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:198:| REQ-REL-109 | TOP_TIER D4 | Provenance attestation; tag-pinned installer asset. | supply chain | `release.yml` | TEST (ACC-SUP-03; test:release.yml, install.sh) | tested | ACC-SUP-03 | RR | REL-09 | SPEC-07 / PLAN-07 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:41:| 3 | Release reso…3402 tokens truncated…e-releases `v0.1.0-alpha.1` and `v0.1.0-alpha.2`; no `v1.0.0-rc.N` artifact/tag or stable v1.0.0 tag, npm package, or GitHub release exists. Follow the staged lifecycle in `ACCEPTANCE.md`: pre-RC source gates, RC construction, artifact-bound RC gates, installed-RC qualification and independent G6 acceptance, then stable promotion/publication and post-publication verification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:147:The 17:16 checkpoint's phrase “nothing has been tagged or published” was too broad. GitHub lists the existing pre-releases `v0.1.0-alpha.1` and `v0.1.0-alpha.2`, with corresponding tags `7e46bb0da88d06552a66ef703f53a05d1de1f37d` and `c3dcafac93b5f52d913b4dfb6eb292bbcede4566`. Post-merge CI run `39146982849` and CodeQL passed on exact integration `6a16cb60635c9182f13be1635d5f44eddebdcde0`. No v1.0.0 release candidate or stable v1.0.0 publication exists. The superseded 17:16 text below is retained verbatim as historical evidence; this correction is authoritative for current release status.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:155:- **Other qualification and release gates:** Provider/standalone, T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, qualification-host validation, and human five-environment × three-size terminal acceptance remain incomplete. Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`; no RC artifact/tag, stable tag, npm publication, or GitHub release exists. Publication authorization remains granted but gated on accepted exact-RC evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:162:- **PR state:** PRs #9, #13, #15, #16, and #44 are integrated. PR #9's stale readiness changes were merged earlier and are retained in history. PR #33 remains open at `0ca77e5ee64f80db02e2b16178c5be551ce5de0c`, based on now-stale `faf9580`; its exact CI run `39141771002` passed all five jobs, including 1,243 CLI tests with zero failures, resource enforcement fixtures, staged Git-history/external-store canaries, security gates, deterministic package/SBOM comparison, and installer/package smoke. Independent review found a release-critical gap: preflight does not compare protected corpus paths with the evaluator's unconditional system mounts such as `/usr/local/lib`. The reviewer requested refusal of protected paths beneath every mounted host path and regression coverage. The evaluator claim remains active; no transfer or remediation checkpoint has been reported. Do not run held-out qualification. PR #33 must incorporate `4bce876`, fix this finding, pass exact-head checks, and receive independent re-review.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:166:- **Version, RC, and publication:** Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`. PR #44's deterministic package checks are source CI evidence for that alpha package; they do not establish cross-runner RC reproducibility or installed-RC acceptance. No RC artifact, installed-RC provider/standalone, held-out, T3/T4, cross-runner, human-terminal, or independent acceptance evidence exists. The staged lifecycle in `ACCEPTANCE.md` remains authoritative. Publication authorization remains granted and gated; no RC tag, stable tag, npm publication, or GitHub release exists.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:197:- **Supply-chain reproducibility and draft-then-publish release workflow (PRs [#20](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/20), [#21](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/21)):**\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:199:  - `.github/workflows/release.yml` and `scripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs` (`a7126aa`, PR #21) build RC tags (`vX.Y.Z-rc.N`) as prereleases and build stable tags (`vX.Y.Z`) as **unpublished drafts** (`draft: true`), requiring via the RC's own checker that a stable tag is a single commit directly on its `vX.Y.Z-rc.N` parent changing only synchronized version metadata.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:260:| `REQ-REL-005` | partial (RR) | Candidate source security gates passed on `a7126aa` (run `39108774170`); exact-RC artifact/security evidence is pending RC tag construction. `security_gates.sh` requires `cargo-deny` or `cargo-audit` and fails closed when neither is installed (`ACC-SUP-04`). | Exact RC and `ACC-SUP-05` release CI matrix | Release engineering | On the frozen RC tag, run and archive the release workflow security evidence. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:266:| `REQ-REL-114` | open (workflow enforced at `86bdbe6`; RC run pending) | `.github/workflows/repro.yml` and `scripts/repro-identity.mjs` (PR #20 `86bdbe6`) enforce fail-closed tag/commit/clean-tree/toolchain/artifact identity across Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 builders, covered by `repro_identity.test.ts`. Live execution on an actual RC tag remains pending RC construction. | Final RC tag and `.github/workflows/repro.yml` run | Release engineering | Dispatch `repro.yml` against the exact `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag/commit and archive both runner manifests and comparison evidence. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:292:2. **Stage 1 — Pre-RC source gates & integration to `main`:** Merge `v1/integration` to `main` (PR #8) once all pre-RC source checks pass, synchronize version metadata to `1.0.0-rc.1` (`scripts/sync-version.mjs`), add `docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.1.md`, and verify green source CI on `main`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:293:3. **Stage 2 — RC artifact construction:** Tag `v1.0.0-rc.1` on the verified `main` commit and build/publish the prerelease RC candidate via `.github/workflows/release.yml`, recording the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance attestation.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:294:4. **Stage 3 — RC artifact gates:** Run `ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08` and dispatch `.github/workflows/repro.yml` (`REQ-REL-114`) against the exact `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag and commit.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:295:5. **Stage 4 — Installed-RC qualification:** Install the workflow-produced `v1.0.0-rc.1` package via the documented installer and execute `ACCEPTANCE.md` §§4–8 (standalone/provider matrix, CI/scripted/manual terminal matrix, T2 40×5 held-out comparison, T4 9×5 fault matrix, T3 8×5 long-task matrix, install matrix, SPEC-09 §3.2 docs checklist, and §8 independent acceptance). Archive all evidence under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.1/`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:296:6. **Stage 5 — G6 decision, version-only stable promotion, draft verification, and publication:** After G6 passes on the accepted RC, create the version-only `v1.0.0` commit directly on the accepted RC commit (enforced by `scripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs` in `release.yml`), run source CI, tag `v1.0.0` to build the unpublished draft release, complete Stage 5 stable artifact/install/attestation checks, record the signed G6 and Stage 5 disposition, and publish the draft release (`gh release edit v1.0.0 --draft=false`).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:54:| VER-03 | S2 | Reasoning models (Qwen3/DeepSeek R1 via llama.cpp/vLLM templates that strip the opening `<think>`) | parser.ts:320-332 | RUNTIME (probe P2, P3). Reasoning is removed only when both tags are present. Text ending in `</think>` (opening tag stripped by the server), or an unclosed `<think>`, stays in the reply and its JSON is parsed. \"Maybe I should run {\"name\":\"run_command\",\"arguments\":{\"command\":\"echo PWNED\"}} ... no.</think>\" → executed. This contradicts the agent.ts:4719 comment that reasoning is never parsed for tools. | Actions the model considered and rejected get executed. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: treat text before a lone `</think>`, and after an unclosed `<think>`, as reasoning. Add tests. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:59:| VER-08 | S2 | `--tdd` / `/tdd` | synthesizer.ts:239-326; agent.ts:5236-5255 | SOURCE + INFERENCE. `runAutonomousTdd` never calls `verifyRedPhase` or `verifyGreenPhase`, ignores every `agent.run` result, and contains dead code (266-272). Success is only a full-suite exit 0, with no check that tests executed. Each `agent.run` calls `resetConversation()` (AGT-01), so GREEN starts with no memory of the RED test. The RED prompt asks the model to call `task_completed` with a deliberately failing test, but the completion oracle runs the discovered verifier, which fails → completion refused (INFERENCE). The success summary claims \"RED -> GREEN -> REFACTOR verified\". | The TDD mode advertises a protocol it does not enforce. RED turns likely end in NOT_ESTABLISHED or stagnation. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: enforce the phases (run the repro target and require fail, then pass), carry the conversation between phases, exempt the RED phase from the completion oracle; or mark the mode experimental. Add an e2e test with a mock model. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:135:| R-VER-2 | Text-embedded tool calls are parsed only on connections without native tool calling, and only from `<tool_call>` tags or a reply that is exactly one fenced call. Prose `{…}` is never executed. | safety | RELEASE-REQUIRED | parser tests P1/P9 yield 0 tool calls; existing local-model tests still pass. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:45:6. **REQ-REL-112.** SECURITY.md defines the reporting channel, the supported versions and the response targets. CHANGELOG.md is maintained, and the release body is taken from `docs/releases/<tag>.md` (the release fails if that file is missing).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:30:| **RC1** | After PLAN-09 task 7's pre-RC source-ledger reconciliation and enforce gate, tag `v1.0.0-rc.1` (owner approves publishing a prerelease; X7) | RC build installed through the documented command | G0–G4 green on the exact RC source; pre-RC requirements enforcement passed | <1 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:107:| AGT-R3 | Work units keep execution tracking (loops, stagnation, cumulative steps) across resume. | failure/convergence (AGT-02c) | RELEASE-REQUIRED | Resume a unit after 2 identical loops; third repetition triggers recovery note, not a fresh count. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:168:| CON-R5 | The video's source commits and run record are published (tag) | evidence | RELEASE-REQUIRED (contest) | `git branch -r --contains 98a8a813` is non-empty |\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16cd4-55fc-7d42-952d-a5ba875e9e0d","create_time":1792841564.3545544}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
