{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T11:57:52.906Z","ordinal":288335,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16cd4-55fc-7d42-952d-a5ba875e9e0d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-9ed4760d-5ed4-42eb-ba66-1e9d7a43211e","process_id":"17049","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -A18 -B3 '^### DEC-06|^## DEC-06|DEC-06' docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md; rg -n 'OpenRouter|ChatGPT sign-in|provider verify|pinned model' docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/ docs/releases 2>/dev/null | tail -40"],"cwd":"file:///tmp/nexus-release-gate-82c5","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -n -A18 -B3 '^### DEC-06|^## DEC-06|DEC-06' docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md; rg -n 'OpenRouter|ChatGPT sign-in|provider verify|pinned model' docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/ docs/releases 2>/dev/null | tail -40"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"11-| [DEC-03](#dec-03-team-and-operation-scope-in-v1) | `/team` and `nexus operation` in v1 | Shipped as **experimental**; data-loss fix still a blocker | No |\n12-| [DEC-04](#dec-04-issue-12-open-normative-blockers) | Issue #12 open blockers | EXT-004 implemented; CTX-001 partially implemented; CTX-002 descoped post-v1 | No |\n13-| [DEC-05](#dec-05-v1-evaluation-protocol-and-thresholds) | Evaluation protocol and thresholds | 40 held-out T2 tasks, 5 runs, 2 peers, thresholds below | Needs an external author (see actions) |\n14:| [DEC-06](#dec-06-supported-providers-for-v1) | Supported providers | Local OpenAI-compatible + OpenRouter supported; others experimental until live-verified | No |\n15-| [DEC-07](#dec-07-experimental-surfaces-nexus-eval-tdd-team-roles) | `nexus eval`, `/tdd`, team roles | eval and tdd experimental; eval's workspace mutation fixed; role tool sets enforced | No |\n16-| [DEC-08](#dec-08-version-identity-and-stale-v1x-tags) | Version identity, stale v1.x tags | `package.json` is the source of truth; local v1.x tags deleted (owner action) | No |\n17-| [DEC-09](#dec-09-release-provenance-mechanism) | Release provenance | GitHub artifact attestations | No |\n18-| [DEC-10](#dec-10-tracking-of-clidist) | Tracking of `cli/dist` | Untrack | No |\n19-| [DEC-11](#dec-11-retention-defaults) | Retention defaults | 90 days / 2 GB; audit log 10 MB × 5; first GC needs acknowledgement | No |\n20-| [DEC-12](#dec-12-platform-scope) | Platform scope | Linux x86-64 glibc only for v1.0.0 | No |\n21-| [DEC-13](#dec-13-contest-track-disposition) | Contest track | Submission completed and judging ended; no contest freeze applies, PLAN-C1 continues as post-contest hardening | No |\n22-| [DEC-14](#dec-14-free-text-on-the-command-line) | Free text on the command line | Explicit `nexus run` required | No |\n23-| [DEC-15](#dec-15-knowledge-auto-extraction) | Knowledge auto-extraction | Off by default, opt-in | No |\n24-| [DEC-16](#dec-16-standalone-qualification-under-a-gateway-only-environment) | Standalone qualification with no direct worker access | Stripping proxy over the gateway for live runs, plus server-kind conformance fixtures | No |\n25-| [DEC-17](#dec-17-token-estimator-floor-versus-the-calibration-band) | Token-estimator floor vs the ACC-VER-07 calibration band | The REQ-AGT-118 ≥ 1 token/char floor takes precedence for merging scripts; the resulting over-estimate is an accepted, bounded bias | No |\n26-\n27----\n28-\n29-## DEC-01: Default execution posture\n30-\n31-**Question.** What protects the user by default from model-initiated command execution and network egress? See SEC-01, VER-01, HIST-05 and TUI-07.\n32-\n--\n111-\n112-**Rationale.** These figures are the pilot's pre-registered thresholds (eval/README), tightened where the pilot showed weakness: false VERIFIED, crash accounting. The absolute floor prevents \"beat a weak peer\" from passing. Thresholds are fixed **before** the RC run.\n113-\n114:## DEC-06: Supported providers for v1\n115-\n116-| Tier | Providers | Condition |\n117-|---|---|---|\n118-| **Supported** | OpenAI-compatible local servers (llama.cpp server, vLLM, LM Studio, Ollama) | The release notes name the server kinds that pass the standalone matrix (≥ 2 required). Others are listed as \"compatible, not qualified\". |\n119-| **Supported (optional integration)** | homelab-ai gateway | Never required (standalone gate). |\n120-| **Supported** | OpenRouter | Live-verified 2026-10-14 at db1ca55 (`evidence/live/verify_openrouter.json`); re-verify at RC with a **pinned** model (not `openrouter/free`). |\n121-| **Experimental → Supported if live-verified at RC** | OpenAI API key (Responses), Anthropic (Messages), generic compatible cloud | Not connected on the owner's install. They stay experimental unless keys are added and `nexus providers verify` passes at RC. |\n122-| **Experimental (always)** | ChatGPT sign-in (the owner's OpenAI OAuth connection), Copilot sign-in | They use unofficial OAuth flows with terms-of-service and stability risk. Opt-in with a visible warning. ChatGPT sign-in was live-verified on 2026-10-14 (`evidence/live/verify_chatgpt.json`), and a live end-to-end run reached a correct VERIFIED (`evidence/live/run1_chatgpt_bugfix.log`). It is still labelled experimental because the sign-in flow is unofficial. |\n123-\n124-## DEC-07: Experimental surfaces (`nexus eval`, `/tdd`, team roles)\n125-\n126-- **`nexus eval`.** Labelled experimental. Its scoring is not fixed in v1, but its unsafe `git checkout` in the operator's workspace **is** fixed: it must run in a worktree (VER-07a). It is excluded from all claims. The SPEC-10 harness (`eval/`) is the qualification tool.\n127-- **`/tdd` / `--tdd`.** Labelled experimental. Fixing the phase enforcement is post-v1.\n128-- **Team roles.** Reviewer and researcher units run with a **read-only tool set** (cheap and safety-relevant). Other role allowlists are post-v1.\n129-\n130-## DEC-08: Version identity and stale v1.x tags\n131-\n132-- `package.json` is the single source of truth. `scripts/sync-version.mjs` updates `cli/package.json` and `core/Cargo.toml`. Release CI asserts that all three equal the tag.\n--\n243-| X1 | ~~`git tag -d v1.1.0 v1.2.0 v1.2.1`~~ **Done by the owner on 2026-10-14.** Verified: `git tag -l` now lists only `v0.1.0-alpha.1` and `v0.1.0-alpha.2`. | DEC-08 | Done |\n244-| X2 | ~~Provide an independent task author~~. **Resolved 2026-10-14 (T2) and 2026-10-18 (T3):** agent authorship authorized and completed for both T2 (`eval/heldout-manifest.json`, sha256 `50895b84…`, 40 tasks) and T3 (`eval/heldout-t3-manifest.json`, sha256 `85fb9caf…`, 8 tasks), each sealed under root-owned `0700` custody. | DEC-05 | Done |\n245-| X3 | ~~Separate standalone host~~. **Withdrawn:** no worker or GPU is available apart from the gateway. Replaced by DEC-16 (stripping proxy plus conformance fixtures). Remaining action: none. Optional: approve a CPU-only llama.cpp container on the dev box for the protocol smoke test. | DEC-16 | — |\n246:| X4 | **Partly resolved 2026-10-14:** the existing ChatGPT sign-in and OpenRouter connections are authorized for small-spend checks; both were live-verified at db1ca55. Optional: add OpenAI API-key or Anthropic keys if those providers should be listed as supported. | DEC-06 | M5 (optional) |\n247-| X5 | Independent reviewer for continuity/compaction acceptance and RC acceptance | REQ-AGT-110, ACCEPTANCE §8 | M5/M6 |\n248-| X6 | Provide a clean Cloudflare account and VM for CON-106; judging is over, so the historical erratum check is no longer applicable | DEC-13 | Post-contest |\n249-| X7 | **Authorized by the owner in the implementation/release handoff, reaffirmed by the 2026-10-18 takeover instruction.** Necessary commits, pushes, PRs, merges, RC tags and final v1.0.0 publication are authorized, conditional on the existing checks and acceptance gates. Release publisher: `codex-api-root`, succeeding rate-limited `claude-code`; no duplicate publisher. See [authorization and handoff](../reviews/evidence/v1/RELEASE-TAKEOVER/authorization-and-handoff.md). | Release | Authorization resolved; execution remains gated |\n250-| X8 | Decide whether to clean the 52k test-polluted records in the real `~/.nexus/tasks` (PER-03). Safe to remove: `task-*.json` whose `workspacePath` starts with `/tmp/nexus-app-test-`. | Hygiene | Any time |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023.json:46:  \"qualification_status\": \"partial; OpenRouter verification and its required live task remain outstanding. This record does not establish overall RC acceptance.\"\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023T1659Z.json:95:  \"qualificationDisposition\": \"Provider verification passed for ChatGPT sign-in and one explicitly pinned OpenRouter model. The separate required live engineering task per ACCEPTANCE.md §4.3 remains incomplete; this record does not establish overall RC acceptance.\",\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":699892817}},"started_at_ms":1792843072205,"completed_at_ms":1792843072906}}
