{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T13:30:09.107Z","ordinal":290139,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016adcb2e0104481a0b4ae94441e63c640","status":"completed","call_id":"call_9290f2413a6b468a80aa9bc9b58ac0a7","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"gh pr view 193 --json state,mergedAt,mergeCommit,closedAt,url,title,body --jq '{state,mergedAt,mergeCommit,closedAt,url,title,body}' && for f in /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/RC3_PROVIDER_MATRIX/owner.json /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/RC3_PROVIDER_MATRIX/claim.json; do if test -f \\\"$f\\\"; then cat \\\"$f\\\"; fi; done && find /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims -maxdepth 2 -name owner.json -print | wc -l\",\"workdir\":\"/home/mike/nexus-code\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":2500}); text(r.output)\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16e19-0589-7f73-b64e-a1d03ef4175b","create_time":1792848608.0659702}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T13:30:09.159Z","ordinal":290140,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16e19-0589-7f73-b64e-a1d03ef4175b","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a16e19-0589-7f73-b64e-a1d03ef4175b","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016adcb2d9efd081a08fc03405643ac042","usage":{"input_tokens":83920,"cached_input_tokens":83328,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":601,"reasoning_output_tokens":415,"total_tokens":84521},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":621695,"cached_input_tokens":602112,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":3112,"reasoning_output_tokens":1931,"total_tokens":624807},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":5261108207,"cached_input_tokens":5205230720,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":14579879,"reasoning_output_tokens":8274371,"total_tokens":5275688086}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T13:30:10.698Z","ordinal":290141,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16e19-0589-7f73-b64e-a1d03ef4175b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-a3cb5d90-5647-4c64-af50-6ad0057c2069","process_id":"79548","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 193 --json state,mergedAt,mergeCommit,closedAt,url,title,body --jq '{state,mergedAt,mergeCommit,closedAt,url,title,body}' && for f in /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/RC3_PROVIDER_MATRIX/owner.json /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/RC3_PROVIDER_MATRIX/claim.json; do if test -f \"$f\"; then cat \"$f\"; fi; done && find /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims -maxdepth 2 -name owner.json -print | wc -l"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 193 --json state,mergedAt,mergeCommit,closedAt,url,title,body --jq '{state,mergedAt,mergeCommit,closedAt,url,title,body}' && for f in /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/RC3_PROVIDER_MATRIX/owner.json /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/RC3_PROVIDER_MATRIX/claim.json; do if test -f \"$f\"; then cat \"$f\"; fi; done && find /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims -maxdepth 2 -name owner.json -print | wc -l"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"body\":\"## Defect\\n\\n`McpClientManager.addServer` persisted `~/.config/nexus/mcp.json` with the default `0644` mode and a `0755` directory, while a server definition's `env` may carry its own token. It also parsed the existing config inside `catch {}`, so an unparseable file was treated as empty and replaced — silently dropping every other server — and the caller was still told \\\"Saved\\\".\\n\\nPre-fix probe: mode `644`, dir `755`, existing `keep` server gone after adding a server to a config with a trailing comma.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n- `~/.config/nexus` is created/tightened to `0700`; the config is written to a `0600` temporary file and renamed atomically (following an existing symlink target).\\n- Existing config is parsed and validated first; a non-object or unparseable file is left byte-for-byte untouched.\\n- `addServer` returns `persisted`/`persistError`; the REPL wizard and `/mcp add` report the failure instead of claiming the config was saved.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- New `cli/test/mcp.test.ts`: 2/2; pre-fix fails with `config mode 644 leaks a server token` and with the overwritten-config assertion.\\n- `workspace_trust.test.ts` + new tests: 7/7; `tsc`; `git diff --check`.\\n- Evidence: `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-MCP-CONFIG-PERSIST-20261024/README.md`.\\n\\n## Residuals\\n\\nUnchmod-able config directory fails closed; a dangling symlink is replaced; an unparseable config must be fixed by the operator before persisting.\\n\\n## Coordination\\n\\nUnclaimed slice; independent review and exact-head CI to follow.\",\"closedAt\":\"2026-10-24T13:29:15Z\",\"mergeCommit\":{\"oid\":\"be2cd2f255414f554572c86baa884d9271ff5ea1\"},\"mergedAt\":\"2026-10-24T13:29:15Z\",\"state\":\"MERGED\",\"title\":\"fix(mcp): save server config owner-only and never clobber it\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/193\"}\n66\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":401360035}},"started_at_ms":1792848610296,"completed_at_ms":1792848610698}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T13:30:11.755Z","ordinal":290142,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a16e1a-c9ab-7992-8059-d5e451857128","call_id":"call_9290f2413a6b468a80aa9bc9b58ac0a7","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"body\":\"## Defect\\n\\n`McpClientManager.addServer` persisted `~/.config/nexus/mcp.json` with the default `0644` mode and a `0755` directory, while a server definition's `env` may carry its own token. It also parsed the existing config inside `catch {}`, so an unparseable file was treated as empty and replaced — silently dropping every other server — and the caller was still told \\\"Saved\\\".\\n\\nPre-fix probe: mode `644`, dir `755`, existing `keep` server gone after adding a server to a config with a trailing comma.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n- `~/.config/nexus` is created/tightened to `0700`; the config is written to a `0600` temporary file and renamed atomically (following an existing symlink target).\\n- Existing config is parsed and validated first; a non-object or unparseable file is left byte-for-byte untouched.\\n- `addServer` returns `persisted`/`persistError`; the REPL wizard and `/mcp add` report the failure instead of claiming the config was saved.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- New `cli/test/mcp.test.ts`: 2/2; pre-fix fails with `config mode 644 leaks a server token` and with the overwritten-config assertion.\\n- `workspace_trust.test.ts` + new tests: 7/7; `tsc`; `git diff --check`.\\n- Evidence: `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-MCP-CONFIG-PERSIST-20261024/README.md`.\\n\\n## Residuals\\n\\nUnchmod-able config directory fails closed; a dangling symlink is replaced; an unparseable config must be fixed by the operator before persisting.\\n\\n## Coordination\\n\\nUnclaimed slice; independent review and exact-head CI to follow.\",\"closedAt\":\"2026-10-24T13:29:15Z\",\"mergeCommit\":{\"oid\":\"be2cd2f255414f554572c86baa884d9271ff5ea1\"},\"mergedAt\":\"2026-10-24T13:29:15Z\",\"state\":\"MERGED\",\"title\":\"fix(mcp): save server config owner-only and never clobber it\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/193\"}\n66\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16e19-0589-7f73-b64e-a1d03ef4175b","create_time":1792848611.7550895}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
