{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T13:31:35.467Z","ordinal":290224,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16e19-0589-7f73-b64e-a1d03ef4175b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-4f163490-7b5c-4826-89fa-398e6a4082d6","process_id":"53822","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '145,235p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/README.md | rg -n -C 2 'terminal|T2|T3|T4|held-out|custod|G6|provider'; git show origin/main:cli/src/startup_trust.ts | sed -n '1,240p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/repro-download-action","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '145,235p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/README.md | rg -n -C 2 'terminal|T2|T3|T4|held-out|custod|G6|provider'; git show origin/main:cli/src/startup_trust.ts | sed -n '1,240p'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"| P-ollama | Emulated `/api/show` and Ollama overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `ollama_show` |\n| Conformance | CI fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama shapes | CI | All pass (ACC-INF-01, -02, -05) |\n\nACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\n\n### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n\n| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\n|---|---|---|\n| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\n| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\n| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\n| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\n\n## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n\n### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\n\nThese must pass:\n\n- `tui_approval_input_e2e`\n- `tui_diff_e2e`\n- `tui_maturity_e2e`\n- `tui_model_picker_e2e`\n- `tui_multiline_e2e`\n- `tui_surface_e2e`\n- new: `repl_approval_e2e`\n- new: `process_lifecycle_e2e`\n- new: `startup_unreachable_e2e`\n- new: the package PTY smoke\n\n### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\n\nThese are ports of `evidence/D_pty/`.\n\n| Scenario | Pass condition |\n|---|---|\n| s1 startup, unreachable endpoint | The endpoint is named, with a fix hint. The turn ends with guidance in ≤ 2.5 min. |\n| s2 approval under continuous typing, paste and burst, at 40×14 | No decision is made by stray input. A deliberate key decides. |\n| s3 completion | The outcome is shown in words: VERIFIED, REGRESSION_FREE or UNVERIFIED. |\n| s4–s6 cancel and steer | Cancel is acknowledged within 1 frame and idle within 5 s. Steering is applied. |\n| s7 resume | The prior conversation is shown. |\n| s8–s9 cancel or quit during a tool | Zero surviving processes. |\n| r1a / r1d REPL approvals | DENIED for a lone Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\n\n### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n\nTerminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\n\nFor each terminal × size, check:\n\n1. Launch `nexus` (the TUI appears).\n2. Approval panel. Type continuously across it. Paste 3 lines. Approve with a deliberate key.\n3. Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter multiline.\n4. Resize during streaming.\n5. Esc during `sleep 30` (no survivors).\n6. Ctrl-C twice (clean terminal restore: echo on, no stray escape codes).\n7. NO_COLOR.\n\nRecord PASS/FAIL per cell, with a screenshot of the approval panel and the post-exit terminal state.\n\n**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\n\n## 6. Task-quality qualification (REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-109)\n\nEnvironment: E4 (gateway direct), serial runs, with matched model fingerprint, budgets and env (REQ-QUAL-102).\n\n### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\n\n- 40 sealed tasks. The manifest is committed before RC1, and authorship is recorded (agent-authored, DEC-05).\n- 5 runs × {Nexus RC, Goose, OpenCode}.\n- Before execution, freeze three qualification configs at `eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json`, `eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json`, and `eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json`. Each must set `qualification: true`, identify the same model fingerprint and sampling settings, and record equal context/output and task budgets; the Nexus config must identify the installed RC and its package digest. Do not derive these files from the pilot configs by silently inheriting or changing settings.\n- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\n- Run each config serially, with identical task selection and five runs per task:\n\n  ```bash\n  set -euo pipefail\n  : \"${T2_TASKS:?set the sealed task directory}\"\n  : \"${T2_OUT:?set a new unique output directory}\"\n  test ! -e \"$T2_OUT\"\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/nexus\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/goose\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/opencode\" --runs 5\n  node eval/score.mjs --pairs \"$T2_OUT/nexus/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/goose/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/opencode/results.jsonl\"\n  ```\n\n  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\n\n### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\n\n9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\n3-This package is the evidence-based path from `v0.1.0-alpha.2` (audited at `db1ca55`, 2026-10-14) to v1.0.0.\n4-\n5:**Verdict: v1.0.0 readiness is BLOCKED.** Candidate source revision `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a` passed an isolated `make build` and full `make test` run on 2026-10-16 (Rust 281/281; CLI 1087/1087; zero skipped). This is source-suite evidence, not RC qualification. Held-out task quality, T3/T4 qualification, standalone/provider qualification, the manual terminal matrix, package/install matrix on the RC, and independent RC acceptance remain incomplete. See [the current readiness reconciliation](READINESS.md) for exact open requirements and gates. The contest entry remains a separate track; judging has concluded and no contest freeze applies.\n6-\n7-## How to read it\n--\n27-| 03 | Untrusted workspace inputs and egress boundary | [SPEC-03](specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md) | [PLAN-03](plans/PLAN-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md) | M1 | SEC-110, 111, 115, 116 |\n28-| 04 | Continuity, resume, durable work units | [SPEC-04](specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md) | [PLAN-04](plans/PLAN-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md) | M3 | AGT-101, 102 |\n29:| 05 | Standalone local inference and provider robustness | [SPEC-05](specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | [PLAN-05](plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | M3/M5 | PRV-101, 102, 106 |\n30-| 06 | Packaged product parity, launcher, versioning, doctor | [SPEC-06](specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md) | [PLAN-06](plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md) | M0/M2 | REL-101, 102, 103 |\n31-| 07 | Supply chain, compliance, release engineering | [SPEC-07](specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md) | [PLAN-07](plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md) | M2 | REL-107 |\nimport * as fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport * as path from \"node:path\";\nimport * as readline from \"node:readline\";\nimport { getProjectRules } from \"./git.js\";\nimport { isWorkspaceTrusted, setWorkspaceTrusted } from \"./workspace_trust.js\";\n\nexport type WorkspaceTrustDecision = \"trusted\" | \"untrusted\" | \"exit\";\n\nexport type TrustPromptInput = NodeJS.ReadStream;\n\nexport type TrustPromptOutput = NodeJS.WriteStream;\n\nexport interface TrustPromptOptions {\n  input?: TrustPromptInput;\n  output?: TrustPromptOutput;\n  trustStore?: {\n    isTrusted: (workspace: string) => boolean;\n    trust: (workspace: string) => unknown;\n  };\n}\n\nconst PROJECT_INSTRUCTION_FILES = [\"AGENTS.md\", \"CLAUDE.md\", \"CODEX.md\", \".nexusrules\"];\n\nfunction projectInstructionFile(workspace: string): string | undefined {\n  return PROJECT_INSTRUCTION_FILES.find((name) => fs.existsSync(path.join(workspace, name)));\n}\n\nfunction safeTerminalText(value: string): string {\n  return value.replace(/[\\u0000-\\u001f\\u007f-\\u009f\\p{Cf}]/gu, \"�\");\n}\n\nfunction codePointCellWidth(character: string): number {\n  const codePoint = character.codePointAt(0)!;\n  if (character === \"\\u200d\" || /[\\p{Mark}\\p{Format}]/u.test(character)) return 0;\n  if (\n    codePoint >= 0x1100 && (\n      codePoint <= 0x115f || codePoint === 0x2329 || codePoint === 0x232a ||\n      (codePoint >= 0x2e80 && codePoint <= 0xa4cf && codePoint !== 0x303f) ||\n      (codePoint >= 0xac00 && codePoint <= 0xd7a3) ||\n      (codePoint >= 0xf900 && codePoint <= 0xfaff) ||\n      (codePoint >= 0xfe10 && codePoint <= 0xfe19) ||\n      (codePoint >= 0xfe30 && codePoint <= 0xfe6f) ||\n      (codePoint >= 0xff00 && codePoint <= 0xff60) ||\n      (codePoint >= 0xffe0 && codePoint <= 0xffe6) ||\n      (codePoint >= 0x1f000 && codePoint <= 0x1faff) ||\n      (codePoint >= 0x20000 && codePoint <= 0x3fffd)\n    )\n  ) return 2;\n  return 1;\n}\n\nfunction terminalCellWidth(value: string): number {\n  const segmenter = new Intl.Segmenter(undefined, { granularity: \"grapheme\" });\n  let width = 0;\n  for (const { segment } of segmenter.segment(value)) {\n    width += Math.max(0, ...[...segment].map(codePointCellWidth));\n  }\n  return width;\n}\n\nfunction fitTerminalText(value: string, maxWidth: number): string {\n  if (terminalCellWidth(value) <= maxWidth) return value;\n  const segments = [...new Intl.Segmenter(undefined, { granularity: \"grapheme\" }).segment(value)].map(({ segment }) => segment);\n  const suffix: string[] = [];\n  let width = 1; // reserve one cell for the leading ellipsis\n  for (let index = segments.length - 1; index >= 0; index--) {\n    const segment = segments[index];\n    const segmentWidth = terminalCellWidth(segment);\n    if (width + segmentWidth > maxWidth) break;\n    suffix.unshift(segment);\n    width += segmentWidth;\n  }\n  return `…${suffix.join(\"\")}`;\n}\n\n/** Project instructions are untrusted workspace input and are injected only after the operator explicitly trusts it. */\nexport function trustedProjectRules(\n  workspace: string,\n  isTrusted: (workspace: string) => boolean = isWorkspaceTrusted,\n): string | null {\n  return isTrusted(workspace) ? getProjectRules(workspace) : null;\n}\n\n/**\n * Ask for explicit trust before starting an interactive Nexus client. Non-interactive launches continue under the\n * existing untrusted-workspace policy and never persist trust implicitly.\n */\nexport function promptWorkspaceTrust(\n  workspace: string,\n  options: TrustPromptOptions = {},\n): Promise<WorkspaceTrustDecision> {\n  const input = options.input ?? process.stdin;\n  const output = options.output ?? process.stdout;\n  const noticeOutput = options.output ?? process.stderr;\n  const trustStore = options.trustStore ?? {\n    isTrusted: isWorkspaceTrusted,\n    trust: (target: string) => setWorkspaceTrusted(target, true),\n  };\n  const resolvedWorkspace = path.resolve(workspace);\n  const displayWorkspace = safeTerminalText(resolvedWorkspace);\n\n  if (trustStore.isTrusted(resolvedWorkspace)) return Promise.resolve(\"trusted\");\n  if (!input.isTTY || !output.isTTY) {\n    noticeOutput.write(\n      `Nexus: ${displayWorkspace} is not trusted. Project instructions and workspace integrations stay unloaded. ` +\n      `Run 'nexus trust .' to trust this folder; untrusted workspaces default to review mode.\\n`,\n    );\n    return Promise.resolve(\"untrusted\");\n  }\n\n  const instructionFile = projectInstructionFile(resolvedWorkspace);\n  const optionsText = [\n    \"Trust and continue\",\n    \"Continue without trusting\",\n    \"Exit\",\n  ];\n  const selected = 0;\n  const oldRawMode = Boolean(input.isRaw);\n\n  return new Promise((resolve) => {\n    let choice = selected;\n    let complete = false;\n    let statusMessage: string | undefined;\n\n    const render = () => {\n      const width = Math.max(32, output.columns ?? 80);\n      const fit = (value: string) => fitTerminalText(value, width);\n      const projectFile = instructionFile ? `Check: ${instructionFile}` : \"No project instruction file found\";\n      const rows = optionsText.map((text, index) => `${choice === index ? \"›\" : \" \"} ${text}`);\n      output.write([\n        \"\\u001b[2J\\u001b[H\",\n        \"Trust this folder?\",\n        \"↑↓ navigate · Enter select · Esc exit\",\n        fit(displayWorkspace),\n        \"Load project instructions\",\n        fit(projectFile),\n        \"Trust saved for future workspace files.\",\n        \"Rules/integrations require trust.\",\n        \"Default mode follows trust.\",\n        \"Trusted: auto · untrusted: review\",\n        \"Explicit mode still applies.\",\n        ...(statusMessage ? [fit(statusMessage)] : []),\n        \"\",\n        ...rows,\n      ].join(\"\\n\"));\n    };\n\n    const finish = (decision: WorkspaceTrustDecision) => {\n      if (complete) return;\n      complete = true;\n      input.removeListener(\"keypress\", onKeypress);\n      input.removeListener(\"close\", onClose);\n      try { input.setRawMode(oldRawMode); } catch {}\n      if (decision === \"exit\") {\n        try { input.pause(); } catch {}\n      }\n      output.write(\"\\u001b[?25h\\n\");\n      resolve(decision);\n    };\n\n    const onClose = () => finish(\"exit\");\n    const onKeypress = (_character: string | undefined, key: readline.Key) => {\n      if (key?.ctrl && key.name === \"c\") return finish(\"exit\");\n      if (key?.name === \"escape\") return finish(\"exit\");\n      if (key?.name === \"up\") {\n        choice = (choice + optionsText.length - 1) % optionsText.length;\n        render();\n        return;\n      }\n      if (key?.name === \"down\") {\n        choice = (choice + 1) % optionsText.length;\n        render();\n        return;\n      }\n      if (key?.name !== \"return\" && key?.name !== \"enter\") return;\n      if (choice === 0) {\n        try {\n          trustStore.trust(resolvedWorkspace);\n          finish(\"trusted\");\n        } catch (error) {\n          statusMessage = `Trust was not saved: ${safeTerminalText(String((error as Error)?.message ?? error))}`;\n          render();\n        }\n      } else if (choice === 1) {\n        finish(\"untrusted\");\n      } else {\n        finish(\"exit\");\n      }\n    };\n\n    readline.emitKeypressEvents(input);\n    input.on(\"keypress\", onKeypress);\n    input.once(\"close\", onClose);\n    try {\n      input.setRawMode(true);\n      input.resume();\n      output.write(\"\\u001b[?25l\");\n      render();\n    } catch {\n      finish(\"exit\");\n      output.write(`Nexus: could not open the trust prompt. Run 'nexus trust .' or restart in an interactive terminal.\\n`);\n    }\n  });\n}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":728559414}},"started_at_ms":1792848694735,"completed_at_ms":1792848695464}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T13:31:36.431Z","ordinal":290225,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a16e1c-146f-7e12-96b2-6a73d704880c","call_id":"call_1d31d99592a341fc839bcf110ad3ea26","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.8 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"| P-ollama | Emulated `/api/show` and Ollama overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `ollama_show` |\n| Conformance | CI fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama shapes | CI | All pass (ACC-INF-01, -02, -05) |\n\nACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\n\n### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n\n| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\n|---|---|---|\n| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\n| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\n| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\n| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\n\n## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n\n### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\n\nThese must pass:\n\n- `tui_approval_input_e2e`\n- `tui_diff_e2e`\n- `tui_maturity_e2e`\n- `tui_model_picker_e2e`\n- `tui_multiline_e2e`\n- `tui_surface_e2e`\n- new: `repl_approval_e2e`\n- new: `process_lifecycle_e2e`\n- new: `startup_unreachable_e2e`\n- new: the package PTY smoke\n\n### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\n\nThese are ports of `evidence/D_pty/`.\n\n| Scenario | Pass condition |\n|---|---|\n| s1 startup, unreachable endpoint | The endpoint is named, with a fix hint. The turn ends with guidance in ≤ 2.5 min. |\n| s2 approval under continuous typing, paste and burst, at 40×14 | No decision is made by stray input. A deliberate key decides. |\n| s3 completion | The outcome is shown in words: VERIFIED, REGRESSION_FREE or UNVERIFIED. |\n| s4–s6 cancel and steer | Cancel is acknowledged within 1 frame and idle within 5 s. Steering is applied. |\n| s7 resume | The prior conversation is shown. |\n| s8–s9 cancel or quit during a tool | Zero surviving processes. |\n| r1a / r1d REPL approvals | DENIED for a lone Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\n\n### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n\nTerminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\n\nFor each terminal × size, check:\n\n1. Launch `nexus` (the TUI appears).\n2. Approval panel. Type continuously across it. Paste 3 lines. Approve with a deliberate key.\n3. Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter multiline.\n4. Resize during streaming.\n5. Esc during `sleep 30` (no survivors).\n6. Ctrl-C twice (clean terminal restore: echo on, no stray escape codes).\n7. NO_COLOR.\n\nRecord PASS/FAIL per cell, with a screenshot of the approval panel and the post-exit terminal state.\n\n**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\n\n## 6. Task-quality qualification (REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-109)\n\nEnvironment: E4 (gateway direct), serial runs, with matched model fingerprint, budgets and env (REQ-QUAL-102).\n\n### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\n\n- 40 sealed tasks. The manifest is committed before RC1, and authorship is recorded (agent-authored, DEC-05).\n- 5 runs × {Nexus RC, Goose, OpenCode}.\n- Before execution, freeze three qualification configs at `eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json`, `eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json`, and `eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json`. Each must set `qualification: true`, identify the same model fingerprint and sampling settings, and record equal context/output and task budgets; the Nexus config must identify the installed RC and its package digest. Do not derive these files from the pilot configs by silently inheriting or changing settings.\n- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\n- Run each config serially, with identical task selection and five runs per task:\n\n  ```bash\n  set -euo pipefail\n  : \"${T2_TASKS:?set the sealed task directory}\"\n  : \"${T2_OUT:?set a new unique output directory}\"\n  test ! -e \"$T2_OUT\"\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/nexus\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/goose\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/opencode\" --runs 5\n  node eval/score.mjs --pairs \"$T2_OUT/nexus/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/goose/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/opencode/results.jsonl\"\n  ```\n\n  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\n\n### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\n\n9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\n3-This package is the evidence-based path from `v0.1.0-alpha.2` (audited at `db1ca55`, 2026-10-14) to v1.0.0.\n4-\n5:**Verdict: v1.0.0 readiness is BLOCKED.** Candidate source revision `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a` passed an isolated `make build` and full `make test` run on 2026-10-16 (Rust 281/281; CLI 1087/1087; zero skipped). This is source-suite evidence, not RC qualification. Held-out task quality, T3/T4 qualification, standalone/provider qualification, the manual terminal matrix, package/install matrix on the RC, and independent RC acceptance remain incomplete. See [the current readiness reconciliation](READINESS.md) for exact open requirements and gates. The contest entry remains a separate track; judging has concluded and no contest freeze applies.\n6-\n7-## How to read it\n--\n27-| 03 | Untrusted workspace inputs and egress boundary | [SPEC-03](specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md) | [PLAN-03](plans/PLAN-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md) | M1 | SEC-110, 111, 115, 116 |\n28-| 04 | Continuity, resume, durable work units | [SPEC-04](specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md) | [PLAN-04](plans/PLAN-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md) | M3 | AGT-101, 102 |\n29:| 05 | Standalone local inference and provider robustness | [SPEC-05](specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | [PLAN-05](plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | M3/M5 | PRV-101, 102, 106 |\n30-| 06 | Packaged product parity, launcher, versioning, doctor | [SPEC-06](specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md) | [PLAN-06](plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md) | M0/M2 | REL-101, 102, 103 |\n31-| 07 | Supply chain, compliance, release engineering | [SPEC-07](specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md) | [PLAN-07](plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md) | M2 | REL-107 |\nimport * as fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport * as path from \"node:path\";\nimport * as readline from \"node:readline\";\nimport { getProjectRules } from \"./git.js\";\nimport { isWorkspaceTrusted, setWorkspaceTrusted } from \"./workspace_trust.js\";\n\nexport type WorkspaceTrustDecision = \"trusted\" | \"untrusted\" | \"exit\";\n\nexport type TrustPromptInput = NodeJS.ReadStream;\n\nexport type TrustPromptOutput = NodeJS.WriteStream;\n\nexport interface TrustPromptOptions {\n  input?: TrustPromptInput;\n  output?: TrustPromptOutput;\n  trustStore?: {\n    isTrusted: (workspace: string) => boolean;\n    trust: (workspace: string) => unknown;\n  };\n}\n\nconst PROJECT_INSTRUCTION_FILES = [\"AGENTS.md\", \"CLAUDE.md\", \"CODEX.md\", \".nexusrules\"];\n\nfunction projectInstructionFile(workspace: string): string | undefined {\n  return PROJECT_INSTRUCTION_FILES.find((name) => fs.existsSync(path.join(workspace, name)));\n}\n\nfunction safeTerminalText(value: string): string {\n  return value.replace(/[\\u0000-\\u001f\\u007f-\\u009f\\p{Cf}]/gu, \"�\");\n}\n\nfunction codePointCellWidth(character: string): number {\n  const codePoint = character.codePointAt(0)!;\n  if (character === \"\\u200d\" || /[\\p{Mark}\\p{Format}]/u.test(character)) return 0;\n  if (\n    codePoint >= 0x1100 && (\n      codePoint <= 0x115f || codePoint === 0x2329 || codePoint === 0x232a ||\n      (codePoint >= 0x2e80 && codePoint <= 0xa4cf && codePoint !== 0x303f) ||\n      (codePoint >= 0xac00 && codePoint <= 0xd7a3) ||\n      (codePoint >= 0xf900 && codePoint <= 0xfaff) ||\n      (codePoint >= 0xfe10 && codePoint <= 0xfe19) ||\n      (codePoint >= 0xfe30 && codePoint <= 0xfe6f) ||\n      (codePoint >= 0xff00 && codePoint <= 0xff60) ||\n      (codePoint >= 0xffe0 && codePoint <= 0xffe6) ||\n      (codePoint >= 0x1f000 && codePoint <= 0x1faff) ||\n      (codePoint >= 0x20000 && codePoint <= 0x3fffd)\n    )\n  ) return 2;\n  return 1;\n}\n\nfunction terminalCellWidth(value: string): number {\n  const segmenter = new Intl.Segmenter(undefined, { granularity: \"grapheme\" });\n  let width = 0;\n  for (const { segment } of segmenter.segment(value)) {\n    width += Math.max(0, ...[...segment].map(codePointCellWidth));\n  }\n  return width;\n}\n\nfunction fitTerminalText(value: string, maxWidth: number): string {\n  if (terminalCellWidth(value) <= maxWidth) return value;\n  const segments = [...new Intl.Segmenter(undefined, { granularity: \"grapheme\" }).segment(value)].map(({ segment }) => segment);\n  const suffix: string[] = [];\n  let width = 1; // reserve one cell for the leading ellipsis\n  for (let index = segments.length - 1; index >= 0; index--) {\n    const segment = segments[index];\n    const segmentWidth = terminalCellWidth(segment);\n    if (width + segmentWidth > maxWidth) break;\n    suffix.unshift(segment);\n    width += segmentWidth;\n  }\n  return `…${suffix.join(\"\")}`;\n}\n\n/** Project instructions are untrusted workspace input and are injected only after the operator explicitly trusts it. */\nexport function trustedProjectRules(\n  workspace: string,\n  isTrusted: (workspace: string) => boolean = isWorkspaceTrusted,\n): string | null {\n  return isTrusted(workspace) ? getProjectRules(workspace) : null;\n}\n\n/**\n * Ask for explicit trust before starting an interactive Nexus client. Non-interactive launches continue under the\n * existing untrusted-workspace policy and never persist trust implicitly.\n */\nexport function promptWorkspaceTrust(\n  workspace: string,\n  options: TrustPromptOptions = {},\n): Promise<WorkspaceTrustDecision> {\n  const input = options.input ?? process.stdin;\n  const output = options.output ?? process.stdout;\n  const noticeOutput = options.output ?? process.stderr;\n  const trustStore = options.trustStore ?? {\n    isTrusted: isWorkspaceTrusted,\n    trust: (target: string) => setWorkspaceTrusted(target, true),\n  };\n  const resolvedWorkspace = path.resolve(workspace);\n  const displayWorkspace = safeTerminalText(resolvedWorkspace);\n\n  if (trustStore.isTrusted(resolvedWorkspace)) return Promise.resolve(\"trusted\");\n  if (!input.isTTY || !output.isTTY) {\n    noticeOutput.write(\n      `Nexus: ${displayWorkspace} is not trusted. Project instructions and workspace integrations stay unloaded. ` +\n      `Run 'nexus trust .' to trust this folder; untrusted workspaces default to review mode.\\n`,\n    );\n    return Promise.resolve(\"untrusted\");\n  }\n\n  const instructionFile = projectInstructionFile(resolvedWorkspace);\n  const optionsText = [\n    \"Trust and continue\",\n    \"Continue without trusting\",\n    \"Exit\",\n  ];\n  const selected = 0;\n  const oldRawMode = Boolean(input.isRaw);\n\n  return new Promise((resolve) => {\n    let choice = selected;\n    let complete = false;\n    let statusMessage: string | undefined;\n\n    const render = () => {\n      const width = Math.max(32, output.columns ?? 80);\n      const fit = (value: string) => fitTerminalText(value, width);\n      const projectFile = instructionFile ? `Check: ${instructionFile}` : \"No project instruction file found\";\n      const rows = optionsText.map((text, index) => `${choice === index ? \"›\" : \" \"} ${text}`);\n      output.write([\n        \"\\u001b[2J\\u001b[H\",\n        \"Trust this folder?\",\n        \"↑↓ navigate · Enter select · Esc exit\",\n        fit(displayWorkspace),\n        \"Load project instructions\",\n        fit(projectFile),\n        \"Trust saved for future workspace files.\",\n        \"Rules/integrations require trust.\",\n        \"Default mode follows trust.\",\n        \"Trusted: auto · untrusted: review\",\n        \"Explicit mode still applies.\",\n        ...(statusMessage ? [fit(statusMessage)] : []),\n        \"\",\n        ...rows,\n      ].join(\"\\n\"));\n    };\n\n    const finish = (decision: WorkspaceTrustDecision) => {\n      if (complete) return;\n      complete = true;\n      input.removeListener(\"keypress\", onKeypress);\n      input.removeListener(\"close\", onClose);\n      try { input.setRawMode(oldRawMode); } catch {}\n      if (decision === \"exit\") {\n        try { input.pause(); } catch {}\n      }\n      output.write(\"\\u001b[?25h\\n\");\n      resolve(decision);\n    };\n\n    const onClose = () => finish(\"exit\");\n    const onKeypress = (_character: string | undefined, key: readline.Key) => {\n      if (key?.ctrl && key.name === \"c\") return finish(\"exit\");\n      if (key?.name === \"escape\") return finish(\"exit\");\n      if (key?.name === \"up\") {\n        choice = (choice + optionsText.length - 1) % optionsText.length;\n        render();\n        return;\n      }\n      if (key?.name === \"down\") {\n        choice = (choice + 1) % optionsText.length;\n        render();\n        return;\n      }\n      if (key?.name !== \"return\" && key?.name !== \"enter\") return;\n      if (choice === 0) {\n        try {\n          trustStore.trust(resolvedWorkspace);\n          finish(\"trusted\");\n        } catch (error) {\n          statusMessage = `Trust was not saved: ${safeTerminalText(String((error as Error)?.message ?? error))}`;\n          render();\n        }\n      } else if (choice === 1) {\n        finish(\"untrusted\");\n      } else {\n        finish(\"exit\");\n      }\n    };\n\n    readline.emitKeypressEvents(input);\n    input.on(\"keypress\", onKeypress);\n    input.once(\"close\", onClose);\n    try {\n      input.setRawMode(true);\n      input.resume();\n      output.write(\"\\u001b[?25l\");\n      render();\n    } catch {\n      finish(\"exit\");\n      output.write(`Nexus: could not open the trust prompt. Run 'nexus trust .' or restart in an interactive terminal.\\n`);\n    }\n  });\n}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16e19-0589-7f73-b64e-a1d03ef4175b","create_time":1792848696.4317153}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
