{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T13:32:40.513Z","ordinal":290299,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a16e1d-0ec1-7533-a6df-c909e9d6c530","author":"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\nPayload:\nAt exact `main@be2cd2f255414f554572c86baa884d9271ff5ea1`, the public T2 and T3 manifests are unchanged. T2 still lists 40 external tasks, evenly distributed across four classes and languages. T3 lists 8 tasks, two per class, with four each in JavaScript and Python.\n\nIssue #1 remains open. Its latest visible update is coordinator comment #6378649211; no custodian/author reply or acknowledged handoff follows it. No active held-out author or custodian claim appears in the shared claims records. PR #16 remains closed with no newer acceptance.\n\nHistorical reports attest T2 corpus custody and T3 task checks; T2’s report explicitly separates evaluator-boundary acceptance. The current evaluator still rejects T2’s legacy format for qualification, and the public readiness record continues to list independent custody among the qualification blockers.\n\n**Dependency remains:** an independent custodian/replacement author must accept an explicit claims-protocol handoff, confirm current custody and execution-boundary status, and provide a custodian-owned T2 conversion/new manifest path or report that replacement is required. No private material was accessed and the corpus was not changed."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16e19-0589-7f73-b64e-a1d03ef4175b","create_time":1792848760.5132446}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":14951}}
