{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T13:33:38.556Z","ordinal":290350,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a16e1d-f17b-7962-8e9c-39c99f5d3feb","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — reviewed merge commit `be2cd2f255414f554572c86baa884d9271ff5ea1` against first parent `13f25f40bc3a251fafa1c08b3f6d4d9c22d463ef`.\n\n`addServer` accepts the supplied server name without filtering. In [mcp.ts](/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/mcp.ts:642), assigning `existing.mcpServers[name]` mishandles the valid name `__proto__`: it changes the object’s prototype instead of adding a JSON property. The write then succeeds and reports `persisted: true`, but the server definition is absent from the serialized config. Use a prototype-safe object/property assignment or reject that name, and add a regression.\n\nThe malformed-config preservation and user-facing failure messages look correct by source inspection. I did not run tests; the focused test results in the evidence README remain implementer-reported. I did not implement this change. The shared checkout contains unrelated dirty files, so I reviewed the exact commit tree and did not modify the worktree."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16e19-0589-7f73-b64e-a1d03ef4175b","create_time":1792848818.5558949}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":14954}}
