{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T13:34:51.823Z","ordinal":290405,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16e19-0589-7f73-b64e-a1d03ef4175b","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a16e19-0589-7f73-b64e-a1d03ef4175b","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016adcb3ed154c81a09eb6d9af74b827b6","usage":{"input_tokens":131434,"cached_input_tokens":129280,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1700,"reasoning_output_tokens":1683,"total_tokens":133134},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":3598916,"cached_input_tokens":3530368,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":22205,"reasoning_output_tokens":16409,"total_tokens":3621121},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":5264085428,"cached_input_tokens":5208158976,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":14598972,"reasoning_output_tokens":8288849,"total_tokens":5278684400}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T13:34:53.091Z","ordinal":290406,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a16e1f-14a3-75c2-82f7-2806f6677e48","call_id":"call_484b3d9bf53247f0a4910a26fb5ee8a9","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/acceptance_stage_clarification\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**Exact main:** `be2cd2f255414f554572c86baa884d9271ff5ea1`, merge of PR #193. The lifecycle remains unchanged: source checks precede RC construction; artifact-bound checks follow it; installed-RC qualification and stable promotion remain later stages ([`ACCEPTANCE.md`, lines 24–34]( /home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md)). The checker still defines bare `--enforce` as the pre-RC source gate and requires a clean worktree ([`check_requirements.mjs`, lines 5–7, 214–230]( /home/mike/nexus-code/scripts/check_requirements.mjs)).\\n\\n**Gate disposition: not yet eligible to construct RC4.** Exact-head CI run `40098339766` and CodeQL run `40098339763` are both still active. Node 22 and Node 24 have passed version sync, requirements *report mode*, build, and Rust tests; both are still building the Rust release binaries. The requirements gate in CI is not `--enforce`. `package.json` remains `1.0.0-rc.4`, but the merged commit is not itself evidence that all pre-RC gates passed.\\n\\nPR #193 has recorded `ACCEPT` review comments, but the available GitHub records show the same owner account authored the PR commits and submitted both reviews. The review text labels them “Independent Review”; the public metadata alone does not establish reviewer independence from implementation.\\n\\n**Next actionable step:** wait for both exact-head checks to finish successfully, then run bare `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` on a clean checkout of `be2cd2f`. CI already records successful version synchronization at this SHA; after the missing source gate and CI pass, the authorized RC4 tag/workflow can construct the candidate. Cross-runner reproduction remains a later artifact-bound gate, not a pre-tag prerequisite.\\n\\nNo files were changed and no checks were run locally.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"At exact `main@be2cd2f255414f554572c86baa884d9271ff5ea1`, the public T2 and T3 manifests are unchanged. T2 still lists 40 external tasks, evenly distributed across four classes and languages. T3 lists 8 tasks, two per class, with four each in JavaScript and Python.\\n\\nIssue #1 remains open. Its latest visible update is coordinator comment #6378649211; no custodian/author reply or acknowledged handoff follows it. No active held-out author or custodian claim appears in the shared claims records. PR #16 remains closed with no newer acceptance.\\n\\nHistorical reports attest T2 corpus custody and T3 task checks; T2’s report explicitly separates evaluator-boundary acceptance. The current evaluator still rejects T2’s legacy format for qualification, and the public readiness record continues to list independent custody among the qualification blockers.\\n\\n**Dependency remains:** an independent custodian/replacement author must accept an explicit claims-protocol handoff, confirm current custody and execution-boundary status, and provide a custodian-owned T2 conversion/new manifest path or report that replacement is required. No private material was accessed and the corpus was not changed.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — reviewed merge commit `be2cd2f255414f554572c86baa884d9271ff5ea1` against first parent `13f25f40bc3a251fafa1c08b3f6d4d9c22d463ef`.\\n\\n`addServer` accepts the supplied server name without filtering. In [mcp.ts](/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/mcp.ts:642), assigning `existing.mcpServers[name]` mishandles the valid name `__proto__`: it changes the object’s prototype instead of adding a JSON property. The write then succeeds and reports `persisted: true`, but the server definition is absent from the serialized config. Use a prototype-safe object/property assignment or reject that name, and add a regression.\\n\\nThe malformed-config preservation and user-facing failure messages look correct by source inspection. I did not run tests; the focused test results in the evidence README remain implementer-reported. I did not implement this change. The shared checkout contains unrelated dirty files, so I reviewed the exact commit tree and did not modify the worktree.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16e19-0589-7f73-b64e-a1d03ef4175b","create_time":1792848893.0911753}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
