/main:docs/releases/v1.0.0.md:103:### TUI Approval Panel Alignment & Narrow Terminal Polish (TUI-09, TUI-10)\norigin/main:docs/releases/v1.0.0.md:104:- **Spatial arrow key alignment (TUI-09):** Approval panel buttons are laid out horizontally: `Approve` (left) · `All later` (center) · `Deny` (right). Left arrow (`←`) focuses `Approve` on the left, and Right arrow (`→`) focuses `Deny` on the right.\norigin/main:docs/releases/v1.0.0.md:105:- **Narrow terminal compact hints (TUI-10):** Under 60 columns (e.g. 40×14 terminal), approval panel instructions switch to compact short-form hints (e.g. `←→ choose, enter · esc denies`), ensuring all directions fit without line wrapping or truncation.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/NEXUS_PARALLEL_DEFECT_INVESTIGATION_2026-10-04.md:52:(1) command `sleep 5` with deadline 1 s → reason `VERIFIER_TIMED_OUT`, partial stdout `before` preserved, elapsed ≈1 s, status ≠ FAILED/VERIFIED; (2) `exit 3` → VERIFICATION_FAILED unchanged; (3) `exit 0` → VERIFIED unchanged; (4) descendant case `(sleep 30 &) ; sleep 30` with deadline 1 s → returns in ≲ deadline+grace and `pgrep` finds no survivors; (5) bridge outer timer never fires before the runner's in (1); (6) after a timeout, the next `run_command` succeeds and no second instance of the first command is running; (7) command that cannot start → EXECUTION_FAILED; (8) operator cancel during verification → CANCELLED, not timeout.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:186:| F1 | P1 | REPRODUCED (unit) | Ordinary typing across the approval panel's appearance decides (incl. \"approve all\"); default focus Approve | `core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_state.rs:1156-1172`, `:812-822` (804c5df) |\norigin/main:docs/reviews/NEXUS_TUI_SURFACE_2026-10-12.md:77:| Approval panel: empty rows between change and buttons; \"Nexus wants to: creates\" | The panel fits its content; copy reads \"Proposed: create config.json · +1 −0\"; compact buttons below 60 columns | screen 10 |\norigin/main:docs/reviews/NEXUS_TUI_SURFACE_2026-10-12.md:198:pauses approved \"all later actions\"), `327570b` makes the PTY drivers ignore inherited `NO_COLOR`, `70ace1d` merges\norigin/main:docs/reviews/NEXUS_TUI_SURFACE_2026-10-12.md:214:| checkout = `dda2e62` | `1.2.1 (dda2e625a4e2, feat/tui-surface)` | PTY scenarios 13 runs (10 serial, 3 under 8 busy-loop processes): 91/91; `make test`: Rust 259/259, CLI 753/754 — the 256-colour check failed only because the agent shell exported `NO_COLOR` (fixed in `327570b`); `nexus doctor --deep` on the real configuration 20/20 incl. one inference request |\norigin/main:docs/reviews/NEXUS_TUI_SURFACE_2026-10-12.md:234:  bar, activity line, composer placeholder and line indicator, approval panel, cleared panel backgrounds, help\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/tools_persistence.md:187:  SIGTERM-ignoring grandchild (`exec -a nxprobeign sleep 300` with `trap \"\" TERM`) is gone 1 s after a 2 s timeout\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/tools_persistence.md:282:  `run_command sleep 30` returns within 1 s and no `sleep` survives.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/tui.md:21:The visible defects are mostly P3 polish. The two worth fixing before acceptance are in the approval panel: a mostly\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/tui.md:44:| 40x10 probe (unit render) | The approval panel shows title, subject, buttons and hint but zero diff rows. The kind line is cut (\"changes src/config/set\") without an ellipsis, and the buttons wrap across two lines (\"a Approve all later / actions n Deny\"). | P2 |\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/tui.md:80:### F1 Ordinary typing that continues across the approval panel's appearance approves, including \"approve all later actions\"\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/tui_surface/tui_surface.cast:134:[26.5815, \"o\", \"\\u001b[2;13H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u256d\\u001b[1m Help \\u001b[22m\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u256e\\u001b[3;1H\\u001b[39;49m           \\u001b[3;13H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[1m\\u001b[38;5;15;49mKeys\\u001b[3;108H\\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[4;1H\\u001b[39;49m            \\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[1m  enter            \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49msend the prompt\\u001b[39;49m                         \\u001b[4;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[5;13H\\u2502\\u001b[1m  shift+enter      \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49mnew line (alt+enter where shift is not reported)\\u001b[5;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[6;1H\\u001b[39;49m           \\u001b[6;13H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[1m  \\u2191 / \\u2193            \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49mmove between lines; recall earlier prompts from the first line\\u001b[6;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[7;1H\\u001b[39;49m            \\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[1m  ctrl+a / ctrl+e  \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49mstart / end of the line\\u001b[7;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[8;1H\\u001b[39;49m            \\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[1m  ctrl+u / ctrl+k  \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49mdelete to the start / end of the line\\u001b[8;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[9;13H\\u2502\\u001b[1m  ctrl+w           \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49mdelete the previous word\\u001b[9;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[10;1H\\u001b[39;49m            \\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[1m  ctrl+l           \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49mclear the draft\\u001b[10;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[11;1H\\u001b[39;49m            \\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[1m  paste            \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49mmulti-line or long pastes become [Pasted text #n] buffers; newlines in \\u001b[11;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[12;13H\\u2502\\u001b[12;33H\\u001b[38;5;15;49mthem never send\\u001b[12;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[13;1H\\u001b[39;49m            \\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[1m  ctrl+o           \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49mview the paste buffer at the cursor\\u001b[13;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[14;1H\\u001b[39;49m            \\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[1m  ctrl+d           \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49mreview the complete diff of the selected (or newest) edit or /diff\\u001b[14;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[15;13H\\u2502\\u001b[1m  ctrl+x           \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49medit the paste buffer at the cursor as ordinary text\\u001b[15;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[16;1H\\u001b[39;49m            \\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[1m  backspace        \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49mright after a paste buffer: remove it\\u001b[16;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[17;13H\\u2502\\u001b[1m  enter (working)  \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49msend steering: the agent applies it at its next step; esc cancels the \\u001b[17;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[18;1H\\u001b[39;49m            \\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[39;49m                   \\u001b[38;5;15;49mturn\\u001b[39;49m                                       \\u001b[18;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[19;1H\\u001b[39;49m            \\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[1m  /                \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49mslash commands: type / to list them, tab completes\\u001b[19;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[20;1H\\u001b[39;49m            \\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[1m  /model           \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49mchoose a model from the appliance or any connected cloud provider\\u001b[20;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[21;1H\\u001b[39;49m            \\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[1m  ctrl+p           \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49min /model: connect a provider (API key or sign-in); /connect opens it \\u001b[21;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[22;13H\\u2502\\u001b[22;33H\\u001b[38;5;15;49mdirectly\\u001b[22;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[23;1H\\u001b[39;49m            \\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[1m  !command         \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49mrun a shell command directly; !n runs prompt n again\\u001b[23;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[24;1H\\u001b[39;49m            \\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[1m  tab              \\u001b[24;34H\\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49mwitch\\u001b[24;40Hbetween th\\u001b[24;51H composer and the transcript\\u001b[39;49m                   \\u001b[24;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[25;13H\\u2502\\u001b[1m  pgup / pgdn      \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49mscroll the transcript\\u001b[25;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[26;1H\\u001b[39;49m            \\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[1m  ctrl+end         \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49mback to the newest output (the badge says when new output arrived)\\u001b[26;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[27;13H\\u2502\\u001b[1m  [ / ]            \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49min the transcript: select the previous / next tool call\\u001b[27;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[28;1H\\u001b[39;49m            \\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[1m  enter            \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49min the transcript: open the selected tool call's details\\u001b[28;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[29;5H\\u001b[39;49m        \\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[1m  v                \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49min the transcript: open the receipt for the last turn\\u001b[39;49m                      \\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[39;49m            \\u001b[30;13H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[30;108H\\u2502\\u001b[31;1H\\u001b[39;49m            \\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[1m\\u001b[38;5;15;49mDiff review (ctrl+d, or enter on an edit)\\u001b[22m\\u001b[39;49m                   \\u001b[31;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[32;13H\\u2502\\u001b[1m  n / p            \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49mnext / previous hunk\\u001b[32;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[33;1H\\u001b[39;49m            \\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[1m  ] / [            \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49mnext / previous edit (workspace diff: file)\\u001b[33;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[34;1H\\u001b[39;49m            \\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2570\\u001b[1m esc\\u001b[22m close  \\u001b[1m\\u2191\\u2193\\u001b[22m scroll  \\u001b[38;2;125;145;158;49m1\\u201331\\u001b[34;42Hof 92\\u001b[34;48H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u256f\\u001b[35;3H\\u001b[38;2;125;145;158;49msc close help \\u001b[38;5;8;49m\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\