  \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49min /model: connect a provider (API key or sign-in); /connect opens it direc\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[20;13H\\u2502\\u001b[1m  !command         \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49mrun a shell command directly; !n runs prompt n again\\u001b[20;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[21;13H\\u2502\\u001b[1m  tab              \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49mswitch between the composer and the transcript\\u001b[39;49m                             \\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[22;13H\\u2502\\u001b[1m  pgup / pgdn      \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49mscroll the transcript\\u001b[22;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[23;13H\\u2502\\u001b[1m  [ / ]            \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49min the transcript: select the previous / next tool call\\u001b[23;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[24;13H\\u2502\\u001b[1m  enter            \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49min the transcript: open the selected tool call's details\\u001b[24;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[25;13H\\u2502\\u001b[1m  v                \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49min the transcript: open the receipt for the last turn\\u001b[39;49m   \\u001b[25;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[26;13H\\u2502\\u001b[26;108H\\u2502\\u001b[27;13H\\u2502\\u001b[1m\\u001b[38;5;15;49mDiff review (ctrl+d, or enter on an edit)\\u001b[27;108H\\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[28;13H\\u2502\\u001b[1m  n / p            \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49mnext / previous hunk\\u001b[28;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[29;13H\\u2502\\u001b[1m  ] / [            \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49mnext / previous edit (workspace diff: file)\\u001b[29;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[30;13H\\u2502\\u001b[1m  \\u2190 \\u2192 / 0          \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49mpan long lines; back to the start\\u001b[30;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[31;13H\\u2502\\u001b[1m  w                \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49mwr\\u001b[31;36Hp long \\u001b[31;44Hines instead of panning\\u001b[39;49m   \\u001b[31;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[32;13H\\u2502\\u001b[1m  i                \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49mthe edit's tool call record\\u001b[32;108H\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[33;13H\\u2502\\u001b[1m  note             \\u001b[22m\\u001b[38;5;15;49medits by file tools show their own diff; changes made by shell commands app\\u001b[38;2;103;232;249;49m\\u2502\\u001b[34;13H\\u2570\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u256f\\u001b[35;3H\\u001b[38;2;125;145;158;49msc close help \\u001b[38;5;8;49m\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u001b[39m\\u001b[49m\\u001b[59m\\u001b[0m\\u001b[?25l\"]\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/tui_surface_baseline/tui_surface.metrics.json:661:      \"            │  shift+enter      new line (alt+enter where shift is not reported)                           │\",\norigin/main:docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-live-spectator.md:28:- **Composer (minimal):** Enter submits; Alt+Enter or Shift+Enter (when the terminal reports it) inserts a newline; bracketed paste inserts the whole block; Backspace; Ctrl-L clears.\norigin/main:docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-live-spectator.md:491:        let sidecar = Sidecar::spawn(&sh(\"exec sleep 30\"), tx).unwrap();\norigin/main:docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-live-spectator.md:1603:        (Link::Ready, false) => \" enter send · alt+enter newline · ctrl-c quit \",\norigin/main:docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-live-spectator.md:1740:        let script = format!(\"{HELLO}; echo 'Compiling project...'; exec sleep 30\");\norigin/main:docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-phase3a-interaction-core.md:7:**Architecture:** The sidecar keeps deciding nothing: for a gated tool call it now sends a structured `review` payload (before/after text, patch, or command) built from the call's arguments and redacted. Rust turns that payload into diff lines with the `similar` crate already in `core/Cargo.toml`. Two new pure modules join the binary: `composer` (text buffer, grapheme cursor, readline keys, history, character-wrapped layout with an exact cursor position) and `review` (payload → diff lines). `live_state` gains focus, overlays, scrollback and decision entries; `live_view` renders the real terminal cursor, the scrolled transcript and the modals, and reports what it measured (`LiveLayout`) so key handling can page and clamp; `live` feeds that back, enables the kitty keyboard protocol when supported, draws a closing frame and handles stop signals.\norigin/main:docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-phase3a-interaction-core.md:17:- **3A Interaction core (this plan):** editor, history, approval modal, help overlay, focus and scrollback, keyboard protocol, shutdown and signals.\norigin/main:docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-phase3a-interaction-core.md:37:- **Composer keys:** Enter submits. Shift+Enter (kitty keyboard protocol) or Alt+Enter inserts a newline. Left/Right move by grapheme; Ctrl or Alt + Left/Right and Alt+B/F move by word; Home/End and Ctrl-A/E go to line start/end; Backspace/Delete remove a grapheme; Ctrl-W, Ctrl+Backspace and Alt+Backspace delete the previous word; Ctrl-U/Ctrl-K delete to line start/end; Ctrl-L clears the draft. Up/Down move between lines; Up on the first line recalls the previous prompt, Down past the newest brings the draft back. History is in memory, at most 200 prompts, blank and repeated prompts skipped. Typing while a turn runs is kept as a draft.\norigin/main:docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-phase3a-interaction-core.md:44:- **Keyboard protocol:** when `supports_keyboard_enhancement()` reports true, push `DISAMBIGUATE_ESCAPE_CODES` and pop it on every exit path.\norigin/main:docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-phase3a-interaction-core.md:62:| `core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live.rs` | Modify | Layout feedback, keyboard protocol, closing frame, stop signals |\norigin/main:docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-phase3a-interaction-core.md:2575:    (\"shift+enter\", \"new line (alt+enter where shift is not reported)\"),\norigin/main:docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-phase3a-interaction-core.md:2720:### Task 9: Event loop: layout feedback, keyboard protocol, closing frame, stop signals\norigin/main:docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-phase3a-interaction-core.md:2855:/// but not bracketed paste or the keyboard protocol, so those are undone here, during unwinding as well.\norigin/main:docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-phase3a-interaction-core.md:2877:    // Lets Shift+Enter arrive as its own key on terminals that speak the kitty keyboard protocol.\norigin/main:docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-phase3a-interaction-core.md:2948:Expected: PASS, 100 tests (98 + 2). Then `pgrep -af 'sidecar.js|sleep 30'` shows nothing left by the tests.\norigin/main:docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-phase3a-interaction-core.md:2958:git commit -m \"feat(tui): layout feedback, kitty keyboard protocol, closing frame and stop signals\"\norigin/main:docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-phase3a-interaction-core.md:2987:- Answer the terminal like a real terminal without the kitty keyboard protocol: whenever new PTY output contains `\\x1b[c`, write `\\x1b[?62c` (send no `\\x1b[?u` answer). Otherwise crossterm waits out its query timeout.\norigin/main:docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-phase3a-interaction-core.md:3087:Run each against the release binary from the worktree. Record the screen text at the key moments, the exit code, and that `\\x1b[?1049l`, `\\x1b[?2004l` and `\\x1b[<u` (keyboard protocol pop) appear at exit.\norigin/main:docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-04-nexus-ratatui-live-default-design.md:68:4. Composer: multi-line by default. Enter submits; Shift+Enter inserts a newline, with Alt+Enter as a fallback for terminals that cannot distinguish Shift+Enter. Pasted text arrives as one block.\norigin/main:docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-04-nexus-ratatui-live-default-design.md:83:| Shift+Enter / Alt+Enter | Newline |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:51:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:81:| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:111:| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:190:### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:192:Terminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:197:2. Approval panel. Type continuously across it. Paste 3 lines. Approve with a deliberate key.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:198:3. Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter multiline.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:200:5. Esc during `sleep 30` (no survivors).\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:202:7. NO_COLOR.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:204:Record PASS/FAIL per cell, with a screenshot of the approval panel and the post-exit terminal state.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:111:| M5 | **Serial on `GATEWAY`.** The eval runner, the stripped-proxy runs and the independent reviewer's live task each take the `GATEWAY` claim. The terminal matrix (E3) and the install matrix (E2) can run in parallel with gateway runs. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:99:- **Terminal evidence** comes from `pyte` emulation plus the repository's PTY suites. Real emulators (kitty keyboard protocol, tmux, VS Code) were not exercised.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:13:**Human terminal matrix:** The required environments remain xterm, kitty with keyboard protocol, tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal, and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14, and 200×60, with the two required screenshots for each cell. This coordination session is on `mike-dev`, an Ubuntu 24.04 remote TTY with no active display; it has tmux 3.4 and Xvfb but not the other terminal applications. Xvfb and PTY evidence do not satisfy the manual gate. The operator selected an Ubuntu/GNOME desktop as the target, but a direct SSH probe failed because `ubuntu-desktop` does not resolve from this runner and no desktop host is connected. The worksheet remains unfilled; no terminal cell is claimed passed. Matrix execution still requires the exact candidate artifact selected for qualification, installed and identified on that desktop.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:23:**Installed-candidate and checkpoint-choice observation:** The published installer completed with `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1` and installed RC3 under `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.3`; installer provenance records the exact archive digest and source revision. `/home/mike/.local/bin/nexus --version` reports `1.0.0-rc.3 (1b9791f07d30)`. The previous RC1 directory remains installed at `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.1` for rollback. The coordinator reported an automated PTY probe of the installed default TUI using a synthetic Git workspace, fake credential-shaped canary, and unreachable loopback endpoint. The reported probe displayed the five choices and selected cancel before inference. Its transcript/capture was not retained in the release evidence tree, so this observation is unarchived and was not independently verified in the readiness review. It is diagnostic context only: it does not establish the checkpoint-choice gate, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, or provider/task qualification.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:25:**Held-out and remaining qualification:** Public Issue #1 has no custodian response after the metadata-only request at 2026-10-23 03:46:59Z. The sealed T2 manifest remains incompatible with the current evaluator's `blackbox-v1` contract because it uses legacy `hidden.command`; the independent custodian must convert or replace it, revalidate it, and accept a new immutable manifest. No hidden task or payload was accessed and no held-out run started. Provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3/T4 including long tasks and nine fault classes, exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility, the real-terminal matrix, and independent RC acceptance remain outstanding.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:55:**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open; the latest custodian metadata request has no response in the available checkpoint, so T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T2/T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:69:**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open, with no custodian response to the latest metadata-only compatibility request posted at 22:08 UTC; T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:93:**RC and publication:** The published `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag resolves to `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779`, an ancestor of current `main`, and is not an artifact built from current source. Its published asset digest is `8d7dd32f3d00adb98d4f0ea2c6a484ea8e04fc547b4d78b21b060000eda22b9d`. The next candidate needs a new immutable identity, currently expected to be `v1.0.0-rc.2`, with synchronized version metadata and release notes. Exact-RC artifact/install checks, held-out T2, provider and standalone qualification, T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, independent RC acceptance, and stable-promotion disposition remain outstanding. Publication authorization is granted but gated on those results. No stable `v1.0.0` tag or release exists.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:119:- **Qualification and release:** PR #102 contributes synthetic host-preflight evidence only. Private held-out custody/schema compatibility, T2/T3/T4 qualification, live provider and standalone checks, exact-RC reproducibility, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, and independent RC acceptance remain outstanding. No RC has been constructed, installed, or accepted.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:165:- **Qualification host and terminal:** Qualification-host tooling is integrated through PR #31 (`8c0ab7b`), but this checkpoint has no evidence that the qualification host was provisioned and validated at `4bce876`. Terminal acceptance procedure is integrated; the required human matrix remains unexecuted. It requires five environments × three sizes on the exact installed RC, with per-cell PASS/FAIL and screenshots of the approval panel and post-exit state.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:172:- **Authoritative integration and CI:** `origin/v1/integration` is `519398495b7c3a2e5915ed76eee0bb731feb0bcf`. The earlier reported `2c70d39` and `d2c4bfc` are ancestors of this revision; they are not competing integration heads. PR #9 and PR #23 are integrated as `64ee88b` and `886766b`; PR #24's terminal acceptance kit is integrated at `5193984`. Exact-head integration CI run [39120013759](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39120013759) is in progress, so there is no current-head green claim yet. PR #24's checks passed on its exact head `91eaee9` in run [39117464186](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39117464186); its accepted procedure does not replace the human terminal matrix.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:274:| `REQ-QUAL-108` | partial | Automated PTY suite passes on `a7126aa`; the human matrix is absent for xterm, kitty (keyboard protocol enabled), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60. | Human terminal access and RC install | Human acceptance operator | Execute the `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 manual matrix on the installed RC across all required terminal×size cells and archive screenshots and verdicts. |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":700570001}},"started_at_ms":1792848910878,"completed_at_ms":1792848912579}}
