{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T13:39:08.435Z","ordinal":290677,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16e19-0589-7f73-b64e-a1d03ef4175b","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcb4fb0db881a0877dc9fd47e3261c","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"That’s the startup trust chooser you meant. It is already implemented in Nexus: **PR #186** added it, and it is included in **RC4**. I verified it is also present in current `origin/main` (`be2cd2f`).\n\nOn an interactive launch in an untrusted folder, Nexus shows the folder and any detected project instruction file, then offers **Trust and continue**, **Continue without trusting**, or **Exit**. A folder already trusted skips the prompt. The shared checkout is dirty and behind, so I left it untouched.\n\nThis confirms the feature is in the code and RC4; it does not establish the remaining v1.0.0 acceptance gates."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1792849147067,"completed_at_ms":1792849148435}}
