{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T13:42:53.739Z","ordinal":290838,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a16e26-6a2b-7240-bf24-4ed6eac80030","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT for the two-commit source delta** — candidate `518c71f5a91de57c85c572584ee61ffddd30f7d1`, based on `a2f2fba0de3288bdd69d377fa664d3aa1a0117dc`. The base-to-head diff hash is `ead7a52cc902ca79a21ced9e2c9204494f58e90ce4eec7d77611031bd99beb83`.\n\nThe fix correctly clears read-only fallback when the operator chooses to continue without a checkpoint in both the REPL and sidecar. The sidecar emits updated session state, and its regression checks that configured `review` mode is restored by requiring approval for a subsequent write. The REPL regression checks the corresponding `[true, false]` fallback transition. The other choice paths remain unchanged.\n\nI found no semantic conflict with current main: its `repl.ts` change is in the separate MCP wizard, and the relevant sidecar and agent code is unchanged. However, this candidate is 15 commits behind current main. **Rebase or merge current main and repeat exact-head validation before testing or integration**; the existing validation notes apply to the recorded base, not the refreshed candidate. I did not edit or run tests, and I did not implement the change."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16e23-3d1b-7571-9aa1-825e60ce3175","create_time":1792849373.7392592}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":14974}}
