86026d7f3e856736ce0ec9b8387f\ndetached\n\nworktree /home/mike/df2/c2exp/wt/w3_r1_control\nHEAD 2860228cb84166d0295961587ad4934184165bd0\ndetached\n\nworktree /home/mike/df2/c2exp/wt/w3_r2_c2\nHEAD 2860228cb84166d0295961587ad4934184165bd0\ndetached\n\nworktree /home/mike/df2/c2exp/wt/w3_r3_c2\nHEAD 2860228cb84166d0295961587ad4934184165bd0\ndetached\n\nworktree /home/mike/df2/c2exp/wt/w3_r4_control\nHEAD 2860228cb84166d0295961587ad4934184165bd0\ndetached\n\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:18:| Run several agents on this plan at once without collisions | [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) (also referenced from the root `AGENTS.md`) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:26:| 03 | Untrusted workspace inputs and egress boundary | [SPEC-03](specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md) | [PLAN-03](plans/PLAN-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md) | M1 | SEC-110, 111, 115, 116 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:72:3. **Files created or changed in the repository.** The audit created `docs/v1.0.0/**`. At the owner's request, it appended a short \"v1.0.0 work and concurrent agents\" section to the root `AGENTS.md`, without changing the existing content. Nothing else in the repository was modified.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:9:| [DEC-01](#dec-01-default-execution-posture) | Default execution posture | Review by default; auto only in trusted workspaces | No (resolved) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:36:| **C (chosen)** | Posture follows workspace trust. **Untrusted workspace → review** for `write_workspace`, `exec`, `egress` and `context_inject`. **Trusted workspace → auto** for `write_workspace` and `exec`; `egress` asks once per origin per session. `--yes` or `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` force auto. `--sandbox` stays available. | Safe for cloned or unknown repos. Low friction on the operator's own repos after one `nexus trust .`. Reuses the existing trust store, so there is no new concept. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:39:**Rationale.** The threat that matters is content from an untrusted repository or the web. Trust is the existing per-workspace boundary that MCP and plugins already honour. Option C closes SEC-01 and VER-01 on exactly the inputs that cause them, and keeps the daily-driver experience on trusted repos.\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:138:| Tools, security, persistence: `tools, safe_fs, sandbox, security, session, session_export, checkpoint, flight, evidence, git, worktree, mcp, plugins, skills, browser, lsp, file_diff, syntax, diagnostics, workspace_trust`, `core/{authority, resources, durable_file, persistence_protection, capabilities, workspace_path, independent_check, tool_groups}` | 28 | Full read for security-critical files. Grep or skim for session_export, file_diff, syntax, diagnostics, resources, browser, lsp, mcp transports. | C_tools_security_persistence; this file (workspace_trust, workspace_path, tool_groups, independent_check, approval_review, read by lead) | MCP remote transports, browser.ts and lsp.ts got only a skim review: **qualification gap** |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:148:| tasks/, AGENTS.md, README, quickstart | 5 | Full read | lead | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:3:These rules apply to every agent (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Nexus itself, or a human) that implements any part of this package at the same time as another. The repository's root `AGENTS.md` points here. The rules come from incidents recorded in `tasks/lessons.md`:\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:5:| Status | Ready. Default posture resolved by [DEC-01](../DECISIONS.md#dec-01-default-execution-posture) (option C: review in untrusted workspaces, auto in trusted ones). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:62:   - In an untrusted workspace, the first verifier run requires a one-time approval. The approval shows the exact command and the script body it resolves to (for example the `scripts.test` entry, or the Makefile `test:` recipe).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:63:   - In a trusted workspace, they run without asking under the auto posture.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:144:- Changing the default for untrusted workspaces from `auto` to review (DEC-01 option C) is a user-visible change. Release notes and the startup banner must state it. Provide `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` and `nexus trust .` + `--yes` for scripted users.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:168:| ACC-SAFE-01 | Fresh HOME, `nexus` (TUI) and `nexus repl`, mock gateway scripted to call `run_command \"echo x > ../outside\"`: in an untrusted workspace the call is not executed without an approval panel. After `nexus trust .` it runs without a panel (DEC-01 option C). | PTY |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:181:- **DEC-01** is resolved as option C (review in untrusted workspaces, auto in trusted ones). Nothing in this spec is blocked.\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:69:| REQ-SEC-002 | EXT-002, TOP_TIER B2 | Workspace MCP configs and plugins load only after `nexus trust`, and never in `--read-only`. | `workspace_trust.ts`; `mcp.ts:509-531`; `plugins.ts:47-76` | TEST + SRC | tested | N | Skills and knowledge are not gated (→ REQ-SEC-113) | ACC-TRUST-04 | K | SPEC-03 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:119:| REQ-SEC-101 | Audit; DEC-01 | Without opt-in, no model-initiated exec or egress happens without a decision. Untrusted workspace → review; trusted → auto. | safety | `config.ts`, `sidecar.ts:935`, `repl.ts:69`, `index.ts:93,115` | TEST `approval_policy.test.ts`, `tui_surface_e2e.test.ts`, `repl_approval_e2e.test.ts` | tested | ACC-SAFE-01 | **B** | SEC-01, TUI-07 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:135:| REQ-SEC-113 | Audit; CTX-001 partial | Workspace skills and knowledge load only when the workspace is trusted. Injected items are annotated with their source. | safety | `skills.ts:31-33`, `knowledge.ts`, `agent.ts:3301` | TEST (SEC-05, AGT-10; test:cli/test/workspace_trust.test.ts::\"ACC-TRUST-04: workspace skills and knowledge load only when workspace is trusted, with source annotations\") | tested | ACC-TRUST-04 | RR | SEC-05, AGT-10 | SPEC-03 / PLAN-03 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md:1:# SPEC-03: Untrusted workspace inputs and the egress boundary\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md:14:Nexus's threat model, as its docs state it, is that the operator's own configuration (`~/.config/nexus`) holds authority. An opened workspace is data until the operator trusts it (USER_MANUAL §4; `cli/src/workspace_trust.ts`). Workspace MCP configs and plugins honour this: they need `nexus trust` and never run in `--read-only`. Several other inputs that come from the workspace or the network do not:\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md:42:4. **REQ-SEC-113.** Workspace skills and workspace `knowledge.json` are loaded only for trusted workspaces. In an untrusted workspace they are listed by `/skills` as \"untrusted (not loaded)\", and `activate_skill` on one is refused with the `nexus trust` hint.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md:46:6. **REQ-SEC-115.** Nexus loads plugins only from its own documented …807 tokens truncated…a hostile repo and asking for any edit runs its test script on the host without a prompt. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: gate discovered verifiers on workspace trust or a one-time approval of the exact command (shown with its script body), and run them sandboxed when one is available. Document this. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:134:| R-VER-1 | Repo-defined verifier commands (discovered) run only in a trusted workspace or after one approval that shows the command and script body. They run sandboxed when a sandbox is available. | safety | RELEASE-REQUIRED | An untrusted temp repo with `\"test\":\"touch /tmp/pwn\"` plus an edit request: no file created without a prompt, in both default and --approve modes. |\ncli/test/doctor.test.ts:259:      // Untrusted: the workspace's own configuration is still inspected, and reported as not loaded.\ncli/test/doctor.test.ts:263:      assert.match(find(untrusted, \"mcp.config\")!.evidence.join(\"\\n\"), /\\.mcp\\.json: not loaded — this workspace is not trusted\\. Trust it with `nexus trust/);\ncli/test/doctor.test.ts:265:      assert.match(find(untrusted, \"plugins.config\")!.evidence.join(\"\\n\"), /p\\.mjs: not loaded — this workspace is not trusted/);\ncli/test/workspace_trust.test.ts:11:import { isWorkspaceTrusted, listTrustedWorkspaces, setWorkspaceTrusted, untrustedWorkspaceExtensions } from \"../src/workspace_trust.js\";\ncli/test/workspace_trust.test.ts:68:      const store = path.join(home, \".config\", \"nexus\", \"trusted_workspaces.json\");\ncli/test/harness.test.ts:2310:  test(\"scanAndOnboardWorkspace discovers stack and writes AGENTS.md with diagram\", () => {\ncli/test/harness.test.ts:2333:      assert.strictEqual(fs.existsSync(path.join(tmpDir, \"AGENTS.md\")), true);\ncli/test/harness.test.ts:2334:      const content = fs.readFileSync(path.join(tmpDir, \"AGENTS.md\"), \"utf-8\");\ncli/src/workspace_trust.ts:11: * is not trusted (or the session is read-only). Empty when there are none or the workspace is trusted.\ncli/src/workspace_trust.ts:13:export function untrustedWorkspaceExtensions(workspace: string, readOnly = false): string[] {\ncli/src/workspace_trust.ts:28:  return path.join(os.homedir(), \".config\", \"nexus\", \"trusted_workspaces.json\");\ncli/src/workspace_trust.ts:55:/** The trusted workspaces (real paths), as recorded in the trust store. */\ncli/src/workspace_trust.ts:66:/** Records (or removes) the operator's trust in a workspace. Returns its real path; throws when the store cannot be written. */\ncli/src/git.ts:49:    \"AGENTS.md\",\ncli/src/git.ts:73:  const target = path.join(workspace, \"AGENTS.md\");\ncli/src/plugins.ts:68:    this.trusted = options?.trusted !== undefined ? options.trusted : isWorkspaceTrusted(this.workspace, this.readOnly);\ncli/src/security.ts:27:  // The operator's list of trusted workspaces: the agent must not trust a workspace for itself.\ncli/src/security.ts:28:  \"trusted_workspaces.json\",\ncli/src/repl.ts:258:    console.log(`  ${pc.bold(pc.yellow(\"/init\"))}               Scaffold AGENTS.md rules file in workspace`);\ncli/src/repl.ts:1352:            console.log(`  • Generated customized ${pc.bold(\"AGENTS.md\")} with architecture diagram.\\n`);\ncli/src/onboard.ts:120:  // Generate AGENTS.md content\ncli/src/onboard.ts:146:    const targetFile = path.join(root, \"AGENTS.md\");\ncli/src/index.ts:386:    const { untrustedWorkspaceExtensions } = await import(\"./workspace_trust.js\");\ncli/src/index.ts:425:    const { untrustedWorkspaceExtensions } = await import(\"./workspace_trust.js\");\ncli/src/index.ts:444:  .option(\"--remove\", \"Stop trusting the workspace\")\ncli/src/index.ts:445:  .option(\"--list\", \"List trusted workspaces\")\ncli/src/index.ts:450:      console.log(list.length ? list.join(\"\\n\") : \"No trusted workspaces.\");\ncli/src/index.ts:460:    console.log(options.remove ? `No longer trusted: ${real}` : `Trusted: ${real}\\nIts .mcp.json servers and plugins will be loaded (they run code from this workspace). Undo with \\`nexus trust --remove\\`.`);\ncli/src/mcp.ts:511:  if (trusted && !readOnly) configs.push(...WORKSPACE_MCP_FILES.map((file) => path.join(workspace, file)));\ncli/src/mcp.ts:531:    this.trusted = options.trusted ?? isWorkspaceTrusted(this.workspace, this.readOnly);\ncli/src/mcp.ts:950:              description: \"Content of AGENTS.md project rules and conventions\",\ncli/src/mcp.ts:976:        const agentsFile = path.join(this.workspace, \"AGENTS.md\");\ncli/src/mcp.ts:977:        const content = fs.existsSync(agentsFile) ? fs.readFileSync(agentsFile, \"utf-8\") : \"# No AGENTS.md found\";\ncli/src/agent.ts:146:import { untrustedWorkspaceExtensions } from \"./workspace_trust.js\";\ncli/src/agent.ts:1345:      const skipped = untrustedWorkspaceExtensions(this.config.workspace, this.config.readOnly);\ncli/src/slash/session_commands.ts:267:    \"Wrote a tailored AGENTS.md.\",\ncli/src/doctor.ts:26:import { untrustedWorkspaceExtensions, WORKSPACE_MCP_FILES } from \"./workspace_trust.js\";\ncli/src/doctor.ts:692:  for (const file of untrustedWorkspaceExtensions(workspace).filter((f) => WORKSPACE_MCP_FILES.includes(path.basename(f)))) {\ncli/src/doctor.ts:693:    problems.push(`${file}: not loaded — this workspace is not trusted. Trust it with \\`nexus trust ${workspace}\\` to use its MCP servers.`);\ncli/src/doctor.ts:705:  for (const file of untrustedWorkspaceExtensions(workspace).filter((f) => !WORKSPACE_MCP_FILES.includes(path.basename(f)))) {\ncli/src/doctor.ts:706:    risky.push(`${file}: not loaded — this workspace is not trusted. Trust it with \\`nexus trust ${workspace}\\` to load its plugins.`);\ncli/src/doctor.ts:723:  if (risky.length) return f(\"plugins.config\", \"extensions\", \"warn\", `${risky.length} plugin problem(s): untrusted workspace plugins are not loaded; world-writable plugin files could be changed by anyone. ${note}`, [...risky, ...found.slice(0, 10)], \"Trust the workspace (`nexus trust`) or remove its plugins; restrict writable files with `chmod o-w <file>`.\");\ncli/src/slash/catalog.ts:114:  { name: \"onboard\", usage: \"/onboard\", summary: \"Scan the workspace and write a tailored AGENTS.md\" },\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:53:| AGT-10 | S3 | Knowledge auto-extraction | knowledge.ts:34-43, 206-231; agent.ts:4934-4936, 3302 | SOURCE. After every depth-0 turn `autoExtract(promptText)` stores prompt fragments matching `always|never|do not|must …` / `use|run|prefer npm|cargo…` as permanent \"rule\"/\"idiom\" entries in `<workspace>/.nexus/knowledge.json`, which `buildSystemPrompt` injects into every future session. Constructor `mkdir`s `<workspace>/.nexus` even in `--read-only`. A workspace-supplied `knowledge.json` is injected without the workspace-trust gate applied to MCP/plugins. | Silent standing instructions from one-off prompts (\"never run the tests\" in a task) or from a cloned repo; read-only mode writes into the workspace. | Make opt-in; no writes in read-only; trust-gate injection. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:63:| TUI-07 | S2 | Default safety posture | sidecar.ts:935; repl.ts:69; quickstart.md:55 | SOURCE + DOC-CLAIM: default mode is `auto` (no approvals) for both surfaces; quickstart says \"Enter a small task, review requested actions\" | New users unknowingly grant the model unprompted write/shell authority | Decide v1 default (recommend review on first run / untrusted workspace); fix quickstart wording |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:147:| TUI-R6 | Default approval posture is an explicit, documented decision; first run in an untrusted workspace states the mode and how to change it | safety (TUI-07) | RELEASE-REQUIRED | PTY first-run screen contains mode + switch hint; docs match |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:35:  - Workspace MCP configs and plugin JS are gated by `~/.config/nexus/trusted_workspaces.json` (workspace_trust.ts:35).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:37:  - `.nexus-security.json` is read from the untrusted workspace (security.ts:48). It can only add entries, except that `allowedDomains` narrows egress and `allowExternalSymlinks` is never consumed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:52:| SEC-04 | S2 | read-only mode | authority.ts:44-136; tools.ts:485-495, 755-779 | RUNTIME (Repro R2). `isSafeReadOnlyCommand` allows `cat ~/.ssh/id_rsa`, `cat /etc/passwd`, `tail -f /dev/null`. The allowlist does not confine paths. The sandbox runs `--ro-bind / /` with the network unshared, so host secrets are readable and returned to the (possibly cloud) model. | `--read-only` reads like \"safe to point at an untrusted repo\", but it still discloses home-directory secrets. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: in read-only/sandbox mode, mask `$HOME` (tmpfs over home, then ro-bind the workspace only), or path-confine the allowlisted commands. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:53:| SEC-05 | S2 | untrusted repo opened | skills.ts:31-33; agent.ts:3301,3789 | SOURCE. Workspace skills (SKILL.md) are loaded and advertised in the system prompt with no workspace-trust check, unlike MCP and plugins (workspace_trust.ts:5-24). `activate_skill` is non-mutating, so it is never approved. | Persistent prompt injection from a cloned repo. Combined with SEC-01 this gives command execution. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: gate workspace skill directories on workspace trust, or show them as untrusted and require approval to activate. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:115:- No shell is used for git (git2) or for worktree ops (execFileSync argv). MCP children get an env allowlist (mcp.ts:56-77). Workspace MCP and plugins require explicit trust, and never get it in read-only mode (workspace_trust.ts:35-53, mcp.ts:509-531).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:116:- Session state: schema version with fail-closed on future versions, legacy migration, identity and workspace binding on load, redaction before persist, and a fsync'd append-only compaction archive with a commit protocol (state.ts:338-460; durable_file.ts). The trust store is written atomically with 0600/0700 (workspace_trust.ts:71-76).\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16e23-3d1b-7571-9aa1-825e60ce3175","create_time":1792849790.846456}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
