{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T13:50:54.375Z","ordinal":291173,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16e23-3d1b-7571-9aa1-825e60ce3175","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcb7bd4d1481a0b87476ffc093430a","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Understood: you meant the **“Trust this folder?” startup prompt**, before Nexus loads project instructions such as `AGENTS.md`.\n\nThat flow is already in Nexus source and in the public RC4 tag. It offers **Trust and continue**, **Continue without trusting**, or **Exit**. Continuing untrusted does not force read-only mode; the normal untrusted-workspace review behavior applies.\n\nThe prompt is skipped for folders already saved as trusted. So if you launched Nexus and didn’t see it, the folder may already be trusted, or you may have launched an older build. I haven’t changed anything in the shared checkout."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1792849853331,"completed_at_ms":1792849854375}}
