{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T13:53:21.352Z","ordinal":291291,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16e2e-05d5-7762-8225-d342ce215792","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a16e2e-05d5-7762-8225-d342ce215792","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016adcb84a717881a0a5cd1aa0eaf9b98e","usage":{"input_tokens":122254,"cached_input_tokens":120448,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":546,"reasoning_output_tokens":529,"total_tokens":122800},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1636165,"cached_input_tokens":1512832,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":5549,"reasoning_output_tokens":4004,"total_tokens":1641714},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":5278078469,"cached_input_tokens":5221751808,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":14675126,"reasoning_output_tokens":8339716,"total_tokens":5292753595}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T13:53:22.122Z","ordinal":291292,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a16e30-00ca-7370-8a68-c3f0e1947050","call_id":"call_0af4171d2c4341c1b2517d22eb88f887","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/acceptance_stage_clarification\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Implemented the prototype-safe persistence fix in isolated worktree `/home/mike/nexus-wt/mcp-proto-name`.\\n\\n- **Commit:** `6f6caa878a193725a62735d6bb10bc862aa485d1`, based on `be2cd2f255414f554572c86baa884d9271ff5ea1`.\\n- **Change:** Defines the server-name entry as an enumerable own data property, so `__proto__` is serialized instead of changing the map’s prototype.\\n- **Regression:** `cli/test/mcp.test.ts` verifies persistence succeeds and the parsed JSON has an own `__proto__` server entry.\\n- **Diff check:** Passed. Diff SHA-256: `0fbd64413456382894c6e95687651192aa59c31e598e1627b29b5175be4db0ff`.\\n- **Test:** Focused MCP test is pending. The protected `SUITE` claim is still held by KimiCode, so I did not run tests.\\n- **Claims:** `DEFECT_MCP_PROTO_NAME_20261024`, `FILE_cli_src_mcp.ts`, and `FILE_cli_test_mcp.test.ts` remain held; the commit and pending-test status are recorded in the claim log.\\n- **PR:** No PR opened or push performed. Branch `v1/defect-mcp-proto-name` is ready for exact-head review; independent review remains required.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"At exact `main@be2cd2f255414f554572c86baa884d9271ff5ea1`, the public T2 and T3 manifests are unchanged. T2 still lists 40 external tasks, evenly distributed across four classes and languages. T3 lists 8 tasks, two per class, with four each in JavaScript and Python.\\n\\nIssue #1 remains open. Its latest visible update is coordinator comment #6378649211; no custodian/author reply or acknowledged handoff follows it. No active held-out author or custodian claim appears in the shared claims records. PR #16 remains closed with no newer acceptance.\\n\\nHistorical reports attest T2 corpus custody and T3 task checks; T2’s report explicitly separates evaluator-boundary acceptance. The current evaluator still rejects T2’s legacy format for qualification, and the public readiness record continues to list independent custody among the qualification blockers.\\n\\n**Dependency remains:** an independent custodian/replacement author must accept an explicit claims-protocol handoff, confirm current custody and execution-boundary status, and provide a custodian-owned T2 conversion/new manifest path or report that replacement is required. No private material was accessed and the corpus was not changed.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — exact commit `6e79dc7e8ebb51bcbbfc389f4e256690ce7bd3f9` against base `be2cd2f255414f554572c86baa884d9271ff5ea1`. The diff hash is `a34a2211eef52d580c6ce300b2ce88b7115b23e4cf60fb011b896af4cd009f20`.\\n\\nThe change is limited to `scripts/package-linux.sh`. In the approved pinned-image path, it canonicalizes the output directory and runs tar and gzip inside that same image, using quoted arguments and normalized archive metadata. The explicit host-build override remains separate and is clearly excluded from reproducibility evidence. I found no release-blocking issue in the changed code. I did not edit files or run tests; the cited build results are implementer-reported.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16e2e-05d5-7762-8225-d342ce215792","create_time":1792850002.1228356}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
