onnector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.list_pr_changed_filenames"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.get_pr_diff"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_file"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.rerun_failed_workflow_run_jobs"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f6-7b50-7a00-9fbb-818f2ac4eed4","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch"},{"first_turn_id":"01a156f6-7b50-7a00-9fbb-818f2ac4eed4","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"fetch_topic"},{"first_turn_id":"01a15e3e-2987-7e62-9699-29ab11a9d023","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"search"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a162a0-311d-7271-a76d-8992331bb312","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_pr_file_patch"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16af7-b30b-7543-b5d3-5d0470af8bf9","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_branches"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16b07-bb74-7501-b966-9445743dc69f","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_issue"},{"first_turn_id":"01a16e23-3d1b-7571-9aa1-825e60ce3175","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"create_agent_identity"}],"status":"complete"}}],"resume_metadata":{"last_started_turn_id":"01a16e34-cb69-7fb3-96f2-8eec5d8c48cb","multi_agent_version":"v2","previous_turn_settings":{"comp_hash":"3000","model":"gpt-6-luna","realtime_active":false},"turn_attribution":{"initiating_agent_path":null,"parent_turn_id":null,"root_turn_id":"01a16e34-cb69-7fb3-96f2-8eec5d8c48cb","turn_id":"01a16e34-cb69-7fb3-96f2-8eec5d8c48cb","turn_trigger":"goal"}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcb7bd4d1481a0b87476ffc093430a","order":14982,"phase":"final_answer","revision":"retained_01a16e2d-bfaa-7841-89fd-96413037f33a","text":"Understood: you meant the **“Trust this folder?” startup prompt**, before Nexus loads project instructions such as `AGENTS.md`.\n\nThat flow is already in Nexus source and in the public RC4 tag. It offers **Trust and continue**, **Continue without trusting**, or **Exit**. Continuing untrusted does not force read-only mode; the normal untrusted-workspace review behavior applies.\n\nThe prompt is skipped for folders already saved as trusted. So if you launched Nexus and didn’t see it, the folder may already be trusted, or you may have launched an older build. I haven’t changed anything in the shared checkout.","turn_id":"01a16e23-3d1b-7571-9aa1-825e60ce3175"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcb7d9c07081a0ace1d1c0dc4a32bc","order":14983,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a16e2e-2c80-7b50-a372-19187e1b5279","text":"I confirmed the startup chooser is already included in RC4. I’m continuing the release work now: I’ll refresh the exact main CI and claim state, then advance the reviewed reproducibility fix as far as the active suite ownership allows.","turn_id":"01a16e2e-05d5-7762-8225-d342ce215792"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcb801006881a0988479567d178a9e","order":14984,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a16e2e-c73c-7523-b012-63ad6e48d099","text":"The exact-main run is not terminal yet: Node 22 and 24 have passed, while Linux packaging/reproducibility is still running. The local SUITE claim remains owned by Kimi; the recorded PID is not visible in this process namespace, so I’m preserving the claim and not starting overlapping tests. I’m checking the owner handoff route and the active CI handle while keeping the package fix ready.","turn_id":"01a16e2e-05d5-7762-8225-d342ce215792"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcb896643081a08e9ab36bbf6ac4e5","order":14987,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a16e31-0f89-7f62-8f92-6b8146bd936f","text":"I confirmed the Linux CI lane is now running the full CLI suite after its build and Rust checks passed. I’ll let that exact-main run finish before starting any candidate validation; this preserves single-suite ownership and keeps evidence tied to one revision.","turn_id":"01a16e2e-05d5-7762-8225-d342ce215792"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcb97a6cdc81a0b60b0d800533df59","order":14991,"phase":"final_answer","revision":"retained_01a16e34-8d29-7d82-9eff-b534ae0d9c1b","text":"**NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE** — acceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**.\n\n- `origin/main` is still `be2cd2f255414f554572c86baa884d9271ff5ea1`. CI run `40098339766` passed Node 22 and 24; its Linux job is still running the CLI test suite.\n- The archive reproducibility fix is committed in the isolated worktree as `6e79dc7`. Independent review accepted it; static checks pass. I have not run its tests or started overlapping CI while the SUITE claim remains protected.\n- The claim owner’s recorded PID is absent, but a Kimi process is live in the repository. There is no acknowledged handoff, so I have not taken the claim.\n- The shared dirty checkout remains untouched. RC4 is still unaccepted; cross-runner reproducibility and the remaining exact-RC qualification gates are unresolved.\n\nI recorded these exact-revision updates in the existing release work state.","turn_id":"01a16e2e-05d5-7762-8225-d342ce215792"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcb98e49ec81a0a1983803929b9948","order":14992,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a16e34-d5e1-79c2-95e5-b5c97b92bbea","text":"I’m checking the same exact-main CI run again and refreshing the SUITE owner’s activity before deciding whether the package candidate can enter validation. I’ll proceed as soon as the active test window closes or an acknowledged handoff makes the suite lane available.","turn_id":"01a16e34-cb69-7fb3-96f2-8eec5d8c48cb"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcba36b96081a096f0c744569efd56","order":14995,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a16e37-6731-7a21-9257-34b5512fdaf2","text":"I’ve sent a safe-boundary coordination request to the release coordinator, explicitly preserving the Kimi claim until the owner replies. The request is still pending; no handoff has been assumed. The exact-main Linux suite remains active, so I’m continuing to wait on that live CI job rather than start a conflicting run.","turn_id":"01a16e34-cb69-7fb3-96f2-8eec5d8c48cb"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcba6c980881a0ac6394d5e245f0b2","order":14997,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a16e38-3b0c-7112-93b4-d24fe79f0f61","text":"The main run has cleared the full Node test suites; Linux packaging and installer checks are now running. I’m assembling the two independently reviewed fixes—the broken RC artifact-download pin and the cross-runner tar metadata fix—into one exact-main candidate so CI can validate them together once the current run finishes.","turn_id":"01a16e34-cb69-7fb3-96f2-8eec5d8c48cb"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":15001,"sender_deliveries":[{"order":7850,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a15e0d-46de-72f1-8e85-967b05e2dfc6","receiver_turn_id":"01a15e0b-8f5d-7b40-aa6b-62735e71e8a0","text":"\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES START\nReceived message: fco_01a15e0d-46de-72f1-8e85-967b05e2dfc6\nSource thread: 01a139bf-d0bf-74e0-b969-dd59f00a9605\nHost: Up to three recent user messages with preceding assistant context, captured at de