{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T14:05:30.807Z","ordinal":291863,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16e3a-6ba7-7961-a9ba-21cec97e40c0","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a16e3a-6ba7-7961-a9ba-21cec97e40c0","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016adcbb291a7081a0b609748399e065b0","usage":{"input_tokens":91778,"cached_input_tokens":86912,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":123,"reasoning_output_tokens":106,"total_tokens":91901},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":755180,"cached_input_tokens":731392,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":2893,"reasoning_output_tokens":1467,"total_tokens":758073},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":5288123258,"cached_input_tokens":5231657600,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":14706172,"reasoning_output_tokens":8358263,"total_tokens":5302829430}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T14:05:33.738Z","ordinal":291864,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a16e3b-2aaa-7191-b21a-8dccdc569e5c","call_id":"call_349ec950604a4ac9bc296797760b938b","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/acceptance_stage_clarification\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Implemented the prototype-safe persistence fix in isolated worktree `/home/mike/nexus-wt/mcp-proto-name`.\\n\\n- **Commit:** `6f6caa878a193725a62735d6bb10bc862aa485d1`, based on `be2cd2f255414f554572c86baa884d9271ff5ea1`.\\n- **Change:** Defines the server-name entry as an enumerable own data property, so `__proto__` is serialized instead of changing the map’s prototype.\\n- **Regression:** `cli/test/mcp.test.ts` verifies persistence succeeds and the parsed JSON has an own `__proto__` server entry.\\n- **Diff check:** Passed. Diff SHA-256: `0fbd64413456382894c6e95687651192aa59c31e598e1627b29b5175be4db0ff`.\\n- **Test:** Focused MCP test is pending. The protected `SUITE` claim is still held by KimiCode, so I did not run tests.\\n- **Claims:** `DEFECT_MCP_PROTO_NAME_20261024`, `FILE_cli_src_mcp.ts`, and `FILE_cli_test_mcp.test.ts` remain held; the commit and pending-test status are recorded in the claim log.\\n- **PR:** No PR opened or push performed. Branch `v1/defect-mcp-proto-name` is ready for exact-head review; independent review remains required.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"At exact `main@be2cd2f255414f554572c86baa884d9271ff5ea1`, the public T2 and T3 manifests are unchanged. T2 still lists 40 external tasks, evenly distributed across four classes and languages. T3 lists 8 tasks, two per class, with four each in JavaScript and Python.\\n\\nIssue #1 remains open. Its latest visible update is coordinator comment #6378649211; no custodian/author reply or acknowledged handoff follows it. No active held-out author or custodian claim appears in the shared claims records. PR #16 remains closed with no newer acceptance.\\n\\nHistorical reports attest T2 corpus custody and T3 task checks; T2’s report explicitly separates evaluator-boundary acceptance. The current evaluator still rejects T2’s legacy format for qualification, and the public readiness record continues to list independent custody among the qualification blockers.\\n\\n**Dependency remains:** an independent custodian/replacement author must accept an explicit claims-protocol handoff, confirm current custody and execution-boundary status, and provide a custodian-owned T2 conversion/new manifest path or report that replacement is required. No private material was accessed and the corpus was not changed.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — exact candidate `0f6bf66ba943eb3c9c64ae563c2b23f6970a6d5a` against base `be2cd2f255414f554572c86baa884d9271ff5ea1`. The diff hash is `40cbd14b712e9f50b49ca769d7260f7f6568db8f4533c15d3eedde9f153f96c1`.\\n\\nThe diff contains only `.github/workflows/repro.yml` and `scripts/package-linux.sh`. The workflow now pins both artifact downloads to the download-artifact v4 action SHA; upload-artifact remains separately pinned. The packaging script uses the approved digest-pinned image for both Rust builds and archive generation, canonicalizes the output directory, and keeps the local host-build path explicitly outside reproducibility evidence. The two changes fit together without altering package contents or the workflow’s exact-source and published-asset comparisons.\\n\\nI found no blocker in the combined diff. I did not run tests or a suite.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16e3a-6ba7-7961-a9ba-21cec97e40c0","create_time":1792850733.7381315}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
