ubtest: non-git checkpoint refuses to copy sensitive workspace files\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SCHEMA2_INTEGRATION/failed-long-tmp-tests.tap:316:ok 24 - non-git checkpoint refuses to copy sensitive workspace files\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SCHEMA2_INTEGRATION/targeted-tests.tap:315:# Subtest: non-git checkpoint refuses to copy sensitive workspace files\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SCHEMA2_INTEGRATION/targeted-tests.tap:316:ok 24 - non-git checkpoint refuses to copy sensitive workspace files\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/broader-failed.txt:683:# Subtest: non-git checkpoint refuses to copy sensitive workspace files\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/broader-failed.txt:684:ok 30 - non-git checkpoint refuses to copy sensitive workspace files\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/focused.txt:92:# Subtest: non-git checkpoint refuses to copy sensitive workspace files\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/focused.txt:93:ok 19 - non-git checkpoint refuses to copy sensitive workspace files\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:9:**RC3, checkpoint choice, and Doctor:** RC3 remains the latest published prerelease, tagged at `1b9791f07d301c885fe48f04a796203583ab5a5c`; its archive digest and provenance are recorded in the snapshot below. The operator's `Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to checkpoint` failure occurred on immutable RC1, which predates the interactive choice flow. RC3 source contains the five choices: read-only, continue in the configured mode without a rollback checkpoint, create a checkpoint with the sensitivity risk acknowledged, cancel, or re-enter the instruction. Current RC3 source also scans saved-state metadata asynchronously in bounded batches, accepts schema-2 task `messageLog` records, and treats a configured model absent from `/models` as unverified rather than unavailable; a `--deep` inference probe can verify it. The interrupted-write temporary file reported by Doctor is a separate real warning and is not automatically repaired. These source checks and existing tests do not substitute for exercising the exact installed candidate on the operator's own state.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:35:**Checkpoint failure:** `/home/mike/.local/bin/nexus` resolves to the installed `v1.0.0-rc.1` package and reports `1.0.0-rc.1 (cb364c386c42)`. That immutable package lacks checkpoint choices, so the reported failure before turn start is reproducible by version identity and will persist on RC1. The fix is integrated in PR #147 (TUI/sidecar) and PR #153 (legacy REPL): before starting a turn, Nexus asks the operator whether to use read-only mode, continue in the configured mode without a rollback checkpoint, create the checkpoint with the sensitive-content risk acknowledged, cancel, or enter a different instruction. Both PRs passed exact-head checks, and the subsequent exact-main CI on `dac465d` passed. No replacement package has been installed. The public release page still has RC1 only; RC2 has a tag but no published release, and RC3 has neither tag nor release.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:49:**Checkpoint failure and remediation:** The operator reports every launch attempt on installed RC1 fails before the turn starts with `Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to checkpoint`. This is confirmed as an RC1 limitation: immutable RC1 source predates the checkpoint-choice flow. PR #153 integrates that flow in current main, offering read-only, continue without a rollback checkpoint, create the checkpoint despite sensitive content, cancel, or re-enter the instruction. This is source-integrated behavior only; the installed candidate must exercise the prompt and selected actions before acceptance. RC1 and RC2 remain unchanged and do not contain this behavior.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:65:**Checkpoint failure and remediation:** The operator reports that every attempt to start Nexus RC1 fails with `Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to checkpoint`. This is consistent with RC1's exact source predating PR #147's checkpoint-choice flow. PR #147 is integrated in current main and its exact-head CI and CodeQL passed; the interactive TUI now offers read-only, continue without a rollback checkpoint, create the checkpoint anyway with a sensitivity warning, cancel, or re-enter the instruction. RC1 and RC2 are immutable and do not contain this behavior. The next candidate must include the fix, and the installed candidate must be exercised to verify the choices before any acceptance claim.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:43:| REQ-SEC-40 | PERS-002 | No unredacted durable copies (sessions, flights, audit, checkpoints, caches, crash) | P2 §18 | Blocker at a4f3e16 → **operator-accepted with bounded envelope** (typed WorkspacePath rule; legacy identity-sensitive files remain plaintext) a2d3051/5774a1a | Y (PERS002_INDEPENDENT_QUALIFICATION) | 10-12 T-08/T10: plaintext in sessions, diffs, audit, task state, flight log — regression vs accepted claim; MCP config not covered (qual Q17) |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":28760}},"started_at_ms":1792850935174,"completed_at_ms":1792850935175}}
