{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T14:11:57.706Z","ordinal":292199,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a16e41-068a-7b22-8fea-9f1230e93594","call_id":"call_c4943f83e49b48caa58b82c8d02c18dc","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 9835)\nTotal output lines: 151\n\n# v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\n\n## Current release convergence status (observed 2026-10-23 13:35 UTC at `1f3c655`)\n\n**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `1f3c655971ade086f55347926db16cf2ecd52d1f`, merging PR #161's pinned Linux builder/reproducibility changes. Exact-main CI [39957281380](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39957281380) completed successfully: Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 jobs all passed, including the full CLI suite, security gates, requirements check, reproducible package builds, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke. Exact-main CodeQL [39957281390](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39957281390) also passed. On a clean detached checkout of this exact SHA with isolated HOME/XDG, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 explicit exact-RC qualification deferrals. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reports all components at `1.0.0-rc.3`. These are source-gate results; the CI package is validation output, not a new published RC.\n\n**Distribution scope:** The release owner confirmed the supported distribution target is the GitHub installer/archive only; npm publication is inapplicable. The current release workflow is the authority for published assets.\n\n**RC3, checkpoint choice, and Doctor:** RC3 remains the latest published prerelease, tagged at `1b9791f07d301c885fe48f04a796203583ab5a5c`; its archive digest and provenance are recorded in the snapshot below. The operator's `Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to checkpoint` failure occurred on immutable RC1, which predates the interactive choice flow. RC3 source contains the five choices: read-only, continue in the configured mode without a rollback checkpoint, create a checkpoint with the sensitivity risk acknowledged, cancel, or re-enter the instruction. Current RC3 source also scans saved-state metadata asynchronously in bounded batches, accepts schema-2 task `messageLog` records, and treats a configured model absent from `/models` as unverified rather than unavailable; a `--deep` inference probe can verify it. The interrupted-write temporary file reported by Doctor is a separate real warning and is not automatically repaired. These source checks and existing tests do not substitute for exercising the exact installed candidate on the operator's own state.\n\n**Qualification evidence and blockers:** The RC3 provider record `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023.json` was independently accepted: ChatGPT sign-in streaming/tool round trip passed; OpenRouter failed authentication and its live task remains outstanding. Public Issue #1 remains open; its latest visible update is coordinator-authored at 10:23 UTC, with no custodian response. The sealed legacy `hidden.command` corpus is not accepted by the current `blackbox-v1` runner; no held-out qualification has started and no private payload was accessed. T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, exact-candidate cross-runner reproducibility, all 15 human terminal cells, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete.\n\n**Human terminal matrix:** The required environments remain xterm, kitty with keyboard protocol, tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal, and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14, and 200×60, with the two required screenshots for each cell. This coordination session is on `mike-dev`, an Ubuntu 24.04 remote TTY with no active display; it has tmux 3.4 and Xvfb but not the other terminal applications. Xvfb and PTY evidence do not satisfy the manual gate. The operator selected an Ubuntu/GNOME desktop as the target, but a direct SSH probe failed because `ubuntu-desktop` does not resolve from this runner and no desktop host is connected. The worksheet remains unfilled; no terminal cell is claimed passed. Matrix execution still requires the exact candidate artifact selected for qualification, installed and identified on that desktop.\n\n**Release disposition and next actions:** Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`. RC3 is published but unaccepted; no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed. Exact-main CI and CodeQL now pass on `1f3c655`; the pinned-builder documentation claim still needs a safe owner handoff and reconciliation. Continue the installed-candidate qualification lanes, resolve held-out corpus compatibility with the independent custodian, and prepare a new versioned RC only through the accepted process after its prerequisites pass. Exact-RC qualification, independent acceptance, and final publication remain gated by their evidence. Publication authorization remains granted and gated.\n\n## Current RC3 artifact and installed-candidate status (observed 2026-10-23 09:11 UTC at `1b9791f`; point-in-time snapshot)\n\n**Exact source gates:** `origin/main` and the signed `v1.0.0-rc.3` tag resolve to source commit `1b9791f07d301c885fe48f04a796203583ab5a5c`. Exact-main CI [39923089278](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089278) and CodeQL [39923089363](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089363) completed successfully on that commit. CI passed Node 22, Node 24, Linux CLI tests, security gates, requirements checks, two-build package reproducibility, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag v1.0.0-rc.3` and `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed at the same source; the latter reports 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 explicit exact-RC qualification deferrals. This is source-gate evidence, not product acceptance.\n\n**RC3 artifact publication and provenance:** The annotated tag object is `dd68c222c57d0be0a4245a5b88092ff9df69201f`; its PGP signature verified good and it points to the source commit above. Release workflow [39927176480](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39927176480) completed successfully and published the [v1.0.0-rc.3 prerelease](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.3). The workflow-produced Linux x86-64 archive is `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.3.tar.gz`, SHA-256 `efb446d2760f2e1aa7890e9d786b8a2ba8e4ebb784fbcac1e66afe827428864d`; `SHA256SUMS` is `9288edb4655a19caa40e1598c0a642ab7f7e93aafbb187c2bfc8cfa9e19f116f`; the CycloneDX SBOM is `3a3176b4b3890c1bc07fb7b3acd80f7372f043819e6a8b296346d014b07f9d3a`. Downloaded checksums and SBOM sidecars passed. GitHub attestations for the archive and `SHA256SUMS` verified against the Release workflow, run `39927176480`, tag `v1.0.0-rc.3`, and source `1b9791f`.\n\n**Installed-candidate and checkpoint-choice observation:** The published installer completed with `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1` and installed RC3 under `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.3`; installer provenance records the exact archive digest and source revision. `/home/mike/.local/bin/nexus --version` reports `1.0.0-rc.3 (1b9791f07d30)`. The previous RC1 directory remains installed at `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.1` for rollback. The coordinator reported an automated PTY probe of the installed default TUI using a synthetic Git workspace, fake credential-shaped canary, and unreachable loopback endpoint. The reported probe displayed the five choices and selected cancel before inference. Its transcript/capture was not retained in the release evidence tree, so this observation is unarchived and was not independently verified in the readiness review. It is diagnostic context only: it does not establish the checkpoint-choice gate, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, or provider/task qualification.\n\n**Held-out and remaining qualification:** Public Issue #1 has no custodian response after the metadata-only request at 2026-10-23 03:46:59Z. The sealed T2 manifest remains incompatible with the current evaluator's `blackbox-v1` contract because it uses legacy `hidden.command`; the independent custodian must convert or replace it, revalidate it, and accept a new immutable manifest. No hidden task or payload was accessed and no held-out run started. Provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3/T4 including long tasks and nine fault classes, exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility, the real-terminal matrix, and independent RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n\n**Release disposition:** Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_RC_QUALIFICATION_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`. RC3 is a published candidate, not an accepted RC. No stable v1.0.0 release is claimed. The installed command now uses RC3; RC1 remains available by its versioned path. The next critical dependency is accepted held-out custody and runner compatibility; other exact-RC gates can proceed independently where their required providers and environments are available.\n\n## Historical readiness snapshot (observed 2026-10-23 08:14 UTC at `1b9791f`; superseded above)\n\n**Release source and branch reconciliation:** Release PRs #147, #153, #157, and #159 target `main`; the current release source is `origin/main@1b9791f07d301c885fe48f04a796203583ab5a5c`. `origin/v1/integration` remains at `7d6673f108316dda015b858c85b2abe20f3a4f78` from 2026-10-21 and is not the source used by the current RC3 candidate PRs. Do not combine evidence from those different heads. The shared checkout remains dirty and was not modified.\n\n**Source gates:** PR #159 (`a81f79df35a76207751ffd8a86640baafca98eeb`) merged as `1b9791f`. Its exact-head Node 22, Node 24, Linux package/reproducibility/install-smoke, and CodeQL checks passed; independent source review accepted the change. The focused Doctor schema-2 empty-history regression passed 1/1 with isolated HOME. At exact post-merge source `1b9791f`, `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passes with all components at `1.0.0-rc.3`; `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passes with 123 rows (108 tested, …4835 tokens truncated…ly). The required `linux-x86_64` job is still running; merge remains gated on its result. CodeQL and both TypeScript checks passed. No results from parent revision `8f4504e` are substituted for this exact-head run.\n- The source requirements gate remains a clean-worktree pass on exact integration `7d6673f`; eleven requirements remain deferred to exact-RC qualification as listed in the checkpoint below. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; this CI progression does not establish RC readiness or acceptance.\n\n## Current state update (2026-10-21 15:26 UTC, `7d6673f`)\n\n**Authoritative integration:** `origin/v1/integration` is `7d6673f108316dda015b858c85b2abe20f3a4f78`, merged from PR #102. The shared checkout remains on `main@db1ca558086014912b20dae8232af111ccb21d67` with unrelated local modifications; it was not changed for this checkpoint.\n\n**Campaign status:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`\n\n**Acceptance status:** `IN_PROGRESS`\n\n**Release status:** no Nexus v1.0.0 RC or stable publication exists. Publication authorization is granted and remains gated on independent acceptance.\n\n- **Exact-head CI:** PR #8 targets `main@db1ca55` from `v1/integration@7d6673f`. On current head, `javascript-typescript` runs [39624982585](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39624982585) and [39624995598](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39624995598) passed, as did CodeQL [119308898279](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/119308898279). The required `test-matrix (20)`, `(22)`, and `(24)` jobs in run [39624995762](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39624995762) were still pending at 15:26 UTC. The successful source workflow [39615105190] ran on parent `8f4504e`, so its results are not represented as exact-`7d6673f` results.\n- **Requirements gate:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` was independently rerun with isolated HOME/XDG on exact `7d6673f` and passed: 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open). Eleven requirements remain explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. This source-stage gate pass does not satisfy those qualification requirements.\n- **Contest:** the contest is over; no contest freeze applies. The contest-contract check has been retired and is not a release gate. Historical contest artifacts remain evidence of past activity only.\n- **Qualification and release:** PR #102 contributes synthetic host-preflight evidence only. Private held-out custody/schema compatibility, T2/T3/T4 qualification, live provider and standalone checks, exact-RC reproducibility, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, and independent RC acceptance remain outstanding. No RC has been constructed, installed, or accepted.\n\nThis update supersedes the 14:56 UTC `8f4504e` checkpoint below for current state. Earlier evidence remains bound to its recorded revisions.\n\n**Updated:** 2026-10-21 15:26 UTC\n**Current integration candidate:** `7d6673f108316dda015b858c85b2abe20f3a4f78` (`v1/integration`)\n**Separate historical candidate branch:** `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a` (`v1/candidate-1`)\n**Campaign status:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`\n**Acceptance status:** `IN_PROGRESS`\n\nExact-source CI and requirements enforcement pass on `8f4504e`, but held-out custody and corpus compatibility, installed-RC qualification, independent RC acceptance, and final publication remain incomplete. No v1.0.0 RC or stable release exists. Publication authorization is granted and remains gated on acceptance.\n\nThis checkpoint reconciles the candidate ledger and acceptance procedure against recorded source and test evidence. It is not a release approval. Historical inspection sections below are preserved as audit evidence and do not represent current branch state where superseded by the 2026-10-21 update.\n\n## Current state update (2026-10-21 14:56 UTC, `8f4504e`)\n\n- **Authoritative integration and source CI:** `origin/v1/integration` is `8f4504ebd3484149bde39b78934c193752a95bfd`, including the PR #101 restore-safety follow-up. PR #101 exact-head CI run [39604909967](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39604909967) passed Node 20/22/24 and Linux packaging; CodeQL [39604909977](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39604909977) passed. Post-merge PR CI [39610114264](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39610114264) passed, but checked out synthetic merge commit `5955b5e` (`8f4504e` merged with `db1ca55`). The separately dispatched source workflow [39615105190](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39615105190) passed all jobs on exact `v1/integration` SHA `8f4504e`; post-merge CodeQL runs [39610114305](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39610114305) and [39610102703](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39610102703) passed on that SHA.\n- **PR and contest state:** PR #8 remains a draft integration-to-`main` candidate. Its CI and CodeQL checks are green, but it is not a release acceptance or publication. PR #102 is open at `3756afe05dbd75c4e6929d87cd50facbb8ab1748`, based on `8f4504e`, to record a synthetic qualification-host preflight; its CodeQL and TypeScript checks passed and its Node matrix was still running at this checkpoint. The preflight report records 10/10 checks using only an empty synthetic marker store; it does not establish private corpus custody or qualification acceptance. The contest has concluded; no contest freeze applies. Historical contest artifacts remain historical evidence only.\n- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed on exact source tree `8f4504e` (tree `2a0799c8a32e88e34322b712cf937d73cbe4d637`), with isolated `HOME`/XDG: 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open). Eleven rows remain below the ordinary tested threshold pending their approved exact-RC evidence: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. The pre-RC checker pass does not imply those RC gates have passed or authorize an acceptance claim.\n- **Evaluator and qualification-host boundary:** Source fixtures for cgroup resource limits, process-tree cleanup, workspace storage, and staged Git-history isolation are in the integration source suite and passed its exact-source CI. A synthetic host preflight at source `8f4504e` recorded 10/10 checks and is being documented in PR #102. Neither source fixtures nor the synthetic-host report establish access separation against the custodian's real store or permit held-out execution before custody acceptance.\n- **Held-out corpus and custody:** Public T2 manifest `eval/heldout-manifest.json` remains the 40-task identity `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`; T3 public manifest identity remains `85fb9cafbe18e846bd64fb13eb4bfa0f92df0792bc93d12adaa685e04c9f1383`. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) has no custodian response since 2026-10-21 12:21 UTC. Current evaluator qualification rejects the sealed T2 corpus's legacy `hidden.command` format; the documented path requires a custodian-owned compatible immutable successor and repeated custody checks. Private digest re-derivation, exposure history, setup/reference validation, effective access separation, and current custody acceptance remain unverified here. No payload, validator, reference solution, or hidden answer was accessed, and no held-out run has started.\n- **Other qualification gates:** No installed-RC provider or standalone matrix, T2/T3/T4 scored qualification, exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility, or independent RC acceptance exists. `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 and `scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md` define the human five-environment × three-size matrix and evidence capture; all 15 real-terminal cells remain unrun because no RC is installed. Automated PTY results do not replace those operator results.\n- **Version, RC, and publication:** Root and CLI package versions remain `0.1.0-alpha.2`. GitHub currently lists only alpha pre-releases `v0.1.0-alpha.1` and `v0.1.0-alpha.2`; no `v1.0.0-rc.N` artifact/tag or stable v1.0.0 tag, npm package, or GitHub release exists. Follow the staged lifecycle in `ACCEPTANCE.md`: pre-RC source gates, RC construction, artifact-bound RC gates, installed-RC qualification and independent G6 acceptance, then stable promotion/publication and post-publication verification.\n\nThe 2026-10-18 checkpoint sections below remain historical evidence. The previously closed PR #46 was never merged; its two readiness commits remain available on the preserved closed-PR branch, not in this reconciliation branch's history, and are superseded by this exact `8f4504e` update.\n\n## Publication status correction (2026-10-18 17:25 UTC)\n\nThe 17:16 checkpoint's phrase “nothing has been tagged or published” was too broad. GitHub lists the existing pre-releases `v0.1.0-alpha.1` and `v0.1.0-alpha.2`, with corresponding tags `7e46bb0da88d06552a66ef703f53a05d1de1f37d` and `c3dcafac93b5f52d913b4dfb6eb292bbcede4566`. Post-merge CI run `39146982849` and CodeQL passed on exact integration `6a16cb60635c9182f13be1635d5f44eddebdcde0`. No v1.0.0 release candidate or stable v1.0.0 publication exists. The superseded 17:16 text below is retained verbatim as historical evidence; this correction is authoritative for current release status.\n\n## Current state update (2026-10-18 17:16 UTC, `6a16cb6`)\n\n[{\"baseRefOid\":\"81976f2586fff9270edfa207195ef2a6bdab0c54\",\"headRefOid\":\"d568125c6d3098d6899b030535157cfd7f75fe4b\",\"number\":170,\"state\":\"MERGED\",\"title\":\"docs(evidence): record RC3 provider verification\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/170\"}]\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16e3a-6ba7-7961-a9ba-21cec97e40c0","create_time":1792851117.7065306}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
