{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T14:14:27.531Z","ordinal":292309,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16e3a-6ba7-7961-a9ba-21cec97e40c0","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-6c2bed5f-ac74-426f-aca8-227c98e24f2d","process_id":"23790","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show origin/main:eval/configs/gateway-engineering-deep.json; git show origin/main:eval/configs/pilot-nexus.json; git show origin/main:eval/README.md | rg -n -C 3 'context|serverProfile|limits' | head -n 100; git show origin/main:eval/run.mjs | sed -n '115,150p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show origin/main:eval/configs/gateway-engineering-deep.json; git show origin/main:eval/configs/pilot-nexus.json; git show origin/main:eval/README.md | rg -n -C 3 'context|serverProfile|limits' | head -n 100; git show origin/main:eval/run.mjs | sed -n '115,150p'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"name\": \"nexus@gateway/engineering/deep\",\n  \"agent\": \"nexus\",\n  \"endpoint\": \"REPLACE_WITH_APPLIANCE_GATEWAY_URL/v1\",\n  \"model\": \"engineering/deep\",\n  \"runs\": 5,\n  \"steps\": 300,\n  \"minutes\": 120,\n  \"args\": [\"--context-limit\", \"65536\"],\n  \"env\": {}\n}\n{\n  \"name\": \"nexus@gateway/engineering/lead\",\n  \"agent\": \"nexus\",\n  \"endpoint\": \"https://10.0.8.5:8443/v1\",\n  \"model\": \"engineering/lead\",\n  \"apiKey\": { \"file\": \"~/.config/nexus/config.env\", \"var\": \"LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY\" },\n  \"caFile\": \"~/.config/nexus/t5820-gateway-ca.crt\",\n  \"limits\": { \"context\": 65536, \"output\": 8192 },\n  \"runs\": 5,\n  \"args\": [\"--context-limit\", \"65536\"]\n}\n36-`--version` command inside the same Bubblewrap filesystem/network boundary, with a cleared environment and bounded\n37-output/time; executable paths and SHA-256 hashes are archived alongside the RC package\n38-digest. `score.mjs --pairs` takes exactly the Nexus,\n39:Goose and OpenCode result files and refuses mismatched model fingerprints, sampling declarations, context/output\n40:limits, explicit per-task request and aggregate requested-output ceilings, run pairs, executable identities, or\n41-effective step/minute budgets. The proxy permits only model-catalog and inference routes, strips client-supplied\n42-authorization and control-plane headers, and enforces configured request/body/output ceilings. These are requested\n43-completion-token ceilings, not exact usage accounting. It reports peer hidden-test results\n44:separately; scores are never combined. The Nexus adapter passes the recorded temperature and step/minute limits;\n45-OpenCode receives a primary evaluation agent with the recorded step limit, temperature and seed; Goose receives the\n46:matching `--max-turns`, context/output limits and temperature settings. Qualification mode currently requires\n47-`sampling.temperature` to be `0` across all three adapters; seed metadata remains recorded when configured.\n48-\n49-## Task format (`eval/tasks/<id>/task.json`)\n--\n61-## Scores\n62-\n63-completion claimed · artifact correct (hidden tests) · false VERIFIED (VERIFIED while hidden tests fail) · regressions\n64:introduced · timed out / harness errors · wall time, steps, tokens (median). Context qualifier (`contextNotRetained`) is\n65-recorded per run.\n66-\n67-## Scoring integrity\n--\n91-| `overloaded` | 503 with `Retry-After: 1` |\n92-| `stream_cut` | The stream is cut after its first tool-call fragment |\n93-| `truncate` | `finish_reason` becomes `length` |\n94:| `context_overflow` | llama.cpp's HTTP 400 `exceed_context_size_error` |\n95-| `malformed_tool_json` | The first tool call's arguments are no longer valid JSON |\n96-\n97-What was injected is recorded in `model.faultsInjected`. Such runs are never treated as infrastructure reruns.\n--\n116-  everything except class and difficulty.\n117-- **The model is identified, not just named.** `fingerprint: { weightsSha256, serverBuild }` and\n118-  `sampling: { temperature, seed }` are set in the config, and the endpoint lists the model. The fingerprint (with the\n119:  listed owner and context) is written to `manifest.json`.\n120-- **Hidden tests are out of the agent's reach.** `runAs` names a separate evaluator user. Candidate execution occurs\n121-  inside the Bubblewrap mount namespace and does not bind the task store or validator sources; its `HOME`, `/tmp`,\n122-  `/run`, and network namespace are isolated. Runtime files are explicit read-only binds. The harness grants the\n--\n150-  archived by the acceptance reviewer before any qualification run. The current candidate task package has not been\n151-  independently accepted.\n152-\n153:### Isolation limits\n154-\n155-Bubblewrap plus the current runner enforces separate mount/user/PID/network namespaces, a cleared task-command\n156-environment, a bounded wall clock, bounded captured output, per-run process-group teardown, and read-only runtime\n157-binds. Black-box qualification keeps oracle expectations outside candidate namespaces. Legacy hidden commands share a\n158-process with candidate code and are rejected during qualification preflight. The hardened legacy path below is only for\n159-development and pilot scoring; it is not qualification evidence. Aggregate CPU, memory, process-count and\n160:writable-storage limits come from the resource contract below, not from request/token ceilings. Appliance-specific\n161-Bubblewrap enforcement is a separate, unverified condition.\n162-\n163-### Hardened legacy hidden tests (development and pilot only)\n--\n240-- Each execution runs under `eval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs` as the only process of its own delegated transient\n241-  `systemd-run --user --scope`. The supervisor writes cgroup v2 `cpu.max` (`cpuPercent`% of one CPU), `memory.max`\n242-  (`memoryBytes`), `memory.swap.max` (0), `memory.oom.group` (1) and `pids.max` (`tasks`) on a `payload` leaf, reads them back, and refuses to\n243:  run on any mismatch. The command joins that leaf before `exec`, so nothing task-controlled runs outside the limits.\n244:  The limits are aggregate over the whole process tree, whatever its uid (`runAs`), session or process group.\n245-- `workspaceRoot` must itself be a dedicated tmpfs mount, not a directory on a shared mount or a bind mount. It must be\n246-  owned by the evaluator harness uid, with owner `rwx` and no group/other read or write permission. Group/other execute\n247-  permission is allowed so a separate evaluator uid can traverse to its per-run ACL-protected directory. For example:\n--\n260-- This contract is supported only on Linux with cgroup v2 CPU, memory and pids controllers, a delegated systemd user\n261-  manager, Bubblewrap and the dedicated tmpfs described above. Missing controllers, mount metadata, user-manager\n262-  delegation or any read-back mismatch fail preflight. Other operating systems and container hosts that cannot expose\n263:  these controls are unsupported for qualification; they must not fall back to process-only or best-effort limits.\n264-- After the command exits or times out, the supervisor records the remaining processes, empties the cgroup with\n265-  `cgroup.kill` (which reaches daemonized processes and other uids), and waits for `populated 0`. A timeout or output\n266-  overflow empties the payload leaf, repeatedly until the supervisor exits, so a stop that arrives before the command\n267-  has joined the leaf is not lost. It also sends the supervisor `SIGTERM` so that it can still report. If the supervisor\n268-  does not exit within 10 s it is killed, and the run fails for lack of a report.\n269:- Each run record carries `resources.{agent,hidden,regression}`: the applied limits, `memoryPeakBytes`, `oomKills`,\n270-  `memoryMaxEvents`, `pidsPeak`, `pidsMaxEvents`, `cpuUsageUsec`, `cpuThrottledUsec`, `survivorsAfterExit` and\n271-  `cleaned`. A missing report, a failed limit read-back or `cleaned: false` makes the run an error. It is never scored\n272-  as a pass or fail.\n--\n303-| Runner, scorer, manifest, per-run logs | done |\n304-| T1 self-test (`selftest-add`, scripted model, in `make test` via `cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`) | done |\n305-| Nexus adapter | done |\n306:| Peer adapters and matched comparison (OpenCode, Goose, Aider; paired scoring requires Nexus, Goose, OpenCode) | adapter versions and effective budgets recorded; `--pairs` verifies the fixed model, limits, sampling, and 5× task/run pairing (Codex CLI excluded: gateway does not serve `/v1/responses`) |\n307-| T2 task set (pilot fixture tasks `t2-*`) | done |\n308-| T3 task set (fact-sheet scorer / steering checks) | not started |\n309-| T4 fault injector | in progress |\n310:| Qualification runs | blocked on independent corpus custody, enforced aggregate sandbox resource limits, completed T3/T4 workloads, exact-RC/provider evidence, and the required operational approvals; the earlier pilot's inference-hour, cloud-budget, and peer-install decisions also remain separate prerequisites |\n311-\n312-## Pilot 2026-10-13 (4 h appliance window)\n313-\n314-Configurations `configs/pilot-*.json`: Nexus, Aider 0.86.2, OpenCode 1.18.35, Goose 1.27.2, all on\n315:`engineering/lead` (Qwen3.6-35B-A3B Q4_K_M, llama.cpp b11347) through the appliance gateway, 64k context. Six T2\n316-fixture tasks (`t2-*`; each hidden test checked to fail on the fixture and pass on a reference fix kept outside the\n317-repo). Budgets 60 steps / 20 min per task (Nexus steps; others by wall clock). The four agents run concurrently on the\n318-same worker, so wall times include queueing.\nif (config.qualification === true) {\n  const corpusProblem = corpusManifestProblem(config, tasksDir, tasks, corpusTaskRows(taskSnapshots, tasks));\n  if (corpusProblem) problems.push(corpusProblem);\n}\nif (config.qualification === true && config.sampling?.temperature !== 0) {\n  problems.push(\"qualification adapters require sampling.temperature=0 so the matched Nexus, Goose and OpenCode runs use the same deterministic setting\");\n}\nif (config.qualification === true) {\n  const budgetProblem = qualificationBudgetProblem(config);\n  if (budgetProblem) problems.push(budgetProblem);\n}\nconst agentIdentity = problems.length ? { record: null, problem: null } : await resolveAgentIdentity(config);\nif (agentIdentity.problem) problems.push(agentIdentity.problem);\nlet fingerprint = null;\nif (!problems.length) {\n  const probe = config.proxy === false ? null : await startModelProxy({ upstream: config.endpoint, caFile });\n  try {\n    const entry = await fetchModelEntry(probe?.url ?? config.endpoint, config.model, apiKey);\n    const fp = modelFingerprint(config, entry);\n    fingerprint = fp.fingerprint;\n    problems.push(...fp.missing.map((m) => `model fingerprint: ${m}`));\n    if (config.qualification === true && (config.agent ?? \"nexus\") === \"nexus\") {\n      const limitsProblem = nexusLimitsProblem(config, entry);\n      if (limitsProblem) problems.push(limitsProblem);\n    }\n  } finally {\n    await probe?.close();\n  }\n}\nif (problems.length) {\n  console.error(`eval/run.mjs: not starting; ${problems.length} problem(s):\\n${problems.map((p) => `  - ${p}`).join(\"\\n\")}`);\n  process.exit(2);\n}\nconst frozenTaskRows = taskRecords.map(({ id }) => corpusTaskRows(taskSnapshots, [id])[0]);\nfs.writeFileSync(path.join(args.out, \"manifest.json\"), JSON.stringify({\n  createdAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":29414}},"started_at_ms":1792851267531,"completed_at_ms":1792851267531}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T14:14:28.592Z","ordinal":292310,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a16e43-53f0-7342-9e6d-f1ce905b1176","call_id":"call_c8edead8788344d284f12cdd0bb9218e","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2564)\nTotal output lines: 151\n\n{\n  \"name\": \"nexus@gateway/engineering/deep\",\n  \"agent\": \"nexus\",\n  \"endpoint\": \"REPLACE_WITH_APPLIANCE_GATEWAY_URL/v1\",\n  \"model\": \"engineering/deep\",\n  \"runs\": 5,\n  \"steps\": 300,\n  \"minutes\": 120,\n  \"args\": [\"--context-limit\", \"65536\"],\n  \"env\": {}\n}\n{\n  \"name\": \"nexus@gateway/engineering/lead\",\n  \"agent\": \"nexus\",\n  \"endpoint\": \"https://10.0.8.5:8443/v1\",\n  \"model\": \"engineering/lead\",\n  \"apiKey\": { \"file\": \"~/.config/nexus/config.env\", \"var\": \"LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY\" },\n  \"caFile\": \"~/.config/nexus/t5820-gateway-ca.crt\",\n  \"limits\": { \"context\": 65536, \"output\": 8192 },\n  \"runs\": 5,\n  \"args\": [\"--context-limit\", \"65536\"]\n}\n36-`--version` command inside the same Bubblewrap filesystem/network boundary, with a cleared environment and bounded\n37-output/time; executable paths and SHA-256 hashes are archived alongside the RC package\n38-digest. `score.mjs --pairs` takes exactly the Nexus,\n39:Goose and OpenCode result files and refuses mismatched model fingerprints, sampling declarations, context/output\n40:limits, explicit per-task request and aggregate requested-output ceilings, run pairs, executable identities, or\n41-effective step/minute budgets. The proxy permits only model-catalog and inference routes, strips client-supplied\n42-authorization and control-plane headers, and enforces configured request/body/output ceilings. These are requested\n43-completion-token ceilings, not exact usage accounting. It reports peer hidden-test results\n44:separately; scores are never combined. The Nexus adapter passes the recorded temperature and step/minute limits;\n45-OpenCode receives a primary evaluation agent with the recorded step limit, temperature and seed; Goose receives the\n46:matching `--max-turns`, context/output limits and temperature settings. Qualification mode currently requires\n47-`sampling.temperature` to be `0` across all three adapters; seed metadata remains recorded when configured.\n48-\n49-## Task format (`eval/tasks/<id>/task.json`)\n--\n61-## Scores\n62-\n63-completion claimed · artifact correct (hidden tests) · false VERIFIED (VERIFIED while hidden tests fail) · regressions\n64:introduced · timed out / harness errors · wall time, steps, tokens (median). Context qualifier (`contextNotRetained`) is\n65-recorded per run.\n66-\n67-## Scoring integrity\n--\n91-| `overloaded` | 503 with `Retry-After: 1` |\n92-| `stream_cut` | The stream is cut after its first tool-call fragment |\n93-| `truncate` | `finish_reason` becomes `length` |\n94:| `context_overflow` | llama.cpp's HTTP 400 `exceed_context_size_error` |\n95-| `malformed_tool_json` | The first tool call's arguments are no longer valid JSON |\n96-\n97-What was injected is recorded in `model.faultsInjected`. Such runs are never treated as infrastructure reruns.\n--\n116-  everything except class and difficulty.\n117-- **The model is identified, not just named.** `fingerprint: { weightsSha256, serverBuild }` and\n118-  `sampling: { temperature, seed }` are set in the config, and the endpoint lists the model. The fingerprint (with the\n119:  listed owner and context) is written to `manifest.json`.\n120-- **Hidden tests are out of the agent's reach.** `runAs` names a separate evaluator user. Candidate execution occurs\n121-  inside the Bubblewrap mount namespace and does not bind the task store or validator sources; its `HOME`, `/tmp`,\n122-  `/run`, and network namespace are isolated. Runtime files are explicit read-only binds. The harness grants the\n--\n150-  archived by the acceptance reviewer before any qualification run. The current candidate task package has not been\n151-  independently accepted.\n152-\n153:### Isolation limits\n154-\n155-Bubblewrap plus the current runner enforces separate mount/user/PID/network namespaces, a cleared task-command\n156-environment, a bounded wall clock, bounded captured output, per-run process-group teardown, and read-only runtime\n157-binds. Black-box qualification keeps oracle expectations outside candidate namespaces. Legacy hidden commands share a\n158-process with candidate code and are rejected during qualification preflight. The hardened legacy path below is only for\n159-development and pilot scoring; it is not qualification evidence. Aggregate CPU, memory, process-count and\n160:writable-storage limits come from the resource contract below, not from request/token ceilings. Appliance-specific\n161-Bubblewrap enforcement is a separate, unverified condition.\n1…364 tokens truncated…ted for qualification; they must not fall back to process-only or best-effort limits.\n264-- After the command exits or times out, the supervisor records the remaining processes, empties the cgroup with\n265-  `cgroup.kill` (which reaches daemonized processes and other uids), and waits for `populated 0`. A timeout or output\n266-  overflow empties the payload leaf, repeatedly until the supervisor exits, so a stop that arrives before the command\n267-  has joined the leaf is not lost. It also sends the supervisor `SIGTERM` so that it can still report. If the supervisor\n268-  does not exit within 10 s it is killed, and the run fails for lack of a report.\n269:- Each run record carries `resources.{agent,hidden,regression}`: the applied limits, `memoryPeakBytes`, `oomKills`,\n270-  `memoryMaxEvents`, `pidsPeak`, `pidsMaxEvents`, `cpuUsageUsec`, `cpuThrottledUsec`, `survivorsAfterExit` and\n271-  `cleaned`. A missing report, a failed limit read-back or `cleaned: false` makes the run an error. It is never scored\n272-  as a pass or fail.\n--\n303-| Runner, scorer, manifest, per-run logs | done |\n304-| T1 self-test (`selftest-add`, scripted model, in `make test` via `cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`) | done |\n305-| Nexus adapter | done |\n306:| Peer adapters and matched comparison (OpenCode, Goose, Aider; paired scoring requires Nexus, Goose, OpenCode) | adapter versions and effective budgets recorded; `--pairs` verifies the fixed model, limits, sampling, and 5× task/run pairing (Codex CLI excluded: gateway does not serve `/v1/responses`) |\n307-| T2 task set (pilot fixture tasks `t2-*`) | done |\n308-| T3 task set (fact-sheet scorer / steering checks) | not started |\n309-| T4 fault injector | in progress |\n310:| Qualification runs | blocked on independent corpus custody, enforced aggregate sandbox resource limits, completed T3/T4 workloads, exact-RC/provider evidence, and the required operational approvals; the earlier pilot's inference-hour, cloud-budget, and peer-install decisions also remain separate prerequisites |\n311-\n312-## Pilot 2026-10-13 (4 h appliance window)\n313-\n314-Configurations `configs/pilot-*.json`: Nexus, Aider 0.86.2, OpenCode 1.18.35, Goose 1.27.2, all on\n315:`engineering/lead` (Qwen3.6-35B-A3B Q4_K_M, llama.cpp b11347) through the appliance gateway, 64k context. Six T2\n316-fixture tasks (`t2-*`; each hidden test checked to fail on the fixture and pass on a reference fix kept outside the\n317-repo). Budgets 60 steps / 20 min per task (Nexus steps; others by wall clock). The four agents run concurrently on the\n318-same worker, so wall times include queueing.\nif (config.qualification === true) {\n  const corpusProblem = corpusManifestProblem(config, tasksDir, tasks, corpusTaskRows(taskSnapshots, tasks));\n  if (corpusProblem) problems.push(corpusProblem);\n}\nif (config.qualification === true && config.sampling?.temperature !== 0) {\n  problems.push(\"qualification adapters require sampling.temperature=0 so the matched Nexus, Goose and OpenCode runs use the same deterministic setting\");\n}\nif (config.qualification === true) {\n  const budgetProblem = qualificationBudgetProblem(config);\n  if (budgetProblem) problems.push(budgetProblem);\n}\nconst agentIdentity = problems.length ? { record: null, problem: null } : await resolveAgentIdentity(config);\nif (agentIdentity.problem) problems.push(agentIdentity.problem);\nlet fingerprint = null;\nif (!problems.length) {\n  const probe = config.proxy === false ? null : await startModelProxy({ upstream: config.endpoint, caFile });\n  try {\n    const entry = await fetchModelEntry(probe?.url ?? config.endpoint, config.model, apiKey);\n    const fp = modelFingerprint(config, entry);\n    fingerprint = fp.fingerprint;\n    problems.push(...fp.missing.map((m) => `model fingerprint: ${m}`));\n    if (config.qualification === true && (config.agent ?? \"nexus\") === \"nexus\") {\n      const limitsProblem = nexusLimitsProblem(config, entry);\n      if (limitsProblem) problems.push(limitsProblem);\n    }\n  } finally {\n    await probe?.close();\n  }\n}\nif (problems.length) {\n  console.error(`eval/run.mjs: not starting; ${problems.length} problem(s):\\n${problems.map((p) => `  - ${p}`).join(\"\\n\")}`);\n  process.exit(2);\n}\nconst frozenTaskRows = taskRecords.map(({ id }) => corpusTaskRows(taskSnapshots, [id])[0]);\nfs.writeFileSync(path.join(args.out, \"manifest.json\"), JSON.stringify({\n  createdAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16e3a-6ba7-7961-a9ba-21cec97e40c0","create_time":1792851268.592202}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
