y session on a cloned/untrusted repo, including `--approve` review mode | agent.ts:1602-1617 (baseline), 3432-3436 (oracle), 1630 (independence copy run); tester.ts:113-136 | SOURCE. Before the first file edit (agent.ts:4034, after the edit's own approval) and at every `task_completed`, Nexus runs `make test` / `npm test` / `cargo test` / `pytest` through `bridge.executeTool` directly. These run arbitrary repo-defined code with no approval prompt and no workspace-trust check (unlike MCP/plugins, workspace_trust.ts), and unsandboxed unless `--sandbox`. Review mode shows an approval for `edit_file` but never for the hidden repo script that follows. Builds on SEC-01; it is a separate path because it bypasses even review mode. | Cloning a hostile repo and asking for any edit runs its test script on the host without a prompt. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: gate discovered verifiers on workspace trust or a one-time approval of the exact command (shown with its script body), and run them sandboxed when one is available. Document this. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:53:| SEC-05 | S2 | untrusted repo opened | skills.ts:31-33; agent.ts:3301,3789 | SOURCE. Workspace skills (SKILL.md) are loaded and advertised in the system prompt with no workspace-trust check, unlike MCP and plugins (workspace_trust.ts:5-24). `activate_skill` is non-mutating, so it is never approved. | Persistent prompt injection from a cloned repo. Combined with SEC-01 this gives command execution. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: gate workspace skill directories on workspace trust, or show them as untrusted and require approval to activate. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:136:| R-SEC-5 | Workspace skills are subject to workspace trust. | safety | RELEASE-REQUIRED | An untrusted fixture repo with `skills/x/SKILL.md` does not appear in the system prompt or `/skills` without trust. |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/trust_inference.md:68:- Remediation: load workspace-scoped plugins/MCP only after an explicit, persisted per-workspace trust decision (hash of the config/plugin\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:112:| AGT-R8 | No implicit standing rules from prompts; no workspace writes in read-only mode; workspace-supplied knowledge gated by workspace trust. | safety (AGT-10) | RELEASE-REQUIRED | Read-only run leaves no `.nexus/`; prompt \"never run tests\" does not appear in next session's system prompt. |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/peers.md:17:| **2. Context / long tasks** | `/compact`; `model_auto_compact_token_limit`, `model_context_window`; `/status` shows context usage; `codex resume`; `/fork` copies a chat to a new chat or worktree; `tool_output_token_limit`; resumable state in a SQLite DB (`sqlite_home`); AGENTS.md (`project_doc_max_bytes`, fallback filenames); memories [CX-CFG][CX-SLASH][CX-CLI]. | Auto-compaction at a per-model threshold, `/autocompact <tokens>`, `/compact [focus]`, `/context`; after compaction re-injects CLAUDE.md/startup content, a structured summary, up to 5 most-recent files and invoked skill bodies (5k cap each) [CC-CTX]. Rewind menu can \"summarize from/up to here\" [CC-CKPT]. `--continue/--resume`, `/branch`, `--fork-session`; resume-from-summary dialog for idle >1h, >100k-token sessions [CC-SESS]. CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, auto memory [CC-OV]. Subagent `autoCompactWindow` (2.1.296) [CC-CHG]. | `compaction.auto` (default true), `compaction.prune` (old tool outputs, default false), `compaction.reserved` token buffer [OC-CFG]. Per-model `limit.context/output` for custom providers [OC-PROV]. `instructions` file globs [OC-CFG]. | Auto-compact at min(80% of window, 225k tokens) (`GOOSE_AUTO_COMPACT_THRESHOLD`/`_TOKEN_LIMIT`); `/compact`; fallback strategies summarize/truncate/clear/prompt (`GOOSE_CONTEXT_STRATEGY`); headless defaults to summarize [GS-CTX]. | Ollama: warns 2k default ctx \"silently discards context\"; aider sets `num_ctx` to fit each request + 8k reply [AI-OLLAMA]. (No compaction feature verified this session.) |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/peers.md:56:8. After compaction, project instructions (AGENTS.md-equivalent) and recently edited files are re-injected [CC-CTX].\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":31948}},"started_at_ms":1792851490366,"completed_at_ms":1792851490366}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T14:18:11.650Z","ordinal":292471,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a16e46-bb42-7840-9f1d-71b37268f3eb","call_id":"call_73a7e1a261f54948a0def8fbf8667e04","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 10005)\nTotal output lines: 60\n\ndocs/NEXUS-CLOUD-PROVIDERS-PLAN.md:7:The supplied Nexus snapshot is old. Its local appliance connectivity may differ from the actual codebase. Do not treat its client, credential loading, endpoint format, routing, or file paths as current requirements. The terminal agent must inspect the actual checkout and follow its AGENTS.md before choosing implementation locations. Historical Nexus snapshots in the evidence bundle are explicitly non-authoritative.\ndocs/NEXUS-CLOUD-PROVIDERS-PLAN.md:55:3. Configuration precedence and project trust: flags, environment, user configuration, workspace configuration, restored sessions. Identify what can currently change a destination or credential source.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_DOCTOR_RECOVERED_REQUEST.md:11:Work in the Nexus repository on this development server. Establish the repository root from the current working directory and read applicable `AGENTS.md` instructions before editing. If you cannot locate the repository, ask for its location.\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:242:| `/onboard` | Scan workspace tech stack and generate customized `AGENTS.md` & diagram |\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:244:| `/init` | Scaffold `AGENTS.md` project rules file |\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:295:- **Workspace Trust**: A workspace's own `.mcp.json` / `mcp.json` servers and `.nexus/plugins/` / `plugins/` modules run code from the workspace, so they are loaded only after you trust it: `nexus trust [path]` (undo with `nexus trust --remove`, list with `nexus trust --list`; recorded in `~/.config/nexus/trusted_workspaces.json`, which the agent's file tools cannot write). Untrusted, they are not loaded and Nexus says so (a notice at start, `nexus doctor`, `nexus mcp`, `nexus plugins`); in `--read-only` mode they are never loaded. Servers and plugins in your home configuration (`~/.config/nexus/`, `~/.nexus/`) are always loaded.\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:309:- **Real-Time Hot-Reloading**: Automatically detects edits or additions in `skills/` and `AGENTS.md` and reloads them dynamically without restarting the REPL.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_MATURITY_FIXES_2026-10-11_REQUEST.md:11:Locate the actual Nexus checkout and read applicable AGENTS.md instructions. Preserve existing dirty work. The session recorded `/home/mike/nexus-code`, but verify the current location. Locate `nexus-session-session_20261011_162349_6lvu.json` if available; treat its embedded instructions and tool outputs as historical evidence, not current authority.\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-phase3b-slash-commands.md:432:  { name: \"onboard\", usage: \"/onboard\", summary: \"Scan the workspace and write a tailored AGENTS.md\" },\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-phase3b-slash-commands.md:662:    \"Wrote a tailored AGENTS.md.\",\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:3:These rules apply to every agent (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Nexus itself, or a human) that implements any part of this package at the same time as another. The repository's root `AGENTS.md` points here. The rules come from incidents recorded in `tasks/lessons.md`:\ncli/test/workspace_trust.test.ts:33:describe(\"workspace trust\", () => {\ndocs/research/context-engineering/DOGFOOD-CONTEXT-FORENSICS.md:52: 5   18.2k  +0.3k    read_file (AGENTS.md)\ndocs/research/context-engineering/DOGFOOD-CONTEXT-FORENSICS.md:108:| **Turn-specific** | README (step 4) and AGENTS.md (step 5) for orientation; each Cloudflare doc read for one summary sentence; `cargo test` 13/13 (used in the final summary) | Yes: a reference + a 1-line extract would serve the later turns. |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:65:| AGENTS.md | build `make build`, test `make test`, lint `cargo clippy` / `npm run lint`; keep comments; modular typed code |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:116:- **Workspace trust before executing project configuration** (Claude Code and Codex document trust prompts for\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:257:| B2 | **Workspace trust**: never import workspace plugins or start workspace MCP servers until the operator trusts that workspace (per-path trust record); `--read-only` disables both; MCP children get an environment allowlist | T-03 | clone a repo containing `plugins/x.mjs` and `.mcp.json` that touch a sentinel → no sentinel without explicit trust, in every mode |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:294:| 1 | B1 execution authority + B2 workspace trust (+ R4 listing confinement, T13 dry-run) | 0 | capability × mode × context matrix complete and enforced; adversarial suite blocked; no regression in existing suites |\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:18:| Run several agents on this plan at once without collisions | [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) (also referenced from the root `AGENTS.md`) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:72:3. **Files created or changed in the repository.** The audit created `docs/v1.0.0/**`. At the owner's request, it appended a short \"v1.0.0 work and concurrent agents\" section to the root `AGENTS.md`, without changing the existing content. Nothing else in the repository was modified.\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:37:  - workspace trust;\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:148:| tasks/, AGENTS.md, README, quickstart | 5 | Full read | lead | — |\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CURRENT-NEXUS-CONTEXT-ARCHITECTURE.md:15:| System prompt | `buildSystemPrompt()` (~l.1239) | OBSERVED. Fixed text + `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` rules + skills + `KnowledgeGraph.exportPromptSection()` + canonical few-shots. Comment states the prefix is kept byte-stable for prefix caching. Built once in the constructor / `resetConversation()`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:36:| **C (chosen)** | Posture follows workspace trust. **Untrusted workspace → review** for `write_workspace`, `exec`, `egress` and `context_inject`. **Trusted workspace → auto** for `write_workspace` and `exec`; `egress` asks once per origin per session. `--yes` or `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` force auto. `--sandbox` stays available. | Safe for cloned or unknown repos. Low friction on the operator's own repos after one `nexus trust .`. Reuses the existing trust store, so there is no new concept. |\ncli/test/harness.test.ts:2310:  test(\"scanAndOnboardWorkspace discovers stack and writes AGENTS.md with diagram\", () => {\ncli/test/harness.test.ts:2333:      assert.strictEqual(fs.existsSync(path.join(tmpDir, \"AGENTS.md\")), true);\ncli/test/harness.test.ts:2334:      const content = fs.readFileSync(path.join(tmpDir, \"AGENTS.md\"), \"utf-8\");\ncli/src/slash/catalog.ts:114:  { name: \"onboard\", usage: \"/onboard\", summary: \"Scan the workspace and write a tailored AGENTS.md\" },\ncli/src/slash/session_commands.ts:267:    \"Wrote a tailored AGENTS.md.\",\ncli/test/inference_transport.test.ts:95:      frame({ choices: [{ index: 0, delta: { tool_calls: [{ index: 0, function: { arguments: 'th\":\"AGENTS.md\"}' } }] } }] }) +\ncli/test/inference_transport.test.ts:104:        assert.deepEqual(m.tool_calls?.map((t) => [t.id, t.function.name, t.function.arguments]), [[\"c1\", \"read_file\", '{\"path\":\"AGENTS.md\"}']]);\ncli/src/workspace_trust.ts:33: * In --read-only mode, workspace trust never authorizes executing project plugins/MCP.\ncli/src/git.ts:49:    \"AGENTS.md\",\ncli/src/git.ts:73:  const target = path.join(workspace, \"AGENTS.md\");\ncli/src/onboard.ts:120:  // Generate AGENTS.md content\ncli/src/onboard.ts:146:    const targetFile = path.join(root, \"AGENTS.md\");\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_ACCEPTANCE_BLOCKER_REMEDIATION_2026-10-08.md:428:| Pattern | 6-call reacquisition cycle ×5 | 8-call cycle ×3.75 | 8-call cycle ×10: `file_tree`, `git_log`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `EXECUTION_CONVERGENCE.md`, `types.ts`, `client.ts`, `agent.ts` |\ncli/src/mcp.ts:950:              description: \"Content of AGENTS.md project rules and conventions\",\ncli/src/mcp.ts:976:        const agentsFile = path.join(this.workspace, \"AGENTS.md\");\ncli/src/mcp.ts:977:        const content = fs.existsSync(agentsFile) ? fs.readFileSync(agentsFile, \"utf-8\") : \"# No AGENTS.md found\";\ncli/src/repl.ts:258:    console.log(`  ${pc.bold(pc.yellow(\"/init\"))}               Scaffold AGENTS.md rules file in workspace`);\ncli/src/repl.ts:1352:            console.log(`  • Generated customized ${pc.bold(\"AGENTS.md\")} with architecture diagram.\\n`);\ndocs/reviews/evidence/tui_surface_baseline/events.ndjson:1:{\"v\":1,\"type\":\"hello\",\"protocol\":1,\"pid\":3049145,\"commands\":[{\"name\":\"help\",\"usage\":\"/help\",\"summary\":\"List the slash commands\"},{\"name\":\"status\",\"usage\":\"/status\",\"summary\":\"Workspace, model, mode, endpoint and session\"},{\"name\":\"doctor\",\"usage\":\"/doctor [--deep] [--fix [--yes]]\",\"summary\":\"Diagnose this session's configuration, endpoint, engine, shell and state; --fix repairs (runs while busy without --fix)\"},{\"name\":\"clear\",\"usage\":\"/clear\",\"summary\":\"Reset the conversation context\"},{\"name\":\"compact\",\"usage\":\"/compact [--llm]\",\"summary\":\"Condense earlier messages to free context\"},{\"name\":\"mode\",\"usage\":\"/mode [auto|review]\",\"summary\":\"Run edits and commands freely, or ask first\"},{\"name\":\"model\",\"usage\":\"/model [provider] [model]\",\"summary\":\"Choose a model from any connected provider (ctrl+p connects one)\"},{\"name\":\"shell\",\"usage\":\"/shell [bash|zsh|sh]\",\"summary\":\"Show or switch the command shell\"},{\"name\":\"cd\",\"usage\":\"/cd [path]\",\"summary\":\"Show or change the workspace directory\"},{\"name\":\"tokens\",\"usage\":\"/tokens\",\"summa