y\"},{\"name\":\"paste\",\"usage\":\"/paste\",\"summary\":\"Put the clipboard into the composer\"},{\"name\":\"sessions\",\"usage\":\"/sessions\",\"summary\":\"Saved sessions\"},{\"name\":\"save\",\"usage\":\"/save [name]\",\"summary\":\"Save this session\"},{\"name\":\"resume\",\"usage\":\"/resume [id]\",\"summary\":\"Load a saved session (the latest by default)\"},{\"name\":\"history\",\"usage\":\"/history [query|run <n>]\",\"summary\":\"Search earlier prompts or run one again\"},{\"name\":\"export\",\"usage\":\"/export [md|json]\",\"summary\":\"Write the session transcript into the workspace\"},{\"name\":\"init\",\"usage\":\"/init\",\"summary\":\"Create a project rules file\"},{\"name\":\"onboard\",\"usage\":\"/onboard\",\"summary\":\"Scan the workspace and write a tailored AGENTS.md\"},{\"name\":\"plan\",\"usage\":\"/plan [add <phase>|start <n>|done <n>|clear]\",\"summary\":\"Show or edit the active plan\"},{\"name\":\"requirements\",\"usage\":\"/requirements [accept <id>...|clear]\",\"summary\":\"The objective's acceptance requirements; accept a scope reduction, or clear the objective to start a new one\"},{\"name\":\"knowledge\",\"usage\":\"/knowledge [set <key> <rule>|delete <key>]\",\"summary\":\"Persistent project knowledge\"},{\"name\":\"skills\",\"usage\":\"/skills\",\"summary\":\"Discovered agent skills\"},{\"name\":\"skill\",\"usage\":\"/skill <name> | init <name>\",\"summary\":\"Show a skill or scaffold a new one\"},{\"name\":\"mcp\",\"usage\":\"/mcp [add|resources|resource <uri>|prompts|prompt <name>]\",\"summary\":\"MCP servers, tools, resources and prompts\"},{\"name\":\"plugins\",\"usage\":\"/plugins\",\"summary\":\"Loaded plugins\"},{\"name\":\"browse\",\"usage\":\"/browse <url>\",\"summary\":\"Open a URL in the headless browser\"},{\"name\":\"image\",\"usage\":\"/image <path> [prompt]\",\"summary\":\"Send an image to the vision model\"},{\"name\":\"tdd\",\"usage\":\"/tdd <issue>\",\"summary\":\"Run a RED → GREEN → REFACTOR cycle\"},{\"name\":\"team\",\"usage\":\"/team <role|full> [--independent-review] <objective>\",\"summary\":\"Run a role or the full team as a durable operation (researcher, architect, implementer, tester, reviewer)\"},{\"name\":\"theme\",\"usage\":\"/theme [name]\",\"summary\":\"Show or save the colour theme\"},{\"name\":\"recover\",\"usage\":\"/recover [task-id]\",\"summary\":\"Recover durable task state\"},{\"name\":\"exit\",\"usage\":\"/exit\",\"summary\":\"Quit Nexus\"}]}\ndocs/reviews/evidence/nexus-ratatui-facelift-2026-10-03/repl-session.typescript:51:  /init               Scaffold AGENTS.md rules file in workspace\r\ndocs/reviews/evidence/nexus-ratatui-facelift-2026-10-03/repl-after.txt:43:  /init               Scaffold AGENTS.md rules file in workspace\ndocs/PHASE3_IMPLEMENTATION_DECOMPOSITION.md:885:| `CTX-011` | SATISFIED_EXISTING | `git.ts` (INC-07) | Project rules injection test | AGENTS.md rules injected |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/RULES.md:9:- AGENTS.md: build `make build`, test `make test`, lint `cargo clippy` / `npm run lint`; keep comments; modular typed code.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:52:| VER-01 | S2 | Any session on a cloned/untrusted repo, including `--approve` review mode | agent.ts:1602-1617 (baseline), 3432-3436 (oracle), 1630 (independence copy run); tester.ts:113-136 | SOURCE. Before the first file edit (agent.ts:4034, after the edit's own approval) and at every `task_completed`, Nexus runs `make test` / `npm test` / `cargo test` / `pytest` through `bridge.executeTool` directly. These run arbitrary repo-defined code with no approval prompt and no workspace-trust check (unlike MCP/plugins, workspace_trust.ts), and unsandboxed unless `--sandbox`. Review mode shows an approval for `edit_file` but never for the hidden repo script that follows. Builds on SEC-01; it is a separate path because it bypasses even review mode. | Cloning a hostile repo and asking for any edit runs its test script on the host without a prompt. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: gate discovered verifiers on workspace trust or a one-time approval of the exact command (shown with its script body), and run them sandboxed when one is available. Document this. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:53:| SEC-05 | S2 | untrusted repo opened | skills.ts:31-33; agent.ts:3301,3789 | SOURCE. Workspace skills (SKILL.md) are loaded and advertised in the system prompt with no workspace-trust check, unlike MCP and plugins (workspace_trust.ts:5-24). `activate_skill` is non-mutating, so it is never approved. | Persistent prompt injection from a cloned repo. Combined with SEC-01 this gives command execution. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: gate workspace skill directories on workspace trust, or show them as untrusted and require approval to activate. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:136:| R-SEC-5 | Workspace skills are subject to workspace trust. | safety | RELEASE-REQUIRED | An untrusted fixture repo with `skills/x/SKILL.md` does not appear in the system prompt or `/skills` without trust. |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/trust_inference.md:68:- Remediation: load workspace-scoped plugins/MCP only after an explicit, persisted per-workspace trust decision (hash of the config/plugin\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:112:| AGT-R8 | No implicit standing rules from prompts; no workspace writes in read-only mode; workspace-supplied knowledge gated by workspace trust. | safety (AGT-10) | RELEASE-REQUIRED | Read-only run leaves no `.nexus/`; prompt \"never run tests\" does not appear in next session's system prompt. |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/peers.md:17:| **2. Context / long tasks** | `/compact`; `model_auto_compact_token_limit`, `model_context_window`; `/status` shows context usage; `codex resume`; `/fork` copies a chat to a new chat or worktree; `tool_output_token_limit`; resumable state in a SQLite DB (`sqlite_home`); AGENTS.md (`project_doc_max_bytes`, fallback filenames); memories [CX-CFG][CX-SLASH][CX-CLI]. | Auto-compaction at a per-model threshold, `/autocompact <tokens>`, `/compact [focus]`, `/context`; after compaction re-injects CLAUDE.md/startup content, a structured summary, up to 5 most-recent files and invoked skill bodies (5k cap each) [CC-CTX]. Rewind menu can \"summarize from/up to here\" [CC-CKPT]. `--continue/--resume`, `/branch`, `--fork-session`; resume-from-summary dialog for idle >1h, >100k-token sessions [CC-SESS]. CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, auto memory [CC-OV]. Subagent `autoCompactWindow` (2.1.296) [CC-CHG]. | `compaction.auto` (default true), `compaction.prune` (old tool outputs, default false), `compaction.reserved` token buffer [OC-CFG]. Per-model `limit.context/output` for custom providers [OC-PROV]. `instructions` file globs [OC-CFG]. | Auto-compact at min(80% of window, 225k tokens) (`GOOSE_AUTO_COMPACT_THRESHOLD`/`_TOKEN_LIMIT`); `/compact`; fallback strategies summarize/truncate/clear/prompt (`GOOSE_CONTEXT_STRATEGY`); headless defaults to summarize [GS-CTX]. | Ollama: warns 2k default ctx \"silently discards context\"; aider sets `num_ctx` to fit each request + 8k reply [AI-OLLAMA]. (No compaction feature verified this session.) |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/peers.md:56:8. After compaction, project instructions (AGENTS.md-equivalent) and recently edited files are re-injected [CC-CTX].\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16e45-93b3-7a42-bd33-3c943d45de73","create_time":1792851491.650193}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
