tartup trust chooser before the REPL or TUI starts in an untrusted workspace.\nL174:   * Offer Trust and continue, Continue without trusting, and Exit. Trust persists through the existing trust store; continuing untrusted does not change the configured permission mode.\nL175:   * Load project instruction files only after explicit workspace trust. Non-interactive launches never grant trust implicitly and continue under the existing untrusted-workspace behavior.\nL176:   * Sanitize terminal control and Unicode format characters in displayed paths and fit text by grapheme display-cell width.\nL177:   * Document the startup behavior and add prompt, trust persistence, failure, non-TTY, prompt ordering behavior, and path display regressions.\nL178: ## Validation\nL179:   * Focused startup/workspace trust tests: 16/16 passed on the committed source.\nL180:   * `npm run build`: passed.\nL181:   * Independent read-only source review: ACCEPT on the exact reviewed diff.\nL182:   * A full CLI `npm test` attempt ran in an isolated snapshot under the suite claim but did not complete. It reported failures across engine-backed, continuity, qualification, and packaged-entrypoint tests; this local attempt omitted the CI job's built Rust binaries and qualification host setup. It is not passing evidence. Exact-head CI is running on this PR.\nL183: ## Scope\nL184: \nL185: This implements the startup folder-trust interaction shown by the operator. It does not change release acceptance status; RC and release qualification remain separate gates.\nL186: \nL187: [Input][Input]\nL188: \nL189: Sorry, something went wrong.\nL190: \nL191: ### Uh oh!\nL192: \nL193: There was an error while loading. Please reload this page.\nL194: \nL195: ###\nL196: \nL197: 【79†coderabbitai】 Bot commented 【80†Oct 24, 2026】 •\nL198: \nL199: edited\nL200: \nL201: Loading\nL202: ### Uh oh!\nL203: \nL204: There was an error while loading. Please reload this page.\nL205: \nL206: Copy link\nL207: \nL208: Copy Markdown\n