mantics.test.ts` was not updated. As a result, the `interactive REPL (pty)` subtests run under `util-linux script` (which provides pseudo-terminal TTY streams), encounter the trust prompt, and hang waiting for user input, causing a 30s timeout failure:\nL256:   1. `cli/test/turn_semantics.test.ts:708`: `Ctrl-C during a delayed mutating trajectory: one interrupt, no new mutation, prompt returns, next turn works`\nL257: \nL258:     `Error: timeout waiting for /❯ /; output tail:\nL259:     Trust this folder?\nL260:     ↑↓ navigate · Enter select · Esc exit\nL261:     /tmp/nexus-turn-...\nL262:     Load project instructions\nL263:     …\nL264:     › Trust and continue\nL265:       Continue without trusting\nL266:       Exit\nL267:     `\nL268:   2. `cli/test/turn_semantics.test.ts:751`: `multiple prompts in one session keep working; Ctrl-C at idle still exits deliberately`\nL269: (Fails with identical timeout waiting for `/❯ /` at the trust prompt).\nL270: #### Recommended Resolution\nL271: \nL272: In `cli/test/turn_semantics.test.ts`, import `trustWorkspace` from `./helpers/fixtures.js` and ensure the workspace is trusted before launching the REPL in the `session` helper:\nL273: \nL274:     import { startGateway, makeRepo, makeHome, Reply, ptyTest, trustWorkspace } from \"./helpers/fixtures.js\";\nL275:     // ...\nL276:     async function session(gw: Gateway, repo: string, home: string) {\nL277:       trustWorkspace(home, repo);\nL278:       const cmd = ...\nL279: Once updated and rebased, exact-head CI should be re-run.\nL280: \nL281: [Input][Input]\nL282: \nL283: Sorry, something went wrong.\nL284: ### Uh oh!\nL285: \nL286: There was an error while loading. Please reload this page.\nL287: \nL288: 【61†mikeholownych】 【89†force-pushed】 the v1/startup-workspace-trust branch from 【90†`f4d40cd`】 to 【91†`fb70052`】 【89†Compare】 【92†October 24, 2026 07:42】\nL289: \nL290: ###\nL291: \nL292: 【61†mikeholownych】 commented 【93†Oct 24, 2026】\nL293: \nL294: Copy link\nL295: \nL296: