{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T14:19:26.945Z","ordinal":292543,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a16e47-e160-7c10-95a9-03902808fbd9","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — reviewed the uncommitted diff at base `be2cd2f255414f554572c86baa884d9271ff5ea1` (diff SHA-256 `8e8ede73663c4d05d8ee286adb43fc052fdb7f35f24d865deb818542c83c3ad5`). I made no edits and ran no suites.\n\n- **Line 11:** The claim that the required live engineering task “remains incomplete” is stale or too broad. A later RC3 live-task evidence record, commit `a7b9c7a`, reports the task passed and received an independent ACCEPT for the RC3 E5 row only. That commit is not present on `be2cd2f`; say so explicitly, while retaining that no RC4-bound evidence or overall RC acceptance exists.\n- **Line 3:** Exact-head CI logs show `check_requirements.mjs` ran in report mode, not `--enforce`. I found no retained enforcement record for `be2cd2f`; the local check in this dirty worktree rejects the dirty source tree. Link clean exact-revision enforcement evidence or describe only the CI requirements report.\n\nThe cited main CI and CodeQL successes, RC4 tag/artifact identity, and PR #194 status matched the checked records at review time. `git diff --check` was clean."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16e45-93b3-7a42-bd33-3c943d45de73","create_time":1792851566.9449735}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":15026}}
