{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T14:19:57.284Z","ordinal":292559,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"task_complete","root_turn_id":"01a16e45-93b3-7a42-bd33-3c943d45de73","turn_id":"01a16e45-93b3-7a42-bd33-3c943d45de73","last_agent_message":"Yes—that is the missing startup behavior: Nexus should ask about an unfamiliar project folder before loading its project instructions. The choices should let you **trust and continue**, **continue without trusting**, or **exit**. Continuing without trust should preserve your chosen permission mode; it should not force read-only.\n\nThis has since been implemented in [PR #186](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/186), which is merged to `main`. The [RC4 release notes](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.4) also list the startup trust prompt. If you still don’t see it, check which Nexus build you launched: the local checkout I inspected is an older, dirty `main` revision, so I can’t verify that it matches the newer release.","started_at":1792851415,"completed_at":1792851597,"duration_ms":181286,"time_to_first_token_ms":3594}}
