61: Issue body actions\nL162: ## Scope\nL163: \nL164: Complete PLAN-10 task 8 without using held-out tasks for tuning. The isolated authoring lane currently reports 4/20 required distinct repository-arm tasks validated, 4 more in validation drafts, and a remaining gap to the 20-task repository-arm minimum. The 40-task T2 corpus must still meet the accepted class/language distribution and include at least 20 externally sourced tasks; the separate 8-task T3 set is also required.\nL165: ## Acceptance\nL166:   * Freeze the task population, fixtures, validators, and manifests before RC qualification.\nL167:   * Validate every required task with independent validators; retain failures and environment limitations.\nL168:   * Establish custody separate from authoring and candidate development; do not claim independent holdout acceptance until the custodian approves and seals it.\nL169:   * Record digests, provenance, contamination declarations, and license/source evidence.\nL170:   * Update REQ-QUAL-101 only after its accepted criteria are met.\nL171: References: `docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md` task 8; `docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md` §6.1, §6.3.\nL172: \nL173: Reactions are currently unavailable\nL174: ## Activity\nL175: \nL176:   1. 【61†mikeholownych】\nL177: \nL178: added this to the 【72†v1.0.0】 milestone 【74†on Oct 17, 2026】\nL179: \nL180:   2. 【61†mikeholownych】\nL181: \nL182: added\nL183: \nL184: 【71†v1.0.0】\nL185: \nL186: 【75†on Oct 17, 2026】\nL187: \nL188:   3. ### mikeholownych commented on Oct 17, 2026\nL189: \nL190: 【61†mikeholownych】\nL191: \nL192: 【76†on Oct 17, 2026】\nL193: \nL194: Owner Author\nL195: \nL196: More actions\nL197: 2026-10-17 qualification checkpoint: the author reports 20/20 repository-arm tasks in candidate v15, but the full T2 package is still invalid. The fixture-arm portion did not match the accepted runner contract; the first isolated Docker validation had permission/setup failures, and a later single-task run was stopped when its harness exposed private validators to the same process boundary. Those are preserved as infrastructure evidence and are not task outcomes.\nL198: The author is rebuilding fixture-arm validation around the accepted Bubblewrap subprocess boundary. No corpus custody/seal or T2 qualification acceptance is claimed; T3 remains paused until T2 is valid.\nL199:   4. ### mikeholownych commented on Oct 18, 2026\nL200: \nL201: 【61†mikeholownych】\nL202: \nL203: 【77†on Oct 18, 2026】\nL204: \nL205: Owner Author\nL206: \nL207: More actions\nL208: \nL209: Status check at `v1/integration` @ `6a16cb6` (claude-code; metadata only, no private payloads read). The 2026-10-17 v15 comment is superseded.\nL210: \nL211: Done\nL212:      * T2 `heldout-v2`: 40 external-repo tasks, 10 per class × 10 per language, sealed at 03:05:52Z and merged in 【78†eval(v1): seal held-out T2 corpus (40 tasks) and record custody #16】. Public manifest `eval/heldout-manifest.json` (sha256 `50895b84…`), custody report `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md`, custodian 40/40 reference validation, contaminated batch `author-b9` quarantined.\nL213:      * T3: 8 tasks sealed (`eval/heldout-t3-manifest.json`, `t3-custody-report-2026-10-18.md`).\nL214:      * Stores are `root:root` 0700 (tasks/reference 0500), so implementer shells running as uid 1000 are denied.\nL215: Still open before this can close\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16e48-57ed-79c2-bd99-946dbd9156e1","create_time":1792851619.2746875}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
