{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T14:35:34.607Z","ordinal":293157,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016adcc235fe7481a0a90f5a95c6dcc0aa","status":"completed","call_id":"call_78cde16ef3f34b85a84b3a9f49213c08","name":"exec","input":"const r=await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '130,188p' cli/src/credentials.ts; sed -n '55,125p' docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-code\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:4000});\ntext(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16e48-57ed-79c2-bd99-946dbd9156e1","create_time":1792852533.9963157}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T14:35:34.729Z","ordinal":293158,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16e48-57ed-79c2-bd99-946dbd9156e1","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a16e48-57ed-79c2-bd99-946dbd9156e1","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016adcc235528081a08db69b090924d63e","usage":{"input_tokens":235761,"cached_input_tokens":233472,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":93,"reasoning_output_tokens":11,"total_tokens":235854},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":14374313,"cached_input_tokens":14228352,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":32941,"reasoning_output_tokens":24146,"total_tokens":14407254},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":5313999870,"cached_input_tokens":5257179776,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":14780785,"reasoning_output_tokens":8410240,"total_tokens":5328780655}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T14:35:35.641Z","ordinal":293159,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16e48-57ed-79c2-bd99-946dbd9156e1","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-13c61549-db59-40ce-874d-4b8658a403e9","process_id":"34896","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '130,188p' cli/src/credentials.ts; sed -n '55,125p' docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '130,188p' cli/src/credentials.ts","name":"credentials.ts","path":"cli/src/credentials.ts"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '55,125p' docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md","name":"CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md","path":"docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"const CRUSH_IDS: Record<string, string[]> = { openrouter: [\"openrouter\"], openai: [\"openai\"], anthropic: [\"anthropic\"], chatgpt: [\"openai\"], copilot: [\"copilot\"] };\n\n/** Connections registered in other clients for `providerId`, best first. Read-only. */\nexport function externalCredentials(providerId: string): ResolvedCredential[] {\n  const home = credentialStorageHome();\n  const out: ResolvedCredential[] = [];\n  const oauthWanted = providerId === \"chatgpt\" || providerId === \"copilot\";\n\n  if (providerId === \"chatgpt\") {\n    const file = path.join(home, \".codex/auth.json\");\n    const codex = readJson(file);\n    const t = codex?.tokens;\n    if (typeof t?.access_token === \"string\" && t.access_token) {\n      out.push({\n        source: \"Codex CLI\",\n        kind: \"external\",\n        file,\n        refreshable: false,\n        credential: {\n          type: \"oauth\",\n          access: t.access_token,\n          expiresAt: jwtExpiry(t.access_token),\n          accountId: t.account_id || chatgptAccountId(t.id_token, t.access_token),\n          savedAt: codex.last_refresh ?? now(),\n        },\n      });\n    }\n  }\n\n  const ocFile = path.join(home, \".local/share/opencode/auth.json\");\n  const oc = readJson(ocFile);\n  for (const id of OPENCODE_IDS[providerId] ?? []) {\n    const e = oc?.[id];\n    if (!e || typeof e !== \"object\") continue;\n    if (oauthWanted && e.type === \"oauth\" && typeof e.access === \"string\") {\n      out.push({\n        source: \"opencode\",\n        kind: \"external\",\n        file: ocFile,\n        refreshable: false,\n        credential: {\n          type: \"oauth\",\n          access: e.access,\n          refresh: providerId === \"copilot\" ? e.refresh : undefined, // Copilot: the GitHub token, exchangeable without rotation\n          expiresAt: typeof e.expires === \"number\" && e.expires > 0 ? e.expires : jwtExpiry(e.access),\n          accountId: e.accountId,\n          savedAt: now(),\n        },\n      });\n    } else if (!oauthWanted && e.type === \"api\" && literalKey(e.key)) {\n      out.push({ source: \"opencode\", kind: \"external\", file: ocFile, refreshable: false, credential: { type: \"api\", key: literalKey(e.key)!, savedAt: now() } });\n    }\n  }\n\n  const crushFile = path.join(home, \".local/share/crush/crush.json\");\n  const crush = readJson(crushFile);\n  for (const id of CRUSH_IDS[providerId] ?? []) {\n    const p = crush?.providers?.[id];\n    if (!p || typeof p !== \"object\") continue;\n2. Select a provider and model, per run or as your default:\n\n   ```bash\n   nexus run --provider anthropic --model claude-sonnet-4-5 \"...\"\n   # or in ~/.config/nexus/config.env\n   NEXUS_PROVIDER=openrouter\n   NEXUS_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.5\n   ```\n\n   Model ids are passed verbatim (slashes and `:free`-style suffixes are fine). There is no auto-detected cloud\n   model: an unset model is a configuration error.\n3. Check it: `nexus providers` shows each provider, whether its credential is set (never its value), each role's\n   destination and the authorized cloud destinations. `nexus providers verify --provider <id> --model <m>` performs a\n   live check — a streamed completion and a tool round trip — sending no workspace content.\n\nRoles: `--planner-provider/--planner-model` and `--coder-provider/--coder-model` (or `PLANNER_LLM_PROVIDER`,\n`CODER_LLM_PROVIDER`) bind a role to a provider. A role without its own provider uses its own `--*-endpoint` if\ngiven, else the main connection. Subagents, the LLM compaction summary and scheduled work units inherit the main\nconnection unless an operation spec resource names `\"providerId\"`. Embeddings are never sent to a cloud provider\n(search falls back to lexical).\n\nOther settings: `--base-url` / `NEXUS_<ID>_BASE_URL` (override, e.g. a regional endpoint; required for\n`compatible`), `NEXUS_COMPATIBLE_AUTH=none` (declare an auth-less compatible service), `NEXUS_REASONING_EFFORT`\n(OpenAI reasoning effort), `NEXUS_ANTHROPIC_THINKING_BUDGET` (Anthropic extended thinking, ≥ 1024),\n`--context-limit` (cloud models keep the conservative 65536 default unless you set the real window).\n\n## Authority and disclosure\n\n- Only the operator selects a cloud destination: command-line flags, the operator's own environment, or\n  `~/.config/nexus/config.env`. A project `.env` cannot set `NEXUS_PROVIDER`, `*_LLM_PROVIDER` or a provider base URL\n  (it is ignored with a warning). A cloud endpoint that only a project `.env` chose is refused before anything is sent.\n- The first request to each cloud origin prints a notice that task content (prompts, tool results, file excerpts) is\n  sent there. Secret tokenization (`InformationFlowBoundary`) still applies to every outbound request.\n- Local-to-cloud fallback is off: a fallback endpoint that is a cloud destination is skipped unless its origin is in\n  `NEXUS_CLOUD_DISCLOSURE_ORIGINS`. Provider connections never use the appliance fallback list.\n- `NEXUS_CLOUD_ROUTED_ORIGINS` marks local-looking origins that forward to a cloud service; they are then treated as\n  cloud destinations (authorization required).\n\n## Credentials\n\nEach provider's key is bound to its connection's origin. A provider connection never receives the appliance gateway\ntoken, `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY`, or another provider's key, and the appliance never receives a cloud key. Provider requests\nrefuse redirects so a key cannot follow a server to another origin. Keys are never persisted in sessions, task state\nor receipts; provider error bodies are bounded and redacted.\n\n## Failures and recovery\n\nProvider failures are typed: `AUTH_FAILURE` (401/403), `QUOTA_EXHAUSTED` (402, `insufficient_quota`, billing),\n`RATE_LIMITED` (429, honours `Retry-After`), `OVERLOADED` (529/503, overloaded error events), `CAPACITY_REJECTED`\n(context too long), `REQUEST_REJECTED`, transport timeouts/interruptions. Temporary conditions are waited out by the\nexisting bounded recovery loop for the same target; auth, quota and request errors stop the turn. A response is used\nonly when the provider's terminal event arrives: an incomplete stream, `max_tokens` truncation or an error frame\ndiscards the partial output and no tool call from it runs. Explicit selections are strict — there is no automatic\nswitch to another provider or model, including after a refusal.\n\n## Usage, cost and limits\n\nEvery provider request (main, planner/coder, subagent, compaction, verification) records a receipt in\n`<workspace>/.nexus/inference_receipts.jsonl`: role, provider, selected and effective model, origin, protocol,\noutcome, provider request id, reported usage, and cost confidence. Cost is recorded only when the provider reports it\n(OpenRouter); otherwise it is `unknown` — never estimated. `/tokens` and `nexus run` show a cloud usage summary;\n`run -j` adds `cloudUsage`.\n\nProcess-wide limits, shared by all roles and subagents and enforced before each provider-connection request (a plain\n`--endpoint` that happens to be a cloud host is disclosure-gated but neither metered nor limited):\n`NEXUS_CLOUD_MAX_REQUESTS`, `NEXUS_CLOUD_MAX_TOKENS` (reported tokens plus in-flight reservations),\n`NEXUS_CLOUD_MAX_COST_USD` (only for providers that report cost; with any other provider the request is refused\nrather than guessed). These are budgets, not a guarantee of the provider's invoice.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":38210}},"started_at_ms":1792852535640,"completed_at_ms":1792852535641}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T14:35:37.041Z","ordinal":293160,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a16e56-aed0-73a3-b581-1088e48d0208","call_id":"call_78cde16ef3f34b85a84b3a9f49213c08","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"const CRUSH_IDS: Record<string, string[]> = { openrouter: [\"openrouter\"], openai: [\"openai\"], anthropic: [\"anthropic\"], chatgpt: [\"openai\"], copilot: [\"copilot\"] };\n\n/** Connections registered in other clients for `providerId`, best first. Read-only. */\nexport function externalCredentials(providerId: string): ResolvedCredential[] {\n  const home = credentialStorageHome();\n  const out: ResolvedCredential[] = [];\n  const oauthWanted = providerId === \"chatgpt\" || providerId === \"copilot\";\n\n  if (providerId === \"chatgpt\") {\n    const file = path.join(home, \".codex/auth.json\");\n    const codex = readJson(file);\n    const t = codex?.tokens;\n    if (typeof t?.access_token === \"string\" && t.access_token) {\n      out.push({\n        source: \"Codex CLI\",\n        kind: \"external\",\n        file,\n        refreshable: false,\n        credential: {\n          type: \"oauth\",\n          access: t.access_token,\n          expiresAt: jwtExpiry(t.access_token),\n          accountId: t.account_id || chatgptAccountId(t.id_token, t.access_token),\n          savedAt: codex.last_refresh ?? now(),\n        },\n      });\n    }\n  }\n\n  const ocFile = path.join(home, \".local/share/opencode/auth.json\");\n  const oc = readJson(ocFile);\n  for (const id of OPENCODE_IDS[providerId] ?? []) {\n    const e = oc?.[id];\n    if (!e || typeof e !== \"object\") continue;\n    if (oauthWanted && e.type === \"oauth\" && typeof e.access === \"string\") {\n      out.push({\n        source: \"opencode\",\n        kind: \"external\",\n        file: ocFile,\n        refreshable: false,\n        credential: {\n          type: \"oauth\",\n          access: e.access,\n          refresh: providerId === \"copilot\" ? e.refresh : undefined, // Copilot: the GitHub token, exchangeable without rotation\n          expiresAt: typeof e.expires === \"number\" && e.expires > 0 ? e.expires : jwtExpiry(e.access),\n          accountId: e.accountId,\n          savedAt: now(),\n        },\n      });\n    } else if (!oauthWanted && e.type === \"api\" && literalKey(e.key)) {\n      out.push({ source: \"opencode\", kind: \"external\", file: ocFile, refreshable: false, credential: { type: \"api\", key: literalKey(e.key)!, savedAt: now() } });\n    }\n  }\n\n  const crushFile = path.join(home, \".local/share/crush/crush.json\");\n  const crush = readJson(crushFile);\n  for (const id of CRUSH_IDS[providerId] ?? []) {\n    const p = crush?.providers?.[id];\n    if (!p || typeof p !== \"object\") continue;\n2. Select a provider and model, per run or as your default:\n\n   ```bash\n   nexus run --provider anthropic --model claude-sonnet-4-5 \"...\"\n   # or in ~/.config/nexus/config.env\n   NEXUS_PROVIDER=openrouter\n   NEXUS_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.5\n   ```\n\n   Model ids are passed verbatim (slashes and `:free`-style suffixes are fine). There is no auto-detected cloud\n   model: an unset model is a configuration error.\n3. Check it: `nexus providers` shows each provider, whether its credential is set (never its value), each role's\n   destination and the authorized cloud destinations. `nexus providers verify --provider <id> --model <m>` performs a\n   live check — a streamed completion and a tool round trip — sending no workspace content.\n\nRoles: `--planner-provider/--planner-model` and `--coder-provider/--coder-model` (or `PLANNER_LLM_PROVIDER`,\n`CODER_LLM_PROVIDER`) bind a role to a provider. A role without its own provider uses its own `--*-endpoint` if\ngiven, else the main connection. Subagents, the LLM compaction summary and scheduled work units inherit the main\nconnection unless an operation spec resource names `\"providerId\"`. Embeddings are never sent to a cloud provider\n(search falls back to lexical).\n\nOther settings: `--base-url` / `NEXUS_<ID>_BASE_URL` (override, e.g. a regional endpoint; required for\n`compatible`), `NEXUS_COMPATIBLE_AUTH=none` (declare an auth-less compatible service), `NEXUS_REASONING_EFFORT`\n(OpenAI reasoning effort), `NEXUS_ANTHROPIC_THINKING_BUDGET` (Anthropic extended thinking, ≥ 1024),\n`--context-limit` (cloud models keep the conservative 65536 default unless you set the real window).\n\n## Authority and disclosure\n\n- Only the operator selects a cloud destination: command-line flags, the operator's own environment, or\n  `~/.config/nexus/config.env`. A project `.env` cannot set `NEXUS_PROVIDER`, `*_LLM_PROVIDER` or a provider base URL\n  (it is ignored with a warning). A cloud endpoint that only a project `.env` chose is refused before anything is sent.\n- The first request to each cloud origin prints a notice that task content (prompts, tool results, file excerpts) is\n  sent there. Secret tokenization (`InformationFlowBoundary`) still applies to every outbound request.\n- Local-to-cloud fallback is off: a fallback endpoint that is a cloud destination is skipped unless its origin is in\n  `NEXUS_CLOUD_DISCLOSURE_ORIGINS`. Provider connections never use the appliance fallback list.\n- `NEXUS_CLOUD_ROUTED_ORIGINS` marks local-looking origins that forward to a cloud service; they are then treated as\n  cloud destinations (authorization required).\n\n## Credentials\n\nEach provider's key is bound to its connection's origin. A provider connection never receives the appliance gateway\ntoken, `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY`, or another provider's key, and the appliance never receives a cloud key. Provider requests\nrefuse redirects so a key cannot follow a server to another origin. Keys are never persisted in sessions, task state\nor receipts; provider error bodies are bounded and redacted.\n\n## Failures and recovery\n\nProvider failures are typed: `AUTH_FAILURE` (401/403), `QUOTA_EXHAUSTED` (402, `insufficient_quota`, billing),\n`RATE_LIMITED` (429, honours `Retry-After`), `OVERLOADED` (529/503, overloaded error events), `CAPACITY_REJECTED`\n(context too long), `REQUEST_REJECTED`, transport timeouts/interruptions. Temporary conditions are waited out by the\nexisting bounded recovery loop for the same target; auth, quota and request errors stop the turn. A response is used\nonly when the provider's terminal event arrives: an incomplete stream, `max_tokens` truncation or an error frame\ndiscards the partial output and no tool call from it runs. Explicit selections are strict — there is no automatic\nswitch to another provider or model, including after a refusal.\n\n## Usage, cost and limits\n\nEvery provider request (main, planner/coder, subagent, compaction, verification) records a receipt in\n`<workspace>/.nexus/inference_receipts.jsonl`: role, provider, selected and effective model, origin, protocol,\noutcome, provider request id, reported usage, and cost confidence. Cost is recorded only when the provider reports it\n(OpenRouter); otherwise it is `unknown` — never estimated. `/tokens` and `nexus run` show a cloud usage summary;\n`run -j` adds `cloudUsage`.\n\nProcess-wide limits, shared by all roles and subagents and enforced before each provider-connection request (a plain\n`--endpoint` that happens to be a cloud host is disclosure-gated but neither metered nor limited):\n`NEXUS_CLOUD_MAX_REQUESTS`, `NEXUS_CLOUD_MAX_TOKENS` (reported tokens plus in-flight reservations),\n`NEXUS_CLOUD_MAX_COST_USD` (only for providers that report cost; with any other provider the request is refused\nrather than guessed). These are budgets, not a guarantee of the provider's invoice.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16e48-57ed-79c2-bd99-946dbd9156e1","create_time":1792852537.0408883}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
