,{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.list_pr_changed_filenames"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.get_pr_diff"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_file"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.rerun_failed_workflow_run_jobs"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f6-7b50-7a00-9fbb-818f2ac4eed4","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch"},{"first_turn_id":"01a156f6-7b50-7a00-9fbb-818f2ac4eed4","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"fetch_topic"},{"first_turn_id":"01a15e3e-2987-7e62-9699-29ab11a9d023","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"search"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a162a0-311d-7271-a76d-8992331bb312","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_pr_file_patch"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16af7-b30b-7543-b5d3-5d0470af8bf9","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_branches"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16b07-bb74-7501-b966-9445743dc69f","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_issue"},{"first_turn_id":"01a16e23-3d1b-7571-9aa1-825e60ce3175","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"create_agent_identity"}],"status":"complete"}}],"resume_metadata":{"last_started_turn_id":"01a16e48-57ed-79c2-bd99-946dbd9156e1","multi_agent_version":"v2","previous_turn_settings":{"comp_hash":"3000","model":"gpt-6-luna","realtime_active":false},"turn_attribution":{"initiating_agent_path":null,"parent_turn_id":null,"root_turn_id":"01a16e48-57ed-79c2-bd99-946dbd9156e1","turn_id":"01a16e48-57ed-79c2-bd99-946dbd9156e1","turn_trigger":"goal"}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcbde0440481a0aca5e8edecb01cfb","order":15024,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a16e45-b47e-70d1-8ada-fc972c9b3e5c","text":"I’m continuing with read-only release checks while avoiding further cleanup or repository edits. I’ll refresh PR #194 and the published RC4 status, and keep the possible home-directory data loss explicitly unresolved until it can be assessed.","turn_id":"01a16e45-93b3-7a42-bd33-3c943d45de73"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcbe1f946481a08b1d6c82a0f966c0","order":15025,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a16e46-af94-7af0-924b-28a2a1ce4e16","text":"The screenshot makes the missing behavior clear: on startup, Nexus should ask whether to trust the current project folder, explain that project instructions such as `AGENTS.md` will be loaded, and let the user choose to continue or exit. I’ll check the current startup flow and its existing safety/permission model before changing anything.\n\nOne operational note: the project’s Claude memory capture is temporarily paused because its five-hour usage reached the configured 98% threshold; existing notes remain available. I’ll continue with the repository state and tools available here.","turn_id":"01a16e45-93b3-7a42-bd33-3c943d45de73"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcbe7ec29481a0a0b08ee97e045927","order":15027,"phase":"final_answer","revision":"retained_01a16e48-252c-74d2-88b3-f76cf06de020","text":"Yes—that is the missing startup behavior: Nexus should ask about an unfamiliar project folder before loading its project instructions. The choices should let you **trust and continue**, **continue without trusting**, or **exit**. Continuing without trust should preserve your chosen permission mode; it should not force read-only.\n\nThis has since been implemented in [PR #186](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/186), which is merged to `main`. The [RC4 release notes](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.4) also list the startup trust prompt. If you still don’t see it, check which Nexus build you launched: the local checkout I inspected is an older, dirty `main` revision, so I can’t verify that it matches the newer release.","turn_id":"01a16e45-93b3-7a42-bd33-3c943d45de73"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcbe92c68081a0b6436b0f44400384","order":15028,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a16e48-6f3f-7ed1-baf7-78808deed586","text":"I’m resuming the release work with read-only checks first. The local checkout is known to be dirty and behind, so I’ll leave it untouched and use current remote revisions and qualification records to find the next actionable release gate.","turn_id":"01a16e48-57ed-79c2-bd99-946dbd9156e1"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcbf2fe22c81a0aad8f02c55e48412","order":15032,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a16e4a-d5f7-7072-9090-be3c6b0491be","text":"The exact remote state is clearer now: `origin/main` is `be2cd2f`, while the local checkout remains at `db1ca558` with pre-existing changes. PR #194 has an independent ACCEPT and CodeQL success; its Node 22/24 full test jobs are still running. The RC4 candidate is public, but its cross-runner comparison failed before it compared artifacts.","turn_id":"01a16e48-57ed-79c2-bd99-946dbd9156e1"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcbfdca25881a09885ccb1159e3037","order":15037,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a16e4d-789a-7ba1-a68c-06a2453b8a4e","text":"PR #194’s CI is progressing: Node 22 has passed, and Node 24 is still in the full CLI test step. The cross-runner workflow fix remains the next integration action; I’m holding it until exact-head CI finishes, then I can trigger RC4’s artifact comparison without touching the dirty checkout.","turn_id":"01a16e48-57ed-79c2-bd99-946dbd9156e1"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcc0458e4481a080c39fdff0507f00","order":15040,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a16e4f-113a-7fa1-ad42-d60b33fadd29","text":"The Ubuntu host is reachable at `10.0.8.3`. It has xterm, kitty, tmux 3.6, VS Code, and GNOME Terminal installed, and GNOME is active with a local `seat0` session. The SSH shell itself is a TTY without a display, so I’m checking how to install and identify the exact RC4 package on that host before treating it as ready for the manual matrix.","turn_id":"01a16e48-57ed-79c2-bd99-946dbd9156e1"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcc2246e2081a0b6d0c97f7fc5f128","order":15046,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a16e56-60fd-76c0-a8f5-8576a52b43f1","text":"RC4 is now installed on both the Ubuntu desktop and an isolated local prefix, with the expected artifact digest and GitHub provenance verified. I also confirmed the terminal matrix’s exact checklist and that the GUI session is active. The desktop lacks Nexus provider configuration, and the current gateway check requires a named cloud provider, so I stopped before sending inference; this is setup evidence, not a qualification pass.","turn_id":"01a16e48-57ed-79c2-bd99-946dbd9156e1"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":15047,"sender_deliveries":[{"order":7850,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a15e0d-46de-72f1-8e85-967b05e2dfc6","receiver_turn_id":"01a15e0b-8f5d-7b40-aa6b-62735e71e8a0","text":"\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES START\nReceived message: fco_01a15e0d-46de-72f1-8e85-967b05e2dfc6\nSource thread: 01a139bf-d0bf-74e0-b969-dd59f00a9605\nHost: Up to three recent user messages with preceding assistant context, captured at delivery. Assistant messages a