ong tasks** | `/compact`; `model_auto_compact_token_limit`, `model_context_window`; `/status` shows context usage; `codex resume`; `/fork` copies a chat to a new chat or worktree; `tool_output_token_limit`; resumable state in a SQLite DB (`sqlite_home`); AGENTS.md (`project_doc_max_bytes`, fallback filenames); memories [CX-CFG][CX-SLASH][CX-CLI]. | Auto-compaction at a per-model threshold, `/autocompact <tokens>`, `/compact [focus]`, `/context`; after compaction re-injects CLAUDE.md/startup content, a structured summary, up to 5 most-recent files and invoked skill bodies (5k cap each) [CC-CTX]. Rewind menu can \"summarize from/up to here\" [CC-CKPT]. `--continue/--resume`, `/branch`, `--fork-session`; resume-from-summary dialog for idle >1h, >100k-token sessions [CC-SESS]. CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, auto memory [CC-OV]. Subagent `autoCompactWindow` (2.1.296) [CC-CHG]. | `compaction.auto` (default true), `compaction.prune` (old tool outputs, default false), `compaction.reserved` token buffer [OC-CFG]. Per-model `limit.context/output` for custom providers [OC-PROV]. `instructions` file globs [OC-CFG]. | Auto-compact at min(80% of window, 225k tokens) (`GOOSE_AUTO_COMPACT_THRESHOLD`/`_TOKEN_LIMIT`); `/compact`; fallback strategies summarize/truncate/clear/prompt (`GOOSE_CONTEXT_STRATEGY`); headless defaults to summarize [GS-CTX]. | Ollama: warns 2k default ctx \"silently discards context\"; aider sets `num_ctx` to fit each request + 8k reply [AI-OLLAMA]. (No compaction feature verified this session.) |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/peers.md:56:8. After compaction, project instructions (AGENTS.md-equivalent) and recently edited files are re-injected [CC-CTX].\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:112:| AGT-R8 | No implicit standing rules from prompts; no workspace writes in read-only mode; workspace-supplied knowledge gated by workspace trust. | safety (AGT-10) | RELEASE-REQUIRED | Read-only run leaves no `.nexus/`; prompt \"never run tests\" does not appear in next session's system prompt. |\ncli/src/mcp.ts:950:              description: \"Content of AGENTS.md project rules and conventions\",\ncli/src/mcp.ts:976:        const agentsFile = path.join(this.workspace, \"AGENTS.md\");\ncli/src/mcp.ts:977:        const content = fs.existsSync(agentsFile) ? fs.readFileSync(agentsFile, \"utf-8\") : \"# No AGENTS.md found\";\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:37:  - workspace trust;\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:148:| tasks/, AGENTS.md, README, quickstart | 5 | Full read | lead | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:203:Record PASS/FAIL per cell, with a screenshot of the approval panel and the post-exit terminal state.\ncli/src/doctor.ts:723:  if (risky.length) return f(\"plugins.config\", \"extensions\", \"warn\", `${risky.length} plugin problem(s): untrusted workspace plugins are not loaded; world-writable plugin files could be changed by anyone. ${note}`, [...risky, ...found.slice(0, 10)], \"Trust the workspace (`nexus trust`) or remove its plugins; restrict writable files with `chmod o-w <file>`.\");\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:3:These rules apply to every agent (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Nexus itself, or a human) that implements any part of this package at the same time as another. The repository's root `AGENTS.md` points here. The rules come from incidents recorded in `tasks/lessons.md`:\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md:1:# PLAN-03: Untrusted workspace inputs and the egress boundary\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:19:| nexus_tui/composer.rs, diff_view.rs, markdown.rs, highlight.rs, models.rs, review.rs, slash.rs, protocol.rs, sidecar.rs, redact.rs | not read line-by-line; exercised indirectly via PTY (diff in approval panel, markdown reply, slash /sessions /quit, sidecar lifecycle). Excluded from deep review for budget; covered by repo tui_*_e2e tests (coordinator running) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:63:| TUI-07 | S2 | Default safety posture | sidecar.ts:935; repl.ts:69; quickstart.md:55 | SOURCE + DOC-CLAIM: default mode is `auto` (no approvals) for both surfaces; quickstart says \"Enter a small task, review requested actions\" | New users unknowingly grant the model unprompted write/shell authority | Decide v1 default (recommend review on first run / untrusted workspace); fix quickstart wording |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:147:| TUI-R6 | Default approval posture is an explicit, documented decision; first run in an untrusted workspace states the mode and how to change it | safety (TUI-07) | RELEASE-REQUIRED | PTY first-run screen contains mode + switch hint; docs match |\ncli/src/git.ts:49:    \"AGENTS.md\",\ncli/src/git.ts:73:  const target = path.join(workspace, \"AGENTS.md\");\ncli/src/index.ts:445:  .option(\"--list\", \"List trusted workspaces\")\ncli/src/index.ts:450:      console.log(list.length ? list.join(\"\\n\") : \"No trusted workspaces.\");\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:37:  - `.nexus-security.json` is read from the untrusted workspace (security.ts:48). It can only add entries, except that `allowedDomains` narrows egress and `allowExternalSymlinks` is never consumed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:53:| SEC-05 | S2 | untrusted repo opened | skills.ts:31-33; agent.ts:3301,3789 | SOURCE. Workspace skills (SKILL.md) are loaded and advertised in the system prompt with no workspace-trust check, unlike MCP and plugins (workspace_trust.ts:5-24). `activate_skill` is non-mutating, so it is never approved. | Persistent prompt injection from a cloned repo. Combined with SEC-01 this gives command execution. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: gate workspace skill directories on workspace trust, or show them as untrusted and require approval to activate. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:136:| R-SEC-5 | Workspace skills are subject to workspace trust. | safety | RELEASE-REQUIRED | An untrusted fixture repo with `skills/x/SKILL.md` does not appear in the system prompt or `/skills` without trust. |\ncli/src/