{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T14:36:47.679Z","ordinal":293214,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16e48-57ed-79c2-bd99-946dbd9156e1","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcc27e5ef881a093b2721a9084aaa8","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Understood—you mean Nexus should ask whether to trust the current folder before loading its project instructions, such as `AGENTS.md`.\n\nThat flow is already in the published **v1.0.0-rc.4** and current `origin/main`: it shows “Trust this folder?”, identifies the instruction file, and offers **Trust and continue**, **Continue without trusting**, or **Exit**. RC4 is not yet accepted; release acceptance remains in progress.\n\nIf you didn’t see the prompt, Nexus skips it for a folder already remembered as trusted. Non-interactive launches also skip the chooser and print an untrusted-workspace notice. The exact prompt is in [startup_trust.ts](/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/startup_trust.ts)."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1792852606413,"completed_at_ms":1792852607679}}
