 (`net.isIP` + CIDR), treat hostnames as external unless loopback/`localhost` or operator-listed. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:35:| PRV-08 | S3 | locality classification | egress.ts:129-141 | RUNTIME R1: `127.0.0.2`, bare LAN host `gpubox`, Tailscale `100.101.102.103` -> cloud. IPv6 ULA / `host.docker.internal` same by SOURCE. | Legit LAN/Tailscale/docker inference servers show a \"Cloud inference\" notice, are refused when chosen by project `.env`/fallback, and get EXTERNAL_PUBLIC egress handling; no \"mark local\" setting (NEXUS_CLOUD_DISCLOSURE_ORIGINS only authorizes). | Add `NEXUS_LOCAL_ORIGINS` (operator-only) and full loopback/CGNAT/ULA handling; document. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:38:| PRV-11 | S4 | homelab assumptions | client.ts:63-69 (`~/.config/opencode/t5820-client-token`), providers.ts:161 + client.ts:644-647 (X-Task-Class to every endpoint), client.ts:947 (`X-Nexus-Purpose`), CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md (`/model appliance engineering/b0`) | SOURCE | Harmless for standalone (token scoped to config.env origin; servers ignore headers) but homelab names leak into product/docs. | Rename/genericise before v1 docs; make gateway token path configurable. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:44:| PRV-17 | S4 | docs | docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md Limitations (\"No model catalog cache\") vs model_catalog.ts:51,86; Credentials (\"error bodies are bounded and redacted\") true only for provider connections (PRV-03); Authority claim (PRV-02); USER_MANUAL.md:3 \"direct parity with OpenAI Codex and Anthropic Claude Code\" | DOC-CLAIM vs SOURCE | Docs overstate guarantees. | Correct docs. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:93:| G2 Live cloud qualification limited to openrouter + chatgpt (docs/reviews/NEXUS_CLOUD_PROVIDERS_LIVE_QUALIFICATION_2026-10-11.md, HISTORICAL). openai, anthropic, copilot, compatible: mock-only. | `nexus providers verify --provider {openai,anthropic,copilot,compatible} --model <m> -j` with operator keys; archive JSON. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:111:| PRV-R10 | Docs match behaviour: remove homelab ids, fix catalog-cache and redaction claims, document custom CA and LAN/Tailscale locality setting. | docs | RELEASE-REQUIRED | Doc review checklist against PRV-11/17/18. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:36:| 11 | Remove homelab coupling: `NEXUS_GATEWAY_TOKEN_FILE` replaces the hardcoded token path; send `X-Task-Class` only when the gateway capability is advertised or configured; neutral doc examples. | `client.ts:63-69,644-647,947`; `providers.ts:161`; `CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md`; `ARCHITECTURE.md` | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md:73:8. **REQ-AGT-119.** Experimental surfaces (DEC-07: `nexus eval`, `/tdd`, team roles) are labelled experimental in help and docs and excluded from qualification claims. `nexus eval` runs in a worktree and never touches the operator's checkout. Team reviewer and researcher roles run with a read-only tool set.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:27:| docs/PERS002_*, WP05_*, CRED003_* | grep for verdicts/claims; PHASE2S review not read (63KB). Excluded for budget. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:55:| VER-04 | S2 | Configured-verifier VERIFIED claims; discovered-verifier coverage | tester.ts:356-360 | RUNTIME (tester_probe). `isVerifierDeliverableBound` matches basenames by substring against the command and the output. If `src/a.ts` changed and the output mentions `src/data.ts`, the run counts as bound. If `README.md` changed and the output says \"see README.md\", it counts as bound. Any changed file under `test/` binds the whole change. With a configured verifier, bound means VERIFIED (agent.ts:5124-5146, no independence check). | VERIFIED can rest on a filename coincidence instead of coverage. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: match whole path tokens (boundary-delimited relative paths). Drop basename matching or require a path separator before it. Require a test-path change to be accompanied by executed tests from that file. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:59:| VER-08 | S2 | `--tdd` / `/tdd` | synthesizer.ts:239-326; agent.ts:5236-5255 | SOURCE + INFERENCE. `runAutonomousTdd` never calls `verifyRedPhase` or `verifyGreenPhase`, ignores every `agent.run` result, and contains dead code (266-272). Success is only a full-suite exit 0, with no check that tests executed. Each `agent.run` calls `resetConversation()` (AGT-01), so GREEN starts with no memory of the RED test. The RED prompt asks the model to call `task_completed` with a deliberately failing test, but the completion oracle runs the discovered verifier, which fails → completion refused (INFERENCE). The success summary claims \"RED -> GREEN -> REFACTOR verified\". | The TDD mode advertises a protocol it does not enforce. RED turns likely end in NOT_ESTABLISHED or stagnation. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: enforce the phases (run the repro target and require fail, then pass), carry the conversation between phases, exempt the RED phase from the completion oracle; or mark the mode experimental. Add an e2e test with a mock model. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:32:| docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST.md, docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST_CRITICAL_PATH_ASSESSMENT.md | full read |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:78:| CON-001 | S1 (contest) | Judge deploy / CI | docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST.md:48-49; .github/workflows/ci.yml:29-39; experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/package.json:5-9, cloudflare.config.ts:6-12, src/index.ts:3-4,66-95 | RUNTIME + SOURCE. The documented `npm run typecheck/deploy --prefix experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice` targets the **Experiment-1 Worker** `artifacts-first-repo`. That Worker has hard-coded namespace `nexus-exp1-oct02`, an **unauthenticated POST /create**, and an unauthenticated GET /readback that returns content. The built `worker.config.json` has name=artifacts-first-repo and namespace=nexus-exp1-oct02; the bundle has 0 occurrences of \"work-state\". The NEXUS_CF_* variables set in CI are inert. The contest Worker (agent-collab-worker/) has no npm scripts, no lockfile, and is never typechecked, built or deployed by any documented command. | A judge following the guide deploys the wrong service: unauthenticated, bound to the operator's namespace name, and lacking `/work-state`. The CI \"contest contract\" job is green without covering the submitted Worker. | Before submission: add build/typecheck/deploy scripts and a lockfile to agent-collab-worker (or point the root config at it); fix CONTEST.md; make CI build the contest Worker. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:81:| CON-004 | S2 (contest) | Provenance of submitted evidence | docs/cloudflare/VIDEO_ASSET.md:17-19; docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST.md:5 | SOURCE (git). The video's recorded source commits are `731f5d44…` (Nexus) and `98a8a813…` (contest-demo). Neither is an ancestor of main. They exist only on local branches (`dogfood/*`, `candidate/*`, `contest-demo`) and are on no remote-tracking branch. The run record and freeze manifest the doc cites are not committed. VIDEO_ASSET itself records a CLI bundle hash delta and says \"No clean Cloudflare-backed replay has been made from the target tree\". | Judges cannot tie the video to published source. The video is HISTORICAL evidence of an operator-host run only. | Publish the run record and freeze manifest, plus a tag or branch containing 98a8a813. Alternatively, state plainly that the source behind the video is unpublished. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:88:| CON-011 | S3 | Worker auth | agent-collab-worker/src/index.ts:10-21 | SOURCE. The single static shared bearer (`EXPERIMENT_AUTH`) is used for every run, with no expiry. The compare is constant-time except for the length check. `/health` is unauthenticated and minimal (OK). The Artifacts binding covers the whole namespace; the Worker reads only the configured repo. | Acceptable for a bounded demo, not for a multi-tenant service. The contest doc already disclaims production security (CONTEST.md:15). | Per-run or HMAC tokens after the contest. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:89:| CON-012 | S4 | Doc staleness | docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST_CRITICAL_PATH_ASSESSMENT.md:11,34,88-90 | DOC-CLAIM. The doc dated 2026-10-02 says \"Nexus currently has no Cloudflare Worker\". This is now false and the doc is not marked superseded. CONTEST.md:65 and :89 *correctly* say \"blocked pending clean-account acceptance\". | Reviewer confusion. | Mark the doc HISTORICAL. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md:38:| 11 | Docs: CLOUD_PROVIDERS (authority, locality, `NEXUS_LOCAL_ORIGINS`), USER_MANUAL §4 (trust covers skills and knowledge; plugin trust model; directories), release notes (migration of project `.env` keys). | docs | all |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md:16:| 2 | Add a HISTORICAL banner to `docs/ISSUE12_*.md`, `docs/PHASE*.md`, `docs/WP*.md`, `docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST_CRITICAL_PATH_ASSESSMENT.md`, and the `docs/reviews/*` older than 2026-10-14. The banner text is \"Historical record. Current requirements: docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md.\" | docs | M0 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md:19:| 5 | Remove the parity claim, homelab identifiers, and the `file:///` link. Correct the ARCHITECTURE controls-and-limits section. | `USER_MANUAL.md:3`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `MCP_GUIDE.md`, `CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md` | M0 (cheap, standalone) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/BRIEF.md:13:- Historical docs/reviews and \"VERIFIED\" claims are evidence to check, not proof.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-C1-contest-submission-track.md:10:| C2 | Fix `CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST.md`: the deploy commands, `NEXUS_PROTECTED_TRANSPORT`, the operator-host-only statement, and replacing the blanket-`setpriv` guidance with the shipped sudoers drop-in (C5). | `docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST.md:31,48-60` | First after judging, with a dated post-submission note |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-C1-contest-submission-track.md:16:| C8 | Mark `CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST_CRITICAL_PATH_ASSESSMENT.md` as HISTORICAL. Print computed demo values instead of static strings (CON-014). Bump the dev dependencies flagged by `npm audit` (CON-009). | docs, `demo/nexus-demo.mjs:124,351-352` | Low |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:47:When several agents work at once, the parallel lanes, hot-file serialisation and the single-`GATEWAY` lock in [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) govern the order in which work merges.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:45:| AGT-02 | S2 | `/team`, `nexus operation run/resume` (work units) | agent.ts:3081 (`durableUnit = this.depth === 0`), 3127, 1136-1139, 4389, 1489-1501; operation_runner.ts:559 | SOURCE + DOC-CLAIM. Work units run as `new AutonomousAgent(config, 1)` and ARE durable (resumed via `recoverFromTaskState`), but every depth-gated rule treats depth 1 as a non-durable in-turn subagent: (a) compaction is applied in memory only — no archive append, no checkpoint, never `PERSISTENCE_FAILED`; the next `persistProgress` then writes the compacted conversation and a `committedCompactions` id that has no archive lines, so originals are lost and `read_archive` cannot return them after resume (contradicts COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:145-160 \"Every compaction ... is committed in a fixed order\"); (b) no objective ledger: no requirement gating, no steering, `update_requirements`/`read_objective` not offered; (c) `ExecutionTracker.fresh()` per turn, so loop/stagnation history and cumulative steps reset at every resume/retry; (d) no change baseline / independence judgement (`captureChangeBaseline` depth 0 only, 4034) so discovered-verifier passes are at best REGRESSION_FREE. `runningAsSubagent` already distinguishes the two cases (5003). | Long team/operation units lose compaction originals and convergence history across resume; doc claims overstate durability. | Gate on `runningAsSubagent` (non-durable) instead of `depth`; add a work-unit compaction+resume test asserting archive lines exist. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:99:| Docs not fully re-verified | Only claims relevant to findings (resume, compaction commit, team 15-step cap) were checked against code; remaining claims in COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md/EXECUTION_CONVERGENCE.md are UNVERIFIED by this audit. |\n","exit_code":1,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":28967}},"started_at_ms":1792852663650,"completed_at_ms":1792852663651}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T14:37:44.657Z","ordinal":293274,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a16e58-a150-78d1-990a-12aa8a4e6a90","call_id":"call_b327ec9463a54398ac44d19fccbbdce0","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 7233)\nTotal output lines: 87\n\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:23:CLAIMS=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:34:- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:35:- **Hot-file claims** use the same mechanism with the name `FILE_<path with / replaced by _>`, for example `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`. See §4.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:36:- **Stale claims.** A claim older than 24 h whose PID is gone may be broken, but only by the owner, or by an agent that first records the broken claim in the log.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:50:| Inference | There is one inference host (DEC-16). Any run that uses the gateway takes the claim `GATEWAY` first. That includes eval runs, live checks and stripped-proxy runs. One gateway run at a time, which keeps eval timings valid and prevents overload. Small cloud checks (E5) take `CLOUD` to avoid duplicate spend. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:75:| `docs/USER_MANUAL.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md`, `quickstart.md` | 05, 09 and doc tasks in every plan | Edit only the sections your slice changes. Hold a short `FILE_` claim. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:85:3. Merge order follows the precedence rules in §4 and the ROADMAP milestone order. Within a milestone, the slice with fewer hot-file claims merges first.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:94:| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:95:| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:101:The following groupings can run at the same time with no hot-file contention beyond §4 claims. They are listed by milestone.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:109:| M4 (alongside M3) | PLAN-08 PR-8b..8e. Coordinate with PLAN-04 on `state.ts` through `FILE_` claims. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:110:| M5 | **Serial on `GATEWAY`.** The eval runner, the stripped-proxy runs and the independent reviewer's live task each take the `GATEWAY` claim. The terminal matrix (E3) and the install matrix (E2) can run in parallel with gateway runs. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:39:0. If more than one agent (or person) will implement in parallel, read [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) first. It covers slice claims, worktrees, hot files, the gateway lock and merge order.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:59:**Options.** (A) Fully supported. **(B, chosen)** Shipped and labelled **experimental** in help and docs. Excluded from the qualification task-quality claims. But the following are still fixed for v1:\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:120:- **`nexus eval`.** Labelled experimental. Its scoring is not fixed in v1, but its unsafe `git checkout` in the operator's workspace **is** fixed: it must run in a worktree (VER-07a). It is excluded from all claims. The SPEC-10 harness (`eval/`) is the qualification tool.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:74:   - the gateway token path becomes configurable (`NEXUS_GATEWAY_TOKEN_FILE`), with the h…5633 tokens truncated…\"Historical record. Current requirements: docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md.\" | docs | M0 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md:19:| 5 | Remove the parity claim, homelab identifiers, and the `file:///` link. Correct the ARCHITECTURE controls-and-limits section. | `USER_MANUAL.md:3`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `MCP_GUIDE.md`, `CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md` | M0 (cheap, standalone) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/BRIEF.md:13:- Historical docs/reviews and \"VERIFIED\" claims are evidence to check, not proof.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-C1-contest-submission-track.md:10:| C2 | Fix `CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST.md`: the deploy commands, `NEXUS_PROTECTED_TRANSPORT`, the operator-host-only statement, and replacing the blanket-`setpriv` guidance with the shipped sudoers drop-in (C5). | `docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST.md:31,48-60` | First after judging, with a dated post-submission note |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-C1-contest-submission-track.md:16:| C8 | Mark `CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST_CRITICAL_PATH_ASSESSMENT.md` as HISTORICAL. Print computed demo values instead of static strings (CON-014). Bump the dev dependencies flagged by `npm audit` (CON-009). | docs, `demo/nexus-demo.mjs:124,351-352` | Low |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:47:When several agents work at once, the parallel lanes, hot-file serialisation and the single-`GATEWAY` lock in [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) govern the order in which work merges.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:45:| AGT-02 | S2 | `/team`, `nexus operation run/resume` (work units) | agent.ts:3081 (`durableUnit = this.depth === 0`), 3127, 1136-1139, 4389, 1489-1501; operation_runner.ts:559 | SOURCE + DOC-CLAIM. Work units run as `new AutonomousAgent(config, 1)` and ARE durable (resumed via `recoverFromTaskState`), but every depth-gated rule treats depth 1 as a non-durable in-turn subagent: (a) compaction is applied in memory only — no archive append, no checkpoint, never `PERSISTENCE_FAILED`; the next `persistProgress` then writes the compacted conversation and a `committedCompactions` id that has no archive lines, so originals are lost and `read_archive` cannot return them after resume (contradicts COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:145-160 \"Every compaction ... is committed in a fixed order\"); (b) no objective ledger: no requirement gating, no steering, `update_requirements`/`read_objective` not offered; (c) `ExecutionTracker.fresh()` per turn, so loop/stagnation history and cumulative steps reset at every resume/retry; (d) no change baseline / independence judgement (`captureChangeBaseline` depth 0 only, 4034) so discovered-verifier passes are at best REGRESSION_FREE. `runningAsSubagent` already distinguishes the two cases (5003). | Long team/operation units lose compaction originals and convergence history across resume; doc claims overstate durability. | Gate on `runningAsSubagent` (non-durable) instead of `depth`; add a work-unit compaction+resume test asserting archive lines exist. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:99:| Docs not fully re-verified | Only claims relevant to findings (resume, compaction commit, team 15-step cap) were checked against code; remaining claims in COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md/EXECUTION_CONVERGENCE.md are UNVERIFIED by this audit. |\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16e58-0fa9-73b3-824f-571bf4a9cd42","create_time":1792852664.656965}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
